window.TOPICS=[{"n":78,"t":"Adão e Eva","en":"Adam and Eve","sum":"Adam and Eve were a Material Son and Daughter of Jerusem who came about thirty-eight thousand years ago as biologic uplifters to Urantia, a world isolated by rebellion. They worked in the Garden of Eden for one hundred and seventeen years, but through Eve's impatience to hasten results and Adam's errors of judgment they turned aside from the divine plan and defaulted. They were reduced to mortal status yet cleared of the charge of rebellion, and through the violet race they made a great contribution to the biologic and cultural progress of mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Sending the Biologic Uplifters","items":[{"x":"Material Sons and Daughters are the offspring of the Creator Son, destined to serve as physical uplifters on the evolutionary worlds.","r":["51:1.1"]},{"x":"After the inspection and recommendation of Tabamantia, Adam and Eve were sent to Urantia, a world retarded and isolated by rebellion.","r":["73:0.3"]},{"x":"They were members of the senior corps of Material Sons on Jerusem, an experienced pair who had led research on the modification of life forms.","r":["74:1.1","74:1.2"]},{"x":"The entire senior corps volunteered, and Adam and Eve, who had stayed loyal during the Lucifer rebellion, were chosen.","r":["74:1.3","74:1.4"]},{"x":"They arrived 37,848 years before A.D. 1934, in the season when the Garden was in full bloom.","r":["74:0.1"]}]},{"h":"The Culture of the Garden of Eden","items":[{"x":"The schools of Eden taught health, the golden rule, individual and group rights, play, and competition, aiming at socialization.","r":["74:7.2","74:7.3"]},{"x":"Adam discouraged set prayers and taught that effective prayer must be the personal longing of the soul.","r":["74:7.21"]},{"x":"Adam sought to awaken sex equality by teaching that woman contributes equally with man to new life.","r":["74:7.22"]},{"x":"Traditions such as the six days of creation and the rib story are later confusions and condensations of events from the Garden days.","r":["74:8.1","74:8.3"]},{"q":"A “idade de ouro” é um mito, mas o Éden foi um fato; e a civilização do Jardim foi de fato arruinada.","r":"74:8.14"}]},{"h":"A Difficult Task and Impatience","items":[{"x":"They faced deep loneliness in a world of spiritual darkness, wholly unprepared to accept brotherhood.","r":["75:1.3","75:1.4"]},{"q":"they were not willing to settle down to the long, long endurance test.","r":"75:1.6"},{"x":"Caligastia often visited the Garden urging easier ways, but at first they firmly rejected every proposal of compromise.","r":["75:2.1"]},{"x":"Serapatatia sincerely wanted to help the world but never knew that he had become Caligastia's tool.","r":["75:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Default and Its Consequences","items":[{"x":"In her secret meeting with Cano, Eve broke the long-standing warning against mixing good and evil.","r":["75:4.4","75:4.5"]},{"q":"it constituted evil because it represented the wrong way to achieve righteous ends, because it departed from the right way, the divine plan.","r":"75:4.6"},{"x":"Realizing the failure, Adam in despair committed the same folly as Eve, and enraged inhabitants destroyed a Nodite settlement.","r":["75:5.2","75:5.3"]},{"x":"They left the Garden for the second garden, and their children who had reached twenty could choose the way to Jerusem.","r":["75:6.2","75:6.3"]},{"x":"Gabriel adjudged them in default but cleared them of the charge of rebellion against the universe government.","r":["75:7.1","75:7.2"]},{"q":"Eles haviam feito algo de mal, no entanto, jamais foram culpados de desrespeito à verdade, nem de se alistarem conscientemente na rebelião contra o governo probo do Pai Universal e do seu Filho Criador.","r":"75:7.7"}]},{"h":"There Was No Fall of Man","items":[{"q":"Não houve uma “queda do homem”.","r":"75:8.2"},{"x":"The Adamic bestowal greatly improved mankind biologically, and Adam should not be regarded as the cause of a curse on the human race.","r":["75:8.2","75:8.3"]},{"x":"After their demotion to mortal status they sincerely repented, and Thought Adjusters came to indwell them.","r":["76:5.2"]},{"x":"In the second garden Adam left his life plasm, adding 1,570 superior men and women to the world.","r":["76:4.8"]},{"x":"Adam lived 530 years and, after death, awoke in a special resurrection and attained citizenship on Jerusem.","r":["76:5.5","76:6.2","76:6.3"]},{"q":"Never, in all your ascent to Paradise, will you gain anything by impatiently attempting to circumvent the established and divine plan by short cuts, personal inventions, or other devices","r":"75:8.5"}]}],"see":["Filhos e Filhas Materiais","Caligástia","Raças","Urântia","Revelação","Rebelião de Lúcifer"]},{"n":53,"t":"Adoração","en":"Worship","sum":"Worship is the act of recognizing and rejoicing in the intimate relationship with the Creator; it is the highest privilege and the first duty of all intelligent beings. Unlike prayer, which contains an element of self-interest, worship asks nothing and adores God for what he is. The worship impulse, beginning in primitive nature worship, was turned by the adjutant spirits toward the God of nature, and on Paradise it becomes the highest delight.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Worship","items":[{"q":"A adoração é o privilégio mais elevado e o dever primordial de todas as inteligências criadas.","r":"27:7.1"},{"x":"Worship is the conscious and joyous recognition of the intimate and personal relationships of the Creators with their creatures.","r":["27:7.1"]},{"x":"In the highest sense, worship is directed, directly or indirectly, to the Universal Father.","r":["5:3.1"]},{"x":"Worship is personal communion with that which is divinely real, the source of reality, not a vain monologue.","r":["196:3.22"]},{"x":"Worship is the act of the part identifying itself with the Whole, the finite with the Infinite, the son with the Father.","r":["143:7.8"]}]},{"h":"Worship and Prayer","items":[{"q":"Worship is for its own sake; prayer embodies a self- or creature-interest element","r":"5:3.3"},{"x":"True worship requests nothing and expects no reward; it is a natural response to the Father's lovable nature.","r":["5:3.3"]},{"x":"When self-interest enters worship, it turns into prayer.","r":["5:3.4"]},{"q":"A prece é como a autolembrança — um pensamento sublime -; a adoração é o auto-esquecimento — o suprapensamento.","r":"143:7.7"},{"x":"Prayer is spiritually sustaining, but worship is divinely creative; prayer enriches life, and worship illuminates destiny.","r":["143:7.5","102:4.5"]},{"x":"Modern religions have overemphasized prayer and neglected the more essential communion of worship.","r":["102:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Worship of Soul and Adjuster","items":[{"x":"Sincere worship is the mobilization of all the powers of the personality under the leadership of the evolving soul and the direction of the Adjuster.","r":["5:3.7"]},{"x":"The mortal mind consents to worship, the soul craves it, and the Adjuster conducts that worship to the Father.","r":["5:3.8"]},{"x":"The fragments of the Father are empowered to register the genuine adoration of their subjects before the Universal Father.","r":["5:3.2"]},{"x":"The Father's spirit speaks best when the human mind is in an attitude of true worship.","r":["146:2.17"]},{"q":"A mente mortal consente em adorar; a alma imortal anseia pela adoração e inicia esse ato; a presença do Ajustador divino conduz essa adoração, em nome da mente mortal e da alma imortal em evolução.","r":"5:3.8"}]},{"h":"Origin of the Worship Impulse","items":[{"x":"Primitive man, fearing the incomprehensible forces of nature, worshiped almost everything on earth and in the heavens.","r":["85:0.4"]},{"x":"The spirit of worship, the sixth adjutant spirit, constantly stimulated the worship urge in the primitive mind.","r":["85:7.1"]},{"x":"The spirit of worship is the mark of spiritual-ascension candidacy, separating beings capable of possessing souls from those who are not.","r":["36:5.11"]},{"x":"When the spirit of wisdom guides the worship impulse, man begins to turn from the objects of nature to the God of nature.","r":["85:7.3"]},{"q":"A adoração é a insígnia da candidatura à ascensão espiritual.","r":"36:5.11"}]},{"h":"The Worshipful Life","items":[{"x":"Worship, or spiritual contemplation, must alternate with service, which keeps contact with material reality.","r":["143:7.3"]},{"q":"A adoração é a técnica de voltar-se para o Um, para receber a inspiração do serviço de muitos.","r":"143:7.6"},{"x":"Worship is effortless attention, the true rest of the soul, a form of restful spiritual activity.","r":["143:7.7"]},{"x":"In time, thought leads to wisdom, and wisdom leads to worship.","r":["112:2.13"]},{"x":"On Paradise worship is the highest delight and a refreshing play, and all the arts are employed in worship.","r":["27:7.2","27:7.5"]},{"x":"On the seventh mansion world the ascender begins a new and more spiritual worship of the invisible Father.","r":["47:9.2"]}]}],"see":["Oração","Pai Universal","Ajustador do Pensamento","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Experiência religiosa","Serviço"]},{"n":71,"t":"Adversidade e provações","en":"Adversity and Trials","sum":"The confusion and trials of Urantia signify not God's indifference but part of the divine plan to forge strong and noble characters between the anvils of necessity and the hammers of anguish. Virtues such as courage, altruism, hope, and faith can grow only in a world of hardship and uncertainty. Jesus corrected the superstition that suffering is God's punishment, and while he did not exempt believers from difficulty, he promised to go with them through all their trials.","sections":[{"h":"Why There Is Adversity","items":[{"x":"The uncertainties and vicissitudes of life are in no way contradictory to the universal sovereignty of God.","r":["3:5.5"]},{"q":"A coragem — a força de caráter — é desejável? Então, o homem deve ser criado em um ambiente que requeira um enfrentamento das dificuldades e uma reação às decepções.","r":"3:5.6"},{"x":"Altruism requires inequality, hope requires insecurity, and faith requires a situation in which one must believe more than one knows.","r":["3:5.7","3:5.8","3:5.9"]},{"x":"Even the satisfaction of happiness is truly experienced only in a world open to the possibility of pain and distress.","r":["3:5.14"]},{"x":"The perfect beings of Havona know neither the sweetness of escaping the potential of pain nor saving faith.","r":["3:5.17"]}]},{"h":"The Anvil and Hammer That Forge Character","items":[{"x":"The Creators could make Urantia a paradise, but such an Eden would not produce strong and noble characters.","r":["23:2.12"]},{"q":"As vossas ansiedades e penas, provações e desapontamentos são tanto uma parte do plano divino para a vossa esfera quanto o são a perfeição aprimorada e a adaptação infinita de todas coisas para o seu supremo propósito nos mundos do universo central e perfeito.","r":"23:2.12"},{"q":"O universo da vossa origem foi forjado entre a bigorna da justiça e o martelo do sofrimento; e aqueles que brandem o martelo são filhos da misericórdia: a progênie espiritual do Espírito Infinito.","r":"9:1.8"},{"q":"Vós não podeis perceber a verdade espiritual até que a vossa experiência a tenha provado, contudo muitas verdades não são realmente sentidas senão na adversidade.","r":"48:7.18"},{"x":"God sometimes disciplines us for our good, but he suffers with us in our fiery trials.","r":["2:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Suffering Is Not Punishment","items":[{"x":"Jesus declared superstitious the belief that prosperity is a sign of God's approval and adversity a sign of his displeasure.","r":["166:4.3"]},{"x":"Those killed by the falling tower of Siloam were not greater sinners but innocent victims of the accidents of time.","r":["166:4.4"]},{"x":"As the story of Job shows, material prosperity is no proof of God's favor, and the Father loves the poor just as much.","r":["148:6.2"]},{"x":"People suffer from the accidents of time, from imperfection, from the consequences of sin, and from the harvest of rebellion; suffering is not a visitation of divine judgment.","r":["148:6.11"]},{"x":"Even in suffering Job pierced the clouds by faith and found the God of comfort and salvation.","r":["148:6.11","148:6.10"]}]},{"h":"The Believer's Attitude Toward Trials","items":[{"q":"Eu não vos prometo livrar-vos das águas da adversidade, mas eu vos prometo estar convosco durante todas elas.","r":"159:3.13"},{"x":"Believing the gospel does not exempt one from accidents and calamities, but it keeps one unafraid when trouble comes.","r":["159:3.13"]},{"q":"Ele sabe como suportar com bravura os sofrimentos inevitáveis; não se queixa quando enfrenta os sofrimentos inescapáveis.","r":"156:5.20"},{"x":"In times of testing a person's soul is revealed, and the loyal who endure trials are entrusted with the work of the kingdom.","r":["165:6.2"]},{"x":"Even when floods of adversity and hatred sweep over the soul, the one who entrusts his soul to the indwelling spirit has a citadel of the spirit that does not fall.","r":["100:2.7"]},{"x":"True religion produces profound courage and confidence even in natural adversity and physical calamity.","r":["101:3.7","34:6.13"]}]},{"h":"The Way Jesus Showed","items":[{"x":"Jesus met suffering with faith, courage, and the determination to do the Father's will, and thus conquered life and death.","r":["194:3.3"]},{"x":"Even before apparent defeat and the anguish of despair, Jesus stood calm and unafraid in the divine presence.","r":["196:0.5"]},{"x":"Jesus encouraged a fear-ridden young man that suffering would give vigor, disappointment a spur, and obstacles a stimulus.","r":["130:6.4"]},{"x":"Jesus taught the multitude gathered at Bethsaida for more than an hour on \"the mission of adversity and the spiritual value of disappointment.\"","r":["151:0.1"]},{"x":"The two hard years before his marriage were a time of real trial in Jesus' earth life.","r":["126:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Mal","Medo e preocupação","Fé","Crescimento","Alegria e felicidade","Caráter de Jesus"]},{"n":33,"t":"Ajustador do Pensamento","en":"Thought Adjuster","sum":"The Thought Adjuster is a fragment of God that comes directly from the Universal Father and indwells the human mind. It is not a created being but divinity itself; it leads man from within to do the Father's will and seeks to become one with the evolving soul and go forward with it in the eternal career. At the center of the personal religion presented in The Urantia Book stands this indwelling spirit of the Father.","sections":[{"h":"A Divine Fragment from the Father","items":[{"x":"Though he dwells on Paradise, the Father is actually present in the human mind as the Mystery Monitor.","r":["107:0.1"]},{"q":"Eles não são seres criados; são entidades fragmentadas do Pai, e constituem a presença factual do Deus infinito.","r":"107:1.2"},{"x":"Adjusters are limited in scope yet absolute in essence, and so they are called the \"qualified absolute fragments\" of the Father.","r":["107:4.2"]},{"x":"The Adjuster is not a personality, yet it is a true reality of the purest order in the universe, a divine presence.","r":["107:7.1"]},{"q":"No Adjuster has ever been disloyal to the Paradise Father","r":"107:4.3"}]},{"h":"When and How It Comes","items":[{"x":"The Adjuster is assigned after the child makes its first moral choice, and on Urantia it arrives, on the average, just before the sixth birthday.","r":["108:2.1"]},{"x":"The preparation of the seven adjutant mind-spirits and the circuitizing of the Holy Spirit must come first before an Adjuster can enter the mind.","r":["108:2.2"]},{"x":"That a perfect Adjuster should volunteer to dwell in a mortal of animal origin is a marvel of divine condescension.","r":["108:6.1"]},{"q":"which came forth from God to find man and sonship him even in the days of the flesh.","r":"107:0.3"}]},{"h":"What the Adjuster Does","items":[{"x":"The basic mission of the Adjuster is to represent the Universal Father to the mortal creature, and indeed to be that Father.","r":["108:0.1"]},{"x":"The Adjuster comes with a plan for the ideal life, but man is free to accept or reject that plan.","r":["110:2.1"]},{"x":"It undertakes the difficult work of an interpreter, receiving counsel from spiritual intelligences and conveying it to the material mind.","r":["108:5.1"]},{"q":"only occasionally do you catch an echo, a faint and distant echo, of the divine voice.","r":"110:3.1"},{"x":"Unless the mind's capacity is wholly destroyed, the Adjuster stays with a person through every calamity and illness.","r":["110:1.5"]}]},{"h":"A Life of Co-operation with the Adjuster","items":[{"q":"The great goal of human existence is to attune to the divinity of the indwelling Adjuster;","r":"110:3.4"},{"x":"Mental poisons such as fear, anger, envy, and suspicion greatly retard the Adjuster's work, as bodily poisons do.","r":["110:1.5"]},{"x":"Confusion, discouragement, or ignorance alone does not prevent survival; only conscious resistance to the Adjuster's leading does.","r":["110:3.5"]},{"x":"When clouds gather, faith should accept the fact of the Adjuster's presence and look to the light beyond.","r":["108:6.8"]}]},{"h":"Fusion and Eternal Destiny","items":[{"x":"The Adjuster is the Father's love incarnate in the human soul, the essence of the finaliter personality foretasted in time.","r":["107:0.2"]},{"x":"Mastering the seven psychic circles is not fusion itself but the preparatory stage leading to fusion.","r":["110:6.1"]},{"q":"but fusion depends on yet other greater and more sublime spiritual achievements, upon the attainment of a final and complete attunement of the mortal will with the will of God as it is resident in the Thought Adjuster.","r":"110:7.1"},{"x":"The eternal union of the Adjuster with a perfected creature brings into being a unique creature that no other universe technique can produce.","r":["108:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Fusão com o Ajustador","Alma","Personalidade","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Vontade de Deus","Sobrevivência"]},{"n":70,"t":"Alegria e felicidade","en":"Joy and Happiness","sum":"True happiness comes from the inner life rather than from wealth or environment, and it is achieved when the selfish desires and the unselfish urges of the indwelling spirit are reconciled in one will. The highest happiness is inseparable from spiritual progress, and joy is experienced not alone but in sharing love and service. Jesus was not a man of sorrows but a man of gladness, and his peace is the joy and satisfaction of one who does the will of God.","sections":[{"h":"Where Happiness Comes From","items":[{"q":"A felicidade e a alegria têm origem na vida interior. Vós não podeis experimentar o regozijo verdadeiro completamente a sós. Uma vida solitária é fatal para a felicidade.","r":"111:4.7"},{"x":"Happiness is the sum of techniques for gratifying natural urges in better ways, and it does not depend greatly on environment.","r":["140:4.10"]},{"x":"Human happiness is achieved when the desires of the self and the unselfish urges of the higher self, the divine spirit, are coordinated in one will.","r":["103:5.5"]},{"x":"Health, mental efficiency, and happiness arise from the unification of body, mind, and spirit.","r":["100:4.3"]},{"q":"O esforço nem sempre produz alegria, mas não existe felicidade sem esforço inteligente.","r":"48:7.10"}]},{"h":"Spiritual Growth and Lasting Joy","items":[{"x":"The highest happiness is inseparable from spiritual progress, and spiritual growth yields lasting joy and a peace that passes understanding.","r":["100:4.3"]},{"x":"The Adjuster respects the value of selfish motives but gives weight to the unselfish urges that lead to happiness and the joys of the kingdom of heaven.","r":["103:2.7"]},{"x":"One born of the spirit is released from the bondage of self-denial and translated into the joyous kingdom of the spirit.","r":["143:2.8"]},{"q":"Science yields knowledge; religion yields happiness; philosophy yields unity","r":"101:2.8"},{"x":"There is an inherent joy in freewill existence independent of all external influences, and the angels of the joy of existence strive to demonstrate it.","r":["28:5.16"]}]},{"h":"Happiness as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"x":"The sermon on the beatitudes opened on the keynote of happiness, and its faith and love strengthen character and create happiness.","r":["140:5.6"]},{"x":"A child's happiness is immediate pleasure, but an adult sows seeds of self-denial for greater happiness.","r":["140:5.7"]},{"x":"Those who humbly seek God do not wait for distant rewards but experience the happiness of the kingdom in their hearts now.","r":["140:5.7"]},{"x":"Asked why some are happier than others, Jesus answered that much depends on willingness to be led by the Father's indwelling spirit.","r":["149:5.1","149:5.2"]},{"x":"Much sorrow comes from thwarted ambition and wounded pride, so after doing one's best one should accept one's lot and exercise ingenuity.","r":["149:5.3"]},{"q":"Seek not, then, for false peace and transient joy but rather for the assurance of faith and the sureties of divine sonship","r":"149:5.4"}]},{"h":"The Joy of Love and Service","items":[{"x":"The new commandment was meant not as a burden but as a new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows.","r":["180:1.2"]},{"q":"Se quiserdes compartilhar a alegria do Mestre, deveis compartilhar o seu amor.","r":"180:1.5"},{"x":"Jesus showed a fear-ridden young man the paths of service and the highways of happiness that lead to the joy of loving activity.","r":["130:6.2"]},{"x":"Loving service rendered with full affection becomes not a sacrifice but supreme joy.","r":["180:1.6"]},{"x":"After Pentecost the believers broke bread together with gladness and singleness of heart, enjoying the spiritual joy of the brotherhood's fellowship.","r":["194:4.3","190:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Jesus, a Man of Gladness","items":[{"q":"Este homem da Galiléia não era um homem de tristezas; era uma alma da alegria.","r":"100:7.13"},{"x":"The peace of Jesus is neither stoic resignation nor vague optimism but the joy and satisfaction of one who has fully learned how to do the will of God.","r":["181:1.7","181:1.8"]},{"x":"The religion of Jesus does not flee from this life but ennobles present living with the joy and peace of a spiritual state of being.","r":["194:3.3"]},{"x":"Morontia life is about half work and half play, and it enjoys the humor of realizing how trivial many past worries were.","r":["48:4.1","48:4.6"]},{"x":"Jesus regarded this world not as a vale of tears but as a vale of soul making, where eternal spirits are born.","r":["149:5.5"]}]}],"see":["Medo e preocupação","Serviço","Amor","Crescimento","Reino do céu","Religião pessoal"]},{"n":35,"t":"Alma","en":"Soul","sum":"The soul is a morontia reality newly arising from the relationship between the material mind and the indwelling Thought Adjuster, the child born of human effort and the divine spirit together. During the life in the flesh it grows like an embryo; it then survives death and becomes the new vehicle of personality on the mansion worlds. The growth of the soul depends on moral choices and the decision to seek God, and personality identity survives in the survival of the soul.","sections":[{"h":"How the Soul Comes into Being","items":[{"x":"When a mortal chooses to do the Father's will, the indwelling spirit becomes the father of a new reality and the material mind becomes its mother.","r":["0:5.10"]},{"x":"Three factors operate in making the soul: the human mind, the indwelling divine spirit, and the relationship between the two.","r":["111:2.4","111:2.5","111:2.6"]},{"q":"A realidade dessa relação única não é nem material nem espiritual, mas moroncial. É a alma.","r":"111:2.7"},{"x":"The divine spirit arrives with the first moral activity of the human mind, and at that very moment the soul is born.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"The morontia life of an ascending mortal actually begins at the moment the soul is conceived, when the Adjuster comes to indwell.","r":["48:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Nature of the Soul","items":[{"x":"The midway creatures called this soul the \"midmind,\" meaning that it lies between the material mind and the cosmic mind.","r":["111:2.8"]},{"x":"The soul is the part that lifts man above the animal level, characterized by moral choice and the urge to know God and be like him.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"Self-consciousness itself is not the soul; moral self-consciousness, as true self-realization, forms the foundation of the soul.","r":["133:6.5"]},{"x":"The soul cannot be proved by material investigation or by purely spiritual tests, yet the morally awakened mortal knows its reality by experience.","r":["133:6.7"]},{"q":"Desde a sua incipiência mais inicial, a alma é real, e traz em si as qualidades cósmicas da sobrevivência.","r":"16:9.2"},{"x":"The morontia soul is the child both of the Father's Adjuster action and of the cosmic reaction of the Supreme Being.","r":["117:6.5"]}]},{"h":"The Growth of the Soul","items":[{"x":"Mind is the human soil on which the Adjuster, with the co-operation of the personality, evolves the morontia soul.","r":["111:1.1"]},{"q":"The material mind of mortal man is the cosmic loom that carries the morontia fabrics","r":"111:2.2"},{"x":"The soul can grow regardless of cultural level, but not without the decision to choose survival and to do the Father's will.","r":["65:8.4"]},{"x":"Mistakes and errors may delay the evolution of the soul, but they cannot prevent the soul evolution that began with the consent of the will.","r":["111:3.1"]},{"q":"A alma do homem não pode existir sem o pensamento moral e a atividade espiritual. Uma alma estagnada é uma alma moribunda.","r":"133:6.5"},{"x":"The more the soul is filled with truth, beauty, and goodness, the more indestructible the resulting being becomes.","r":["111:3.7"]}]},{"h":"The Soul and the Human Will","items":[{"x":"During life the deciding will resides in the material mind, but as the self grows, it becomes increasingly identified with the emerging morontia soul.","r":["111:3.2"]},{"q":"A alma é, assim, o embrião do futuro veículo moroncial de identidade da personalidade.","r":"111:3.2"},{"x":"By its own choice the mortal personality can transfer the seat of its identity from the transient material-intellect system to the morontia-soul system.","r":["112:5.4","112:2.20"]},{"q":"The faith-activated soul of man cannot stop short of the attainment of this goal of destiny;","r":"132:3.7"},{"x":"Whether a soul is saved or lost depends on whether moral consciousness gains survival value through eternal alliance with its immortal spirit endowment.","r":["133:6.6"]}]},{"h":"The Soul After Death","items":[{"q":"Essa entidade recém-surgida é a alma; e ela sobrevive tanto à morte do vosso corpo físico quanto à da vossa mente material.","r":"112:5.12"},{"x":"From death until repersonalization the soul is wholly unconscious, in the keeping of the seraphic guardian of destiny.","r":["112:5.13"]},{"x":"In the resurrection halls the seraphim bestow the sleeping soul upon a new morontia form and unite it with the returning Adjuster.","r":["112:5.18","112:5.19"]},{"x":"If a mortal does not survive, the spiritual values of his experience remain in the Adjuster, but his identity does not survive.","r":["16:9.3"]},{"x":"The soul in the body is embryonic; it is born into the morontia life and grows through the mansion worlds.","r":["66:4.9"]},{"x":"The immortal soul is at first morontial but rises to true spirit levels and usually fuses with the spirit of the Father who started it.","r":["111:3.3"]}]},{"h":"Human Ideas About the Soul","items":[{"x":"Primitive man associated the soul with blood, breath, shadows, and reflections in water, or believed it dwelt in various organs of the body.","r":["111:0.3"]},{"x":"Early man took the other self of dreams to be the soul, and this idea led on to belief in nature spirits.","r":["86:5.1"]},{"x":"Hindu teachers, in the concept of the atman, almost discerned the Adjuster, but they failed to distinguish the co-evolving soul.","r":["111:0.4"]}]}],"see":["Ajustador do Pensamento","Personalidade","Mente","Morôncia","Sobrevivência","Fusão com o Ajustador"]},{"n":60,"t":"Amor","en":"Love","sum":"\"God is love.\" In The Urantia Book love is the dominant characteristic of all God's personal dealings with his creatures, and it embraces truth, beauty, and goodness. The Father's love individualizes each person as an irreplaceable child and dwells within man through the Adjuster. Love is the desire to do good to others; it cannot be held captive and becomes real only when bestowed upon one's fellows. Jesus gave the new commandment to love one another \"as I have loved you.\"","sections":[{"h":"God Is Love","items":[{"x":"Because God is love, his only personal attitude toward the affairs of the universe is always a reaction of divine affection.","r":["2:5.1"]},{"x":"The love of God is not induced by sacrifice or intercession; the Father himself loves us.","r":["2:5.2"]},{"q":"Deus é amor, mas o amor não é Deus.","r":"2:5.10"},{"x":"The love of God is a farseeing parental affection that functions in unity with wisdom and sometimes includes discipline for our good.","r":["2:5.3","2:5.10"]},{"x":"Love is the dominant characteristic of all God's personal dealings with his creatures.","r":["2:5.12"]}]},{"h":"Manifestations of the Father's Love","items":[{"x":"The Father's love individualizes each personality as a unique child, eternally irreplaceable.","r":["12:7.9"]},{"x":"The greatest manifestation of divine love for mortals is the bestowal of the Adjusters, and its greatest revelation is the bestowal life of Michael.","r":["2:5.10"]},{"x":"The love and devotion an Adjuster gives to its subject is the most truly divine affection in all creation.","r":["110:0.2"]},{"x":"God is love and the Son is mercy; mercy is applied love, love in action.","r":["6:3.5"]},{"x":"We love God because we discern that he truly loves us; the experience of loving is a response to the experience of being loved.","r":["2:5.8"]},{"q":"O amor do Pai acompanha-nos, agora e em todo o círculo interminável das idades eternas.","r":"2:5.9"}]},{"h":"What Love Is","items":[{"q":"O amor é o desejo de fazer o bem aos outros.","r":"56:10.21"},{"x":"In its true sense, love, whether human or divine, connotes the mutual regard of whole personalities.","r":["112:2.7"]},{"q":"it cannot be created, manufactured, or purchased; it must grow.","r":"100:3.7"},{"x":"Love is born only of thoroughgoing understanding of a neighbor's motives and sentiments; one cannot love fellows by mere willpower.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"x":"Love must continually readapt its concept of the highest good of the one loved, under the guidance of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["180:5.10"]}]},{"h":"The Circuit of Love","items":[{"x":"All true love is from God, and man receives the divine affection as he bestows that love upon his neighbors.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"q":"O homem nunca pode tomar o amor do Pai e aprisioná-lo no fundo do seu coração.","r":"117:6.10"},{"x":"The circuit of love proceeds from the Father, through sons to brothers, and thence to the Supreme.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"x":"Love is the soil of religious growth; love is the essence of religion and the wellspring of superior civilization.","r":["100:0.2","102:6.3"]}]},{"h":"Love as Jesus Revealed It","items":[{"x":"Jesus revealed a God of love, and that love embraces truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["5:4.6"]},{"q":"O amor é a maior de todas as realidades do espírito.","r":"143:1.4"},{"x":"Beyond the commandment to love one's neighbor as oneself, Jesus gave the new commandment: \"Love one another as I have loved you.\"","r":["180:1.1"]},{"x":"The new commandment is not a new burden but a new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows, and the greatest love is to lay down one's life for one's friends.","r":["180:1.2","180:1.3"]},{"x":"To share the Master's love is to share his service; that love does not make a new world but makes the old world new.","r":["180:1.5"]},{"x":"Advanced mortals on worlds settled in light and life have learned that love is the greatest thing in the universe and know that God is love.","r":["56:10.20"]}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Misericórdia","Serviço","Irmandade dos homens","Bondade","Ajustador do Pensamento"]},{"n":21,"t":"Anciães dos Dias","en":"Ancients of Days","sum":"The Ancients of Days are twenty-one supreme rulers of Paradise Trinity origin who, in groups of three, each govern one of the seven superuniverses. They alone render the final executive verdicts on the eternal life and death of will creatures, and by the technique of reflectivity they see and hear at once Paradise above and the local universes below. They are the summit of the superuniverse government that mortals meet on their ascension journey after graduating from the local universe.","sections":[{"h":"Rulers from the Trinity","items":[{"x":"The Ancients of Days are the third of the seven orders of Supreme Trinity Personalities; their number is fixed, and no more are coming into being.","r":["18:0.4","18:0.9"]},{"q":"Basicamente, os Anciães dos Dias são idênticos entre si; eles revelam o caráter e a natureza unificada da Trindade.","r":"18:3.2"},{"x":"The Seven Master Spirits differ in nature, but the Ancients of Days, though possessing individuality, are uniform and superperfect offspring of the Trinity.","r":["18:3.2"]},{"x":"All twenty-one were trinitized at the same time, and the very first entry in the personality records of Paradise is the recital of their trinitization.","r":["18:3.4"]},{"q":"Eles representam o início dos registros para as personalidades do universo dos universos, daí o seu nome — Anciães dos Dias.","r":"18:3.4"},{"x":"Beings of Trinity origin are in no danger of failure or rebellion, and these rulers have never deviated from the path of perfect personality conduct.","r":["18:0.11"]}]},{"h":"The Supergovernment Ruled by Three","items":[{"q":"Cada superuniverso é presidido por três Anciães dos Dias, os principais executivos conjuntos do supergoverno.","r":"15:10.3"},{"x":"In high administration the three always act together; though they never leave their headquarters world, its position as the focus of the reflectivity system leaves their rule unhindered.","r":["18:3.5"]},{"x":"While the Master Spirits determine the nature of a superuniverse, the Ancients of Days determine its administration, providing uniform rule over otherwise differing superuniverses.","r":["18:3.3"]},{"x":"They are assisted by the Perfectors of Wisdom, Divine Counselors, and Universal Censors, and by Trinitized Sons drawn from glorified ascendant mortals.","r":["15:10.11","15:10.12"]},{"x":"The observations and recommendations gathered by the rulers of the major and minor sectors rise step by step until at last they reach the courts of the Ancients of Days.","r":["15:13.6"]},{"q":"E a sabedoria da originalidade e a iniciativa da individualidade caracterizam todos os decretos e ditames dos Anciães dos Dias.","r":"18:3.9"}]},{"h":"The Final Judgment of Eternal Life and Death","items":[{"x":"They are the most powerful of the direct rulers of the time-space creations, and they alone have the power to pass final sentence on the eternal extinction of will creatures.","r":["18:3.7"]},{"q":"Os Filhos soberanos dos universos locais podem decretar a sobrevivência do homem mortal, mas apenas os Anciães dos Dias podem reunir-se para o julgamento executivo nas questões de vida e morte eternas.","r":"15:12.2"},{"x":"When the restoring love of the Creator Sons is finally rejected, the sentence of extinction is carried out by forces under their jurisdiction.","r":["2:3.6","2:3.3"]},{"q":"Não há desacordos, nem opiniões minoritárias nos decretos desses tribunais supremos e superlativos.","r":"15:12.3"},{"x":"There is no appeal from the verdicts of a superuniverse, for they are the united opinion of the Ancients of Days and of the Master Spirit presiding over that superuniverse.","r":["15:12.4"]},{"q":"Quando os três Anciães dos Dias atuam, a Trindade do Paraíso atua.","r":"19:3.5"},{"x":"They and their associates of Trinity origin render the righteous judgments of supreme equity throughout the seven superuniverses.","r":["10:6.17"]}]},{"h":"The Reflective Rule That Sees and Hears All","items":[{"q":"the Ancients of Days from their position midway between the inhabited worlds and Paradise—between man and God—can instantly look both ways, hear both ways, and know both ways.","r":"28:4.1"},{"x":"The primary seconaphim serve as living mirrors, reflecting before them the minds and voices of the Infinite Spirit, the Creator Sons, and the angelic hosts.","r":["28:4.4","28:4.6","28:4.11"]},{"x":"They infer the Father's will by harmonizing the voice of spirit from above with the voices of the Michaels below, and because this requires all three together, a superuniverse is always presided over by three.","r":["28:4.10"]},{"x":"The superuniverses are isolated from one another, and direct personal communication with the rulers of another superuniverse must go through the Solitary Messengers.","r":["23:2.15","15:10.23"]}]},{"h":"Relation to the Local Universes, and the Future","items":[{"x":"A Creator Son pledges to the Trinity not to assume full sovereignty until his seven creature bestowals have been certified by the Ancients of Days.","r":["119:0.3"]},{"x":"They do not certify a Creator Son as universe sovereign until he has actually lived as a creature and gained the creature's point of view.","r":["119:0.6"]},{"x":"At Michael's petition they authorized the detention of the personalities involved in the Lucifer rebellion, and the final disposition of the archrebels remains in their hands.","r":["53:9.3","53:9.6"]},{"x":"Since their prerogatives of rule were not earned by experience, they will someday be superseded by the Supreme Being, the experiential sovereign, and become his vicegerents.","r":["18:3.8"]},{"x":"The mortal's journey of finding God begins with the Creator Son and proceeds through the Ancients of Days and the Master Spirit of the superuniverse to the Universal Father.","r":["0:8.9"]}]}],"see":["Trindade do Paraíso","Os sete superuniversos","Deus, o Sétuplo","Ser Supremo","Sete Espíritos Mestres","Filho Criador Michael"]},{"n":46,"t":"Ascensão mortal","en":"Mortal Ascension","sum":"The mortal ascension is the long road by which a human being of animal origin sets out from an evolutionary planet, passes through the mansion worlds and the morontia worlds of the local universe, the spirit training worlds of the superuniverse, and the central universe of Havona, and at last finds the Universal Father on Paradise and becomes a finaliter. The command \"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect\" is both the starting point and the goal of this journey, and the way must be walked step by step in experience.","sections":[{"h":"The Call to Be Perfect","items":[{"x":"The will creatures of all the universes have embarked on the eternal adventure of reaching God the Father, the long journey to Paradise.","r":["1:0.3"]},{"x":"Striving for the perfection of divinity should be the first duty and highest ambition of every creature.","r":["1:0.4"]},{"x":"Though man cannot be perfect in the infinite sense, he can fully attain the divine goal that God has set for him.","r":["1:0.5"]},{"q":"Essa busca sublime, pelo Deus dos universos, é a aventura suprema dos habitantes de todos os mundos do tempo e do espaço.","r":"1:0.6"}]},{"h":"An Outline of the Seven Stages","items":[{"x":"The ascending career is summed up in seven stages: planetary mortals, sleeping survivors, mansion world students, morontia progressors, superuniverse wards, Havona pilgrims, and Paradise arrivals.","r":["30:4.1","30:4.2","30:4.8"]},{"x":"For sleeping survivors the passing of time does not matter; one who has slept five thousand years awakens no differently from one who has rested five days.","r":["30:4.12"]},{"x":"Ascenders progress individually within a sphere, but between the stages of universe study they always move in classes.","r":["30:4.17"]},{"x":"Just before leaving the local universe they acquire true spirit identity, and from then on the ascender's status is forever settled.","r":["30:4.20","30:4.21"]}]},{"h":"Through the Local Universe and the Superuniverse","items":[{"x":"Passing from the mansion worlds through the spheres of the system, the constellation, and the universe headquarters, the ascender as a morontia progressor develops in intellect, spirit, and form.","r":["30:4.18","30:4.19"]},{"q":"A mente, a personalidade e o caráter permanecem imutáveis durante esse avanço; apenas a forma passa por uma modificação.","r":"30:4.20"},{"x":"On the superuniverse training worlds the young spirits share what they have learned with others and master local universe and superuniverse administration.","r":["30:4.22","30:4.23","30:4.24"]},{"q":"Não se conhece nenhum caso de desvio dos pupilos do superuniverso.","r":"30:4.21"}]},{"h":"Havona and Paradise","items":[{"x":"The journey from superuniverse headquarters to Havona is always made alone, and the instruction of Havona is personal and individual.","r":["30:4.27"]},{"x":"The pilgrim arrives in Havona possessing only one perfection, perfection of purpose, and his faith has already been tested.","r":["26:4.13"]},{"q":"A aptidão para compreender é o passaporte dos mortais para o Paraíso. A vontade de acreditar é a chave de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Attaining the Universal Father on the third circle of Havona, with the help of the Father guides, becomes the passport to eternity.","r":["26:9.1","26:9.2"]},{"x":"Residence on Paradise means that God has been found, and Father-fused mortals are mustered into the mortal Corps of the Finality.","r":["30:4.31"]},{"q":"On earth you were a creature of flesh and blood; through the local universe you were a morontia being; through the superuniverse you were an evolving spirit;","r":"30:4.26"}]},{"h":"The Purpose of the Journey and Beyond","items":[{"x":"Step by step, life by life, world by world, the ascending career is mastered and the goal of Deity is attained, and survival is completed in perfection.","r":["26:9.4"]},{"x":"Finaliters are recorded as spirits of the sixth stage, so a destiny of the unrevealed seventh stage still remains.","r":["31:3.3","31:3.5"]},{"x":"The long and tremendous training of the ascension must surely be designed to fit them for tests of greater trust and more sublime service.","r":["31:3.2","48:8.3"]},{"x":"The destinies of Adjuster-fused, Son-fused, and Spirit-fused mortals differ, but none is greater or lesser, for God loves all his sons alike.","r":["40:10.5","40:10.13"]},{"x":"Every facility and power is provided so that the Paradise goal of divine perfection may at last be attained.","r":["40:10.14"]},{"q":"A sobrevivência foi completada, na perfeição, e a perfeição está repleta, na supremacia da divindade.","r":"26:9.4"}]}],"see":["Mundos das mansões","Morôncia","Corpo de Finalidade","Havona","Paraíso","Busca da perfeição"]},{"n":2,"t":"Atributos de Deus","en":"Attributes of God","sum":"Os atributos de Deus mostram como o Pai infinito Se relaciona com a Sua criação. Ele está presente em toda parte, é todo-poderoso e tudo sabe. Ele Se outorga sem reservas e, no entanto, de modo algum é diminuído, e governa por meio dos Seus Filhos, reservando para Si a soberania final. Todos esses atributos estão unificados e coordenados no amor e na sabedoria, na justiça e na misericórdia.","sections":[{"h":"Criatividade e onipresença","items":[{"x":"A criatividade não é tanto um atributo quanto a totalidade da natureza atuante de Deus, que culmina na verdade da paternidade de Deus.","r":["3:0.3"]},{"x":"Só Deus pode estar em inúmeros lugares ao mesmo tempo; Ele está presente em todas as partes da Sua criação e em todos os corações.","r":["3:1.1","3:1.2"]},{"q":"Deus revela-se em todo o cosmo, mas o cosmo não pode jamais conter ou abranger a totalidade da infinitude de Deus.","r":"3:1.2"},{"x":"Deus só está presente de modo plenamente discernível no Paraíso e no universo central; nas criações exteriores, Ele limita a Sua presença direta por respeito à soberania dos Seus criadores coordenados.","r":["3:1.6"]},{"x":"A presença efetiva do Pai no homem é determinada pelo grau em que a mente dele coopera com o Ajustador residente.","r":["3:1.11","3:1.12"]}]},{"h":"Poder infinito","items":[{"x":"A longa evolução das raças, dos planetas e dos universos desenrola-se de modo ordenado segundo o propósito eterno do Pai, sob o controle dos criadores.","r":["3:2.2"]},{"x":"Considerado nos fenômenos não espirituais, Deus é energia; toda energia física procede Dele e é mantida dentro do controle da gravidade do Paraíso inferior.","r":["3:2.3","3:2.4"]},{"q":"A despeito das aparências, o poder de Deus não funciona no universo como uma força cega.","r":"3:2.6"},{"x":"Os atos de Deus às vezes parecem impiedosos apenas por causa da visão finita; todos eles visam ao bem maior de todos os envolvidos.","r":["3:2.8","3:2.10"]},{"x":"O poder de Deus só é limitado pela Sua natureza (amor, verdade, beleza e bondade), pela Sua vontade (misericórdia) e pela Sua lei (a justiça da Trindade).","r":["3:2.12","3:2.13","3:2.14"]}]},{"h":"Conhecimento universal","items":[{"x":"Deus tem consciência dos pensamentos de toda a criação e é a única personalidade que conhece de fato o número das estrelas e dos planetas do espaço.","r":["3:3.1","3:3.2"]},{"x":"O Seu conhecimento é complementado pelo circuito da personalidade, que abrange todas as personalidades, pelos Filhos divinos descendentes e pelos Ajustadores do Pensamento residentes.","r":["3:3.3"]},{"x":"Ainda que Deus conhecesse de antemão os atos de livre-arbítrio dos Seus filhos, tal presciência de modo algum anularia a liberdade deles.","r":["3:3.4"]},{"q":"Uma coisa é certa: Deus nunca está sujeito a surpreender-Se.","r":"3:3.4"},{"x":"A onipotência não implica o poder de fazer o que não é próprio de Deus, e a onisciência não significa conhecer o incognoscível.","r":["3:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Infinitude não diminuída","items":[{"x":"Tendo-Se outorgado sem reservas aos Seus Filhos e à Sua criação, o Pai de modo algum é diminuído no Seu potencial de poder, sabedoria e amor.","r":["3:4.1","3:4.3"]},{"x":"Ainda que a criação prosseguisse sem fim, o poder de controle do Paraíso seria suficiente, e o Infinito continuaria repleto da mesma força e energia.","r":["3:4.2"]},{"x":"O homem não pode conceber plenamente a infinitude do Pai, mas pode experimentar verdadeiramente o impacto do Seu amor; a qualidade dessa experiência é ilimitada, enquanto a sua quantidade depende da capacidade espiritual.","r":["3:4.6"]},{"q":"Por conseguinte, o acesso mais querido e de maior aproximação a Deus, que o homem tem, é o amor, e por intermédio do amor, pois Deus é amor.","r":"3:4.7"}]},{"h":"Supremacia e primazia","items":[{"x":"Fora de Havona, o Pai exerce o Seu poder por meio dos Seus Filhos e das personalidades a eles subordinadas, e só atua diretamente quando um agente delegado falha na sua missão.","r":["3:5.1","3:5.2"]},{"x":"No coração dos homens, a vontade do Pai pode nem sempre ser feita, mas no curso e no destino de um planeta o plano divino prevalece.","r":["3:5.3"]},{"x":"A adversidade, a desigualdade, a incerteza e a possibilidade de erro são condições de vida necessárias para desenvolver qualidades como a coragem, o altruísmo, a esperança e a fé.","r":["3:5.6","3:5.7","3:5.9"]},{"x":"O Pai delega a autoridade livremente, mas reserva para Si a decisão final e o veto quanto ao bem-estar e ao destino da criação.","r":["3:6.1"]},{"q":"A soberania de Deus é ilimitada; é o fato fundamental em toda a criação.","r":"3:6.2"}]},{"h":"Perfeição, justiça e misericórdia","items":[{"x":"Os planos e propósitos da Primeira Fonte e Centro são, como Ele próprio, eternos, perfeitos e imutáveis; embora possam parecer mudar, o propósito subjacente não muda.","r":["2:2.1","2:2.3"]},{"x":"A justiça do Pai não depende da conduta das Suas criaturas e, mesmo quando Ele as deixa colher os resultados das más ações, ela é sempre temperada pela misericórdia.","r":["2:3.1","2:3.2"]},{"q":"A misericórdia é simplesmente a justiça temperada por aquela sabedoria que surge da perfeição do conhecimento e que advém do reconhecimento pleno da fraqueza natural e das limitações ambientais, das criaturas finitas.","r":"2:4.1"},{"x":"Por causa da Sua sabedoria infinita, Deus concede justiça e misericórdia ao mesmo tempo e nunca é dividido por atitudes conflitantes para com os Seus filhos.","r":["2:4.3"]}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Personalidade de Deus","Misericórdia","Justiça","Amor","Vontade de Deus"]},{"n":84,"t":"Auto-outorga de Jesus","en":"Bestowal of Jesus","sum":"The bestowal of Jesus is the event in which Michael, Creator Son of Nebadon, in his seventh and final bestowal, was born on Urantia as a mortal infant and lived a human life to its end. Through this bestowal Michael completed his universe sovereignty by experience and ended the Lucifer rebellion; above all, he revealed God to man and showed God a man made perfect. The Urantia Book stresses that the supreme purpose of the bestowal was to enhance the revelation of God.","sections":[{"h":"Seven Bestowals and Sovereignty Earned by Experience","items":[{"x":"A Creator Son must live the life of his creatures in their likeness, and this is part of the price paid for universe sovereignty.","r":["120:0.1"]},{"x":"After six bestowals, as a Melchizedek, a Lanonandek, an Adam, a seraphim, a mortal, and a morontia mortal, Michael became a mortal of flesh and blood on Urantia in his seventh.","r":["119:8.4","120:0.2"]},{"q":"Michael nasceu um criador, foi educado como um administrador e aperfeiçoado como um executivo; no entanto, foi-lhe pedido que conquistasse a sua própria soberania, por meio da experiência.","r":"119:8.2"},{"x":"In each bestowal Michael subjected himself to a different will of the Paradise Deities, and on Urantia he submitted wholly to the will of the Universal Father.","r":["120:0.4","120:1.2"]},{"x":"The sum of the seven bestowals became Nebadon's new revelation of the Supreme Being and also contributed to expanding the sovereignty of the Supreme.","r":["119:8.3","119:8.5"]},{"x":"The Eternal Son shares creature experience through the incarnations of the Paradise Sons, and so in Michael he actually came to mortal man.","r":["7:5.3","7:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Immanuel's Charge","items":[{"x":"Unlike his earlier bestowals, Michael had to appear on Urantia not as a fully grown being but as a helpless infant.","r":["120:1.1"]},{"x":"Michael was to lay aside all extraplanetary help and live his mortal life relying only on the Paradise Father.","r":["120:1.3"]},{"q":"Throughout your Urantia bestowal you need be concerned with but one thing, the unbroken communion between you and your Paradise Father","r":"120:1.4"},{"x":"Immanuel advised him to be chiefly a teacher, first liberating man's spiritual nature, enlightening his mind, and freeing him from age-old fears.","r":["120:2.5"]},{"x":"He was also counseled not to become involved in economic and political matters, not to form an organized cult, and to leave no writings or portraits.","r":["120:3.4","120:3.6","120:3.7"]},{"x":"Since a bestowal Son leaves no human offspring on a planet, Jesus would not enter the marriage relation.","r":["120:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Purposes of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"One goal of the bestowal was, as the Son of Man, to formally terminate the Lucifer rebellion in Satania and be recognized as the Planetary Prince of Urantia.","r":["120:2.2","120:2.3"]},{"x":"His life was intended less as an example for the people of Urantia than as an inspiration for all generations in all of Nebadon.","r":["120:2.7"]},{"x":"He revealed the Father to the creatures of flesh and at the same time showed God a new revelation of man.","r":["120:2.8"]},{"x":"He was charged to pour out the Spirit of Truth at the end of his bestowal, so that all normal mortals would have immediate access to the ministry of the Adjusters.","r":["120:2.6"]},{"q":"Nunca percais de vista o fato de que o propósito supremo da auto-outorga de Michael foi o de acentuar e engrandecer a revelação de Deus.","r":"120:4.4"},{"x":"His life of self-forgetful service forever silenced those who had charged the Creators with selfishly holding on to power.","r":["120:4.1"]}]},{"h":"God and Man","items":[{"q":"Ele não foi Deus, em associação com o homem; mas foi, sim, Deus encarnado no homem.","r":"120:4.2"},{"x":"Jesus did not gradually become God, nor did he become man at some moment; he was always God and man, and what grew was his awareness of that fact.","r":["120:4.2","120:4.3"]},{"x":"A bestowal in which a Paradise Son appears in the world by natural processes is the most fascinating of miracles even to local universe citizens.","r":["120:4.5","120:4.6"]}]},{"h":"A Full Human Life","items":[{"x":"Jesus passed through every stage of human life from infancy to death and personally experienced a wide range of emotions, from joy to deep sorrow.","r":["129:4.4","129:4.5"]},{"x":"He did not set a detailed example for all to copy but lived a truly human life so that each person could live his own life in his own time.","r":["129:4.7"]},{"x":"His life fully revealed God to man and offered God a perfected human personality, and it was wholly accepted by the Father.","r":["129:4.6"]},{"q":"Ele veio à Terra trazendo a plenitude de Deus para manifestar-se ao homem; e agora transformava-se quase na perfeição de homem, aguardando a ocasião de tornar-se manifesto para Deus.","r":"129:4.8"},{"x":"At his baptism in the Jordan he was a perfected mortal at the height of mind mastery, and his Adjuster stood by him as a Personalized Adjuster instead of fusing.","r":["136:2.2","136:2.3"]}]},{"h":"The Completion of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"Having completed the Urantia bestowal, Michael was recognized by the Ancients of Days and the Universal Father as the settled ruler of Nebadon.","r":["119:8.1"]},{"x":"Your little world has become known throughout Nebadon as the place where the Creator Son completed the experience required for sovereignty.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"q":"Em Jesus, o universo produziu um homem mortal em quem o espírito do amor triunfou sobre as limitações materiais do tempo e suplantou o fato da origem física.","r":"195:10.2"}]}],"see":["Filho Criador Michael","Caráter de Jesus","Ensinamentos de Jesus","Morte na cruz","Ressurreição de Jesus","Rebelião de Lúcifer"]},{"n":58,"t":"Beleza","en":"Beauty","sum":"Beauty, together with truth and goodness, is one of the three ways in which man comprehends divinity; it is the recognition of the harmonious unification of diverse realities. In the physical universe we see divine beauty, and its climax is the cosmic drama of man seeking God and God seeking man. Art and the appreciation of beauty become part of religion when they are linked with ethics and spiritual motivation, and Jesus valued the power of beauty to lead to worship.","sections":[{"h":"A Face of Divinity","items":[{"x":"Creatures can comprehend divinity as truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["0:1.17"]},{"x":"In the physical universe one sees divine beauty, in the intellectual world one discerns truth, and goodness is found in religious experience.","r":["2:6.1"]},{"x":"The Father enjoys the response of divine beauty that Havona presents and delights in providing the evolving universes with patterns of harmony.","r":["14:6.8"]},{"x":"Even beauty and truth would be divorced from the hope of survival were they not attributes of a loving Father.","r":["1:7.3"]}]},{"h":"What Beauty Is","items":[{"x":"Beauty, or art, is largely a matter of the unification of contrasts, and diversity is essential to the concept of beauty.","r":["56:10.3"]},{"x":"Beauty is the intellectual recognition of the harmonious synthesis of the diversities of phenomenal reality, derived from eternal oneness.","r":["56:10.11"]},{"q":"The discernment of supreme beauty is the discovery and integration of reality","r":"2:7.8"},{"q":"The discernment of the divine goodness in the eternal truth, that is ultimate beauty.","r":"2:7.8"},{"x":"Universal beauty is the recognition of the reflection of the Isle of Paradise in the material creation.","r":["56:10.17"]},{"q":"A beleza, o ritmo e a harmonia estão intelectualmente associados e são espiritualmente afins.","r":"44:7.2"}]},{"h":"The Climax of Universe Art","items":[{"x":"The climax of finite art is the drama of uniting the two poles of Creator and creature: man seeking God and God seeking man.","r":["56:10.3"]},{"q":"Daí, materialismo e ateísmo serem a maximização da fealdade, o clímax da antítese finita do belo.","r":"56:10.4"},{"x":"The existence of beauty implies the presence of an appreciative creature mind.","r":["56:10.11"]},{"x":"Cosmologic thinking is accompanied by curiosity toward harmony, aesthetic appreciation, and ethical sensitivity leading to God-consciousness.","r":["56:10.6","56:10.7","56:10.8"]}]},{"h":"Art and Religion","items":[{"x":"The search for beauty becomes part of religion only when it enriches ethical and moral concepts.","r":["101:9.4"]},{"q":"A arte só é religiosa quando se confunde com o propósito derivado da motivação espiritual elevada.","r":"101:9.4"},{"x":"The high mission of all art is to foreshadow higher reality and to crystallize the emotions of time into the thought of eternity.","r":["48:7.23"]},{"x":"Art arises from the attempt to escape the lack of beauty in the material environment; it is a gesture toward the morontia level.","r":["196:3.30"]},{"x":"If truth, beauty, and goodness are not unified in the experience of the artist or philosopher, the expression lacks a true soul.","r":["44:7.3"]},{"x":"The celestial artists of the morontia worlds portray in art the divine beauty of the Paradise Creators.","r":["44:8.6"]}]},{"h":"Beauty and Jesus","items":[{"x":"Viewing Flavius's art treasures, Jesus said there was no reason to condemn the appreciation of the beauty of things created by the Father and fashioned by man.","r":["142:4.2","142:4.3"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that beauty has great value in leading to the worship impulse, especially in children.","r":["167:6.5"]},{"x":"The spirit that Jesus and the Father send is not only the spirit of truth but also the spirit of idealistic beauty.","r":["155:6.11"]},{"x":"The Hebrews based their religion on goodness and the Greeks on beauty, but the love Jesus revealed embraces truth, beauty, and goodness together.","r":["5:4.6","196:3.19"]},{"x":"The beauty of divine love, once fully admitted to the human heart, forever destroys the charm of sin and the power of evil.","r":["188:5.3"]},{"q":"Assim, construais para vós próprios, e em vós próprios, galerias de reserva de beleza, bondade e grandeza artística.","r":"160:4.12"}]}],"see":["Verdade","Bondade","Amor","Adoração","Filosofia","Luz e vida"]},{"n":59,"t":"Bondade","en":"Goodness","sum":"Goodness, together with truth and beauty, is one of the three ways of comprehending divinity, but it is understood only in relation to personality. God's primal perfection consists in the perfection of the goodness inherent in his nature, and that goodness is fully revealed only in personal religious experience. For man, goodness is always relative and growing, more a quest than a possession until Paradise is attained. The goodness of God leads people to repentance.","sections":[{"h":"The Goodness of God","items":[{"q":"A perfeição primordial de Deus não consiste em uma retidão presumida, mas sim na perfeição inerente à bondade da Sua natureza divina.","r":"2:2.5"},{"q":"A bondade de Deus permanece no cerne do livre-arbítrio divino — a tendência universal para amar manifesta misericórdia, demonstra paciência e ministra o perdão.","r":"2:6.9"},{"x":"God is supremely great and good, and greatness and goodness are inseparably one in him.","r":["28:6.21"]},{"x":"The infinite goodness of the Father is beyond the finite mind's comprehension and is discerned only by contrast with relative imperfection.","r":["4:3.6"]},{"x":"God the Supreme is truth, beauty, and goodness, for these concepts are the finite maximum of ideational experience.","r":["117:1.7"]}]},{"h":"Goodness in Personality and Religion","items":[{"x":"Truth and beauty may be conceived without personality, but divine goodness is understood only in relation to personality.","r":["1:7.3"]},{"x":"The goodness of God is found only in the spiritual world of personal religious experience, and religion is essentially faith-trust in that goodness.","r":["2:6.1"]},{"q":"O homem poderia temer a um Deus grande, mas ama e confia apenas em um Deus de bondade.","r":"2:6.1"},{"x":"Goodness is the mind's recognition of the relative values of the levels of divine perfection, and it implies a moral mind that discriminates between good and evil.","r":["56:10.12"]},{"x":"Goodness embraces ethics, morality, and religion, the craving for experiential perfection.","r":["56:10.10"]}]},{"h":"Goodness Is Relative and Growing","items":[{"x":"Good and evil are words denoting relative levels of human comprehension of the observable universe.","r":["132:2.2"]},{"x":"One should not take social custom or religious tradition as the standard of goodness but choose the good by the spiritual standards set by the indwelling spirit.","r":["132:2.2"]},{"x":"Experience is good when it heightens the appreciation of beauty, strengthens the moral will, and enlarges the capacity to love and serve one's fellows.","r":["132:2.5"]},{"q":"Enquanto não alcançardes os níveis do Paraíso, a bondade será sempre mais uma busca do que uma posse, mais uma meta do que uma experiência de realização.","r":"132:2.8"},{"x":"As one ascends the universe scale, goodness increases and evil diminishes, and on Paradise goodness is no longer contrastive but perfect.","r":["132:2.6","132:2.9"]},{"q":"A bondade é viva, relativa, sempre em progressão, é uma experiência invariavelmente pessoal e eternamente correlacionada ao discernimento da verdade e da beleza.","r":"132:2.7"}]},{"h":"Goodness and the Possibility of Evil","items":[{"x":"The possibility of evil is necessary to moral choosing, but actual evil need not exist.","r":["132:2.10"]},{"x":"The presence of good and evil in the world is proof of the reality of personality, with a moral will that chooses between them.","r":["132:2.8"]},{"x":"Spiritual evolution is an experience of increasingly choosing the good, with a corresponding decrease in the potential of evil.","r":["132:3.8"]},{"x":"No good deed is ever wholly lost; it remains forever effective in proportion to the divinity of its motivation.","r":["48:6.7"]}]},{"h":"How Goodness Leads Men","items":[{"q":"A bondade de Deus conduz ao arrependimento; a beneficência de Deus conduz ao serviço; a misericórdia de Deus conduz à salvação; enquanto o amor de Deus conduz à adoração espontânea e inteligente e de todo o coração.","r":"149:6.4"},{"x":"Goodness without graciousness commands respect but repels affection; only when it is gracious is it universally attractive.","r":["171:7.2"]},{"x":"Righteousness of conduct must be judged by motives, so the highest goodness is unconscious.","r":["170:3.9"]},{"x":"An isolated morality that overemphasizes goodness while excluding truth and neglecting beauty fails to hold many modern minds.","r":["2:7.9"]},{"x":"All true goodness, whether personal morality, social fairness, or divine ministry, is equally true and beautiful.","r":["2:7.11"]}]}],"see":["Verdade","Beleza","Mal","Moralidade","Amor","Pai Universal"]},{"n":100,"t":"Busca da perfeição","en":"Quest for Perfection","sum":"The Father's command, \"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect,\" is an invitation calling every creature of time and space to the long and fascinating ascent toward Paradise. Urantia mortals cannot attain perfection in the infinite sense, but it is entirely possible for them to reach divine perfection on their own level. This journey begins with the hunger for perfection that the Adjuster awakens, passes through Havona to the Father bearing a perfection of purpose forged by faith, and continues beyond into the finaliter career.","sections":[{"h":"The Command to Be Perfect","items":[{"x":"The will creatures of all the universe have embarked on the eternal adventure of attaining God the Father, the long, long journey to Paradise.","r":["1:0.3"]},{"x":"The effort to achieve the perfection of divinity should be the first duty and the highest ambition of every struggling creature.","r":["1:0.4"]},{"x":"Mortals cannot be perfect in the sense of infinity, but it is entirely possible for them, from their starting point, to reach the divine goal God has set.","r":["1:0.5"]},{"q":"Essa busca sublime, pelo Deus dos universos, é a aventura suprema dos habitantes de todos os mundos do tempo e do espaço.","r":"1:0.6"},{"x":"The Eternal Son, together with the Father, broadcast this command to all creation, and it has motivated every survival plan and bestowal plan.","r":["7:5.1"]}]},{"h":"The Hunger for Perfection","items":[{"x":"The indwelling Adjuster unfailingly arouses in man's soul a searching hunger for perfection, which can be satisfied only by communion with God.","r":["102:1.6"]},{"q":"A alma faminta do homem recusa-se a se satisfazer com algo menor do que alcançar pessoalmente o Deus vivo.","r":"102:1.6"},{"x":"The names of Andon and Fonta, the first parents of mankind, mean the first creatures to show the longing for human perfection.","r":["63:0.3"]},{"x":"Spiritual progress rests on the recognition of spiritual poverty, the hunger for perfection, the desire to be like God, and the purpose to do the Father's will.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"The cosmic tension arising as all creatures and Creators together pursue divine perfection is resolved in the Supreme Being.","r":["116:7.6"]}]},{"h":"The Meaning of an Imperfect World","items":[{"x":"Courage requires an environment of hardship, altruism of inequality, and hope of uncertainty.","r":["3:5.6","3:5.7","3:5.8"]},{"x":"Faith grows where more can always be believed than known, and loyalty amid the possibility of disloyalty.","r":["3:5.9","3:5.12"]},{"x":"Had the Father made all mortals perfect from the start, he would have deprived them of the adventure and training of the long, gradual ascent.","r":["32:3.11"]},{"x":"The perfection that creatures of time finally attain is a true personal possession gained through personal effort.","r":["32:3.9"]}]},{"h":"Perfection of Purpose and Faith","items":[{"x":"On arriving in Havona the pilgrim brings only one perfection, perfection of purpose.","r":["26:4.12","26:4.13"]},{"x":"Faith has won perfection of purpose, and now the pilgrim must develop perfection of understanding.","r":["26:4.14"]},{"q":"A aptidão para compreender é o passaporte dos mortais para o Paraíso.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Long before reaching Havona, ascenders have learned to feast upon uncertainty and to fatten upon disappointment.","r":["26:5.3"]},{"q":"“Junto com Deus, nada — absolutamente nada — é impossível”.","r":"26:5.3"}]},{"h":"Havona and Attaining the Father","items":[{"x":"After the brief test on Urantia, the morontia stages of the mansion worlds and the local universe, and spiritual training in the superuniverse, the pilgrim goes to Havona.","r":["14:5.1"]},{"x":"In the circuits of Havona ascenders progress inward, coming to comprehend in turn God the Supreme, the Infinite Spirit, and the Eternal Son.","r":["26:6.2","26:8.1"]},{"x":"Those who fail in Deity attainment are comforted and try again; their disappointment differs only in magnitude from many experiences in rising from chaos to glory.","r":["26:10.2"]},{"x":"Attaining the Universal Father is the passport to eternity, and it forever demonstrates the justice of the command to be perfect.","r":["26:9.2","26:9.3"]},{"q":"O teste do tempo está quase chegando ao fim; a escalada para a eternidade já foi quase inteiramente percorrida.","r":"26:9.3"}]},{"h":"The Endless Journey","items":[{"q":"Nós, de Uversa, não sabemos o “destino da finalidade” dos mortais ascendentes do tempo.","r":"31:3.2"},{"x":"Finaliters are recorded only as spirits of the sixth stage, suggesting that yet another stage lies before them.","r":["31:3.3"]},{"x":"Even the splendid development of worlds settled in light and life is only the first stage of an endless ascending career.","r":["55:6.7"]},{"x":"Though his body came from the dust, man, if he truly wills it, will become a child of God the Supreme and a divine son of the Paradise Father.","r":["112:7.19"]}]}],"see":["Ascensão mortal","Havona","Corpo de Finalidade","Crescimento","Fé","Pai Universal"]},{"n":77,"t":"Caligástia","en":"Caligastia","sum":"Caligastia was the Planetary Prince who came to Urantia some five hundred thousand years ago, a Lanonandek Son of rich experience and a brilliant career, who joined the Lucifer rebellion and betrayed the world entrusted to him. His apostasy isolated Urantia from the universe circuits, sixty members of the planetary staff followed him, and the culture of Dalamatia collapsed. He later entrapped Adam and Eve, and after Jesus defeated him on Mount Hermon he lost the power to invade the minds of men.","sections":[{"h":"A Brilliant Planetary Prince","items":[{"x":"Caligastia was a secondary Lanonandek Son with rich experience in the administration of the local universe and of Satania.","r":["66:1.1"]},{"x":"Lucifer promoted him to his personal staff, and he had long sought appointment as a Planetary Prince.","r":["66:1.2","66:1.3"]},{"x":"He had a record of loyalty and devotion, but also a restless temperament and a tendency to oppose the established order.","r":["66:1.4"]},{"q":"Nenhum príncipe dos planetas jamais embarcou em uma carreira de governo de um mundo com uma experiência preparatória mais rica ou de melhores perspectivas do que Caligástia, naquele dia memorável, há meio milhão de anos.","r":"66:1.5"},{"x":"He arrived about five hundred thousand years ago, when the Sangik races were appearing, and set up his headquarters in the Mesopotamian region.","r":["66:0.2"]}]},{"h":"Dalamatia and the One Hundred","items":[{"x":"His associate assistant, Daligastia, headed the staff, and one hundred volunteers chosen from Jerusem formed the corporeal staff.","r":["66:2.2","66:2.4"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers transplanted the life plasm of one hundred male and female descendants of Andon and Fonta into the material bodies of the staff.","r":["66:2.6","66:2.7"]},{"x":"The Dalamatian revelation, the first teaching of the staff, lasted more than three hundred thousand years until it was interrupted by secession.","r":["92:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Betrayal and Isolation","items":[{"x":"At Satan's visit in the three hundred thousandth year of his rule, Caligastia agreed to betray the planet once the rebellion was proclaimed.","r":["67:1.1","67:1.2"]},{"q":"E, de todas as formas do mal, nenhuma é mais destrutiva para a constituição da personalidade do que a traição da confiança e a deslealdade à confiança dos amigos.","r":"67:1.3"},{"x":"Daligastia proclaimed Caligastia \"God of Urantia,\" and at that moment the system circuits were cut and Urantia was isolated.","r":["67:2.3","67:2.4"]},{"x":"Van declared this tantamount to planetary rebellion and protested, and after a struggle of more than seven years the loyalists were vindicated.","r":["67:2.2","67:2.6"]},{"x":"Forty members of the staff refused to rebel; the sixty who rebelled chose Nod as their leader and were reduced to mortal status.","r":["67:3.2","67:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Consequences of the Rebellion","items":[{"q":"Caligástia, com um máximo de inteligência e uma vasta experiência nos assuntos do universo, desviou-se — abraçou o pecado.","r":"67:3.9"},{"x":"Amadon, of lesser intellect, remained loyal to the end, showing that loyalty counts more than intelligence in spiritual choice.","r":["67:3.8","67:3.9"]},{"x":"His plan to rebuild society at once on his ideas of personal and group liberty failed, plunging the world into deeper confusion.","r":["67:5.3"]},{"x":"One hundred and sixty-two years after the rebellion, Dalamatia sank beneath the sea.","r":["67:5.4"]},{"x":"Afterward twelve Melchizedek receivers administered the planet, and Van established outposts of civilization throughout the world.","r":["67:6.5","67:6.6"]}]},{"h":"From the Days of Adam to the Days of Jesus","items":[{"x":"Caligastia and Daligastia hindered the preparation of the Garden of Eden and confused its inhabitants with teachings of unbridled liberty.","r":["73:2.5","74:5.6"]},{"q":"Caligástia tivera êxito na armadilha feita para Adão e Eva, mas não realizou o seu propósito de levá-los à rebelião aberta contra o governo do universo.","r":"75:7.7"},{"x":"Serapatatia, though well-meaning, never realized that he was playing into the hands of Caligastia and Daligastia.","r":["75:3.6"]},{"x":"Jesus met Caligastia alone on Mount Hermon and prevailed, after which Caligastia's apostasy was virtually settled.","r":["134:8.6","134:8.9","136:3.1"]},{"x":"Before leaving Urantia, Michael offered mercy to Caligastia and Daligastia, but they rejected his offer.","r":["53:8.6"]},{"q":"he has absolutely no power to enter the minds of men, neither can he draw near to their souls to tempt or corrupt them unless they really desire to be cursed with his wicked presence.","r":"53:8.6"},{"q":"Caligástia tem sido relativamente impotente, desde a cruz de Cristo.","r":"53:8.9"}]}],"see":["Rebelião de Lúcifer","Urântia","Adão e Eva","Criaturas intermediárias","Maquiventa Melquisedeque","Civilização"]},{"n":85,"t":"Caráter de Jesus","en":"Character of Jesus","sum":"In The Urantia Book's portrayal of the character of Jesus, the most distinctive feature is not so much flawlessness as symmetry, the exquisite and balanced unification of all his qualities. He was enthusiastic but never fanatical, courageous but never foolhardy, full of gladness yet humble. At the center stood a childlike trust in God and a deep love for people, and he asked his followers not so much to believe in him as to believe with him.","sections":[{"h":"Balance and Unity","items":[{"q":"O aspecto singular da personalidade do Mestre não era tanto a sua perfeição, quanto a sua simetria, a sua unificação extraordinária e equilibrada.","r":"100:7.1"},{"x":"An ordinary mortal cannot attain Jesus' perfection of character, but it is altogether possible to develop a strong and unified personality along the lines of his.","r":["100:7.1"]},{"x":"He was emotional but not flighty, sympathetic but not sentimental, pious but not sanctimonious.","r":["100:7.4"]},{"x":"His plans were marked by consecrated common sense, with nothing queer, erratic, or hysterical about them.","r":["100:7.3"]},{"x":"As a perfectly unified personality, Jesus still today unifies human experience and simplifies life.","r":["100:7.18"]},{"q":"Jesus foi grande, porque era bom e, mais, ele confraternizava com as crianças pequenas.","r":"100:7.17"}]},{"h":"Sincerity and Courage","items":[{"x":"He was free from affectation and hypocrisy and lived as he taught, staying true to the truth even when his sincerity brought him suffering.","r":["100:7.2"]},{"x":"He was frank but always kind; he hated sin but loved the sinner, and in all his honesty he was fair.","r":["100:7.11"]},{"q":"A coragem de Jesus foi magnífica, mas ele nunca era irrefletido. A sua palavra-chave foi: “não temais”.","r":"100:7.15"},{"x":"Even when urged, he did not hurry, saying his hour had not yet come; when indignant at evil, his anger was never directed at the sinner.","r":["100:7.14"]},{"x":"He did not seek popular support and was not swayed by people's opinions; he was brave but never proud.","r":["161:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Gladness and Kindness","items":[{"q":"Este homem da Galiléia não era um homem de tristezas; era uma alma da alegria.","r":"100:7.13"},{"x":"He was not a blind optimist, but out of trust in God and confidence in man he always encouraged others to be of good cheer.","r":["100:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus was a child of joy and a man of rare humor, and at the same time a man acquainted with sorrow.","r":["129:4.4"]},{"x":"Graciousness is the aroma of friendliness from a love-saturated soul, and Jesus spread that gladness wherever he went.","r":["171:7.1","171:7.2"]},{"x":"He was always generous, repeating that it is more blessed to give than to receive, but he was never wasteful or extravagant.","r":["100:7.10"]}]},{"h":"His Way with People","items":[{"x":"Because Jesus truly understood people, he showed genuine sympathy, yet he never indulged in pity or fostered their self-pity.","r":["171:7.3"]},{"x":"He never hurried and comforted people \"as he passed by\"; they felt they were consulting with him rather than confessing to him.","r":["171:7.5"]},{"x":"He did not try to direct or manage people, and those who received his smile felt their power to solve their own problems increase.","r":["171:7.6"]},{"x":"Great things happened because people not only believed in him but he also believed greatly in them.","r":["171:7.8"]},{"q":"Era literalmente certo que, “ele caminhava fazendo o bem”.","r":"171:7.9"},{"x":"The apostles remembered him as a loyal friend who treated all with equal kindness without flattery, and who loved even sinners and enemies.","r":["161:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Childlike Faith","items":[{"x":"Jesus' faith was not tradition or intellectual belief but wholly personal and spiritual, born of experience with the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["196:0.1","196:0.5"]},{"x":"He did not hold faith as a consolation in hardship but enjoyed it as the serenity and thrill of living in the Father's presence.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"q":"Jesus confiou em Deus, do mesmo modo que uma criança confia em um pai.","r":"196:0.11"},{"x":"His strong faith never turned into fanaticism and was always in harmony with balanced judgment about family love, social obligation, and economic necessity.","r":["196:0.6","196:0.7"]},{"x":"His sublime self-forgetfulness shows in his reply when called good teacher: \"Why do you call me good?\"","r":["196:0.9"]}]},{"h":"What It Means to Follow Him","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not ask his disciples to believe in him but to believe with him in the love of God.","r":["196:0.13"]},{"x":"To follow Jesus means to share his faith and to take part in his spirit of unselfish service to men.","r":["196:1.3"]},{"x":"A great service of this revelation will be to bring back the living Jesus, the human Jesus buried in theological tradition.","r":["196:1.1","196:1.2"]}]}],"see":["Auto-outorga de Jesus","Ensinamentos de Jesus","Fé","Amor","Alegria e felicidade","Os doze apóstolos"]},{"n":81,"t":"Casamento e família","en":"Marriage and Family","sum":"Marriage is human society's institutional response to the biologic fact of bisexuality, and the home is the crowning fruit of that long evolutionary struggle. The Urantia Book says that marriage is not a sacrament but an essentially human institution, yet it teaches that pair marriage and the good home are the roots of civilization's stability and of morality, and the place where the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man are first learned.","sections":[{"h":"The Origin and Social Meaning of Marriage","items":[{"x":"Marriage is not the mating instinct itself but the institutional reaction society developed to regulate that instinct.","r":["82:1.1","82:3.1"]},{"q":"O casamento deu o lar à humanidade, e o lar é a glória que coroa toda a longa e renhida luta evolucionária.","r":"82:0.1"},{"x":"Marriage always has an outer domain regulated by mores and law and a private, personal domain between man and woman.","r":["82:3.2"]},{"x":"Marriage has always been bound up with property and religion: property stabilized marriage, and religion moralized it.","r":["82:4.1"]},{"x":"Material necessity founded marriage, sex appetite embellished it, religion sanctioned it, and love later came to justify it.","r":["84:0.1"]},{"x":"Intelligently adjusting the strong sex urge to social regulation is the supreme test of the reality of civilization, and it always demands self-control.","r":["82:1.10"]}]},{"h":"Monogamy and Pair Marriage","items":[{"x":"Monogamy is not natural to evolving man at first, but it has great cultural value and is unquestionably best for the children.","r":["83:6.1","83:6.2"]},{"q":"A monogamia tem sido sempre, é agora, e para sempre será a meta idealista da evolução sexual humana.","r":"83:6.6"},{"x":"The ideal of pair marriage entails self-denial, so it often fails when the partners lack rugged self-control.","r":["83:6.6"]},{"x":"Monogamy fosters delicate sentiments, refinement of moral character, and spiritual growth, and is best for the happiness of parents and the welfare of children.","r":["83:6.7","83:6.8"]},{"x":"Society should not ignore the plight of those who fail to obtain mates but should always treat them with kindness and consideration.","r":["83:6.4","83:6.5"]}]},{"h":"A Human Institution, Not a Sacrament","items":[{"q":"Marriage which culminates in the home is indeed man's most exalted institution, but it is essentially human","r":"83:8.1"},{"x":"Comparing the union of husband and wife to the relation of the Adjuster and man, or to a divine union, is an unfortunate analogy that has caused great confusion.","r":["83:8.2","83:8.3"]},{"x":"The very fact that marriage can be dissolved shows that God is not a party to the union.","r":["83:8.4"]},{"x":"Yet there is an ideal of marriage on the high spheres, embodied supremely by the Material Sons and Daughters; ideal mortal marriage is humanly sacred.","r":["83:8.5"]},{"x":"The marriage ideals of youth should not be crushed, but they should be balanced by learning the realities of home life beforehand, with a degree of disillusionment.","r":["83:8.6","83:8.7"]}]},{"h":"The Home, Chief Civilizing Agency","items":[{"x":"Religious, social, and educational institutions are needed, but since children learn most essentials of life from home and neighborhood, the home is the chief civilizing agency.","r":["82:0.2","82:0.3"]},{"q":"O matrimônio é a mãe de todas as instituições humanas, pois conduz diretamente à fundação e manutenção do lar, que é a base estrutural da sociedade.","r":"84:6.8"},{"q":"Se as famílias são boas, do mesmo modo a sociedade o é.","r":"84:7.1"},{"x":"Man and woman can never fully understand each other, but they complement each other effectively, and their differences continue into the morontia and spirit careers.","r":["84:6.3","84:6.6","84:6.7"]},{"x":"Marriage is now passing beyond the stage that regarded the wife as property into a new era that respects personality.","r":["84:7.3","84:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Parents, Children, and the Spiritual Meaning of the Home","items":[{"x":"Bearing children is not a parental right but the supreme responsibility of human existence; civilization places duties on parents and rights on children.","r":["84:7.25","84:7.26"]},{"x":"The home is the basic unit of brotherhood, where parents and children together learn the patience, altruism, tolerance, and forbearance that brotherhood requires.","r":["84:7.28"]},{"x":"Society would be greatly improved by returning to the practice of the family council, as among the Andites, where family affairs were discussed freely and fraternally.","r":["84:7.29"]},{"q":"A vida familiar é progenitora da verdadeira moralidade, é o ancestral da consciência da lealdade ao dever.","r":"84:7.30"},{"x":"Jesus said the gospel of the kingdom would be better received when understood in family terms, as the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that the true family rests on seven facts: existence, safety and pleasure, education, discipline, companionship, love and mercy, and provision for the future.","r":["142:7.5","142:7.11"]},{"x":"After Joseph's death the young Jesus made the support of the family his first duty and acted as a father to his brothers and sisters.","r":["126:3.2","126:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Threats to the Home","items":[{"x":"The greatest threat to family life is the modern pleasure mania that pursues self-gratification.","r":["84:8.1"]},{"q":"A fome da alma não pode ser satisfeita por meio dos prazeres físicos; o amor do lar e das crianças não aumenta com uma busca pouco sábia do prazer.","r":"84:8.4"},{"x":"Wholesome play and recreation have value, but pleasure that brings the breakup of marriage and the home is self-destructive.","r":["84:8.5","84:8.6"]},{"x":"Attempts to shift parental responsibility to the state or the church would be suicidal to the welfare and progress of civilization.","r":["84:7.27"]}]}],"see":["Civilização","Moralidade","Irmandade dos homens","Amor","Filhos e Filhas Materiais","Governo e sociedade"]},{"n":73,"t":"Ciência e religião","en":"Science and Religion","sum":"Science explores the world of facts and energy-matter by reason, and religion experiences values and spiritual realities by faith. They are independent domains starting from different postulates; philosophy seeks to coordinate them, and revelation affirms that the First Cause of science and the saving God of religion are one and the same. Science purifies religion by clearing away superstition, and religion gives the impulse of brotherhood by which the civilization of a scientific age can live together.","sections":[{"h":"Two Different Domains","items":[{"q":"A ciência lida com os fatos; a religião ocupa-se apenas dos valores.","r":"101:5.2"},{"q":"A razão é o método da ciência; a fé o método da religião; a lógica é a técnica com que a filosofia tenta lidar.","r":"101:2.2"},{"x":"Science assumes without proof the reality of matter, motion, and life; religion assumes mind, spirit, and the Supreme.","r":["103:7.11","103:7.10"]},{"q":"As convicções da ciência procedem integralmente do intelecto; as certezas da religião brotam das próprias fundações da personalidade inteira.","r":"102:1.4"},{"x":"In science the idea precedes its expression, but in religion the experience of realization precedes the expression of the idea.","r":["102:3.13"]}]},{"h":"Different Eyes for Seeing God","items":[{"x":"God is to science a cause, to philosophy an idea, and to religion a person, the loving heavenly Father.","r":["1:6.2","4:4.7"]},{"x":"The existence of God can never be proved by scientific experiment or pure logic; it is realized only in human experience.","r":["1:2.7","101:10.6"]},{"x":"Reason may reach a First Cause by studying nature, but faith is needed to transform it into a God of salvation.","r":["101:2.3"]},{"x":"Revelation affirms that the First Cause of science and the saving God of religion are the same Deity.","r":["101:2.7"]},{"x":"In science God is a possibility, in philosophy a probability, and in religion a certainty.","r":["102:6.8"]}]},{"h":"A Relationship of Mutual Help","items":[{"q":"E a ciência também estabiliza a filosofia por meio da eliminação do erro: enquanto purifica a religião, ao exterminar a superstição.","r":"81:6.10"},{"x":"Evolutionary religion must be continually refined by the censorship of revelation and in the crucible of true science.","r":["92:3.10","99:3.7"]},{"x":"Science enables man to control his physical environment, and religion gives the impulse of brotherhood that lets people live together in the complex civilization of a scientific age.","r":["103:7.9"]},{"x":"Both science and religion need more searching and fearless self-criticism, and teachers in both fields are often too dogmatic.","r":["103:7.7"]},{"x":"Harmonizing the discoveries of science with the insights of religion requires a sincere desire to follow truth wherever it leads.","r":["103:7.5"]}]},{"h":"Coordinating Philosophy and Revelation","items":[{"x":"Science discovers the material world, religion evaluates it, and philosophy seeks to interpret meanings by coordinating both viewpoints.","r":["103:7.15"]},{"x":"Harmonizing science and religion is difficult because of ignorance of the intervening domain of morontia; the morontia viewpoint removes the difference.","r":["103:6.7"]},{"x":"Metaphysics is man's earnest but futile attempt to compensate for the absence of the morontia mota.","r":["103:6.7"]},{"x":"Revelation does not originate science or religion; its function is to coordinate both with the truth of reality.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"x":"True revelation never renders science unnatural, religion unreasonable, or philosophy illogical.","r":["101:2.2","102:3.15"]}]},{"h":"Beyond the Materialistic Age","items":[{"x":"The statements on physical science in revelatory papers will soon need revision, and their cosmology is not inspired.","r":["101:4.2"]},{"q":"Quanto mais souberdes da ciência, tanto menos certos podereis estar; quanto mais de religião tiverdes, tanto mais seguros estareis.","r":"102:1.3"},{"x":"Scientists unintentionally plunged mankind into a materialistic panic, but the religion of Jesus has never become bankrupt.","r":["195:6.1"]},{"x":"What science has destroyed is only childish illusions born of mistaken interpretations; true religion remains untouched.","r":["195:6.4"]},{"q":"Os fatos nunca contradizem a fé espiritual real; as teorias, sim, podem contradizer.","r":"195:7.1"}]}],"see":["Filosofia","Revelação","Verdade","Fé","Experiência religiosa","Morôncia"]},{"n":82,"t":"Civilização","en":"Civilization","sum":"Civilization is a racial acquirement that mankind won through a long and arduous struggle, starting from a state close to the animal. Because it is not passed on automatically by heredity, each generation must hand it on anew through the home and education. The Urantia Book examines one by one the material, intellectual, and social factors that sustain civilization, yet it says that the power that truly lifts culture is spiritual idealism.","sections":[{"h":"Civilization, an Acquired Heritage","items":[{"q":"Civilization is a racial acquirement; it is not biologically inherent","r":"68:0.2"},{"x":"Scientific, philosophic, and religious achievements are not inherited; they are kept only by wisely conserving social inheritance and educating each generation anew.","r":["68:0.2"]},{"x":"Biologic evolution and cultural civilization do not necessarily go together, but culture cannot flourish without a background of adequate racial progress.","r":["81:5.1"]},{"x":"Even though the missions of Caligastia and Adam failed, evolution kept the races moving forward; evolution may be delayed but it cannot be stopped.","r":["81:0.1"]},{"x":"The slogan \"back to nature\" is an ignorant delusion based on belief in a golden age that never existed.","r":["68:1.7"]}]},{"h":"How Society Arose","items":[{"x":"Primitive man was not naturally brotherly; through bitter experience he learned that to survive he must unite, and so he cooperated reluctantly.","r":["68:1.1","68:1.4"]},{"x":"Civilization became man's insurance against violent death, and man pays the premium by submitting to society's mores.","r":["68:1.2","81:5.4"]},{"x":"Hunger, sex love, vanity, and fear of ghosts drew people together and bound them into society.","r":["68:2.4","68:2.6"]},{"q":"Quase tudo de valor perdurável na civilização tem as suas raízes na família.","r":"68:2.8"},{"x":"The one hundred of Dalamatia did not try to change the primitive races all at once but trained the best of the tribes and sent them back as emissaries of social uplift.","r":["66:6.3","66:6.4"]},{"x":"The chief purpose of the Material Sons and Daughters is to move evolving man from the hunting and herding stages to the agricultural stage.","r":["52:3.3"]}]},{"h":"Factors Sustaining Civilization","items":[{"x":"Factors such as the natural environment, capital goods, scientific knowledge, human resources, language, machines, and the coordination of experts sustain present civilization.","r":["81:6.2","81:6.3","81:6.29"]},{"q":"A cultura nunca se desenvolve sob condições de pobreza; o lazer é essencial ao progresso da civilização.","r":"81:6.6"},{"x":"Science stabilizes philosophy by eliminating error and purifies religion by destroying superstition.","r":["81:6.10"]},{"x":"A common language promotes peace and insures culture, and international exchange in language, trade, art, science, and religion should be encouraged.","r":["81:6.18","81:6.19"]},{"x":"Science guided by wisdom can liberate mankind, but it becomes a calamity for nations lacking the wisdom to adjust the transitional problems of mechanization.","r":["81:6.22"]}]},{"h":"Ideals, Education, and Leadership","items":[{"x":"The basic institution for passing the torch of culture to the next generation is the home, followed by play, social life, and the school.","r":["81:6.23","81:6.24"]},{"q":"Os ideais de uma geração esculpem os canais do destino da posteridade imediata.","r":"81:6.26"},{"x":"Intelligence controls the machinery of civilization and wisdom directs it, but the energy that lifts culture from level to level is spiritual idealism.","r":["81:6.27"]},{"q":"At first life was a struggle for existence; now, for a standard of living; next it will be for quality of thinking","r":"81:6.28"},{"x":"High civilization is born when material wealth, intellectual greatness, moral worth, social cleverness, and cosmic insight are wisely coordinated.","r":["81:6.38"]},{"x":"Civilization is jeopardized only when able and wise leadership disappears, and such leadership has never exceeded one per cent of the population.","r":["81:6.37","81:6.42"]}]},{"h":"Duties and Dangers of Civilization","items":[{"x":"Cultural society is not a club of free memberships but a union of workers making a better world for their descendants.","r":["81:5.3"]},{"x":"Every right is linked with social obligation, and liberty that accepts collective regulation is the legitimate goal of social evolution.","r":["81:5.6","81:5.7"]},{"q":"A automanutenção origina a sociedade, ao passo que a autogratificação excessiva destrói a civilização.","r":"68:2.2"},{"x":"Society is not a divine institution but a phenomenon of evolution, so it may be experimented with fearlessly, but great changes should not be attempted suddenly.","r":["81:6.39","81:6.40"]},{"x":"Modern civilization has grown intellectually and scientifically but has stagnated in ethical awareness, spiritual development, and the safeguarding of the home.","r":["81:6.25"]}]},{"h":"Civilization and Religion","items":[{"x":"Religion renders its highest social service when least entangled with secular institutions, and it should not directly engage in building a new order or preserving the old.","r":["99:0.1","99:0.2"]},{"x":"As civilization advances, the attitude of seeking first heavenly realities becomes all the more necessary, even amid efforts to solve material problems.","r":["195:5.1"]},{"x":"Modern culture must become spiritually baptized with a new revelation of Jesus' life.","r":["195:10.1"]}]}],"see":["Governo e sociedade","Casamento e família","Raças","Evolução","Ciência e religião","Adão e Eva"]},{"n":16,"t":"Constelações e sistemas locais","en":"Constellations and Local Systems","sum":"Um universo local divide-se em cem constelações, e cada constelação em cem sistemas locais. A constelação, governada pelos Altíssimos da ordem Vorondadeque, é uma unidade legislativa que socializa os mortais ascendentes em sedes como Edêntia; o sistema local, governado por um Soberano do Sistema da ordem Lanonandeque, é uma unidade executiva que recebe em Jerusém e nos mundos das mansões os mortais recém-sobreviventes. Urântia pertence ao sistema de Satânia, na constelação de Norlatiadeque, e tem recebido cuidados especiais desde a rebelião de Lúcifer.","sections":[{"h":"As divisões do universo local","items":[{"x":"Urântia é o 606º mundo habitado do sistema de Satânia, em Norlatiadeque, uma das cem constelações de Nébadon.","r":["43:0.1"]},{"x":"Um sistema é composto de cerca de mil mundos habitáveis, e uma constelação, de cem sistemas.","r":["15:2.3","15:2.4"]},{"x":"As constelações funcionam como unidades legislativas e os sistemas locais como unidades executivas, ao passo que o governo de Sálvington é a autoridade judicial e coordenadora suprema.","r":["43:2.2"]},{"x":"Os governantes das constelações ligam os sistemas locais à administração do universo em Sálvington e, por meio da refletividade, aos Anciães dos Dias em Uversa.","r":["43:0.1"]}]},{"h":"O governo da constelação e os Altíssimos","items":[{"x":"Uma constelação é governada por três Altíssimos da ordem Vorondadeque, sendo aquele que preside chamado de Pai da Constelação.","r":["43:3.2"]},{"q":"no disaffection of the Vorondadek Sons has ever occurred in Nebadon.","r":"43:3.1"},{"x":"A assembleia legislativa da constelação compõe-se de três grupos: uma câmara baixa de ascendentes, uma terceira câmara de serafins e outros seres, e uma câmara alta dos Filhos divinos.","r":["43:2.5","43:2.6","43:2.7"]},{"x":"Os Altíssimos ocupam-se do bem-estar das nações e das raças, mais do que dos indivíduos, governando nos reinos dos homens, mais do que no coração individual.","r":["43:3.5","43:9.4"]},{"x":"Nos mundos isolados pela rebelião há um observador Vorondadeque estacionado, e é ele quem de fato “governa nos reinos dos homens”.","r":["43:5.17"]},{"x":"O Fiel dos Dias em Edêntia está ao lado dos Pais da Constelação como representante da Trindade, mas nunca dá conselho a menos que lhe seja pedido.","r":["43:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Edêntia: o jardim de Deus","items":[{"x":"Edêntia, a sede da constelação, é cerca de cem vezes maior que Urântia, e setenta esferas principais e setecentos satélites giram em torno dela.","r":["43:0.2"]},{"x":"A capital da constelação é rica em ornamentação viva e é chamada de “os jardins de Deus”; metade da área de Edêntia é dedicada aos jardins dos Altíssimos.","r":["43:6.1","43:6.2"]},{"q":"there is nothing in all Edentia to make any living being afraid.","r":"43:6.5"},{"x":"Passando pelos setenta mundos, os mortais ascendentes vivem com os univitátias e aprendem a ética de grupo e a verdadeira socialização da personalidade moroncial.","r":["43:8.3","43:8.4"]},{"q":"Intelectual, social e espiritualmente, duas criaturas morais não duplicam, meramente, os seus potenciais pessoais de realização no universo, pela técnica da associação; elas estão muito mais próximas de quadruplicar as suas possibilidades de êxito e de realização.","r":"43:8.11"},{"x":"A permanência na constelação é o ponto médio do caminho entre o ser semelhante ao animal e o espírito ascendente, o período mais uniforme e estável da carreira moroncial.","r":["43:9.2","43:9.3"]}]},{"h":"O sistema local e Jerusém","items":[{"x":"O executivo-chefe de um sistema local é o Soberano do Sistema, um Filho Lanonandeque primário; o atual soberano de Satânia é Lanaforge, sucessor de Lúcifer.","r":["45:2.1","45:3.2"]},{"x":"Na história de Nébadon houve três casos de deslealdade entre os Soberanos dos Sistemas, sendo a rebelião de Lúcifer em Satânia o último e o mais extenso.","r":["45:2.1"]},{"x":"Jerusém é circundado por sete mundos de cultura de transição e pelos seus satélites, e os sete mundos das mansões são satélites do primeiro mundo de transição.","r":["45:0.1","45:0.2"]},{"q":"As capitais dos sistemas são singulares, como únicos mundos que exibem quase perfeitamente todas as três fases da existência no universo: a material, a moroncial e a espiritual.","r":"46:4.8"},{"x":"Em Jerusém não há dia e noite separados nem estações, e a luz é filtrada uniformemente de todo o céu, e não de uma única fonte.","r":["46:1.4","46:1.5"]},{"q":"O governo representativo é o ideal divino do autogoverno entre os seres que não são perfeitos.","r":"45:7.3"}]},{"h":"O treinamento para a ascensão na capital do sistema","items":[{"x":"Os mundos das mansões são o lugar onde os mortais que não se fusionaram com o seu Ajustador na vida na carne recebem a oportunidade de retomar a sua realização espiritual interrompida.","r":["45:7.1"]},{"x":"Os Filhos e Filhas Materiais, cidadãos permanentes de Jerusém, tornam-se os patrocinadores e instrutores imediatos dos mortais ascendentes.","r":["45:5.5","45:6.2"]},{"x":"Os ascendentes a quem falta a experiência de pais devem adquirir essa experiência essencial nos lares dos Filhos Materiais em Jerusém ou nos berçários probatórios.","r":["45:6.4","45:6.6"]},{"x":"Nas eleições de Jerusém, o valor de um voto varia segundo o grau de sabedoria moroncial, e só se pode partir para a constelação depois de alcançar a personalidade mota.","r":["45:7.6","45:7.8"]},{"x":"As assembleias realizadas no mundo dos finalitores asseguram aos que permanecem nos mundos das mansões que também eles podem completar a longa jornada.","r":["45:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Cuidados especiais após a rebelião","items":[{"x":"Desde a rebelião de Lúcifer, os Altíssimos de Edêntia assumiram certas fases da autoridade planetária nos mundos rebeldes e ainda as exercem.","r":["43:3.7"]},{"x":"Lúcifer e a maioria das personalidades que o seguiram estão confinados nos mundos-prisão que circundam o mundo do Pai em Jerusém, uma solene advertência para toda Nébadon.","r":["45:1.11"]},{"x":"Depois do triunfo de Cristo Michael, Satã foi rejeitado por unanimidade pelos Soberanos dos Sistemas em um conclave em Edêntia.","r":["43:4.9"]},{"q":"Quando não há nenhuma porta aberta para a recepção do mal, não existe oportunidade para se nutrir o pecado.","r":"43:4.9"},{"x":"Os vinte e quatro conselheiros de Jerusém são pessoas originárias de Urântia que representam Michael nas chamadas nominais de Satânia e nos planos de ascensão dos mundos isolados.","r":["45:4.1","45:4.2"]}]}],"see":["Universo local de Nébadon","Mundos das mansões","Rebelião de Lúcifer","Ascensão mortal","Filhos e Filhas Materiais","Melquisedeques"]},{"n":32,"t":"Corpo de Finalidade","en":"Corps of the Finality","sum":"The Corps of the Finality is the presently known destination of the ascending mortals of time, who are mustered into it after finding God and attaining Paradise. Centered on glorified mortals, it also includes Havona natives, Gravity Messengers, adopted seraphim, Material Sons, and midway creatures, and its members now serve on worlds settled in light and life. Their ultimate destiny has not been revealed, but it is conjectured to concern the future universes of outer space.","sections":[{"h":"Composition of the Corps","items":[{"x":"The primary Corps of the Finality consists of Havona natives, Gravity Messengers, glorified mortals, adopted seraphim, and glorified Material Sons and midway creatures.","r":["31:0.1","31:0.8"]},{"x":"The corps is organized in companies of one thousand, of which mortals and seraphim make up 990, leaving only ten places for the other beings.","r":["31:1.3","31:3.1"]},{"x":"All are received as equals, yet that equality does not erase individuality or personal identity.","r":["31:0.9"]},{"x":"Gravity Messengers are personalized Adjusters who transcend time and space, and they share a deep affection with mortals who have fused with Adjusters.","r":["31:2.2","31:2.4"]},{"q":"De fato são as almas cumulativamente comprovadas e verdadeiras do tempo e do espaço — o sal evolucionário do universo — e são, para sempre, à prova do mal e a salvo do pecado.","r":"31:0.13"},{"x":"Evangels of light are attached temporarily without taking the oath, and the one vacancy beyond the 999 permanent members remains a mystery.","r":["31:7.1","31:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Who Enters","items":[{"x":"Of all the creatures of the grand universe, only those fused with the Father are mustered into the mortal Corps of the Finality and take the finaliter oath.","r":["30:4.31"]},{"x":"Spirit-fused mortals usually remain in local universe service and do not share the destiny of the Paradise Corps of the Finality.","r":["40:9.9"]},{"x":"Many guardian seraphim ascend with their mortal wards, take the same finaliter oath, and are mustered into the corps.","r":["31:4.1","40:1.1"]},{"x":"Children who die early, deprived of the experience of mortal life, become Paradise citizens but do not enter the Corps of the Finality.","r":["47:2.8"]},{"q":"E todo mortal, ciente de Deus, almeja ser um finalitor.","r":"14:6.39"}]},{"h":"The Way to Paradise","items":[{"x":"Mortals ascend through the stages of spirit one by one and become spirits of the sixth stage when they take the oath of the Corps of the Finality.","r":["31:3.4"]},{"x":"The seventh jubilee celebrates entrance into the mortal Corps of the Finality and the beginning of eternal service.","r":["27:7.8"]},{"x":"In the finaliter receiving circle, the chief of the Transcendentalers administers the eternity oath of the Trinity.","r":["31:8.4"]},{"q":"Os mortais evolucionários nascem nos planetas do espaço, passam pelos mundos moronciais, ascendem aos universos do espírito, atravessam as esferas de Havona, encontram Deus, alcançam o Paraíso e são integrados ao Corpo primário de Finalidade; e ali aguardam pelo próximo compromisso de serviço no universo.","r":"31:10.20"}]},{"h":"Present Service and Organization","items":[{"x":"Finaliters are not assigned to their native superuniverse until they have served in the other six, and so they gain a sevenfold concept of the Supreme Being.","r":["31:0.10"]},{"q":"Uma ou mais companhias de finalitores mortais estão constantemente a serviço em Urântia.","r":"31:0.11"},{"x":"The finaliters are a self-governing body that chooses its own leaders, and their oath of allegiance is given to the Paradise Trinity alone.","r":["31:0.12"]},{"x":"The first transition world of Satania is the headquarters of more than one hundred thousand finaliter companies, and finaliters remain invisible until true spirit vision is attained.","r":["47:0.2","47:1.3"]},{"x":"The mortal Corps of the Finality serves in various roles on worlds settled in light and life, but it seems to have no settled duties as yet.","r":["30:4.32"]}]},{"h":"A Destiny Not Yet Finished","items":[{"x":"Finaliters have reached the present limits of creature perfection, but not yet the ultimate spirit status or the finality of creature service.","r":["31:3.6"]},{"q":"Why should the Gods be so concerned in so thoroughly training surviving mortals in the technique of universe management?","r":"31:3.8"},{"x":"In the finaliter circle on Jerusem stands a sealed and empty temple inscribed \"Not yet dedicated to the seventh stage of spirit.\"","r":["46:5.32"]},{"x":"Having found the Father, the finaliters may one day have to begin a new search for the superfinite Father.","r":["10:8.7"]}]},{"h":"Prospects Toward Outer Space","items":[{"x":"The seven corps of finality are supervised by the senior Master Architect, and Grandfanda is head of the council of supreme destiny.","r":["31:10.1","31:10.9"]},{"x":"It is conjectured that the finaliters will compensate for the experiential deficiency of the outer universes, which cannot share in the evolution of the Supreme Being.","r":["31:10.11","31:10.13"]},{"q":"Acreditamos que os mortais fusionados com os Ajustadores, junto com os seus companheiros finalitores, estejam destinados a funcionar de alguma maneira na administração dos universos do primeiro nível do espaço exterior.","r":"112:7.17"},{"x":"Even if there were no unrevealed future destiny, the present assignments of the finaliters would fully justify the ascension plan.","r":["30:4.33"]}]}],"see":["Ascensão mortal","Fusão com o Ajustador","Havona","Paraíso","Ser Supremo","Busca da perfeição"]},{"n":72,"t":"Crescimento","en":"Growth","sum":"Growth is the process in which the actual and the potential combine and values are realized in experience; unlike perfect Havona, it is the hallmark of the evolving grand universe and the Supreme Being. Man's spiritual growth proceeds from an awakening to needs to the discernment of meanings and the discovery of values, and it always takes place unconsciously. Man cannot cause growth, but through devotion to supreme values and living faith he can supply its conditions.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Growth","items":[{"q":"A conjunção dos factuais e dos potenciais equivale ao crescimento, à realização dos valores na experiência.","r":"100:3.6"},{"x":"Growth is not mere progress; progress is meaningful, but without growth it is relatively valueless.","r":["100:3.6"]},{"x":"Values are never static, and change that does not enlarge meanings and elevate values is potential evil.","r":["100:3.5"]},{"x":"The supreme value of human life lies in the growth of values, the progress of meanings, and the realization of their cosmic interrelatedness.","r":["100:3.6"]},{"x":"Growth of a part is not the same as maturity of the whole; to traverse the psychic circles, the whole personality must grow harmoniously.","r":["110:6.3"]}]},{"h":"The Growing Universe and the Supreme Being","items":[{"q":"O crescimento é a marca da Deidade experiencial: Havona não cresceu;","r":"116:0.3"},{"x":"Experiential growth implies a creature-Creator partnership, the association of God and man.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"The Supreme Being is first a spirit personality derived from the Trinity and second a God of evolutionary growth.","r":["115:4.2"]},{"x":"The growth of the whole is the sum of the growth of all its parts, and its completion is an act of the Almighty Supreme.","r":["116:6.6"]},{"x":"Creative growth is endless, but along the way moments of satisfying goal attainment become preludes to new adventure.","r":["118:0.10"]}]},{"h":"Stages and Signs of Spiritual Growth","items":[{"q":"Inicialmente o crescimento espiritual é um despertar para as necessidades e, em seguida, um discernimento dos significados e, depois, uma descoberta dos valores.","r":"100:2.2"},{"x":"True spiritual development shows itself in a life motivated by love, activated by unselfish ministry, and dominated by wholehearted worship.","r":["100:2.2"]},{"x":"Spiritual development depends on maintaining a living connection with true spiritual forces and bearing fruit by sharing what one receives with one's fellows.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"Spiritual growth is mutually stimulated by intimate association with other religionists, and love is the soil of that growth.","r":["100:0.2"]},{"x":"Loyal persons are growing persons, and children are lastingly impressed by the loyalties of the adults with whom they live.","r":["100:1.4"]}]},{"h":"Conditions That Favor Growth","items":[{"q":"O homem não pode provocar o crescimento, mas ele pode gerar as condições favoráveis para tanto.","r":"100:3.7"},{"x":"Growth, whether physical, intellectual, or spiritual, is always unconscious; like love, it must grow.","r":["100:3.7","100:1.9"]},{"x":"Habits such as sensitivity to divine values, reflective meditation, worshipful problem solving, and avoidance of selfishness favor growth.","r":["100:1.8"]},{"x":"The innate drive toward growth is most surely fostered by an attitude of wholehearted devotion to supreme values.","r":["100:1.6"]},{"q":"O crescimento espiritual é maior quando todas as pressões externas estão minimizadas.","r":"103:5.11"}]},{"h":"Hindrances to Growth and the Teaching of Jesus","items":[{"q":"Algumas pessoas acham-se ocupadas demais para poderem crescer e, por isso, ficam expostas ao grave perigo da estagnação espiritual.","r":"100:1.2"},{"x":"Jesus taught not the building of character but the growth of character, and he likened the kingdom of heaven to a mustard seed.","r":["140:8.27","151:4.2"]},{"x":"With a carpenter's analogy Jesus taught that the soul is a living growth, and mind and morals are the soil from which its higher expressions spring.","r":["156:5.2"]},{"x":"The true believer should ask whether he is becoming more skillful in showing goodness today than yesterday, this year than last.","r":["156:5.15"]},{"x":"The morontia life forever uproots animal vestiges such as procrastination and evasion, so that growth may continue.","r":["48:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Experiência","Ser Supremo","Alma","Busca da perfeição","Adversidade e provações","Religião pessoal"]},{"n":29,"t":"Criaturas intermediárias","en":"Midwayers","sum":"Midwayers, or midway creatures, are beings native to the planet who exist on a level midway between mortals and angels. On Urantia the primary midwayers came from the corporeal staff of Prince Caligastia, and the secondary midwayers from the unique children of Adamson and Ratta. Many went astray in the rebellion, but the loyal ones, as the United Midwayers, assist the seraphim and keep the memory of the planet; when the age of light and life arrives, they will set out on the Paradise career as ascending sons of God.","sections":[{"h":"Beings Between Man and Angel","items":[{"x":"They are called midway creatures because they function on a level of life between mortals and the angelic orders, and they appear on most inhabited planets and on all decimal planets.","r":["77:0.1","38:9.2"]},{"x":"They are not an accident of evolution but an essential part of a plan foreordained by the universe architects and designed by the Life Carriers.","r":["38:9.5"]},{"x":"They have a threefold classification: ascending sons by origin, virtually permanent citizens in fact, and numbered with the ministering spirits of time in function.","r":["38:9.1"]},{"q":"Midwayers are not men, neither are they angels, but secondary midwayers are, in nature, nearer man than angel","r":"77:8.4"},{"q":"O abismo entre os mundos material e espiritual fica perfeitamente preenchido pela ligação consecutiva feita em série, entre o homem mortal e a intermediária secundária, a intermediária primária, o querubim moroncial, o querubim de fase intermediária e os serafins.","r":"38:9.9"}]},{"h":"Origin of the Primary Midwayers","items":[{"q":"It was immediately discovered that a creature of this order, midway between the mortal and angelic levels, would be of great service in carrying on the affairs of the Prince's headquarters,","r":"77:1.3"},{"x":"Permission was granted to the couples of Prince Caligastia's corporeal staff, and the first fifty were born, followed in time by the original corps of fifty thousand.","r":["77:1.3","77:1.4"]},{"x":"As the intelligence corps of the Prince's administration, they studied the races of the world and helped influence human societies far from headquarters.","r":["77:1.6"]},{"x":"In the planetary rebellion, 40,119 of the original fifty thousand joined the Caligastia secession.","r":["77:7.1"]},{"x":"The loyal primary midwayers entered the service of the Melchizedek receivers, and their leader, the first 1-2-3, stood firm with Van and Amadon on the day of rebellion.","r":["77:1.7","77:9.5"]}]},{"h":"Origin of the Secondary Midwayers","items":[{"x":"The secondary midwayers came from the children of Adamson, eldest son of Adam and Eve, and Ratta, the last pure-line descendant of the Prince's staff.","r":["77:5.1","77:5.5"]},{"x":"Sixteen unique children of Adamson, forming eight couples, each produced a secondary midwayer every seventy days, until they numbered 1,984 in all.","r":["77:6.2","77:6.4"]},{"q":"E esse fenômeno nunca havia sido possível na Terra antes daquela época, e não mais aconteceu desde então.","r":"77:6.2"},{"x":"After Adamson's death the secondary midwayers drifted without organization, and 873 of them who would not follow Michael's rule were interned with the Pentecost adjudication.","r":["77:6.6","77:7.2"]},{"x":"Before Pentecost rebel midwayers could influence the minds of inferior mortals, but since the outpouring of the Spirit of Truth no disloyal spirit can invade the human mind.","r":["77:7.5","77:7.8"]}]},{"h":"The Service of the United Midwayers","items":[{"x":"At present the two orders on Urantia function as one group of 10,992, governed alternately by the senior member of each order.","r":["77:8.1"]},{"x":"They are nonmaterial beings who neither sleep nor reproduce, yet they can enjoy human humor and follow human worship.","r":["77:8.3"]},{"x":"Organized as midway messengers, planetary sentinels, contact personalities, and progress helpers, they serve with the planetary seraphim.","r":["77:8.5","77:8.7","77:8.8"]},{"x":"Secondary midwayers can make physical contact with material things, and many of the literal phenomena ascribed to angels were their work.","r":["77:8.11","77:8.12"]},{"x":"Today their chief task is to be the unrecognized associates of the men and women who make up the reserve corps of destiny.","r":["77:8.13"]},{"q":"A sua determinação é sugerida no lema da sua ordem: “Tudo o que as Criaturas Intermediárias Unidas querem fazer, as Criaturas Intermediárias Unidas o fazem”.","r":"77:9.3"}]},{"h":"Permanent Citizens of the Planet and Their Destiny","items":[{"q":"The seraphim come and go, but the midway creatures remain","r":"77:9.2"},{"x":"They have pledged not to leave the planet until released by the universe authorities, and they remain on the planet until the age of light and life.","r":["77:9.4"]},{"q":"As gerações de homens esquecem; o corpo das criaturas intermediárias relembra; e tal memória é a sede do tesouro das tradições do vosso mundo habitado.","r":"77:9.9"},{"x":"Urantia civilization is the joint product of mortals and midwayers, and the gap between the two cultural levels will not be bridged before the age of light and life.","r":["77:9.8"]},{"x":"When the planet reaches light and life, both groups are released from planetary service, enrolled as ascending sons of God, and begin the Paradise ascent with their earthly brethren.","r":["40:3.1","38:9.13"]},{"x":"All the secondary midwayers eventually fuse with Adjusters and are mustered into the mortal Corps of the Finality.","r":["31:6.2"]}]}],"see":["Caligástia","Adão e Eva","Rebelião de Lúcifer","Serafins","Urântia","Luz e vida"]},{"n":7,"t":"Deus, o Sétuplo","en":"God the Sevenfold","sum":"Deus, o Sétuplo, é a associação sétupla de Deidade providenciada pelo Pai Universal para que as criaturas finitas possam aproximar-se da Deidade. Ela se estende desde o Filho Criador do universo local, passando pelos Anciães dos Dias, pelos Sete Espíritos Mestres, pelo Ser Supremo, pelo Espírito Infinito e pelo Filho Eterno, até o Pai Universal, e os mortais ascendentes descobrem a Deidade experiencialmente nessa ordem. Os seus três primeiros níveis são também a fonte do poder todo-poderoso do Ser Supremo.","sections":[{"h":"Sete degraus em direção à Deidade","items":[{"x":"Para compensar as limitações da condição e do conceito finitos, o Pai Universal estabeleceu a aproximação sétupla das criaturas evolucionárias à Deidade.","r":["0:8.1"]},{"x":"Os sete níveis são os Filhos Criadores do Paraíso, os Anciães dos Dias, os Sete Espíritos Mestres, o Ser Supremo, Deus, o Espírito, Deus, o Filho, e Deus, o Pai.","r":["0:8.2","0:8.8"]},{"q":"Deus, o Sétuplo, significa o reconhecimento, da parte da Deidade do Paraíso, das barreiras do tempo nos universos evolucionários do espaço.","r":"106:1.3"},{"x":"A carreira experiencial de encontrar Deus começa com o reconhecimento da divindade do Filho Criador do universo local e prossegue, por meio dos Anciães dos Dias e dos Espíritos Mestres, até o Pai do Paraíso.","r":["0:8.9"]},{"x":"Deus, o Sétuplo, é a Deidade que atua de fato para os mortais evolucionários na carreira de ascensão ao Paraíso.","r":["0:8.9"]}]},{"h":"Supremos Criadores e Deidades do Paraíso","items":[{"x":"Dos sete níveis, os três primeiros são os Supremos Criadores e os três últimos as Deidades do Paraíso, com o Ser Supremo sempre interposto entre eles.","r":["116:2.4","116:2.12"]},{"x":"A Deidade do Paraíso atenuou e qualificou a personalização da divindade fora do Paraíso para trazer à existência os Supremos Criadores, e estes levam a luz da vida aos mundos evolucionários.","r":["116:2.3"]},{"x":"Os atos combinados dos três primeiros níveis não equivalem à Deidade do Paraíso; eles constituem um novo potencial de poder de Deidade experiencial.","r":["116:2.13"]},{"q":"Os Filhos Criadores, na associação de Deidade, que é Deus, o Sétuplo, proporcionam o mecanismo pelo qual o mortal se torna imortal e pelo qual o finito encontra o amplexo da infinitude.","r":"0:8.11"},{"x":"A ministração de divindade do Sétuplo alcança, para dentro, por meio do Filho Eterno, o Pai do Paraíso e, para fora, por meio dos Anciães dos Dias, os Filhos Criadores.","r":["106:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Relação com o Ser Supremo","items":[{"x":"Deus, o Supremo, deriva da Trindade os Seus atributos de personalidade e de espírito, mas o Seu poder é factualizado nas ações dos Filhos Criadores, dos Anciães dos Dias e dos Espíritos Mestres.","r":["0:8.10","116:2.2"]},{"x":"Deus, o Supremo, manifesta-Se às criaturas evolucionárias como uma personalidade de poder somente quando os três primeiros níveis de Deus, o Sétuplo, atuam de modo coordenado.","r":["116:2.14"]},{"q":"O Ser Supremo é a revelação máxima da Deidade para os sete superuniversos e para a presente idade do universo.","r":"116:2.12"},{"x":"Na experiência mortal, o Ser Supremo é o unificador de Deus, o Sétuplo, o máximo de Deidade que as criaturas finitas podem compreender de fato.","r":["56:8.1"]},{"x":"Os vários aspectos da Deidade sétupla estão agora integrados de diversas maneiras, mas todos estão destinados a unificar-se na Supremacia.","r":["106:1.4"]}]},{"h":"Os controladores sétuplos e a função cósmica","items":[{"x":"Deus, o Sétuplo, inclui não apenas os criadores, mas também os controladores sétuplos do grande universo, como os Mestres Controladores Físicos, os Centros Supremos de Potência e os Diretores Supremos de Potência.","r":["116:5.1","116:5.9"]},{"x":"O conselho dos Sete Espíritos Mestres parece coordenar as vastas atividades de Deus, o Sétuplo, e contribui também para o último nível, a união do Filho Criador com o Espírito Criativo.","r":["17:8.3","17:8.8"]},{"q":"A função de Deus, o Sétuplo, data da organização dos sete superuniversos e, provavelmente, ampliar-se-á junto com a evolução futura das criações do espaço exterior.","r":"0:8.12"},{"q":"Os Absolutos são coordenados no Último, condicionados no Supremo, e modificados, no tempo-espaço, em Deus, o Sétuplo.","r":"56:9.1"},{"x":"Por meio da ministração de Deus, o Sétuplo, o imperfeito liga-se ao perfeito no intervalo do tempo, e a criatura torna-se parceira do Criador na sua própria evolução.","r":["106:1.2"]},{"x":"O poder que surge das realizações de Deus, o Sétuplo, é um poder experiencial, conquistado e demonstrado, em contraste com o poder existencial das Deidades do Paraíso.","r":["106:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Revelação em luz e vida","items":[{"x":"A evolução do tempo e do espaço começa em planetas presididos pela união do Filho Criador com o Espírito Criativo, a primeira manifestação de Deus, o Sétuplo, e, à medida que um universo local se estabelece, Deus, o Sétuplo, é revelado com mais clareza.","r":["56:7.2"]},{"x":"À medida que as criações se estabelecem, as três primeiras manifestações retiram-se e aparece uma atividade mais plena de Deus, o Supremo, mas o que vem depois ainda não foi revelado.","r":["56:7.6"]},{"q":"Contudo, sabemos que nos universos do tempo e do espaço, Deus, o Sétuplo, provê uma aproximação progressiva ao Pai Universal e que essa aproximação evolucionária é experiencialmente unificada em Deus, o Supremo.","r":"56:7.8"},{"x":"Os mundos de luz e vida apreendem sucessivamente a realidade de Deus, o Sétuplo, desde a adoração do Filho Criador até a adoração do Pai do Paraíso.","r":["56:10.1"]},{"x":"Qualquer que seja o nível de Deidade alcançado, o ascendente redescobre a cada vez, em um novo nível de experiência, o Pai do Paraíso de todas as personalidades.","r":["56:9.10"]}]}],"see":["Ser Supremo","Filho Criador Michael","Anciães dos Dias","Sete Espíritos Mestres","Trindade do Paraíso","Ascensão mortal"]},{"n":9,"t":"Deus, o Último","en":"God the Ultimate","sum":"Deus, o Último, é a segunda Deidade experiencial, que se manifesta depois do Ser Supremo; é uma personalidade-poder transcendental que atua no nível absonito, o qual transcende o tempo e o espaço do universo-mestre. Ele se manifesta a partir da unificação da Trindade Última, que será composta pelos Supremos Criadores, pelo Ser Supremo e pelos Arquitetos do Universo-Mestre, e a Sua plena emergência significa a conclusão da criação do universo-mestre. Ele é o objeto da busca seguinte dos finalitores e dos cidadãos aperfeiçoados, uma vez que o grande universo esteja estabelecido em luz e vida.","sections":[{"h":"Deidade do nível absonito","items":[{"q":"Deus, o Último — o Deus em processamento corrente, do supratempo e do espaço transcendido.","r":"0:2.17"},{"x":"As realidades absonitas são coisas e seres que se manifestam, em vez de serem criados, sem começo nem fim e transcendendo o tempo e o espaço, e a função da Deidade em relação a elas é a Ultimidade.","r":["0:1.12"]},{"q":"O Supremo é a unificação da Trindade, segundo é compreendida pelos seres finitos; o Último é a unificação da Trindade do Paraíso, segundo é compreendida pelos seres absonitos.","r":"0:9.2"},{"x":"Entre as sete naturezas da Deidade, a Supremacia é o eu evolucionário-experiencial e a Ultimidade, o eu transcendental-experiencial.","r":["118:0.5","118:0.7"]},{"x":"Deus, o Último, transcende o tempo e o espaço e é capaz de associar-Se funcionalmente aos Absolutos, mas Ele é absonito.","r":["106:4.4"]}]},{"h":"Supremacia e Ultimidade","items":[{"q":"Do mesmo modo que Deus, o Sétuplo, é indispensável à realização evolucionária do Supremo, o Supremo também é indispensável à emergência final do Último.","r":"118:0.9"},{"x":"O Supremo e o Último complementam-se na realização do destino, formando a ponte experiencial que liga os começos e as conclusões de todo crescimento criativo no universo-mestre.","r":["118:0.9"]},{"x":"A Ultimidade e a Supremacia são comparáveis, mas não idênticas, e a Ultimidade não é apenas uma ampliação da Supremacia.","r":["106:8.15"]},{"x":"Assim como o Ser Supremo evolui a partir dos potenciais do grande universo, Deus, o Último, manifesta-Se a partir dos potenciais de divindade dos domínios do universo-mestre que transcendem o tempo e o espaço.","r":["0:9.1"]},{"x":"Quando Deus, o Supremo, vier a governar diretamente os universos do tempo e do espaço, essa administração funcionará sob o supracontrole da Ultimidade, e Deus, o Último, começará a aparecer como o Todo-Poderoso transcendental.","r":["118:2.4"]}]},{"h":"A Trindade Última","items":[{"x":"A Trindade Última é a associação de Deidade dos Supremos Criadores, de Deus, o Supremo, e dos Arquitetos do Universo-Mestre, e está agora em evolução.","r":["0:12.6","106:8.10"]},{"q":"Deus, o Último, final e inevitavelmente, adquirirá poder e personalizar-se-á como a Deidade-conseqüência da unificação desta Trindade Última experiencial, na arena em expansão do universo-mestre quase ilimitado.","r":"0:12.6"},{"x":"Quando a presente idade do universo terminar e o Supremo Todo-Poderoso emergir, a primeira Trindade experiencial funcionará plenamente e integrará ainda mais a evolução da criação-mestra.","r":["106:3.2"]},{"x":"Essa Trindade inclui os Filhos Criadores Mestres, de modo que a experiência factual das criaturas fica abrangida na sua associação.","r":["106:3.3"]},{"q":"A realização completa do Último implica o completar da criação do universo-mestre e denota a emergência plena dessa Deidade transcendental.","r":"106:4.2"},{"x":"A unificação do universo-mestre é o ato de manifestação do Último e, acredita-se, reflete alguma fase do supracontrole absonito da Trindade do Paraíso.","r":["10:8.2"]}]},{"h":"A Ultimidade revelada agora","items":[{"x":"Assim como o Supremo está espiritual e pessoalmente presente em Havona, a Ultimidade existe ali em um sentido absonito e suprapessoal.","r":["106:4.3"]},{"x":"Sabe-se que os Vice-Regentes Qualificáveis do Último já existem, mas a sua localização e a sua função atuais não foram reveladas.","r":["106:4.3","117:7.4"]},{"x":"Deus, o Último, prenuncia o Seu supracontrole transcendental nos estágios mais avançados dos universos locais estabelecidos em luz e vida.","r":["56:7.5"]},{"x":"Os mortais que alcançam o sétimo estágio de luz e vida, ao mesmo tempo em que chegam a conhecer Deus, o Supremo, discernem vagamente a ministração onipresente de Deus, o Último.","r":["56:10.1"]},{"x":"A “manifestação da capacidade do universo”, que transforma o potencial indiferenciado em planos definidos de universo, é a atividade da Ultimidade e das agências transcendentais.","r":["118:4.6"]}]},{"h":"A próxima meta dos finalitores","items":[{"x":"Os ascendentes encontram Deus, o Supremo, em Havona e, depois de se tornarem finalitores, procuram conhecê-Lo como Ultimidade.","r":["118:2.2"]},{"x":"Quando a verdade, a beleza e a bondade do Ser Supremo os tiverem permeado plenamente, as qualidades absonitas da divindade última, além desse nível conceitual, abrir-se-ão diante das criaturas em progresso.","r":["115:3.19"]},{"x":"Deus, o Último, existe para oferecer um destino de serviço último a todas as criaturas que alcançam os níveis absonitos por meio da ministração de Deus, o Sétuplo.","r":["0:9.1"]},{"q":"Certa, segura e inexoravelmente, o enigma da Deidade emergente de Deus, o Último, desafiará os cidadãos perfeccionados dos universos estabelecidos, exatamente como os seus antepassados de luta evolucionária, certa vez, foram desafiados pela busca de Deus, o Supremo.","r":"117:7.17"},{"x":"Para os finalitores que alcançaram a Ultimidade, o caminho que resta é a busca do Absoluto, e eles sabem que, no fim desse caminho, encontrarão o mesmo Pai do Paraíso.","r":["118:2.2"]},{"x":"Deus, o Supremo, e Deus, o Último, são Deidades eternas somente no futuro e não no passado: têm um começo de personalidade, mas não um fim.","r":["0:9.5"]}]}],"see":["Ser Supremo","Trindade do Paraíso","Os três Absolutos","Corpo de Finalidade","Grande universo e universo-mestre","Luz e vida"]},{"n":89,"t":"Os doze apóstolos","en":"Twelve Apostles","sum":"The twelve apostles were ordinary Galileans whom Jesus personally called, trained, and ordained to proclaim the gospel of the kingdom of heaven. They were not ignorant men but men of varied temperaments who had received synagogue schooling, and each, with his own strengths and weaknesses, was transformed by living with Jesus. That only one of them deserted him, even though Jesus repeatedly shattered their worldly expectations, testifies to the charm of his life.","sections":[{"h":"Calling and Training","items":[{"x":"Jesus chose the first six himself, and each of them recommended one more, making twelve.","r":["139:6.1","138:5.1"]},{"x":"The first six apostles went out two by two, preaching the gospel by personal contact, and learned that religion is a purely personal experience.","r":["138:1.1","138:2.1"]},{"x":"The monotonous period of alternating fishing and personal work was a severe test, but they endured it through loyalty to the Master.","r":["138:9.1"]},{"x":"On January 12, A.D. 27, Jesus ordained the twelve as public preachers of the gospel of the kingdom.","r":["140:0.1"]},{"x":"The so-called Sermon on the Mount was not the gospel itself but Jesus' ordination charge to the twelve.","r":["140:4.1"]}]},{"h":"Ordinary and Diverse Men","items":[{"q":"Não cometais o erro de tomar os apóstolos como sendo de todo ignorantes e pouco instruídos.","r":"139:0.3"},{"x":"\"Unlearned\" means they were laymen untrained in rabbinical lore and methods of scriptural interpretation.","r":["139:0.4"]},{"x":"The apostles learned about the kingdom of heaven from Jesus, and Jesus learned much about human nature from them.","r":["139:0.2"]},{"x":"All the apostles loved Jesus, but each was drawn by some trait of his character that especially appealed to him.","r":["139:1.11"]}]},{"h":"The Four Chief Apostles","items":[{"x":"Andrew, the eldest, became chief of the apostolic corps and held that place to the end; not a great preacher, he was an effective personal worker.","r":["139:1.2","139:1.3","139:1.4"]},{"x":"Peter was impulsive and optimistic, a born leader and eloquent speaker, but his speech often ran ahead of his thinking.","r":["139:2.3","139:2.4"]},{"x":"James Zebedee had a fierce temper, but his ability to see a problem from many sides brought him closest to the real meaning of Jesus' teaching.","r":["139:3.2","139:3.4"]},{"x":"John, the youngest, served as Jesus' personal representative in many matters, but the phrase \"the disciple whom Jesus loved\" is not accurate.","r":["139:4.2","139:4.4"]},{"x":"Peter, James, and John were appointed by Andrew as personal aides to attend to Jesus at his side.","r":["139:4.3"]},{"q":"Andrew was a man of clear insight, logical thought, and firm decision","r":"139:1.10"}]},{"h":"The Other Apostles","items":[{"x":"Philip, with his \"show me,\" lacked imagination but was a faithful steward who did small things in a great way.","r":["139:5.2","139:5.3","139:5.4"]},{"x":"Nathaniel was an honest man \"in whom there is no guile\" and the philosopher of the twelve; his weakness was a pride that verged on prejudice.","r":["139:6.3","139:6.4"]},{"x":"Matthew, the former publican, handled the finances of the group and was most deeply grateful for the Master's forgiving nature.","r":["139:7.2","139:7.4"]},{"x":"Thomas was the real scientist of the group, with an analytic mind and unflinching courage, but he struggled with doubt all his life.","r":["139:8.2","139:8.4"]},{"x":"The Alpheus twins were ordinary men with neither strong nor weak points, yet through them many timid believers entered the kingdom.","r":["139:9.4","139:9.5"]},{"x":"Simon Zelotes led the hesitant into the kingdom by his inspiring loyalty, but he never fully shed his nationalistic thinking.","r":["139:11.3","139:11.4"]},{"q":"Eles eram “os menores entre os apóstolos”; eles sabiam disso e sentiam-se bem com isso.","r":"139:9.5"}]},{"h":"Judas Iscariot","items":[{"x":"Judas was the only Judean among the apostles and the best educated; he handled the treasury honestly and efficiently.","r":["139:12.2","139:12.3"]},{"q":"Judas realmente não queria entender a si próprio; ele não era realmente sincero ao lidar consigo mesmo.","r":"139:12.2"},{"x":"He never overcame his prejudice against his Galilean associates and inwardly criticized Jesus as timid.","r":["139:12.4"]},{"q":"Jesus olhou para o traidor apenas com piedade.","r":"139:12.14"}]},{"h":"Ambassadors of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"Jesus told the apostles that, as citizens of another, heavenly kingdom, they must now live better lives than before.","r":["140:3.1"]},{"x":"He taught the apostles at length not so much what they should do as what they should be.","r":["140:10.1"]},{"q":"UM TESTEMUNHO eloqüente do encanto e da retidão da vida de Jesus na Terra é que apenas um dos seus apóstolos o tenha deserdado, embora repetidamente houvesse ele reduzido a pedaços e rasgado em trapos as esperanças e a ambição que os seus apóstolos alimentavam de exaltação pessoal.","r":"139:0.1"}]}],"see":["Ensinamentos de Jesus","Caráter de Jesus","Pentecostes","Ressurreição de Jesus","Morte na cruz","Reino do céu"]},{"n":17,"t":"Energia e matéria","en":"Energy and Matter","sum":"A energia é a base de toda existência, uma realidade eterna, mas não infinita, que sai do Paraíso e retorna ao Paraíso. Desde a potência do espaço, passando pela força primordial e pela energia emergente, até a potência do universo e a matéria, ela é transmutada pelos organizadores da força e pelos diretores de potência, e a luz, o calor, a eletricidade e a matéria são uma só coisa na origem e no destino. Contudo, o universo não é mecânico; situa-se dentro de uma ordem na qual a mente domina a matéria e o espírito governa a mente.","sections":[{"h":"A energia que vem do Paraíso","items":[{"x":"A energia é a base de toda existência, e a energia pura é controlada pelo Pai Universal; o fluxo de energia que sai do Paraíso nunca cessou.","r":["42:0.1"]},{"q":"A base do universo é material, mas a essência da vida é espírito.","r":"42:1.1"},{"x":"Considerado nos fenômenos não espirituais, Deus é energia, e toda energia física procede Dele.","r":["3:2.3"]},{"x":"A criação da energia e a outorga da vida são prerrogativas do Pai e das Suas personalidades criadoras; por mais avançado que seja, um cientista nunca poderá criar um átomo nem acrescentar vida à matéria.","r":["42:1.4","42:1.5"]},{"q":"Energy is eternal but not infinite","r":"42:1.8"},{"x":"A força-energia é imperecível e indestrutível; pode ser transmutada sem fim, mas nunca aniquilada.","r":["42:1.7"]}]},{"h":"Os estágios da transmutação","items":[{"x":"A potência do espaço (absoluta) é a presença espacial livre do Absoluto Inqualificável, que responde somente à ação pessoal do Pai Universal.","r":["42:2.3","42:2.5"]},{"x":"Os organizadores da força do Paraíso transformam a potência do espaço em força primordial (segregata) e transmutam-na depois em energia potente e em energia gravitacional (ultimata).","r":["42:2.7","42:2.10","42:2.13"]},{"x":"Quando a energia chega ao estágio de resposta à gravidade do Paraíso, os diretores de potência assumem e manipulam a potência do universo (gravita).","r":["42:2.12","42:2.14"]},{"x":"A energia de Havona não é dual, mas trina (triata), e a energia do Paraíso, a monota, distingue-se do espírito do Paraíso apenas pelo nome.","r":["42:2.16","42:2.19","42:2.20"]},{"x":"A força cósmica, a energia emergente e a potência do universo distinguem-se pelo modo como respondem à gravidade do Paraíso e à gravidade linear.","r":["0:6.5","0:6.6","0:6.7"]}]},{"h":"A estrutura da matéria","items":[{"q":"A luz, o calor, a eletricidade, o magnetismo, a química, a energia e a matéria são — em origem, natureza e destino — uma única e mesma coisa, junto com outras realidades materiais ainda não descobertas em Urântia.","r":"42:4.1"},{"x":"A unidade primária da existência material é o ultímatom, e exatamente cem ultímatons constituem um elétron.","r":["42:3.3","42:6.5"]},{"x":"O universo local tem uma estrutura decimal, de modo que os átomos existem em apenas cem formas, com de um a cem elétrons orbitais.","r":["42:7.4"]},{"x":"O núcleo atômico é mantido coeso pelo mésotron, cento e oitenta vezes mais pesado que o elétron, que transporta cargas entre prótons e nêutrons.","r":["42:8.3","42:8.4"]},{"x":"O espaço não é vazio; mesmo o espaço mais vazio conhecido em Nébadon contém cerca de cem ultímatons por polegada cúbica.","r":["42:4.6"]},{"x":"A recorrência das propriedades dos elementos de sete em sete é uma marca de nascença da sua origem espiritual sétupla, deixada no mundo material.","r":["42:9.2","42:9.3"]}]},{"h":"O circuito e o equilíbrio da energia","items":[{"x":"Embora passe pelas transmutações do tempo, a matéria oscila sempre no circuito da eternidade, sempre sensível à fonte da qual saiu.","r":["42:4.2"]},{"x":"Os sóis ardentes transformam a matéria em energia, ao passo que o espaço frio e os mundos escuros desaceleram a energia, convertendo-a de novo em matéria.","r":["42:4.9"]},{"x":"A integridade da matéria é assegurada pelo fato de a energia ser absorvida ou emitida somente em unidades quânticas.","r":["42:4.13"]},{"x":"Não há éter; a luz e a energia são correntes de partículas que viajam em linha reta e só parecem ondulatórias por causa da resistência do espaço.","r":["42:5.14","42:5.16"]},{"q":"A energia física é a única realidade verdadeira e fiel, na sua obediência à lei universal.","r":"12:8.3"},{"x":"Os diretores de potência e os organizadores da força, que são seres vivos, dirigem inteligentemente as metamorfoses sem fim da formação, da desagregação e da reformação dos universos.","r":["15:8.10"]}]},{"h":"A mente e o mecanismo do universo","items":[{"x":"O universo não é mecânico nem mágico; é uma criação da mente e um mecanismo da lei.","r":["42:11.1"]},{"x":"O universo dos universos é planejado, feito e administrado pela mente, mas o seu mecanismo é tão perfeito que os métodos da ciência não conseguem discernir o rastro da mente infinita.","r":["42:11.2"]},{"x":"As energias não espirituais reúnem-se novamente em sistemas vivos de mente, como a mente espiritual pré-ajudante, a mente dos espíritos ajudantes, a mente moroncial e a mente cósmica.","r":["42:10.2","42:10.6"]},{"q":"A mente é sempre criativa.","r":"42:12.9"},{"q":"O espírito é o arquiteto, a mente é o construtor, o corpo é a edificação material.","r":"42:12.12"},{"x":"A mente domina a matéria e responde ao supracontrole do espírito, e somente a mente que segue livremente a condução do espírito pode sobreviver além da existência mortal.","r":["42:12.15"]},{"x":"No Paraíso, as energias física, mental e espiritual são coordenadas entre si; em Havona, estão coordenadas; e nos níveis absolutos o espírito é claramente dominante.","r":["42:12.13"]}]}],"see":["Gravidade","Paraíso","Mente cósmica","Os três Absolutos","Tempo e espaço","Realidade"]},{"n":86,"t":"Ensinamentos de Jesus","en":"Teachings of Jesus","sum":"The teachings of Jesus are rooted in the simple gospel that God is the Father of all men and that men, recognizing by faith that they are his sons, become brothers to one another. The kingdom of heaven is not a political realm but a spiritual experience that begins within each person, and faith opens its door. Jesus gave the new commandment to love not merely as one loves oneself but as he loved, and he called people out of the religion of tradition and authority into the religion of the spirit that knows God directly.","sections":[{"h":"The Heart of the Gospel","items":[{"q":"“Deus é o vosso Pai; e a religião — meu evangelho — nada mais é, nem nada menos, do que o reconhecimento crente da verdade de que vós sois os filhos Dele.","r":"141:4.2"},{"x":"Jesus taught a new concept of God, not as a judge keeping a ledger of sins but as a Father who loves each person.","r":["141:4.1"]},{"x":"The kingdom of heaven is built on the truths of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man, and this teaching frees man from age-old animal fears.","r":["170:2.1","170:2.2"]},{"x":"Jesus said that people of other ages would better understand the gospel if it were presented in terms of family relationships rather than of a kingdom.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"His gospel delivered man from the superstition that he is a child of the devil and lifted him to the dignity of a faith son of God.","r":["194:2.1"]}]},{"h":"The Kingdom of Heaven","items":[{"x":"Jesus said the kingdom of heaven had nothing to do with earthly kingdoms or temporal governments, but the idea of a temporal king rooted deep in the Jewish mind was not easily removed.","r":["170:0.1"]},{"q":"A respeito do Reino, a sua última palavra foi: “o Reino está dentro de vós”.","r":"170:1.13"},{"x":"Simple, childlike faith is the key that opens the door of the kingdom; once inside, one must grow through the steps of righteousness.","r":["170:3.2"]},{"x":"God's forgiveness is actually experienced in the measure that a person forgives his fellows.","r":["170:3.3","170:3.4"]},{"x":"The kingdom is an evolutionary experience that begins on earth and advances through successive stages of life to Paradise.","r":["142:7.3"]}]},{"h":"Love and the New Commandment","items":[{"x":"Brotherly love is loving one's neighbor as oneself, but fatherly love is loving people as Jesus loved them.","r":["140:5.1"]},{"x":"Disciples should strive to see people as God sees them and so begin to show fatherly affection.","r":["140:5.3"]},{"q":"Amai uns aos outros como eu vos amei.","r":"180:1.1"},{"x":"The new commandment is not a new burden but meant to bring the new joy of sharing affection with one's fellows.","r":["180:1.2"]},{"x":"\"Resist not evil\" did not mean condoning sin but forgiving rather than retaliating against personal insults.","r":["141:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Religion of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"Jesus said not to patch new teaching onto the old but to be born again like little children and make a fresh start.","r":["140:6.2"]},{"x":"The righteousness he required is not buying favor through alms, prayer, and fasting, but the desire to do the Father's will in love, mercy, and truth.","r":["140:6.3"]},{"x":"The greatest discovery a human soul can make is to find God within and to make that a fact of personal experience.","r":["155:6.3"]},{"q":"The religion of the mind ties you hopelessly to the past; the religion of the spirit consists in progressive revelation","r":"155:6.4"},{"x":"Jesus did not teach that all should think alike; believers are united in their diversity by the motive and goal of doing the Father's will.","r":["141:5.1","141:5.3"]},{"q":"Eu vim ao mundo para proclamar a liberdade espiritual, com o fito de que os mortais pudessem ter o poder de viver vidas individuais de originalidade e de liberdade, diante de Deus.","r":"141:5.1"}]},{"h":"Ways of Spreading the Teaching","items":[{"x":"Always respect human personality, and never sweep people into the kingdom by overpowering them with logic, eloquence, fear, or sentiment.","r":["159:3.2"]},{"x":"The gospel restores self-respect to those who have lost it and restrains those who have too much.","r":["159:3.3"]},{"x":"The teaching to trust God is not passive fatalism; what Jesus opposed was not forethought but worry and anxiety.","r":["140:8.2","140:8.3"]},{"x":"His teaching was not the talk of a meek mystic but dynamic; he not only meant well but actually did good.","r":["141:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Religion of Jesus","items":[{"q":"Vós podeis pregar uma religião sobre Jesus, mas, por força, vós deveis viver a religião de Jesus.","r":"196:2.1"},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom rests on Jesus' own religious experience, while Christianity rests mainly on Paul's.","r":["196:2.1"]},{"x":"As the Messiah of the kingdom became the Redeemer of the church, Jesus' teachings were transplanted from Jewish to gentile soil.","r":["170:5.3"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth restates Jesus' message anew for each generation, helping it remember and understand his teachings.","r":["194:2.1","194:2.5"]}]}],"see":["Reino do céu","Filiação a Deus","Irmandade dos homens","Parábolas","Caráter de Jesus","Fé"]},{"n":39,"t":"Espírito da Verdade","en":"Spirit of Truth","sum":"The Spirit of Truth is the Creator Son's own spirit, the Comforter, which he pours out upon all flesh after completing his bestowal career. On Urantia it was poured out at Pentecost as the spirit of Michael, preparing every normal mind to receive an Adjuster. This spirit teaches truth not as law or creed but as living conviction; it creates consciousness not of itself but of Michael, and it shows forth anew the life of Jesus in the lives of believers.","sections":[{"h":"The Bestowal Spirit of the Creator Son","items":[{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the first is the bestowal spirit of the Creator Son, the Spirit of Truth, the Comforter.","r":["34:4.2","15:9.12"]},{"q":"Esse Confortador outorgado é a força espiritual que sempre atrai todos os buscadores da verdade para Ele, que é a personificação da verdade no universo local.","r":"34:4.5"},{"x":"This spirit proceeds from the personality of the Son but is functionally focalized in the Divine Minister, so it works without hindrance wherever the Son may be.","r":["34:4.6","34:4.7"]},{"x":"In a sense the Spirit of Truth is the spirit of both the Universal Father and the Creator Son, and it is commonly regarded as the spirit of the Universe Son.","r":["194:2.3","194:2.16"]},{"x":"On Avonal bestowal worlds it comes as the joint spirit of the bestowal Avonal and the Creator Son, but after Michael's final bestowal it becomes more literally the spirit of Michael.","r":["52:5.6","20:6.8","20:6.9"]}]},{"h":"The Promise and Pentecost","items":[{"x":"Before departing, Jesus promised that, if the Father permitted, he would pour out the Spirit of Truth upon all flesh and send it as another teacher.","r":["180:4.1","180:4.2"]},{"q":"Dentro de pouco tempo eu enviarei a vós o meu espírito, que é exatamente como eu, exceto por esse corpo material.","r":"180:4.5"},{"x":"Not only the one hundred and twenty in the upper chamber but every honest person in the world received this teacher according to his love of truth and his capacity for spiritual understanding.","r":["194:3.6"]},{"x":"The bestowal of the spirit was independent of forms, ceremonies, and sacred places; prayer did not bring the spirit, but it determined the capacity of the vessel that received it.","r":["194:3.10","194:3.20"]},{"x":"At that time the \"baptism of the spirit\" meant only the conscious reception and recognition of the gift of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["194:2.10"]},{"q":"since Pentecost, man is still searching for God, but there shines out over the world the spectacle of God also seeking for man and sending his spirit to dwell within him when he has found him.","r":"194:3.13"}]},{"h":"The Work of the Spirit of Truth","items":[{"q":"A primeira missão desse espírito é, está claro, fomentar e personalizar a verdade, pois é a compreensão da verdade que constitui a mais elevada forma de liberdade humana.","r":"194:2.2"},{"x":"It also destroys the believer's feeling of orphanhood and helps him remember and understand the Master's words and reinterpret his life on earth.","r":["194:2.2","194:2.5"]},{"x":"Living within men, the Spirit of Truth restates the message of Jesus for each new generation in terms suited to its time.","r":["194:2.1"]},{"x":"This spirit teaches the truths of the Father's love and the Son's mercy, revealing the Father's spirit nature and the Son's moral character.","r":["194:3.1"]},{"q":"O Filho Criador, quando esteve encarnado, revelou Deus aos homens; o Espírito da Verdade, no coração, revela o Filho Criador aos homens.","r":"194:3.1"},{"x":"This spirit creates no consciousness of itself, only consciousness of Michael, so its evidence is found in deepening communion with Michael.","r":["194:2.4"]}]},{"h":"Living Truth","items":[{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is not the letter or the law of truth but the conviction of its true meaning on spirit levels, a spirit that grows and unfolds of itself.","r":["180:5.1"]},{"q":"Verdade estática é verdade morta, e apenas a verdade morta pode ser mantida como uma teoria.","r":"180:5.2"},{"x":"Without the insight of the Spirit of Truth the golden rule is only a rule of ethics; its true meaning appears when the spirit of the Son interprets the law of conduct to the spirit of the Father.","r":["180:5.5","180:5.8"]},{"x":"Love must pass through ever-new interpretations, readjusting itself under the guidance of the Spirit of Truth toward the highest good of the one loved.","r":["180:5.10"]},{"x":"The bestowed Spirit of Truth responds unerringly to truth, the living relationship in which all beings are attuned toward God.","r":["56:10.13","2:7.6"]}]},{"h":"Preparation and Guidance for the Adjuster","items":[{"x":"Until a bestowal Son releases the Spirit of Truth, not every normal mind is automatically prepared to receive an Adjuster.","r":["34:5.4","20:5.3","194:2.3"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is poured out upon all flesh, but its function and power depend almost entirely on the degree to which a person personally receives it.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"x":"Spiritual philosophy, the wisdom of spirit realities, is the endowment of the Spirit of Truth given by the bestowal Sons.","r":["101:3.2"]},{"x":"Even when the ascender leaves his local universe, he is not wholly beyond the ministry of the Spirit of Truth, which points the way in every crisis of the ascent.","r":["117:5.9"]},{"q":"for in every dark hour, at every crossroad in the forward struggle, the Spirit of Truth will always speak, saying, \"This is the way.\"","r":"34:7.8"}]}],"see":["Filho Criador Michael","Pentecostes","Espírito Santo","Verdade","Auto-outorga de Jesus","Ajustador do Pensamento"]},{"n":5,"t":"Espírito Infinito","en":"Infinite Spirit","sum":"O Espírito Infinito é a terceira pessoa da Deidade, o Agente Conjunto e Criador Conjunto, que veio à existência no momento em que o Pai e o Filho conceberam uma ação conjunta. Como executivo da parceria entre o Pai e o Filho, Ele é a fonte da mente, o manipulador da energia e o espírito onipresente que concede a todas as criaturas o amor do Pai e a misericórdia do Filho. Os Seus muitos filhos espirituais formam a escada viva pela qual os mortais sobem ao Paraíso.","sections":[{"h":"O Deus da Ação","items":[{"x":"No exato momento em que o Pai e o Filho conceberam juntos uma ação infinita, a execução de um plano-pensamento absoluto, o Espírito Infinito surgiu em existência completa.","r":["8:0.3"]},{"x":"Essa ordem de origem é apenas uma explicação para ajudar a compreensão humana; os três existem desde a eternidade, sem começo nem fim.","r":["8:0.4"]},{"x":"O Espírito Infinito prometeu lealdade eterna ao Pai e reconheceu a Sua dependência eterna do Filho, e assim veio à existência a Trindade do Paraíso.","r":["8:1.2","8:1.3"]},{"x":"O Espírito Infinito tornou-Se eternizado com o nascimento do universo central de Havona e, por esse ato criador conjunto, tornou-Se o eterno Criador Conjunto.","r":["8:1.7"]},{"q":"Em suma, o Espírito Infinito atesta que, sendo Ele eterno, assim também o universo central é eterno.","r":"8:1.9"}]},{"h":"Natureza e posição","items":[{"x":"Ele é conhecido por muitos nomes, entre eles o Espírito Universal, o Criador Conjunto, a Mente Infinita, o Espírito dos Espíritos e o Agente Conjunto, e em Urântia é às vezes confundido com a mente cósmica.","r":["8:2.2"]},{"x":"O Espírito Infinito compartilha a perfeição, a retidão e o amor do Pai, mas inclina-Se para a misericórdia do Filho Eterno, tornando-Se o ministro da misericórdia das Deidades do Paraíso.","r":["8:2.6"]},{"x":"Após a personalização da Terceira Fonte, o Pai já não participa pessoalmente da criação do universo; Ele confia ao Filho tudo o que pode, e o Filho, por sua vez, ao Criador Conjunto.","r":["8:3.2"]},{"q":"O Filho Eterno é a única via de aproximação até o Pai Universal; e o Espírito Infinito é o único meio de alcançar o Filho Eterno.","r":"8:3.7"},{"x":"O Espírito Infinito é a primeira Deidade do Paraíso alcançada pelos peregrinos ascendentes no centro de todas as coisas.","r":["8:3.8"]}]},{"h":"O Espírito ministrador","items":[{"q":"God is love, the Son is mercy, the Spirit is ministry","r":"8:4.2"},{"x":"No universo local, por meio do Espírito Materno, a Sua Filha Criadora, Ele Se une ao Filho Criador para incentivar a ascensão espiritual das criaturas materiais.","r":["8:4.4"]},{"x":"O Espírito não desce na carne, mas submete-Se de bom grado a uma série de atenuações da divindade, até que por fim Se coloca ao nosso lado, como os anjos, para nos guiar no nosso caminho terreno.","r":["8:4.5"]},{"x":"O nosso universo é moldado entre a bigorna da justiça e o martelo do sofrimento, mas os que manejam o martelo são os seres da misericórdia, os filhos do Espírito Infinito.","r":["9:1.8"]},{"x":"As personalidades espirituais do Espírito Infinito formam a escada viva pela qual o homem mortal sobe do caos à glória.","r":["9:8.25"]}]},{"h":"O Espírito onipresente de Deus","items":[{"x":"O atributo mais notável do Espírito Infinito é a onipresença; Ele compartilha a onisciência do Pai, mas é onipotente apenas no domínio da mente.","r":["8:5.1","9:1.5"]},{"x":"O Espírito Santo é o circuito espiritual característico que a Filha Criadora do Espírito Infinito estende sobre cada universo local, enquanto o próprio Espírito Infinito está presente em toda parte.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"q":"Há muitas influências espirituais, e todas são como uma.","r":"8:5.4"},{"x":"Embora de origens diferentes, o Ajustador, o espírito do Filho Eterno e a presença do Espírito Infinito cooperam perfeitamente na mente e na alma do homem, atuando como um só espírito.","r":["8:5.4","9:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Manipulador da energia e mente absoluta","items":[{"x":"O Criador Conjunto não é a própria energia, mas o manipulador da energia, e possui o poder da antigravidade, que não se observa nem no Pai nem no Filho.","r":["9:3.2","9:3.5"]},{"q":"O Paraíso é o modelo da infinitude; o Deus da Ação é o ativador desse arquétipo.","r":"9:3.8"},{"x":"A mente das criaturas origina-se exclusivamente na Terceira Fonte, e nem mesmo um fragmento do Pai pode residir no homem antes que o Espírito Infinito tenha preparado o caminho da mente.","r":["9:5.2"]},{"x":"O fato de a fonte da mente ser divina não torna divino todo fenômeno mental; o intelecto humano tem raízes em origens animais.","r":["9:5.5"]},{"x":"Assim como o Pai atrai toda personalidade e o Filho todo espírito, o Agente Conjunto atrai toda mente por meio do circuito da gravidade da mente.","r":["9:6.2"]}]},{"h":"Uma verdadeira personalidade","items":[{"x":"O Espírito Infinito é uma presença universal, um poder e a mente universal, e mais ainda; mas Ele é, ao mesmo tempo, uma personalidade verdadeira e divina.","r":["8:6.1"]},{"x":"O Espírito Infinito tem vontade, além de mente; o Seu amor e as Suas tristezas são reais, e Ele reage ao universo como uma pessoa.","r":["8:6.3","8:6.4"]},{"q":"therefore \"Grieve not the Spirit of God.\"","r":"8:6.4"},{"x":"No Espírito Infinito, o Pai e o Filho estão mutuamente presentes, sempre em perfeição inqualificável.","r":["8:6.7"]}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Filho Eterno","Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Mente cósmica","Sete Espíritos Mestres","Espírito Santo"]},{"n":23,"t":"Espírito Materno do Universo Local","en":"Local Universe Mother Spirit","sum":"The local universe Mother Spirit is the Creative Daughter individualized by the Infinite Spirit for each local universe, the co-ordinate companion who builds the universe, brings forth life, and rules together with the Creator Son. In Nebadon she is called the Divine Minister, and through the breath of life, the seven adjutant mind-spirits, and the Holy Spirit she bestows mind and spirit on all creatures. As Michael functions as a father, she fills the role of a mother, never coercing but gently leading men along the path of sonship.","sections":[{"h":"The Local Universe Daughter of the Infinite Spirit","items":[{"x":"When a Creator Son is personalized, the Infinite Spirit individualizes a new and unique representation of himself to go out into space with him as his companion.","r":["34:0.1","17:6.3"]},{"x":"The Universe Mother Spirits receive prepersonal training on the worlds of Havona, learning to co-operate with the Paradise Sons under the will of the Father.","r":["14:6.32"]},{"q":"She volunteered to accompany Michael on the occasion of his liberation from Paradise obligations","r":"33:3.2"},{"x":"The Mother Spirit of Nebadon is the 611,121st of the sixth group of Supreme Spirits, and she has created and governed this universe together with Michael.","r":["33:3.2"]},{"x":"When a Creator Son departs for space, the Universal Father's proclamation of the eternal union of the two is one of the most touching events on Paradise.","r":["17:6.5"]}]},{"h":"Personalization and Career Stages","items":[{"x":"When Michael proclaims the creation of life, a \"primary eruption\" occurs on Paradise, and at that moment the Creative Spirit becomes a personal being, the Divine Minister.","r":["34:1.1","17:6.7"]},{"x":"The personalized Mother Spirit acquires a personal nature tinged with the nature of the Master Spirit who presides over that superuniverse.","r":["34:1.3"]},{"x":"In the stage of physical creation, the Universe Son provides the pattern and the Universe Spirit materializes these energy creations into physical substance.","r":["34:0.3"]},{"x":"When Michael returned from his seventh bestowal, the Mother Spirit pledged her subordination to him, and Michael established her as coruler.","r":["33:3.5","33:3.6","17:6.8"]},{"q":"the Son published to the worlds the fact of the Spirit's equality with him in all endowments of personality and attributes of divine character.","r":"33:3.6"},{"x":"This \"Proclamation of Equality\" is the transcendent pattern for family organization and government and the high ideal of the human home and voluntary marriage.","r":["33:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Mother of Life and of Spirit Personalities","items":[{"x":"When the Life Carriers have prepared the physical bodies, the Universe Spirit contributes \"the breath of life,\" activating the lifeless patterns and imparting the power of reproduction.","r":["34:2.5","36:6.3"]},{"x":"Michael and the Mother Spirit are literally the father-son and spirit-mother of all native creatures of Nebadon.","r":["37:0.1"]},{"q":"Such a Divine Minister is in reality the mother of spirits and spirit personalities, the ever-present and all-wise adviser of the Creator Son","r":"33:3.3"},{"x":"The seraphim were created as the first solitary spirit reproduction of the Mother Spirit, and her creative activity never ceases as Nebadon grows.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"x":"When rebellion arises only the Son can act as savior, but the Spirit always sustains him in all that he undergoes.","r":["33:3.4"]}]},{"h":"Ministry of Mind and Spirit","items":[{"q":"Ela está presente, igual e difusamente, em todo o seu universo local e, portanto, está tão literal e pessoalmente presente em um mundo como em outro qualquer.","r":"34:3.3"},{"x":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits are created by the Divine Minister and are called the spirits of wisdom, worship, counsel, knowledge, courage, understanding, and intuition.","r":["34:4.10"]},{"x":"As soon as a mind reaches the level of receiving the adjutants of worship and wisdom, it is included in the spirit circuit of the Divine Minister, the ministry of the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:5.3","36:5.15"]},{"x":"The Mother Spirit never leaves Salvington, and because she is fixed there the Spirit of Truth functions independently of Michael's whereabouts.","r":["34:4.7"]},{"q":"O Espírito Materno do Universo atua como o foco e o centro, no universo, do Espírito da Verdade, bem como o centro da sua própria influência pessoal, o Espírito Santo.","r":"34:4.7"},{"x":"The joint presence of the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of Truth, and the Adjuster in one mortal is a symmetry of spiritual endowment that brings consciousness of sonship with God.","r":["34:5.7"]}]},{"h":"The Spirit at Work in Man","items":[{"q":"From the heights of eternal glory the divine Spirit descends, by a long series of steps, to meet you as you are and where you are","r":"34:6.3"},{"x":"The ministry of the Holy Spirit is partly independent of man's attitude, but the more fully man follows divine leading, the more effective it becomes in sanctifying the inner life.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"q":"O Espírito nunca constrange, apenas guia.","r":"34:6.11"},{"x":"Between the animal nature and spiritual urges, the combined spirits help man throughout life to subject the flesh increasingly to the leading of the spirit.","r":["34:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Filho Criador Michael","Espírito Infinito","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Espírito Santo","Espírito da Verdade","Serafins"]},{"n":40,"t":"Espírito Santo","en":"Holy Spirit","sum":"The Holy Spirit is the spirit circuit, and the personal influence, that the local universe Mother Spirit, the Divine Minister, extends throughout her universe. Proceeding from the Creative Daughter of the Paradise Infinite Spirit, it is indigenous to that local universe and bound to her personal presence on Salvington. A mind in which the adjutants of worship and wisdom function is soon encircuited in it; this is the first supermind endowment man receives and the foundation for receiving the Adjuster.","sections":[{"h":"The Spirit Circuit of the Mother Spirit","items":[{"q":"O Espírito Santo é o circuito espiritual dessa Filha Criativa do Espírito Infinito do Paraíso.","r":"8:5.3"},{"x":"The Holy Spirit is a circuit indigenous to each local universe and confined to the spiritual realm of that creation, whereas the Infinite Spirit is everywhere present.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"x":"In the sacred writings the term \"Spirit of God\" seems to refer interchangeably to the Infinite Spirit on Paradise and the Creative Spirit of the local universe.","r":["8:5.3"]},{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the second is the spirit circuit of the Divine Minister, the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:4.3","15:9.13"]},{"x":"As the spirit of the Infinite Spirit and of the Universe Mother Spirit, the Holy Spirit is often regarded as the spirit of the Universe Spirit, the \"spirit of spirit\" in the threefold spirit endowment.","r":["194:2.17","194:2.11"]},{"x":"Mortals too can know the presence of the Infinite Spirit, for they actually experience his grace working through the Holy Spirit bestowed by the local universe.","r":["9:2.5"]}]},{"h":"A Presence Bound to Salvington","items":[{"q":"O Espírito Santo, da Ministra Divina, deixaria de funcionar se a presença pessoal dela fosse removida de Sálvington.","r":"34:4.7"},{"x":"The Mother Spirit never leaves the universe headquarters world, and she acts as the universe focus not only of her Holy Spirit but also of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["34:4.7"]},{"x":"The Holy Spirit and the Spirit of Truth go out from the local universe headquarters and, with the ministry of the adjutant mind-spirits, reach the lower levels of material mind.","r":["56:3.3"]},{"x":"Because the Holy Spirit \"searches all things,\" the Mother Spirit on Salvington knows mortals fully.","r":["28:5.22"]}]},{"h":"The First Supermind Endowment","items":[{"q":"Man's first supermind endowment is that of personality encircuitment in the Holy Spirit of the Universe Creative Spirit;","r":"103:0.1"},{"x":"This influence functions long before the bestowals of the divine Sons or the universal bestowal of the Adjusters, enlarging man's view of ethics, religion, and spirituality.","r":["103:0.1"]},{"q":"O Espírito Santo — essa é a dotação inicial da supramente e, infalivelmente, aparece em todas as personalidades humanas de boa fé.","r":"92:0.4"},{"x":"This ministry to a mind that craves worship and desires wisdom creates the capacity to realize human survival both as a concept and as actual experience.","r":["92:0.4"]},{"x":"A mind in which the adjutants of worship and wisdom function is at once included in the spiritual circuit of the Divine Minister.","r":["34:5.3","36:5.15"]},{"x":"A mind ministered by the Holy Spirit has the capacity to choose the Adjuster, and the Adjuster enters only after the preparation of the adjutants and encircuitment in the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:5.4","108:2.2","110:6.13"]}]},{"h":"Inner Ministry and the Fruits of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"Spiritual reason, the intelligence of the soul, is the endowment of the Holy Spirit, the gift of the Creative Spirit to man.","r":["101:3.2"]},{"x":"The Holy Spirit works partly independently of human attitude and partly according to the co-operation of the will, sanctifying the inner life of one who fully follows its leading.","r":["34:5.5"]},{"q":"A semente da verdade teórica torna-se morta, os mais elevados conceitos morais tornam-se sem efeito, a menos que, e até que, o Espírito divino sopre sobre as formas da verdade e vivifique as fórmulas da retidão.","r":"34:6.6"},{"q":"O Espírito nunca constrange, apenas guia.","r":"34:6.11"},{"x":"In a life led by the spirit, the fruits of the spirit such as love, joy, and peace appear, and the kingdom of God is righteousness, peace, and joy in the Holy Spirit.","r":["34:6.13","137:8.9"]},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, the ministry of the Holy Spirit and the angels becomes ever more effective as the ages pass.","r":["55:6.4"]}]},{"h":"Oneness with Other Spirit Ministries","items":[{"x":"Man possesses no separate part of the Creator Son or the Mother Spirit; these ministries do not indwell the mind as the Adjuster does.","r":["34:5.6"]},{"x":"The presence in mortals of the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of Truth, and the Adjuster is a symmetry of spiritual endowment that qualifies them to realize sonship with God.","r":["34:5.7"]},{"q":"Independentemente da pluralidade da sua origem, todas as influências espirituais são unas, na sua atuação.","r":"34:6.2"},{"x":"The three supermortal endowments, the Adjuster, the Spirit of Truth, and the Holy Spirit, are unified in human experience as the ministry of the Supreme.","r":["101:2.12","113:4.6"]},{"x":"The ascender uses spirit circuits such as the Holy Spirit but does not possess them, and these circuits convey to the Supreme the values emerging in the personality.","r":["117:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Espírito Infinito","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Espírito da Verdade","Ajustador do Pensamento","Reino do céu"]},{"n":38,"t":"Espíritos ajudantes da mente","en":"Adjutant Mind-Spirits","sum":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits are circuits of mind ministry created by the local universe Mother Spirit and named the spirits of intuition, understanding, courage, knowledge, counsel, worship, and wisdom. More like circuits than independent personalities, they act on animal and human minds that can learn by experience, conditioning evolution so that it proceeds purposefully rather than by accident. When the adjutants of worship and wisdom begin to function, mind crosses the threshold of spiritual ministry and is prepared to receive the circuit of the Holy Spirit and the Thought Adjuster.","sections":[{"h":"The Mind Circuits of the Mother Spirit","items":[{"x":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits were created by the Divine Minister of the local universe; alike in character but diverse in power, they can hardly be regarded as personalities apart from their mother.","r":["34:4.10"]},{"x":"Of the three spirit circuits of Nebadon, the third is the intelligence-ministry circuit of the seven adjutant mind-spirits.","r":["34:4.4"]},{"q":"Os sete espíritos ajudantes da mente sempre acompanham os Portadores da Vida a um novo planeta, mas não devem ser encarados como entidades; eles são mais semelhantes a circuitos.","r":"36:5.4"},{"x":"They are in fact a level of consciousness of the Divine Minister and are always subordinate to the action and presence of their creative mother.","r":["36:5.4"]},{"x":"The adjutants grow in function through experience, yet they never become personal beings.","r":["36:5.13"]},{"x":"This ministry emanates from the local universe headquarters, but the actual direction of the lower levels of mind function is centered at the system capitals.","r":["65:7.1"]},{"x":"In the early stages of evolution the mortal races climb the grades of intelligence as they progressively make contact with the seven adjutant mind-spirits of the Mother Spirit.","r":["194:2.12","194:2.18"]}]},{"h":"The Names and Functions of the Seven Adjutants","items":[{"x":"The spirit of intuition gives quick perception, reflex instincts, and the sense of direction, and it is the only adjutant that makes extensive contact with the mechanical levels of mind.","r":["36:5.6","34:4.12"]},{"x":"The spirit of understanding is the gift of spontaneously associating and co-ordinating ideas, shown in quick reasoning and prompt decision.","r":["36:5.7"]},{"q":"O espírito da coragem — o dom da fidelidade — nos seres pessoais, a base da aquisição do caráter e raiz intelectual da fibra moral e da bravura espiritual.","r":"36:5.8"},{"x":"The spirit of knowledge is the mother of the curiosity that leads to adventure and discovery, and the spirit of counsel is the urge to social co-operation that brings harmony with one's fellows.","r":["36:5.9","36:5.10"]},{"q":"A adoração é a insígnia da candidatura à ascensão espiritual.","r":"36:5.11"},{"q":"Este é o mais elevado dos ajudantes, o espírito coordenador e articulador do trabalho de todos os outros.","r":"36:5.12"},{"x":"When knowledge is elevated to new levels of meaning and activated by the presence of the adjutant of wisdom, it becomes wisdom.","r":["180:5.3"]}]},{"h":"A Ministry That Guides Evolution","items":[{"x":"Because the presence of the adjutant mind-spirits conditions organic evolution, evolution is purposeful rather than accidental.","r":["36:5.1"]},{"x":"The adjutants do not contact purely mechanical responses; they begin to minister the moment the capacity to learn by experience appears.","r":["65:7.5","65:7.6"]},{"x":"They are not concerned with physical evolution, yet they mesh with it so perfectly that man sees in mind phenomena only the workings of nature.","r":["65:7.2"]},{"x":"Because of Urantia's unique life pattern, the lower adjutants had greater difficulty in making contact here than almost anywhere else in Nebadon.","r":["65:7.3","65:7.4"]},{"x":"Since the functioning of the first five adjutants in the animal stage is essential to human intellect, animals are indispensable to the intellectual evolution of man as well.","r":["36:5.13"]},{"x":"The central focus at Life Carrier headquarters registers the function of the first five adjutants, but the quantitative activity of worship and wisdom is registered in the presence of the Mother Spirit on Salvington.","r":["36:5.3"]},{"x":"The work of the Mother Spirit is done chiefly through the seven adjutants, the spirits of promise, always leading mankind toward higher thoughts and ideals.","r":["34:5.2"]}]},{"h":"The Threshold of Spiritual Ministry","items":[{"q":"Os ajudantes funcionam exclusivamente na evolução da mente experiencial até o nível da sexta fase, o espírito da adoração.","r":"65:7.7"},{"x":"When mind becomes able to receive the adjutants of worship and wisdom, the mortal first experiences the ministry of spirit joined with mind.","r":["34:5.3"]},{"x":"Creature mind before it recognizes and worships divinity is the exclusive domain of the adjutants, but as soon as spiritual response appears, it becomes supermind.","r":["36:5.15"]},{"x":"The adjutants are not directly concerned with the highly spiritual functions of the Holy Spirit, but in evolutionary man they prepare the way ahead of the appearance of that spirit.","r":["36:5.16"]},{"q":"E isso requer a atuação coordenada de todos sete ajudantes, para qualificar a mente humana para a recepção de um Ajustador.","r":"108:2.2"},{"x":"All genuinely religious reactions of man are sponsored by the adjutant of worship and censored by the adjutant of wisdom.","r":["103:0.1"]}]}],"see":["Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Mente","Espírito Santo","Portadores da Vida","Evolução","Ajustador do Pensamento"]},{"n":94,"t":"Evolução","en":"Evolution","sum":"In The Urantia Book evolution is not a chance process but the divine technique by which the universes of time and space progressively grow. Life implanted by the Life Carriers advanced, under the ministry of the physical controllers and the adjutant mind-spirits, from the protoplasm of the seas to human beings with will, and society, religion, and government have followed the same evolutionary path. All this growth is bound up with the evolution of the Supreme Being and moves at last toward the age of light and life.","sections":[{"h":"The Evolving Universe","items":[{"q":"Esses universos do tempo e do espaço são todos evolucionários.","r":"32:0.2"},{"x":"Unlike Havona, which was created perfect, growth is the characteristic of the grand universe and the mark of experiential Deity.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"The confusion and inequality of Urantia show that this world is the work of subabsolute Creators who are not yet perfect.","r":["116:0.2"]},{"x":"Continuing evolution corrects nature, increasing the share of Paradise perfection and decreasing that of evil, error, and disharmony.","r":["4:2.4"]},{"x":"We evolve in God the Supreme, and he also evolves in us.","r":["31:10.12"]}]},{"h":"Plan, Not Chance","items":[{"q":"A evolução cósmica pode nem sempre ser compreensível (previsível), mas é estritamente não acidental.","r":"49:1.1"},{"x":"Urantia was a life-experiment world, but the establishment of life was not an experiment in the sense of the haphazard or accidental.","r":["65:4.1","65:4.2"]},{"x":"Features of human existence such as cells that heal their own wounds show that life was intelligently planned.","r":["65:4.3"]},{"q":"A física e a química sozinhas não conseguem explicar como um ser humano evoluiu vindo do protoplasma primevo dos mares primitivos.","r":"65:6.8"},{"x":"In every living thing dwells an innate, unsatisfied longing for greater perfection.","r":["65:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Life","items":[{"x":"Material life arises from the cooperation of a threefold creativity: the physical controllers, the Seven Master Spirits, and the Life Carriers.","r":["65:0.1"]},{"x":"The development of life passes through three stages: physical energy, the mind ministry of the adjutant spirits, and spiritual endowment completed by the Adjuster bestowal.","r":["65:0.2","65:0.5"]},{"x":"The primitive ancestors of mankind were the mud of the warm bays and lagoons of ancient inland seas, and the transition from plant to animal occurred 450,000,000 years ago.","r":["65:2.1","58:6.1"]},{"x":"New species appear suddenly as fully developed new orders, not by the accumulation of small variations.","r":["58:6.3"]},{"x":"About a million years ago the immediate ancestors of mankind came from a lemur type of mammal through three successive sudden mutations.","r":["62:0.1"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers complete their work when beings with will appear, and thereafter they cannot interfere with will.","r":["36:3.8"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Mind and Spirit","items":[{"x":"As life rises higher, the adjutant mind-spirits act one by one, and mind becomes ever more coordinating, creative, and integrating.","r":["65:6.7","62:6.3"]},{"x":"Biologic evolution finally reached the dignity of human will, and Urantia was recognized as a planet of human habitation 993,408 years ago.","r":["62:7.7"]},{"q":"Nos laboratórios evolucionários cósmicos, a mente é sempre dominante sobre a matéria, e o espírito está sempre correlacionado à mente.","r":"65:8.5"},{"x":"Spiritual progress depends on mental expansion and is slowed by intellectual retardation, yet the soul can evolve regardless of the cultural level of the mind.","r":["65:8.4"]},{"x":"Evolution seems long because creatures make their own lifespan the measure of time.","r":["65:8.2","65:8.3"]}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Society and Religion","items":[{"x":"Like marriage, industry, and religion, civil government is a product of gradual evolution.","r":["70:5.1"]},{"x":"Early evolution is marked by the survival of the fittest, but later civilization advances better through intelligent cooperation and spiritual brotherhood.","r":["71:5.3"]},{"x":"Until the Planetary Prince arrives, religion is wholly an evolutionary process; thereafter evolution and revelation advance religion together.","r":["52:2.3"]},{"x":"Attempts to overturn the mores by revolution are fatal to civilization, for the mores are the thread of continuity that has held civilization together.","r":["68:4.6"]},{"q":"A evolução pode ser retardada, mas não pode ser detida.","r":"81:0.1"}]},{"h":"The Purpose of Evolution","items":[{"x":"The march of the universes has a great and glorious purpose, and none of the struggles of mortals is in vain.","r":["32:5.1"]},{"q":"Os acontecimentos do tempo e as lutas da existência material não são senão um andaime transitório, a fazer uma ponte para o outro lado, para a terra prometida da realidade espiritual e da existência superna.","r":"32:5.2"},{"x":"The final attainment of an evolutionary world is the age of light and life, and the achievements of settled worlds alone justify the creation of man.","r":["55:0.1","55:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Portadores da Vida","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Ser Supremo","Luz e vida","Urântia","Civilização"]},{"n":99,"t":"Experiência","en":"Experience","sum":"In The Urantia Book experience is the way the evolutionary universe lives and the source of its growth. Paradise and Havona are existentially perfect, but the creatures of time and space and the Supreme Being become perfect through experience. Even a Creator Son earned his sovereignty by experience, and the Adjuster too accumulates experience together with man. Above all, the personal religious experience of knowing God remains true and valid even when theology and philosophy waver, and it transforms people and leads them to service.","sections":[{"h":"What Is Experience?","items":[{"q":"É simplesmente qualquer interação entre um eu ativo e questionador, e qualquer outra realidade ativa e externa.","r":"102:4.2"},{"x":"The mass of experience is determined by depth of concept and totality of recognition of external reality, and its fact is found in other things, minds, and spirits.","r":["102:4.2"]},{"x":"Man experiences matter in his mind and spiritual reality in his soul, but it is the mind that is conscious of this experience.","r":["103:6.6"]},{"q":"Without experience, no evolutionary creature could even exist","r":"106:9.2"}]},{"h":"Existential and Experiential Perfection","items":[{"x":"Paradise Deity is existential, but the emerging Supreme and Ultimate are experiential.","r":["0:4.9"]},{"x":"The Father has achieved existential expression in the Son and the Spirit and is now achieving experiential expression as God the Supreme, Ultimate, and Absolute.","r":["0:7.6"]},{"x":"The perfection of the creatures of time, though mixed with grace, is a true personal possession gained through personal effort and actual living.","r":["32:3.9"]},{"x":"The experiential nature of evolutionary personalities is the natural complement of the ever-perfect nature of the Paradise-Havona creatures.","r":["32:3.12"]},{"x":"The experience of every evolving creature personality is a phase of the experience of the Almighty Supreme.","r":["116:1.1"]}]},{"h":"The Good Fortune of Starting at the Bottom","items":[{"x":"Animal evolutionary origin is no stigma on any personality; there is greater honor for those who have climbed the ladder of life from the very bottom.","r":["32:3.10"]},{"x":"It would have been easy for the Father to make all mortals perfect from the start, but that would deprive them of the adventure and training of the long, gradual ascent.","r":["32:3.11"]},{"q":"an experience to be had only by those who are so fortunate as to begin at the very bottom of living existence.","r":"32:3.11"},{"x":"The mortal career, the evolution of the soul, is not so much a probation as an education.","r":["111:3.5"]}]},{"h":"The Experience of Divine Beings","items":[{"x":"Michael was born a creator, yet his sovereignty had to be earned through the experience of seven bestowals.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"x":"All the human experiences Jesus passed through became the eternal possession of the Universe Sovereign, making him an experienced sovereign.","r":["127:6.13"]},{"x":"Virgin Adjusters too must gain experience while the mortal creature grows, rehearsing in advance the techniques of the next stage of life.","r":["109:0.1"]},{"x":"A Personalized Adjuster possesses as an eternal endowment all the experience gained while indwelling various mortal minds.","r":["109:6.2"]}]},{"h":"Religious Experience","items":[{"q":"A experiência religiosa é a realização da consciência de haver encontrado Deus.","r":"102:3.4"},{"q":"São os vossos pensamentos, não os vossos sentimentos, que vos conduzem a Deus.","r":"101:1.3"},{"x":"Religion may be accompanied by feeling but is not itself the experience of feeling, and the conditions that induce mystic experience rather show its dangers.","r":["101:5.9","100:5.10"]},{"x":"Though theology and philosophy may be distorted, the spiritual experience of personal religion remains true and valid.","r":["103:9.1"]},{"x":"The experience of God-consciousness is the same in every generation, but philosophic concepts and theologic definitions of God must change with knowledge.","r":["5:5.12"]},{"x":"Religious experience results in a certain consciousness of God and an unquestioned assurance of the survival of personality.","r":["101:1.6"]}]},{"h":"The Fruits of Experience","items":[{"q":"A EXPERIÊNCIA da vivência religiosa dinâmica transforma o indivíduo medíocre numa personalidade de poder idealístico.","r":"100:0.1"},{"x":"One who has found God is impelled by overflowing goodness to serve his fellows; true religion leads to increased social service.","r":["102:3.4"]},{"x":"The senses reveal the existence of things and the mind their meaning, but spiritual experience reveals the true values of life.","r":["100:4.4"]},{"x":"Faith always triumphs over doubt, for experience is superior to theory, and spiritual reality to isolated facts.","r":["102:6.7"]},{"x":"The Adjuster restores only the memories and experiences needed for the universe career; many memories without spiritual meaning perish with the brain.","r":["112:5.22"]}]}],"see":["Experiência religiosa","Ser Supremo","Crescimento","Realidade","Fé","Busca da perfeição"]},{"n":54,"t":"Experiência religiosa","en":"Religious Experience","sum":"Religious experience is the personal experience of living knowledge of God and supreme values under the guidance of the indwelling spirit. It is neither a reasoned system of belief nor a mystic ecstasy; it sprouts from moral consciousness and grows through faith and insight. However erroneous one's theology, the experience itself can be genuine, and its certainty cannot be refuted. Religious experience culminates in a certain consciousness of God and assurance of survival.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Religious Experience","items":[{"x":"True religion is neither a philosophic system proved by reason nor a mystic ecstasy enjoyed by a favored few.","r":["101:1.1"]},{"q":"São os vossos pensamentos, não os vossos sentimentos, que vos conduzem a Deus.","r":"101:1.3"},{"x":"Religion is not the search for new facts but the discovery of new spiritual meanings in facts already known.","r":["101:1.4"]},{"x":"The religious tendency is innate and universal; it is fostered by the spirit of worship and censored by the spirit of wisdom.","r":["103:0.1","103:0.2"]},{"x":"The experience of realizing spiritual values is superideational and hard to express in human language; it is called God-consciousness.","r":["103:1.6"]}]},{"h":"Where Experience Begins","items":[{"x":"Every person early experiences conflict between selfish and altruistic urges, and in its resolution may first experience God-consciousness.","r":["103:2.4"]},{"x":"When a moral being makes an unselfish choice against the urge to be selfish, that is primitive religious experience.","r":["103:2.8"]},{"x":"It is right to identify altruistic desire with an influence outside oneself, with God, for it comes from the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["103:2.10"]},{"x":"Religious \"birth\" is usually gradual, though there is a day of spirit rebirth; those who grow without crisis and those who pass through crisis should not disparage one another.","r":["103:2.1","103:2.2"]},{"q":"Quando um ser moral escolhe não ser egoísta, ao deparar com o impulso de ser egoísta, esta é a experiência religiosa primitiva.","r":"103:2.8"}]},{"h":"Conversion and Mysticism","items":[{"x":"Religious growth moves from stagnation to adjustment, from insecurity to faith, and from the bondage of fear to the liberty of sonship.","r":["100:5.2"]},{"x":"God-consciousness may grow gradually or arrive in a dramatic moment, as with Paul on the Damascus road.","r":["100:5.3"]},{"q":"But emotion alone is a false conversion; one must have faith as well as feeling.","r":"100:5.5"},{"x":"Rather than seeking conversion, living faith, sincere worship, and unselfish prayer are a better way of approach to the Adjuster.","r":["100:5.7"]},{"x":"Trances and visions should not be sought as religious experience, and Jesus never resorted to such methods.","r":["100:5.8","100:5.11"]}]},{"h":"Experience and Theology","items":[{"x":"Religion begins with the quest for values, and systems of interpretive belief come later, so people agree more readily on values than on creeds.","r":["103:1.4"]},{"q":"Não importa quão ilusória e errônea seja a teologia de alguém, a sua religião pode ser totalmente genuína e verdadeira para sempre.","r":"103:9.2"},{"q":"When theology masters religion, religion dies; it becomes a doctrine instead of a life.","r":"103:9.6"},{"x":"Knowing the varied religious experiences of others keeps one's own religion from becoming selfish and narrow.","r":["103:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Fruits and Certainty of Experience","items":[{"x":"True religion is a living love and a life of service; it takes nothing away from a person and adds new meaning to all of life.","r":["100:6.5"]},{"x":"A remarkable trait of the religious life is a peace that passes all understanding, unshaken by any disappointment.","r":["100:6.6"]},{"x":"Religion rests on the Adjuster-derived postulate that God is knowable and attainable.","r":["103:9.8"]},{"x":"The reality of religious experience is proportional to its spiritual content; its certainties are unassailable and its devotion beyond question.","r":["103:9.12"]},{"x":"Religious experience culminates in a sure consciousness of God and an unquestioned assurance of the survival of the believer.","r":["101:1.6"]},{"q":"A verdadeira religião, contudo, é um amor vivo, uma vida de serviço.","r":"100:6.5"}]}],"see":["Religião pessoal","Fé","Adoração","Ajustador do Pensamento","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Filosofia"]},{"n":51,"t":"Fé","en":"Faith","sum":"Faith is a living trust in God and in spiritual values, distinct from belief, which merely accepts a doctrine as true. Belief becomes faith only when it actually guides and shapes life, and faith transforms the philosophic God of probability into the God of experiential certainty. Faith is the price of entrance into the family of God and the key to Havona, and Jesus lived out its highest example.","sections":[{"h":"Belief and Faith","items":[{"x":"Accepting a teaching as true is only belief; belief becomes faith when it actually dominates the mode of living.","r":["101:8.1"]},{"q":"A crença fixa, a fé liberta.","r":"101:8.2"},{"x":"Beliefs may become group possessions, but faith must always be personal.","r":["101:8.2"]},{"x":"Faith is a God-knowing and man-serving life, a living experience concerned with spiritual meanings and supreme values.","r":["101:8.2"]},{"q":"Belief may not be able to resist doubt and withstand fear, but faith is always triumphant over doubting","r":"102:6.7"},{"q":"A aceitação de um ensinamento como verdadeiro não é fé; é mais uma crença.","r":"101:8.1"}]},{"h":"Faith and Certainty","items":[{"x":"Faith transforms the philosophic God of probability into the saving God of certainty in personal religious experience.","r":["102:6.4"]},{"q":"As convicções sobre Deus podem ser alcançadas por meio do raciocínio sábio, mas os indivíduos tornam-se conhecedores de Deus apenas pela fé, por meio da experiência pessoal.","r":"102:6.5"},{"x":"In science God is a possibility and in philosophy a probability, but in religion he is a certainty.","r":["102:6.8"]},{"x":"God is not revealed by miracles or material proofs; he is known by trusting him.","r":["102:1.5"]},{"x":"The more one knows of science, the less sure one becomes; the more religion one has, the more certain one is.","r":["102:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Marks of True Faith","items":[{"x":"True faith trusts in the goodness of God even amid bitter disappointment and defeat, and it generates profound courage in the face of calamity.","r":["101:3.6","101:3.7"]},{"x":"Faith maintains an inexplicable poise and serenity in the midst of illness and suffering, abuse and injustice.","r":["101:3.8","101:3.9"]},{"x":"True faith worships God in every circumstance and declares, \"Though he slay me, yet will I serve him.\"","r":["101:3.16"]},{"x":"Faith does not violate intellectual honesty, foster intolerance and persecution, or turn away from scientific discoveries.","r":["101:8.3","101:8.4"]},{"x":"Faith vitalizes religion and moves the religionist to live the golden rule heroically.","r":["101:8.4"]},{"q":"A fé revitaliza a religião e obriga o religioso a viver heroicamente a regra de ouro.","r":"101:8.4"}]},{"h":"Faith and Salvation","items":[{"x":"Faith links moral consciousness with the spiritual concept of enduring reality, making religion a technique of salvation.","r":["101:9.9"]},{"x":"Faith is the price of entrance into the family of God, and forgiveness is the act of God in accepting that faith.","r":["170:3.3"]},{"x":"Faith releases the divine spark that lives within man, the potential of eternal survival.","r":["132:3.6"]},{"x":"The Adjuster's success in achieving survival depends less on theories of belief than on decisions, determinations, and steadfast faith.","r":["110:3.2"]},{"q":"A vontade de acreditar é a chave de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"}]},{"h":"The Faith of Jesus","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not use faith as a consolation in suffering or a comfort in despair; he enjoyed serenity in an unquestioning trust in God.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"x":"Jesus' great contribution was less a new idea of God than the human demonstration of a new and higher type of living faith.","r":["196:0.3"]},{"x":"Jesus asks people not so much to believe in him as to believe with him, to believe as he believed.","r":["196:0.13"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that simple, childlike faith is the key that opens the door of the kingdom.","r":["170:3.2"]}]}],"see":["Experiência religiosa","Religião pessoal","Verdade","Reino do céu","Sobrevivência","Caráter de Jesus"]},{"n":22,"t":"Filho Criador Michael","en":"Creator Son Michael","sum":"A Creator Son is a primary Paradise Son, born of the Universal Father and the Eternal Son together, who designs, creates, and rules a local universe. The creator of our universe of Nebadon is Michael, who earned his sovereignty experientially by bestowing himself seven times in the likeness of his creatures, his final bestowal being the life he lived on Urantia as Jesus of Nazareth. To us he is, for all practical purposes, God, and the way by which the Father is revealed.","sections":[{"h":"Origin and Nature","items":[{"x":"A Creator Son is a being of dual origin, born in a flash when the Father's absolute concept of personality and the Eternal Son's absolute spiritual idea are perfectly united.","r":["21:0.1","21:1.1"]},{"q":"But each Creator Son is different from every other","r":"21:0.1"},{"x":"Michael of Nebadon is the 611,121st personalization of an original concept of infinite identity, and he shows characteristics more like those of the Eternal Son.","r":["33:1.1","33:2.1"]},{"x":"Michael is not a member of the Paradise Trinity, yet in his universe he possesses all the divine attributes and powers the Eternal Son would have if present.","r":["33:1.2","33:1.3"]},{"q":"To our universe and all its inhabited worlds the Sovereign Son is, to all practical intents and purposes, God.","r":"33:1.4"}]},{"h":"Creator of a Local Universe","items":[{"x":"Before choosing his space site, a Creator Son spends long periods observing and learning from the creations of his elder brothers in the same superuniverse.","r":["21:2.1"]},{"x":"When he leaves Paradise he is accompanied by a Creative Daughter of the Infinite Spirit, who later personalizes as the local universe Mother Spirit.","r":["21:2.2","21:2.9"]},{"x":"New modifications of energy-matter require the consent of the Infinite Spirit, and new designs of creatures that of the Eternal Son, while personality is bestowed by the Father alone.","r":["21:2.4","21:2.5","21:2.6"]},{"x":"Because creators differ, the life forms of the local universes they design are each original.","r":["21:2.10"]},{"x":"When Michael is absent, Gabriel, the Bright and Morning Star, directs the universe, and the Mother Spirit supervises in place of his spiritual presence.","r":["21:2.11","33:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Seven Bestowals and Sovereignty","items":[{"x":"A Creator Son could claim sovereignty from the beginning, but he pledges to the Trinity not to assume supreme sovereignty until he has completed seven bestowals.","r":["21:3.2","21:3.12"]},{"q":"but they all could, they are truly freewill Sons.","r":"21:3.3"},{"x":"In his seven bestowals he penetrates seven levels of creature life, revealing one by one the sevenfold will of Deity as personalized in the Seven Master Spirits.","r":["21:3.17","21:3.18","119:8.4"]},{"q":"These divine Sons are innately just, but they become understandingly merciful as a result of these successive bestowal experiences","r":"119:0.4"},{"x":"Having completed his bestowals, a Creator Son becomes a Master Son, and the addition of creature experience to his nature brings about a permanent change.","r":["21:4.6"]},{"q":"Michael nasceu um criador, foi educado como um administrador e aperfeiçoado como um executivo; no entanto, foi-lhe pedido que conquistasse a sua própria soberania, por meio da experiência.","r":"119:8.2"}]},{"h":"The Urantia Bestowal","items":[{"x":"After six bestowals, Michael came down to Urantia in the likeness of mortal flesh, the lowest of will creatures.","r":["120:0.2"]},{"x":"The final bestowal went beyond earning sovereignty; it was a plan for the supreme revelation of submission to the will of the Universal Father.","r":["120:0.7","120:0.8"]},{"q":"Jesus foi Deus e homem — sempre e para sempre.","r":"120:4.3"},{"q":"Nunca percais de vista o fato de que o propósito supremo da auto-outorga de Michael foi o de acentuar e engrandecer a revelação de Deus.","r":"120:4.4"},{"x":"Because his death on Urantia completed his bestowal career, he could truly say, \"It is finished.\"","r":["21:4.5"]},{"x":"And so this little planet, the mortal home of the sovereign Christ Michael, has become the sentimental shrine of all Nebadon.","r":["119:8.8"]}]},{"h":"The Rule and Destiny of the Master Son","items":[{"x":"After the Urantia bestowal, Michael was acknowledged by the Ancients of Days and the Universal Father as the settled sovereign of Nebadon.","r":["119:8.1"]},{"x":"When the Mother Spirit subordinated herself to him, Michael became the personal repository of divinity, with all power in heaven and on earth.","r":["33:2.3","33:2.4"]},{"x":"The Master Son pours out the Spirit of Truth \"upon all flesh\" and so communicates unceasingly with the worlds where he has sojourned.","r":["21:5.10"]},{"x":"The sum of the seven bestowals is a new Nebadon revelation of the Supreme Being, and it has also augmented the sovereignty of the evolving God the Supreme.","r":["119:8.3","119:8.5"]},{"x":"The Michaels are believed to be destined to become, in eternity, literally \"the way, the truth, and the life.\"","r":["21:6.4"]}]}],"see":["Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Universo local de Nébadon","Espírito da Verdade","Filhos Avonais","Ser Supremo","Anciães dos Dias"]},{"n":4,"t":"Filho Eterno","en":"Eternal Son","sum":"O Filho Eterno é a Segunda Fonte e Centro, a expressão perfeita do primeiro conceito pessoal e absoluto do Pai Universal. Ele é o Verbo divino vivo, a revelação final do espírito e da personalidade do Pai, e o administrador espiritual que mantém toda a realidade espiritual no circuito da gravidade espiritual. Estendendo o amor do Pai como misericórdia, Ele Se aproxima das criaturas por meio das auto-outorgas dos Filhos do Paraíso.","sections":[{"h":"Identidade e natureza","items":[{"x":"O Filho Eterno é a expressão completa do primeiro conceito pessoal e absoluto do Pai; sempre que o Pai Se expressa pessoalmente, Ele o faz por meio do Filho.","r":["6:0.1"]},{"x":"A expressão “primeiro pensamento” é apenas uma concessão às mentes presas ao tempo; o Filho não tem começo e é coeterno com o Pai.","r":["6:0.2","6:0.4"]},{"q":"A Primeira Fonte e Centro é o Absoluto Volicional; a Segunda Fonte e Centro é o Absoluto da Personalidade.","r":"6:1.2"},{"x":"O Pai nunca atua pessoalmente como criador a não ser em conjunção com o Filho ou com a ação coordenada do Filho.","r":["6:1.3"]},{"x":"Em Urântia, o Filho Original tem sido confundido com o Filho auto-outorgado, Michael de Nébadon, mas o título de “Filho Eterno” pertence somente ao Filho Original.","r":["6:1.5","6:1.6"]}]},{"h":"Ministro da misericórdia","items":[{"x":"O Filho é tão imutável e infinitamente digno de confiança quanto o Pai, e a nós Ele parece mais pessoal, por estar um passo mais próximo do nosso alcance.","r":["6:2.1"]},{"q":"Como Deus é amor, o Filho é misericórdia.","r":"6:3.1"},{"x":"O Filho não é um intercessor que implora misericórdia ao Pai; toda misericórdia demonstrada pelo Filho é uma revelação direta do amor do Pai.","r":["6:3.4"]},{"x":"A misericórdia é amor aplicado; por analogia, o amor de Deus assemelha-se mais ao amor de um pai, ao passo que o amor do Filho Eterno se assemelha mais à afeição de uma mãe.","r":["6:3.5"]},{"x":"O Pai ama os Seus filhos do universo como um pai, ao passo que o Filho Eterno vê cada criatura ao mesmo tempo como pai e como irmão.","r":["6:2.8"]}]},{"h":"O circuito da gravidade espiritual","items":[{"x":"O Filho é onipotente apenas no domínio espiritual; Ele não atua pessoalmente nos domínios físicos nem na ministração da mente, a não ser por meio do Agente Conjunto.","r":["6:4.2","6:5.1"]},{"x":"A gravidade espiritual é livre de defasagem temporal, não é diminuída pelo espaço e não decresce com o quadrado da distância.","r":["7:1.2"]},{"x":"As realidades espirituais respondem à gravidade espiritual segundo o seu valor qualitativo, e essa resposta é tão confiável e previsível quanto a resposta da matéria à gravidade.","r":["7:1.3","7:1.8"]},{"q":"O pecado e a rebelião podem interferir no funcionamento dos circuitos do universo local, mas nada pode suspender a gravidade espiritual do Filho Eterno.","r":"7:1.7"},{"q":"O circuito da gravidade do espírito atrai a alma do homem literalmente em direção ao Paraíso.","r":"7:3.2"}]},{"h":"A prece e a relação com o indivíduo","items":[{"x":"O espírito do Filho Eterno nos envolve, mas não reside em nós nem se torna parte de nós, como o faz o Monitor Misterioso.","r":["6:4.6"]},{"x":"O conteúdo espiritual da prece sincera é transmitido instantaneamente, pelo circuito da gravidade espiritual, a toda personalidade divina envolvida.","r":["7:3.3"]},{"x":"Os pedidos puramente materiais e egocêntricos não podem entrar no circuito espiritual e caem mortos.","r":["7:3.6"]},{"q":"É o pensamento motivador do conteúdo espiritual que valida a súplica do mortal. As palavras não têm valor.","r":"7:3.7"}]},{"h":"A auto-outorga e o plano de perfeição","items":[{"x":"O Filho aceitou sem reservas o plano do Pai de realização progressiva, e Ele próprio propôs o plano de auto-outorga, que consiste em enviar os Filhos de Deus aos mundos evolucionários.","r":["7:4.4","7:4.5"]},{"x":"O Filho Eterno é o curador pessoal e o guardião divino do plano de ascensão das criaturas que o Pai Lhe confiou.","r":["7:4.7"]},{"x":"Como a personalidade do Filho não pode ser fragmentada, Ele participa da experiência das criaturas por meio das encarnações dos Filhos do Paraíso.","r":["7:5.3","7:5.4"]},{"x":"O Filho Eterno auto-outorgou-Se sete vezes nos sete circuitos de Havona, fato que é um encorajamento eterno para todo peregrino que atravessa Havona.","r":["7:5.5","7:5.9"]},{"q":"É literalmente verdade que quem tiver visto um Filho do Paraíso, haverá visto o Filho Eterno de Deus.","r":"7:5.11"}]},{"h":"Revelação suprema do Pai","items":[{"x":"O Filho Eterno é a revelação completa e final do espírito e da personalidade do Pai, e todo conhecimento do Pai vem do Filho e dos Seus Filhos.","r":["7:7.1"]},{"x":"O Pai Se aproxima de nós como personalidade somente por meio dos Filhos divinos do Filho Eterno, e, por esse caminho vivo, também nós ascendemos ao Pai.","r":["7:7.4"]},{"x":"Os peregrinos que atravessam os circuitos de Havona podem alcançar o Filho muito antes de estarem preparados para discernir o Pai.","r":["7:7.5"]},{"x":"A personalidade do Filho não brilha intensamente para a mente material ou moroncial; somente quando começa a ascensão espiritual ela se torna cada vez mais real.","r":["6:8.5","6:8.6"]},{"q":"Do mesmo modo que Deus é o Pai Universal, o Filho é a Mãe Universal.","r":"6:8.1"}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Espírito Infinito","Trindade do Paraíso","Filho Criador Michael","Oração","Misericórdia"]},{"n":25,"t":"Filhos Avonais","en":"Avonal Sons","sum":"The Avonal Sons, or Magisterial Sons, are the second order of Paradise Sons, issuing from the Eternal Son and the Infinite Spirit. On the evolutionary worlds they serve as judges of dispensations, as magistrates who raise a planetary age one step higher, and as bestowal Sons born of woman who live as mortals. Through these \"lesser Christs,\" fully backed by the power of the Creator Son, nearly all inhabited worlds receive the Spirit of Truth and the Thought Adjusters, yet Urantia has never received a magisterial mission.","sections":[{"h":"The Second Order of Paradise Sons","items":[{"x":"Whenever an absolute concept of the Eternal Son unites with a new ideal of loving service of the Infinite Spirit, a new Paradise Magisterial Son appears.","r":["20:2.1","20:1.11"]},{"x":"The Magisterial Sons of the grand universe are estimated at about one billion; they are directed by the supreme council of Paradise and, once assigned to a local universe, serve under the Creator Son.","r":["20:2.2"]},{"q":"since each Avonal Son has an exclusive personality, since no two are alike","r":"20:2.3"},{"q":"E esses “Cristos menores” são tão eficientes e Todo-Poderosos, nas suas auto-outorgas planetárias, quanto foi o Filho Criador e Filho Mestre, em Urântia.","r":"35:0.1"},{"x":"While the Creator Sons reveal the character of the Father, the Avonals, Sons of merciful bestowal, reveal the nature of the Eternal Son with his infinite compassion.","r":["20:10.3","20:10.4"]}]},{"h":"Judges of the Dispensations","items":[{"x":"The Avonals are the magistrates of the realms who awaken the sleeping survivors, terminate a dispensation, and reassign the planetary ministers to the tasks of the new age.","r":["20:3.1"]},{"q":"though they may render judgments extinguishing the identity of personal creatures, they do not execute such sentences.","r":"20:3.2"},{"x":"On \"technical\" visits made solely for dispensational judgment they do not incarnate but come as spiritual beings invisible to material creatures.","r":["20:3.3","52:4.3"]},{"x":"The closing roll call of a dispensation is proclaimed by the archangel attending the Avonal, and the seraphic guardians of the sleepers respond to that \"voice of the archangel.\"","r":["37:3.6"]},{"x":"Even on worlds settled in light and life their judicial acts continue, but they then become formal, not altering the course of planetary events.","r":["55:0.2"]}]},{"h":"Magisterial Missions","items":[{"x":"World peace, with racial strife and national hostility gone, is the sign that a planet is mature enough to receive a Magisterial Son.","r":["52:3.12"]},{"x":"On the first magisterial mission the Avonal incarnates without birth as a full-grown adult of the race, appearing as one whom men can see and touch.","r":["20:4.1","20:2.6"]},{"q":"Each new dispensation extends the horizon of revealed religion","r":"52:4.4"},{"x":"Soon after the first visit of a Magisterial Son, mankind attains economic liberation, the daily labor needed for self-support falling to about two and one-half hours.","r":["52:4.5"]},{"x":"If one magisterial mission does not prepare the world for a bestowal Son, a second or later Magisterial Son comes and advances mankind one age at a time.","r":["52:4.9"]}]},{"h":"Bestowal Missions","items":[{"x":"Every Avonal bestows himself at least once upon some mortal race, and on each planet only one bestowal Son appears, born of woman.","r":["20:2.7","20:5.4"]},{"q":"Um Avonal auto-outorgado, entretanto, declara: “Quem tiver visto a mim, terá visto o Filho Eterno de Deus”.","r":"20:6.5"},{"x":"A Magisterial Son always bestows himself not subject to the Father's will but subject to the will of the Eternal Son of Paradise.","r":["20:6.5"]},{"x":"Bestowal Sons must die, but a violent death is not required by the divine plan, and most worlds treat them more considerately.","r":["20:6.6","20:6.7"]},{"q":"Nunca fracassam na realização da meta da sua missão de auto-outorga.","r":"20:5.7"},{"x":"When an Avonal who has completed his bestowal and the Creator Son together send forth the Spirit of Truth, the normal will creatures of that world receive Thought Adjusters.","r":["52:5.6","20:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Helpers, and Urantia","items":[{"x":"On planetary missions the Avonals are aided by Melchizedeks and archangels, and on bestowal missions they are accompanied by Brilliant Evening Stars and a bestowal retinue of 144.","r":["20:2.9","39:1.4"]},{"x":"After usually seven missions an Avonal yields the opportunity to other Sons and joins in universe administration in the high councils of the Creator Son.","r":["20:2.8"]},{"q":"Urântia nunca recebeu um Filho Avonal, em uma missão magisterial.","r":"20:4.4"},{"x":"The bestowal Son of Urantia was not an Avonal but Michael himself, though any bestowal Son would have been equally adequate for spiritual rehabilitation.","r":["49:5.26","20:5.6"]},{"x":"Since the world of Michael's bestowal is a ward of the Master Son, only time will reveal when a Magisterial Son will come to Urantia.","r":["20:4.5"]}]}],"see":["Filho Criador Michael","Filhos Instrutores da Trindade","Melquisedeques","Filho Eterno","Espírito da Verdade","Luz e vida"]},{"n":31,"t":"Filhos e Filhas Materiais","en":"Material Sons and Daughters","sum":"The Material Sons and Daughters are an order of sex-endowed Sons produced by the Creator Son for each local system; sent to the evolutionary worlds as Adam and Eve, they are charged with the biologic uplift of the races. Being material, they are visible to mortals and form the last link between the invisible Planetary Prince and human beings. The Adam and Eve of Urantia defaulted in their mission, yet their contribution greatly improved mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Origin and Nature","items":[{"x":"The Material Sons and Daughters are the offspring of the Creator Son; the Universe Mother Spirit takes no part in their production.","r":["51:1.1"]},{"x":"For each system the Creator Son makes only the original pair, fashioned to the life pattern of that system, and all the rest are their descendants.","r":["51:1.2"]},{"x":"They stand eight to ten feet tall and shine with a violet radiance; Adam and Eve are equal yet complementary and usually work as a pair.","r":["51:1.3"]},{"x":"With a dual constitution that takes in both material food and cosmic energy, they are cut off from their life source if they rebel and in the end meet material death.","r":["51:1.4"]},{"q":"Esses Filhos Materiais são o último vínculo físico, na cadeia das personalidades, que se estende desde a divindade e a perfeição acima, até a humanidade e a existência material abaixo.","r":"45:5.3"}]},{"h":"Life on Jerusem, the System Capital","items":[{"x":"Each family of Material Sons and Daughters lives in the Adamic domain of one thousand centers on Jerusem, and their numbers increase by natural reproduction.","r":["45:5.2","45:5.4"]},{"x":"The Adamites of Jerusem experiment with self-government through elections and representative government, and they handle most of the routine affairs of the capital sphere.","r":["45:5.5","45:5.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks maintain a faculty at each system headquarters for the education and spiritual training of young Material Sons and Daughters.","r":["45:5.7"]},{"x":"While living on the system capital, Material Sons have no Thought Adjusters, but through service they gain capacity for Adjuster indwelling and the ascending career.","r":["51:1.6"]}]},{"h":"The Mission of a Planetary Adam","items":[{"x":"When an evolutionary world reaches the peak of its physical evolution, a volunteer pair is chosen, dematerialized, and carried to that world by seraphim.","r":["51:2.1","51:2.2"]},{"x":"On arrival they are rematerialized under the direction of the Life Carriers, and they remain in the unconsciousness of seraphic sleep throughout the process.","r":["51:2.4"]},{"q":"A principal ocupação desse casal importado é multiplicar-se e elevar os filhos do tempo.","r":"51:3.3"},{"x":"Adam and Eve do not mate directly with the evolutionary races; their children voluntarily unite with superior men and women brought to the garden.","r":["51:5.3"]},{"x":"With the added strain of the violet race, more progress is made in one hundred thousand years than in the previous million.","r":["51:5.6"]},{"x":"The garden schools teach practical arts, economics, and civil government, and with the schools of the Planetary Prince they set the pace of civilization.","r":["51:6.2","51:6.4"]}]},{"h":"The Link Between God and Man","items":[{"x":"Unlike the other planetary Sons, Material Sons are visible to mortals, understandable to them, and can actually associate with them.","r":["51:1.7"]},{"q":"Nesses Filhos e Filhas Materiais imortais, encontramos o último e indispensável elo que conecta Deus ao homem, elo este que reduz o abismo quase infinito entre o Criador eterno e as personalidades finitas inferiores do tempo.","r":"51:6.5"},{"x":"They can see the invisible Planetary Prince and his staff, and so they can interpret him to mortals.","r":["51:6.5"]},{"x":"On the ascending path mortals come to recognize seven fathers, the second of whom is the Planetary Adam, the father of the realm.","r":["51:6.6","51:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Adam and Eve of Urantia","items":[{"x":"The Adam and Eve who came to Urantia were number 14,311 of the senior corps on Jerusem and had been heads of the laboratory dealing with the modification of life forms.","r":["74:1.1","74:1.2"]},{"x":"They were overcome by the subtle counterplans of Caligastia and violated their covenant, but they did not join the Lucifer rebellion.","r":["51:3.4"]},{"q":"Não houve uma “queda do homem”.","r":"75:8.2"},{"x":"Though the divine plan miscarried, the Adamic bestowal left the peoples of Urantia biologically far better than before.","r":["75:8.1","75:8.3"]},{"x":"Adam and Eve awoke again on the mansion worlds in a special resurrection and returned to Jerusem as ascending citizens.","r":["76:6.2","76:6.3"]},{"q":"É o povo que faz uma civilização; a civilização não faz o povo.","r":"76:6.4"}]},{"h":"Ascending Material Sons","items":[{"q":"E, de fato, os Adãos Planetários — os Filhos e Filhas Materiais dos mundos evolucionários — são Filhos descendentes, pois descem aos mundos habitados vindos das suas altas esferas de origem, as capitais dos sistemas locais.","r":"40:2.1"},{"x":"An Adam and Eve who succeed in their mission may, once the world is settled in light and life, retire from administration and register as perfected Material Sons.","r":["40:2.2"]},{"x":"Material Sons whose planetary assignment is long delayed may also be released from citizenship status and advance toward Paradise with the ascending pilgrims.","r":["31:5.1"]},{"x":"Material Sons are rare in the finaliter companies but are always chosen as leaders, and an Edenic pair sometimes works together as one personality.","r":["31:5.3"]}]}],"see":["Adão e Eva","Raças","Corpo de Finalidade","Portadores da Vida","Criaturas intermediárias","Luz e vida"]},{"n":26,"t":"Filhos Instrutores da Trindade","en":"Trinity Teacher Sons","sum":"The Trinity Teacher Sons, or Daynals, are Sons who come directly from the Paradise Trinity and, together with the Creator Sons and the Magisterial Sons, make up the third order of Paradise Sons. They neither rule nor judge; they are the educators of the universes, dedicated to the moral enlightenment and spiritual awakening of mortals and spirit beings alike. On the evolutionary worlds they carry out the last divine mission, opening a spiritual age that leads a planet into the era of light and life.","sections":[{"h":"Sons of Trinity Origin","items":[{"x":"These Sons were brought into being by the Paradise Trinity; they are called Daynals in Havona, Trinity Teacher Sons in Orvonton, and Paradise Spiritual Sons on Salvington.","r":["20:7.1"]},{"q":"Esses seres formam o único grupo revelado a vós, de Filhos de Deus, cuja origem é a Trindade do Paraíso.","r":"19:1.3"},{"x":"Trinity in origin yet serving in the ministry of divine sonship, they hold a dual status as liaison beings between personalities of Trinity origin and those of dual origin.","r":["19:1.1"]},{"x":"Unlike the stationary Sons of the Trinity, whose number is fixed, the Teacher Sons keep increasing; the reported number is a little over twenty-one billion, with large reserves on Paradise besides.","r":["19:1.2","20:7.2"]},{"x":"They share the combined natures of the three Deities, yet in Havona they seem to reflect more of the Father, in the superuniverses the Eternal Son, and in the local creations the Infinite Spirit.","r":["20:7.4"]},{"q":"Em todos os universos, eles são a incorporação do serviço e a prudência da sabedoria.","r":"20:7.4"}]},{"h":"Sons Who Teach Rather Than Rule","items":[{"x":"They are neither creators nor retrievers, neither judges nor rulers, and so are not an organic part of the local or superuniverse governments.","r":["20:7.3"]},{"q":"Eles são os educadores universais, permanecendo dedicados ao despertar espiritual e à orientação moral de todos os reinos.","r":"20:7.3"},{"x":"They are sent directly to the superuniverse headquarters without preliminary training in the central universe, and having no spirit drawing power of their own, they use the spiritual influence of the Creator Sons and Magisterial Sons.","r":["20:7.5"]},{"x":"They begin their ministry in the local systems, advance through the constellations to the highest work of the local creation, and are equally concerned with educating mortals and native local universe beings such as the seraphim.","r":["20:8.1","20:8.2"]},{"x":"They are the faculty in charge of the qualifying tests and examinations for the lower stages of universe service, directing training courses from planetary schools up to the high colleges of wisdom on Salvington.","r":["20:8.3"]},{"x":"The educational system of Nebadon is jointly administered by the Teacher Sons and the Melchizedek teaching corps, and the whole universe is described as one vast school.","r":["37:6.1","37:6.2"]},{"x":"They adopt creature-trinitized sons as apprentices, train them, and may nominate them for the embrace of the Trinity.","r":["22:8.3","22:8.4"]}]},{"h":"Opening a Spiritual Age on a Planet","items":[{"x":"They have nothing to do with ending dispensations or judging the dead; they are wholly concerned with bringing the dawn of the era of spiritual realities to an evolutionary planet.","r":["20:9.2"]},{"q":"Eles tornam reais as contrapartes espirituais do conhecimento material e da sabedoria temporal.","r":"20:9.2"},{"x":"A planetary Teacher Son is assisted by seventy primary Sons, twelve secondary Sons, and three of the supreme order, and the corps remains for not less than a thousand years of planetary time.","r":["52:7.2","20:9.3"]},{"q":"Essa missão é uma contribuição da Trindade para com os esforços anteriores de todas as personalidades divinas que ministraram a um mundo habitado.","r":"52:7.2"},{"x":"Since they do not materialize to become visible to mortals, the Brilliant Evening Stars serve as liaison between the unseen corps of Teacher Sons and the mortals of the world.","r":["20:9.3","37:2.9"]},{"x":"In this age many mortals are translated from among the living, and as Adjuster fusion increases, natural death becomes less and less frequent.","r":["52:7.4"]}]},{"h":"Urantia and the Future of Light and Life","items":[{"x":"Having never passed through a spiritual age, Urantia is unfamiliar with these Sons, but Teacher Sons even now visit the world to plan their future sojourn.","r":["20:9.1"]},{"x":"They will appear after the inhabitants of this world have become relatively free from the shackles of animalism and the fetters of materialism.","r":["20:9.1"]},{"x":"No one knows whether the second coming promised by Jesus will come before or after the appearance of a Magisterial Son or of the Teacher Sons.","r":["52:7.1"]},{"x":"At the end of one of their repeated missions the Planetary Prince is elevated to the status of Planetary Sovereign, and the System Sovereign proclaims the opening of the era of light and life.","r":["52:7.10"]},{"q":"sooner or later the grace of God and the ministry of angels will usher in the day of the advent of the Trinity Teacher Sons;","r":"52:7.14"},{"x":"It is believed on Uversa that the Teacher Sons, long associated with the lives of evolutionary mortals, will be eternally united with the Corps of the Finality when the superuniverse is settled in light and life.","r":["20:9.5"]}]},{"h":"The Co-operation of the Three Paradise Sons","items":[{"x":"The Creator Sons reveal the character of the Father, the Avonals the mercy of the Eternal Son, and the Daynals the teaching personality of the Infinite Spirit; together they realize the sovereignty of God the Supreme.","r":["20:10.4"]},{"q":"Nos Filhos Instrutores da Trindade, o amor, a misericórdia e o ministério das três Deidades do Paraíso estão coordenados nos níveis de valores mais elevados do espaço-tempo e são apresentados, aos universos, como a verdade viva, a divina bondade e a verdadeira beleza espiritual.","r":"20:10.3"},{"x":"The Teacher Sons are the supreme co-ordinating personalities of Trinity origin; in the vast universe there is always great danger of narrow viewpoints and fragmented concepts of reality.","r":["19:1.4"]},{"q":"São os professores excelsos de todas as personalidades espirituais, sendo até mesmo os instrutores experimentados, aprovados e verdadeiros, dos próprios Filhos de Deus.","r":"20:8.4"}]}],"see":["Trindade do Paraíso","Filhos Avonais","Filho Criador Michael","Luz e vida","Melquisedeques","Corpo de Finalidade"]},{"n":47,"t":"Filiação a Deus","en":"Sonship with God","sum":"Sonship with God is the family relationship between the heavenly Father and the individual that becomes real when a person accepts God as Father by faith. At the center of the gospel of the kingdom that Jesus proclaimed stand the fatherhood of God and the sonship of man that follows from it. This sonship is not earned by deeds but received as a gift, and the indwelling Adjuster, the Spirit of Truth, and the Holy Spirit bear witness to this fact with the human spirit.","sections":[{"h":"Sonship Received by Faith","items":[{"x":"By accepting the status of sonship and believing in its reality, a person makes sonship with God an eternal reality.","r":["40:6.4"]},{"q":"Pela fé na paternidade de Deus, vós podeis entrar no Reino do céu, tornando-vos assim os filhos de Deus.","r":"142:1.3"},{"q":"Se receberdes Deus como o vosso Pai, então, de fato e verdade sois os filhos de Deus.","r":"142:5.2"},{"x":"Salvation is the gift of the Father, and those who receive it by faith partake of the divine nature and become sons or daughters of God.","r":["150:5.3"]},{"x":"The first condition for entering the kingdom is the faith and sincerity of coming as a little child and receiving the bestowal of sonship as a gift.","r":["170:2.21"]}]},{"h":"Why Mortals Are Sons","items":[{"x":"It is a solemn and sublime fact that lowly and material man is a faith child of the Most High.","r":["40:6.2"]},{"x":"Because the Creator Son became man and our elder brother, we who are his brothers are sons of the same Father.","r":["40:6.5"]},{"x":"We are sons because the spirit of the Son has been poured out upon all races, because we have received personality from the Father, and because a fragment of the Father indwells us.","r":["40:6.6","40:6.7","40:6.8"]},{"x":"Because the Holy Spirit, the Spirit of Truth, and the Adjuster are present together, mortals are qualified for the conscious realization of sonship with God.","r":["34:5.7"]},{"x":"The spirit bears witness not \"to\" our spirits but \"with\" our spirits that we are children of God.","r":["34:6.12"]},{"q":"he is your elder brother in fact","r":"40:6.5"}]},{"h":"From Servant to Free Son","items":[{"x":"The subjects of a kingdom hear the laws of a ruler, but one who discovers sonship by faith sees himself as the privileged son of a loving Father.","r":["141:2.2"]},{"x":"When the Father's will is your law, you are a noble slave; when the Father's will becomes your will, you are a free child of God.","r":["141:2.2"]},{"x":"As a good earthly father does not keep his children in anxiety, so the heavenly Father does not leave his faith children in doubt.","r":["142:5.2"]},{"q":"whosoever has been born of the spirit has in himself the power to overcome all doubt, and this is the victory that overcomes all uncertainty, even your faith.","r":"142:5.3"}]},{"h":"The Fruits of Sonship","items":[{"x":"Righteousness is not the condition of salvation but the natural fruit of the spirit-born life of sonship.","r":["150:5.5"]},{"q":"A compreensão da filiação é incompatível com o desejo de pecar.","r":"150:5.5"},{"x":"The evidence to the world of being born of the spirit is that believers sincerely love one another.","r":["142:5.4"]},{"x":"When we accept by living faith that our ideals come from a superhuman source, belief in sonship becomes effective and brotherhood becomes real.","r":["103:5.9"]},{"x":"Religion is the experience that leads from the bondage of primitive fear to the liberty of faith that realizes sonship with God.","r":["101:0.1"]},{"q":"and the evidence to all the world that you have been born of the spirit is that you sincerely love one another.\"","r":"142:5.4"}]},{"h":"The Center of the Gospel Jesus Proclaimed","items":[{"x":"By proclaiming that every mortal creature is a child of a loving Father, a son of God, Jesus raised the concept of the Father to a sublime experience.","r":["196:0.2"]},{"x":"Jesus told his disciples first to make known that God is Father and man his son, and only then to discuss doctrine.","r":["141:6.4"]},{"x":"Jesus said that people of other ages would better understand the gospel in family terms: the fatherhood of God, the brotherhood of man, and sonship with God.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom is the fact of the fatherhood of God joined with the truth of the sonship-brotherhood of men.","r":["194:0.4"]},{"x":"The Spirit of Truth came to lead believers into a growing consciousness of eternal and ascending sonship with God.","r":["194:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Irmandade dos homens","Reino do céu","Fé","Espírito da Verdade","Ajustador do Pensamento"]},{"n":74,"t":"Filosofia","en":"Philosophy","sum":"Philosophy is the effort of the human mind to weave the facts revealed by science and the values experienced by religion into one coherent view of the universe; it is the domain of wisdom. Its body is founded on material facts, while its soul and energy come from spiritual insight. The highest attainable philosophy rests on the reason of science, the faith of religion, and the truth insight of revelation, and the philosophic quest does not end even on Paradise.","sections":[{"h":"Wisdom Seeking Unity","items":[{"q":"É por meio da filosofia que a unidade fica mais bem localizada na experiência humana.","r":"102:2.6"},{"x":"The body of philosophic thought must be founded on material facts, but its soul and energy is mortal spiritual insight.","r":["102:2.6"]},{"x":"Philosophy arose from the effort to organize the separate findings of science and religion into a reasoned and unified attitude toward the universe.","r":["103:6.9"]},{"x":"Science is the domain of knowledge, religion the sphere of the faith experience, and philosophy the realm of wisdom.","r":["101:5.2"]},{"x":"Science is satisfied with a First Cause, religion with a supreme personality, and philosophy with unity.","r":["102:3.15"]},{"q":"A filosofia é uma tentativa do homem de unificar a experiência humana.","r":"196:3.30"}]},{"h":"The Place and Limits of Philosophy","items":[{"x":"In science the self observes the material world, philosophy observes this observation, and religion experiences the reality that observes it all.","r":["112:2.12"]},{"q":"A filosofia é, inevitavelmente, supracientífica. O homem é um fato material da natureza, mas a sua vida é um fenômeno que transcende os níveis materiais da natureza, pois ela tem os atributos de controle da mente e as qualidades criativas do espírito.","r":"195:7.9"},{"x":"Philosophy inclined to matter becomes naturalism, overweighted toward spirit becomes mysticism, and leaning on metaphysics ends in skepticism and confusion.","r":["103:6.14"]},{"x":"Philosophy should not project reality only by straight-line logic but should allow for the elliptic symmetry of reality and the curvature of relation concepts.","r":["103:6.14"]},{"x":"A philosophy useful to both science and religion avoids the extremes of materialism and pantheism and recognizes the reality of personality, the changeless in the midst of change.","r":["103:8.6"]}]},{"h":"The Highest Philosophy","items":[{"q":"A mais elevada das filosofias alcançáveis pelo homem mortal deve basear-se logicamente na razão da ciência, na fé da religião e no discernimento da verdade propiciados pela revelação.","r":"103:6.15"},{"x":"Philosophy clarified by revelation can function adequately even in the absence of the morontia mota and despite the failure of metaphysics.","r":["103:6.9","103:8.6"]},{"x":"True philosophy grows out of the wisdom that seeks to correlate the quantitative observations of science with the qualitative observations of religion.","r":["133:5.4"]},{"x":"The lower planes of the morontia mota join directly with the highest levels of human philosophy.","r":["48:7.1"]},{"x":"The ideal human state is one in which wisdom, faith, and experience work together, meaningfully fusing philosophy, religion, and science into one.","r":["98:2.12"]}]},{"h":"The Formation of a Philosophy of Religion","items":[{"x":"An individual's philosophy of religion is formed from many factors, including inner experience, environment, temperament, education, and social conditions.","r":["101:7.1"]},{"q":"Moral cowards never achieve high planes of philosophic thinking","r":"101:7.2"},{"x":"The philosophy of religion evolves through four levels, from conformity to tradition to fearless and sincere thinking and living.","r":["101:7.4"]},{"x":"A sound philosophy of religion distinguishes material and spiritual realities while recognizing their unity in intellectual striving and social service.","r":["101:7.5"]},{"x":"An effective philosophy of living weaves together cosmic insight and emotional reactions to the environment.","r":["140:4.8"]}]},{"h":"Philosophy in History and the Eternal Quest","items":[{"q":"Na Grécia, acreditar estava subordinado a pensar; na Palestina, o pensar era mantido como súdito do crer.","r":"98:2.8"},{"x":"The Greek philosophers achieved lofty ethical systems, but their concept of God dissolved in a pantheistic haze and failed to satisfy the masses' longing for salvation.","r":["98:2.9","98:2.10"]},{"x":"Religion has long endured without philosophy, but philosophy wholly unconnected with religion has seldom endured long.","r":["98:2.12"]},{"x":"Even on Paradise endless mysteries remain for philosophy to solve, and the exhilaration of philosophy is a satisfaction second only to worship.","r":["27:6.1"]},{"x":"The masters of philosophy on Paradise delight in leading ascenders in the thrilling quest of solving universe problems.","r":["27:6.2","27:6.5"]}]}],"see":["Sabedoria","Ciência e religião","Revelação","Verdade","Realidade","Morôncia"]},{"n":34,"t":"Fusão com o Ajustador","en":"Adjuster Fusion","sum":"Adjuster fusion is the event in which the evolving immortal soul becomes eternally one with the indwelling Thought Adjuster. It usually takes place on the mansion worlds after death, but rarely it is achieved by translation during the life in the flesh. Fusion announces to the universe the mortal's final choice to do the Father's will; by it the ascender's eternal career is assured, and the way opens to the Paradise Corps of the Finality.","sections":[{"h":"What Fusion Is","items":[{"q":"E essa fusão constitui o mistério de fazer um, de Deus e do homem, o mistério da evolução da criatura finita, mistério que é eternamente verdadeiro.","r":"112:7.2"},{"x":"Since the Adjuster is an immortal spirit, union with it confers eternal life on the soul of the fused mortal.","r":["40:7.1"]},{"x":"In fusion the Adjuster and the soul share all of each other's experiences and values and actually become one being.","r":["110:7.4","110:7.5"]},{"x":"The fused being is one personality, and no universe intelligence can distinguish the human and the Adjuster separately.","r":["112:7.8"]},{"x":"The fused Adjuster keeps its existential divine nature yet is transformed to the level of finite experience and inseparably linked with the ascending personality.","r":["107:2.7"]}]},{"h":"When It Occurs","items":[{"x":"Fusion usually occurs during the sojourn in the local system, and sometimes it is delayed until the ascender reaches the constellation or the local universe capital.","r":["112:7.3"]},{"x":"Fusion that is actually effective is often not achieved until the sojourn on the fifth or sixth mansion world.","r":["47:8.3"]},{"x":"When the seven cosmic circles are attained and the final choice of the will is added, fusion may occur during the life in the flesh, and the body is instantly consumed.","r":["110:7.2"]},{"x":"In the case of most Urantians, the Adjuster must wait patiently for the deliverance of death.","r":["110:7.6"]},{"q":"A morte natural, física, não é uma inevitabilidade para os mortais.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, fusion translations steadily increase, and by the fourth stage more than half of all mortals are translated from among the living.","r":["55:2.2","55:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Conditions of Fusion","items":[{"q":"A fusão com o Ajustador nunca ocorre até que os mandados do superuniverso tenham pronunciado que a natureza humana haja, de fato, feito uma escolha final e irrevogável pela carreira eterna.","r":"112:7.5"},{"x":"Until fusion an ascender may at any time forsake the Father's will, but fusion announces that he has chosen the Father's will without reservation.","r":["111:3.1"]},{"x":"The Adjuster of one who has made the supreme decision foresees the time of fusion and regards the union as an already existing fact.","r":["109:2.4"]},{"x":"When Adjuster fusion proclaims the final choice to the universe, the eternal destiny of the human being is assured.","r":["5:1.11"]}]},{"h":"The Scene of Fusion","items":[{"q":"and then, in the presence of such a survivor's morontia associates, these messengers of confirmation speak: \"This is a beloved son in whom I am well pleased.\"","r":"47:8.4"},{"x":"The new being is presented under a new name, spends forty days in spiritual retirement, and chooses a route to Havona.","r":["47:8.5"]},{"x":"On settled worlds the candidate for fusion departs in a flash of life before family and friends gathered in the temple.","r":["55:2.3","55:2.4"]},{"q":"the human beings who might witness such a spectacle would only observe the translating mortal disappear \"in chariots of fire.\"","r":"110:7.2"},{"x":"Those fused during the life in the flesh do not pass through death but go to the higher morontia spheres by direct Adjuster transit.","r":["49:6.18","49:6.19"]}]},{"h":"When Fusion Does Not Take Place","items":[{"x":"Mortals are divided into three groups according to their relation to the Adjuster: temporary indwelling, nonfusion, and fusion-potential types.","r":["40:5.4","40:5.5","40:5.7"]},{"x":"Mortals of primitive ages may survive through the ministry of Adjusters, yet they do not become eternally united with them.","r":["40:5.9","40:5.10"]},{"x":"Mortals of the nonfusion type are also indwelt by Adjusters throughout life, but if they survive, their souls fuse with spirit.","r":["40:5.13","40:5.14"]},{"x":"The few whose survival is recognized but who never become one with their Adjusters go, after the verdict of the courts of inquiry, on the path of fusion with the Son.","r":["40:8.1","40:8.3"]},{"q":"In the fusion experience there is no overlapping","r":"40:9.1"}]},{"h":"Results of Fusion","items":[{"q":"Quando a fusão com o Ajustador houver sido efetivada, não mais poderá haver perigo futuro para a carreira eterna de tal personalidade.","r":"112:7.4"},{"x":"Fusion confers on the personality actualities that were only potential: fixation of divinity qualities, past-eternity experience and memory, and immortality.","r":["112:7.1"]},{"x":"In matters of personality the human leads in the fused ascender, whose headquarters is Ascendington rather than Divinington.","r":["112:7.12"]},{"x":"The number of a fused Adjuster is stricken from the superuniverse records, and its destiny becomes the same as that of the ascending mortal: the Corps of the Finality.","r":["112:7.11","112:7.13"]},{"x":"Through fusion the Universal Father fulfills his promise to give himself to his material creatures.","r":["112:7.14"]},{"x":"Adjuster-fused mortals are the only human order that passes through the Havona circuits and finds God on Paradise.","r":["40:7.5"]}]}],"see":["Ajustador do Pensamento","Alma","Corpo de Finalidade","Mundos das mansões","Sobrevivência","Luz e vida"]},{"n":83,"t":"Governo e sociedade","en":"Government and Society","sum":"Government was not designed by anyone; it is an institution that evolved through trial and error in efforts to adjust human antagonisms and keep the peace. The Urantia Book traces its development from the council of elders to modern representative government and names the separation of executive, legislative, and judicial functions as the only sacred feature of government. It teaches that a state can never rise above the moral values of its citizens, and that true world peace will come when a government of all mankind is established.","sections":[{"h":"The Evolutionary Origin of Government","items":[{"x":"Once man had partly solved the problem of making a living, he faced the task of regulating human relations, and private property made government necessary.","r":["70:0.1"]},{"q":"O governo é um desenvolvimento inconsciente; ele evolui por meio de tentativas e de erros.","r":"70:0.3"},{"q":"A guerra é um estado natural e uma herança do homem em evolução; a paz é o padrão social que mede o avanço da civilização.","r":"70:1.1"},{"x":"Peace groups widened from the family to the clan, the tribe, and the nation, and then to the territorial state, now embracing many nations beyond ties of blood.","r":["70:4.1"]},{"x":"The first organ of government was the council of elders, which already contained the seeds of executive, legislative, and judicial functions.","r":["70:5.2","70:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Rights, Justice, and the Gifts of Society","items":[{"x":"Nature confers no rights on man, and the supreme gift of society to man is security.","r":["70:9.1"]},{"x":"Natural justice is a man-made theory; the only justice nature gives is the unfailing conformity of results to causes.","r":["70:10.1","70:10.2"]},{"x":"Liberty is a gift of civilization made possible by the enforcement of law; for one person to be absolutely free, another must be a slave.","r":["134:6.1"]},{"x":"The chief task of government is to define what is right, regulate class differences fairly, and enforce equality of opportunity under the rule of law.","r":["81:5.6"]}]},{"h":"Representative Government and the Separation of Powers","items":[{"x":"Universe administrators have learned by experience that evolutionary peoples are best governed by representative government with three balanced branches.","r":["70:12.1","70:12.2"]},{"q":"O único aspecto sagrado de qualquer governo humano é a divisão do estado nos três domínios de funções, o executivo, o legislativo e o judiciário.","r":"71:8.1"},{"x":"Mortals must create their own government and constitution and choose the ablest and most worthy as their leaders and judges.","r":["70:12.5"]},{"q":"A democracia, como um ideal, é um produto da civilização, não da evolução.","r":"71:2.1"},{"x":"Democracy carries dangers such as the glorification of mediocrity, the choice of ignorant rulers, and enslavement to public opinion.","r":["71:2.2","71:2.6"]},{"x":"Educating public opinion is the only safe way to accelerate civilization, and voting is the right method even when doing the wrong thing.","r":["71:2.7","71:2.8"]}]},{"h":"The Ideal State","items":[{"x":"What the state does matters more than its form of government, and no state can rise above the moral values of its citizens.","r":["71:3.1"]},{"x":"The ideal state is moved by three impulses: the love loyalty born of realizing brotherhood, wise patriotism, and cosmic insight.","r":["71:3.3","71:3.6"]},{"q":"O melhor estado é aquele que coordena o máximo, enquanto governa o mínimo.","r":"71:3.9"},{"x":"In advanced states political service is honored as the highest devotion of the citizen, and public office is regarded as an honor, not a burden.","r":["71:3.10","71:3.12"]},{"x":"An enduring state is founded on culture, ruled by ideals, and motivated by service, and its education aims at wisdom and spiritual values.","r":["71:7.1","71:7.2"]},{"x":"An economy of profit motivation alone is doomed unless supplemented by service motives, yet it must not be abolished suddenly before higher motives are established.","r":["71:6.1","71:6.3"]},{"x":"A continental nation on a neighboring planet, with a federation of one hundred states and a three-branch representative government, has a society more advanced than Urantia's.","r":["72:2.1","72:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Sovereignty and World Peace","items":[{"x":"Relative sovereignty exists on only two levels, the spiritual free will of the individual and the collective sovereignty of mankind as a whole; all groups between are temporary.","r":["134:5.2"]},{"q":"A soberania global impedirá as guerras globais — nenhuma outra coisa poderá fazê-lo.","r":"134:6.4"},{"x":"Even if all weapons were abolished, nations clinging to the illusion of national sovereignty would fight with fists and stones.","r":["134:6.6"]},{"x":"The Most Highs rule in the kingdoms of men to bring about the greatest good for all men, not for any chosen people.","r":["134:5.3","134:5.4"]}]},{"h":"The Believer and the State","items":[{"x":"Sonship in the kingdom should make believers better citizens of earthly nations, and believers bear a twofold duty to God and to man.","r":["178:1.4","178:1.5"]},{"x":"Believers must not worship temporal rulers nor try to extend the spiritual kingdom by temporal power.","r":["178:1.6"]},{"x":"The persistent spread of the gospel will in time separate politics from religion and bring intellectual and religious liberty to all peoples.","r":["178:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Civilização","Casamento e família","Irmandade dos homens","Justiça","Serviço","Reino do céu"]},{"n":13,"t":"Grande universo e universo-mestre","en":"Grand and Master Universe","sum":"O universo-mestre é a totalidade da criação, formada por seis níveis espaciais elípticos e concêntricos centrados no Paraíso: Havona, os sete superuniversos e os quatro níveis do espaço exterior. A parte atualmente organizada e habitada, Havona e os sete superuniversos, chama-se grande universo. Vastas criações futuras já estão tomando forma no espaço exterior, e os ascendentes do grande universo aperfeiçoado parecem destinados a servir ali nos tempos vindouros.","sections":[{"h":"Grande universo e universo-mestre","items":[{"x":"O universo central e divino, juntamente com os sete superuniversos que o circundam, chama-se grande universo: a criação atualmente organizada e habitada.","r":["0:0.6"]},{"x":"O universo-mestre inclui, além do grande universo, os universos do espaço exterior, ainda desabitados e em processo de organização.","r":["0:0.6"]},{"x":"Urântia pertence ao universo local de Nébadon, Nébadon ao sétimo superuniverso, Orvônton, e os sete superuniversos giram em torno do universo central de Havona.","r":["0:0.5","12:1.12"]},{"x":"O grande universo tem um potencial evolucionário de cerca de sete trilhões de planetas habitados, mas as suas bordas irregulares ainda não estão terminadas.","r":["12:1.13"]},{"q":"To created beings the master universe might appear to be almost infinite, but it is far from finished","r":"12:0.3"}]},{"h":"Seis níveis espaciais","items":[{"x":"O universo-mestre não é um plano infinito nem um círculo sem fim; funciona como uma única unidade espacial coordenada, com dimensões e limites definidos.","r":["12:1.1"]},{"x":"Do Paraíso para fora estão Havona, os sete superuniversos e quatro níveis do espaço exterior, dispostos como elipses concêntricas.","r":["12:1.3","12:1.9"]},{"q":"The Paradise-Havona System, the eternal universe encircling the eternal Isle, constitutes the perfect and eternal nucleus of the master universe","r":"12:1.11"},{"x":"Entre os níveis espaciais há zonas de relativa quietude, e os níveis sucessivos giram alternadamente em direções opostas, equilibrando as tensões da gravidade.","r":["11:7.7","12:4.15"]},{"q":"The central universe is the creation of eternity; the seven superuniverses are the creations of time","r":"12:1.16"},{"x":"Os quatro níveis do espaço exterior estão destinados a fazer manifestar-se e evoluir a ultimidade da criação.","r":["12:1.16"]}]},{"h":"As criações futuras do espaço exterior","items":[{"x":"O primeiro nível do espaço exterior é uma vasta zona de atividade energética que começa a cerca de meio milhão de anos-luz além da periferia do grande universo e se estende por mais de vinte e cinco milhões de anos-luz.","r":["12:1.14"]},{"x":"O espaço além dos sete superuniversos é considerado, em grande parte, domínio do Absoluto Inqualificável, e as suas energias são transmutadas pelos organizadores da força do Paraíso.","r":["12:2.1","12:2.4"]},{"x":"A energia e a matéria do espaço exterior já equivalem a muitas vezes a massa total dos sete superuniversos, mas ali não vivem seres materiais nem anjos conhecidos.","r":["12:2.4","12:2.5"]},{"x":"Cerca de noventa e cinco por cento da gravidade absoluta do Paraíso estão agora empenhados em manter sistemas materiais além das fronteiras dos universos atualmente organizados.","r":["12:3.8"]},{"x":"A gravidade espiritual atua quase inteiramente no grande universo, de modo que os universos exteriores parecem ainda não espirituais, ao passo que cerca de quinze por cento da gravidade da mente atuam fora do grande universo.","r":["12:3.9","12:3.10"]},{"q":"Uma criação maior, para o futuro, está em processo de formação.","r":"12:2.5"}]},{"h":"Espaço e tempo em expansão","items":[{"x":"A criação física de todo o espaço permeado está agora se expandindo uniformemente para fora, segundo o ciclo de respiração do espaço, de cerca de dois bilhões de anos.","r":["12:4.12"]},{"x":"As aparentes velocidades de afastamento dos universos distantes não são reais, mas decorrem de vários fatores de erro, como os ângulos de observação e as distorções do tempo-espaço.","r":["12:4.14"]},{"x":"O espaço origina-se do Paraíso, mas não é infinito, e o tempo e o espaço são inseparáveis apenas nas criações tempo-espaciais dos sete superuniversos.","r":["12:5.2","12:5.3"]},{"q":"Absolutamente nada é estacionário em todo o universo-mestre, exceto o centro mesmo de Havona, a eterna Ilha do Paraíso, o centro da gravidade.","r":"12:4.1"}]},{"h":"O cuidado que abrange o todo","items":[{"x":"As necessidades de todo o universo-mestre dependem dos Absolutos quanto ao potencial, do Último quanto à direção, do Supremo quanto à coordenação evolucionária e dos Arquitetos do Universo-Mestre quanto à administração inicial.","r":["12:6.8","12:6.12"]},{"x":"Os Arquitetos absonitos fazem os planos, os Supremos Criadores trazem-nos à existência e o Ser Supremo completa a sua plenitude.","r":["106:3.1"]},{"x":"A misericórdia é a atitude de Deus para com o indivíduo, e a equidade, a Sua atitude para com o todo, e a vontade de Deus finalmente prevalece em todo o universo dos universos.","r":["12:7.1"]},{"x":"O tempo e o espaço são um mecanismo cósmico que permite às criaturas finitas existir no cosmo juntamente com o Infinito.","r":["118:9.1"]},{"x":"Acredita-se que as novas criações do espaço exterior sejam o futuro campo de atividade dos Corpos de Finalidade que se estão reunindo.","r":["12:2.6"]},{"x":"Nas idades futuras, os sete superuniversos parecem destinados a tornar-se as escolas intermediárias dos seres do espaço exterior, e Havona, a sua escola de aperfeiçoamento final.","r":["14:6.41"]},{"q":"Nesse momento da eternidade futura, o universo-mestre ainda parecerá jovem; de fato, será sempre jovem, em face das possibilidades sem limites da eternidade, que nunca terá fim.","r":"106:7.8"}]}],"see":["Havona","Os sete superuniversos","Paraíso","Deus, o Último","Corpo de Finalidade","Tempo e espaço"]},{"n":18,"t":"Gravidade","en":"Gravity","sum":"A gravidade é a atração todo-poderosa com que a presença física do Paraíso mantém seguros os mundos de todo o espaço. Há no universo quatro circuitos absolutos: a gravidade da personalidade do Pai, a gravidade espiritual do Filho, a gravidade da mente do Agente Conjunto e a gravidade cósmica da Ilha do Paraíso, e eles operam independentemente do tempo e do espaço. A matéria é mantida pela gravidade do Paraíso e pela gravidade linear, mas, quanto mais espiritual se torna uma mente humana, menos ela responde à gravidade material e mais é atraída pela gravidade espiritual em direção ao Paraíso.","sections":[{"h":"O domínio todo-poderoso do Paraíso","items":[{"q":"A gravidade é a garra da atração todo-poderosa da presença física do Paraíso.","r":"11:8.1"},{"x":"O centro da gravidade material absoluta é a Ilha do Paraíso, complementada e equilibrada pelos corpos escuros de gravidade que circundam Havona e pelos reservatórios de espaço situados acima e abaixo.","r":["11:8.2"]},{"x":"O Controlador Universal está potencialmente presente nos circuitos da gravidade da Ilha do Paraíso, e essa presença alcança todas as partes do universo no mesmo grau, segundo a massa.","r":["3:1.7"]},{"x":"Uma vez que as linhas da gravidade vindas dos confins da criação convergem para a morada do Pai, o caos universal resultaria instantaneamente se Ele Se deslocasse desse lugar.","r":["11:1.4"]},{"x":"Cada novo universo requer um novo ajuste da gravidade, mas o poder de controle do Paraíso é suficiente mesmo para um universo infinito.","r":["3:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Os quatro circuitos absolutos","items":[{"x":"Há no universo quatro circuitos absolutos: a gravidade da personalidade do Pai, a gravidade espiritual do Filho, a gravidade da mente do Agente Conjunto e a gravidade cósmica da Ilha do Paraíso, e o Pai atua por meio de todos eles.","r":["12:3.1","12:3.5"]},{"q":"Eles são circuitos de presença absoluta e, como Deus, são independentes do tempo e do espaço.","r":"12:3.6"},{"x":"Toda gravidade está em circuito na Ilha do Paraíso, toda mente no Agente Conjunto, todo espírito no Filho Eterno e toda personalidade na presença pessoal do Pai.","r":["5:6.11"]},{"x":"Assim como o Pai atrai toda personalidade e o Filho toda realidade espiritual, o Agente Conjunto exerce um poder de atração sobre toda mente.","r":["9:6.2"]},{"x":"A atuação da gravidade da personalidade é sempre um ato volitivo do Pai Universal, e a realidade que responde ao seu circuito não pode ser medida.","r":["9:6.4","12:3.12"]}]},{"h":"Os estágios da gravidade física","items":[{"x":"A gravidade absoluta é a gravidade do Paraíso, ao passo que a gravidade local ou linear pertence ao estágio elétrico da energia e da matéria.","r":["11:8.3"]},{"x":"A energia responde à gravidade do Paraíso em três estágios: pré-gravidade (força), gravidade (energia) e pós-gravidade (potência do universo).","r":["11:8.4","11:8.5","11:8.7"]},{"x":"A gravidade linear torna-se plenamente operante quando aparece a organização atômica da matéria, ao passo que os ultímatons não combinados respondem somente à gravidade circular do Paraíso.","r":["42:6.2","42:6.3"]},{"q":"A gravidade é o único controle da matéria-energia.","r":"0:6.11"},{"x":"A gravidade linear é a força coesiva de curto alcance do grande universo, e a expressão “inversamente proporcional ao quadrado da distância” é apenas uma aproximação grosseira, por causa da influência do espaço.","r":["42:11.5"]},{"x":"O zero absoluto teórico nunca é realmente alcançado, por causa da presença e da ação da gravidade.","r":["42:4.6"]}]},{"h":"Equilíbrio e antigravidade","items":[{"q":"O espaço não reage à gravidade, mas age como um equilibrador da gravidade.","r":"11:8.3"},{"x":"O Espírito Infinito possui o poder da antigravidade, que não se observa nem no Pai nem no Filho, e pode transmiti-lo a personalidades superiores.","r":["9:3.2"]},{"x":"A disposição dos níveis espaciais, que giram alternadamente em direções opostas, impede que as pressões da gravidade se acumulem até pontos destrutivos.","r":["11:7.9"]},{"x":"Os corpos escuros de gravidade de Havona, com os seus cinturões interior e exterior girando em direções opostas, estabilizam perfeitamente o universo central.","r":["14:1.15"]},{"x":"Os universos atualmente organizados utilizam apenas cerca de cinco por cento da gravidade absoluta do Paraíso; o restante está empenhado em manter os sistemas materiais do espaço exterior.","r":["12:3.8"]}]},{"h":"A gravidade espiritual e a ascensão","items":[{"x":"A gravidade espiritual é livre de defasagem temporal, não é diminuída pelo espaço e não é retardada pela massa material.","r":["7:1.2"]},{"x":"As realidades espirituais respondem à gravidade espiritual segundo o seu valor qualitativo, assim como a matéria responde à gravidade física segundo a sua quantidade.","r":["7:1.3"]},{"q":"À medida que a mente de qualquer personalidade no universo torna-se mais espiritual — mais semelhante a Deus — ela passa a ser menos sensível à gravidade material.","r":"12:8.5"},{"x":"A ação da gravidade física é a medida quantitativa da energia não espiritual, e a ação da gravidade espiritual é a medida qualitativa da energia viva da divindade.","r":["12:8.5"]},{"x":"A espiritualidade no tempo e no espaço é medida inversamente à resposta à gravidade linear.","r":["42:11.4"]},{"q":"O circuito da gravidade do espírito atrai a alma do homem literalmente em direção ao Paraíso.","r":"7:3.2"}]}],"see":["Paraíso","Energia e matéria","Filho Eterno","Espírito Infinito","Os três Absolutos","Pai Universal"]},{"n":28,"t":"Guardiães seráficos","en":"Guardian Seraphim","sum":"Guardian seraphim are the seraphim who watch over individual mortals. When a person reaches the third circle, makes the supreme decision to become like God, or enters the reserve corps of destiny, a personal guardian, a guardian of destiny, is assigned. They work through outward circumstances without invading the human will; after death they hold the survival values of the soul, help with repersonalization on the mansion worlds, and accompany the ascender on the upward career. For seraphim this assignment is the surest way to Paradise.","sections":[{"h":"How Guardian Angels Are Assigned","items":[{"q":"The teaching about guardian angels is not a myth","r":"113:1.1"},{"x":"Since Michael's bestowal, seraphim are assigned not according to race but according to the intellect, spirituality, and destiny of human beings.","r":["113:1.2"]},{"x":"Ordinary people are cared for by guardian seraphim according to circle attainment: in groups of one thousand in the seventh circle, five hundred in the sixth, one hundred in the fifth, and ten in the fourth.","r":["113:1.6","113:1.7"]},{"x":"On reaching the third circle, a personal angel (actually two) is devoted wholly to that mortal.","r":["113:1.8"]},{"x":"When a person is enrolled in the reserve corps of destiny or makes the supreme decision, a true betrothal with the Adjuster, a personal guardian is assigned at once, whatever the circle.","r":["113:1.5"]},{"x":"For reservists chosen as guardians of planetary destiny, the chief of planetary seraphim appoints personal guardians of destiny.","r":["114:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Guardians of Destiny","items":[{"x":"Seraphim are not called guardians of destiny until the human has made the supreme decision, entered the third circle, or been mustered into the reserve corps of destiny.","r":["113:2.1"]},{"x":"The first mortal on Urantia to receive a personal guardian was Rantowoc, a wise man of the red race, long ago.","r":["113:2.2"]},{"x":"Assignments are always made from volunteers among experienced and tested seraphim, and more than a hundred seraphim have applied for the guardianship of a single person.","r":["113:2.3","113:2.7"]},{"x":"One of the pair is always on duty, while the complement acts as the person's recording angel, and the records are kept by the associated cherubim and sanobim.","r":["113:2.7","113:2.9"]},{"x":"Seraphim crave equally to attend an incarnated Son and to be attached as guardians of destiny, the latter being the surest passport to Paradise.","r":["39:1.6"]},{"x":"Angels feel lasting affection for their human associates, yet they find it hard to understand the animal fears that dominate even human faith.","r":["113:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Helping from Without, Not Within","items":[{"x":"The guardian personally co-ordinates the many impersonal influences of the Infinite Spirit and correlates them with the spirit presence of the Father and the Son.","r":["113:3.1","113:3.2"]},{"q":"Os servidores angélicos são dotados para combinar o amor do Pai e a misericórdia do Filho, nas suas ministrações às criaturas mortais.","r":"113:3.3"},{"x":"Whereas the Adjuster works from within through the soul, the seraphim act from without inward through the social, ethical, and moral environment of human beings.","r":["113:4.1"]},{"q":"The Adjuster is the essence of man's eternal nature; the seraphim is the teacher of man's evolving nature","r":"113:4.2"},{"x":"Accepting seraphic guidance does not make life easy; rather, one meets the rugged hills of moral choosing and spiritual progress.","r":["113:4.3"]},{"x":"The prayer impulse of God-conscious persons often arises from seraphic influence, and the guardian is most active when the Adjuster is least active.","r":["113:4.4","113:4.5"]}]},{"h":"A Ministry That Respects the Human Will","items":[{"q":"Os anjos não invadem o santuário da mente humana; eles não manipulam a vontade dos mortais; nem fazem contato direto com os Ajustadores residentes.","r":"113:5.1"},{"x":"Seraphim have no physical tears, bodies, or wings, yet they experience spiritual emotions somewhat like human feelings.","r":["113:5.2"]},{"x":"They do not respond directly to prayers but act on the orders of their superiors, and so they function independently of human whims and moods.","r":["113:5.3"]},{"q":"Não são supervisores nem diretores; são simplesmente guardiães.","r":"113:5.4"},{"x":"When a person charts his own course, the angels help make the best possible use of it, intervening only in emergencies and then usually on the orders of their superiors.","r":["113:5.4"]}]},{"h":"After Death and the Ascending Career","items":[{"x":"At death the guardian preserves the person's records, identity specifications, and the morontia reality of the soul, and awaits the awakening of its ward on the first mansion world.","r":["113:6.1","113:6.2"]},{"q":"O Ajustador identificar-vos-á; o serafim guardião irá repersonalizar-vos e então vos reapresentar ao fiel Monitor dos vossos dias na Terra.","r":"113:6.6"},{"x":"Those of the lower circles who had no personal guardian are reassembled by group guardians in the resurrection halls of the mansion spheres at the end of a dispensation.","r":["113:6.7"]},{"x":"Every mortal acquires a permanent guardian before leaving the mansion worlds, and that guardian stays until the ascender is enseconaphimed for the departure to Havona.","r":["113:7.4"]},{"q":"Para os serafins, o caminho mais seguro de alcançar as Deidades do Paraíso é o de guiar, com êxito, uma alma de origem evolucionária até os portais do Paraíso.","r":"113:7.7"},{"x":"Only pairs of guardians of destiny attain spiritual unity and enter the primary, or mortal, Corps of the Finality, becoming the eternal companions of human beings.","r":["113:7.8"]}]}],"see":["Serafins","Hostes angélicas","Ajustador do Pensamento","Mundos das mansões","Morte","Sobrevivência"]},{"n":12,"t":"Havona","en":"Havona","sum":"Havona é o universo central eterno, de um bilhão de mundos perfeitos, que circunda a Ilha do Paraíso. Não sendo produto da evolução, mas um universo criado perfeito desde o princípio, é o modelo de todos os universos, e os mundos dos seus sete circuitos são o campo final de treinamento pelo qual passam os peregrinos ascendentes dos universos do tempo antes de entrarem no Paraíso. Na sua perfeição, sem governo e sem pecado, Havona dá satisfação ao Pai e aos criadores e um encantamento sem fim aos ascendentes.","sections":[{"h":"O universo central eterno e perfeito","items":[{"x":"Havona é o universo perfeito e divino situado no centro de toda a criação, em torno do qual giram as vastas criações do tempo e do espaço.","r":["14:0.1"]},{"q":"É um universo criado em plenitude e perfeição; não se trata de um desenvolvimento evolucionário.","r":"14:0.2"},{"x":"Os Filhos Criadores aspiram a duplicar no tempo e a reproduzir no espaço a perfeição divina deste universo-modelo.","r":["14:0.2"]},{"x":"Havona não é exatamente finito nem absoluto; serve de amortecedor entre o Paraíso absoluto e as criações finitas.","r":["105:7.2"]},{"x":"Havona é eterno, mas não estático no sentido de não ter crescimento; nesta idade ele passa por certas mudanças progressivas em coordenação com os superuniversos em evolução.","r":["105:7.2","106:0.18"]}]},{"h":"Circuitos e estrutura","items":[{"x":"O bilhão de mundos de Havona está disposto em sete circuitos concêntricos que circundam os três circuitos dos satélites do Paraíso.","r":["14:1.9"]},{"x":"Cada circuito é permeado por um Espírito do Circuito, uma expressão especializada do Espírito Infinito, que coordena os assuntos celestes desse circuito.","r":["14:1.9"]},{"x":"Do lado de fora ficam os enormes corpos escuros de gravidade, que não refletem nem absorvem a luz e giram em direções opostas, ocultando e estabilizando Havona.","r":["14:1.14","14:1.15"]},{"x":"Um dia de Paraíso-Havona equivale a quase mil anos de Urântia e serve de tempo-padrão para os sete superuniversos.","r":["14:1.12","14:1.13"]},{"x":"A matéria de Havona está organizada em um sistema tríplice de energia, fundamentalmente diferente do sistema dual de energia dos superuniversos.","r":["14:2.2","14:2.6"]},{"q":"If a Urantia mortal could be transported to Havona, he would there be deaf, blind, and utterly lacking in all other sense reactions","r":"14:2.4"}]},{"h":"Mundos perfeitos sem governo","items":[{"q":"Quanto ao governo, no universo central, não há nenhum.","r":"14:3.1"},{"x":"Cada esfera de Havona é dirigida por um Eterno dos Dias, de origem trinitária, e é desenvolvida segundo os planos dele, com tal originalidade que não há duas iguais.","r":["14:3.3","14:5.6"]},{"x":"Em Havona nenhuma criatura, nativa ou peregrina, jamais pecou, e nenhuma alma ascendente jamais entrou antes do seu tempo.","r":["14:2.9"]},{"x":"A decadência e a morte não fazem parte do ciclo de vida de Havona; os seres vivos inferiores mudam de forma, mas nunca se desintegram.","r":["14:4.9"]},{"x":"Os nativos de Havona são descendentes da Trindade do Paraíso sem pais criaturas e, pela sua própria natureza, vivem a vontade de Deus.","r":["14:4.10","14:4.13"]}]},{"h":"O campo final de treinamento dos ascendentes","items":[{"x":"Os peregrinos do tempo chegam aos mundos de recepção do sétimo circuito e avançam para dentro, planeta por planeta e circuito por circuito, até que por fim alcançam o Paraíso.","r":["14:3.4"]},{"x":"O peregrino chega a Havona possuindo apenas uma perfeição: a perfeição de propósito, testada e comprovada.","r":["26:4.12","26:4.13"]},{"q":"A aptidão para compreender é o passaporte dos mortais para o Paraíso. A vontade de acreditar é a chave de Havona.","r":"26:4.15"},{"x":"Avançando para dentro através dos circuitos, o peregrino alcança sucessivamente a identidade de um Espírito Mestre, do Ser Supremo, do Espírito Infinito, do Filho Eterno e do Pai Universal.","r":["14:5.4"]},{"x":"A expressão “círculos de progresso”, aplicada à mente humana, deriva dessa disposição em circuitos do universo central.","r":["14:5.4"]}]},{"h":"Encantamento sem fim","items":[{"x":"A vida no universo central é tão rica e plena que transcende os conceitos humanos daquilo que os seres criados podem experimentar.","r":["14:5.2"]},{"q":"A monotonia não faz parte da carreira em Havona.","r":"14:5.9"},{"x":"Cada um do bilhão de mundos é uma verdadeira universidade de surpresas, e a cada circuito atravessado o peregrino encontra mudanças inimagináveis.","r":["14:5.9"]},{"x":"A aventura e a curiosidade, muitas vezes reprimidas na Terra, são dons divinos concedidos para serem plenamente satisfeitos nas longas idades por vir.","r":["14:5.10","14:5.11"]}]},{"h":"O propósito do universo central","items":[{"x":"O Pai obtém da perfeição de Havona uma satisfação paterna suprema e deleita-Se na adoração de criaturas perfeitas.","r":["14:6.6"]},{"x":"Havona é o campo de treinamento onde os Filhos Criadores se preparam para a criação de universos, e todo Filho Criador procura levar o seu próprio universo a esse nível de perfeição.","r":["14:6.27"]},{"x":"Havona é uma revelação da natureza espiritual perfeita do Ser Supremo e um prenúncio da Sua unificação futura.","r":["14:6.23","14:6.24"]},{"q":"O Paraíso é o lar, e Havona é a oficina, o local de estudos e lazer e a área de operações dos finalitores.","r":"14:6.39"},{"x":"Também nas idades futuras, Havona parece ter um potencial ilimitado como universo de treinamento para seres absonitos.","r":["14:6.41"]}]}],"see":["Paraíso","Os sete superuniversos","Ser Supremo","Ascensão mortal","Corpo de Finalidade","Grande universo e universo-mestre"]},{"n":96,"t":"Hostes angélicas","en":"Angelic Hosts","sum":"The angelic hosts are ministering spirits deriving from the Infinite Spirit: the supernaphim of the central universe, the seconaphim of the superuniverses, and the seraphim, cherubim, and sanobim of the local universes. They have no material bodies, yet they possess distinct individual personalities, and as associates of evolving will creatures they minister to man in daily life and through death and resurrection. Without ever invading the human will, the angels help mortals on their ascending journey with love and sympathy.","sections":[{"h":"Ministering Spirits of Time","items":[{"x":"The personalities of the Infinite Spirit comprise three orders: the angels, ministering spirits of time; the messenger hosts of space; and the higher spirits.","r":["38:0.1"]},{"x":"Supernaphim form the angelic corps of the central universe, seconaphim of the superuniverses, and seraphim, cherubim, and sanobim of the local universes.","r":["38:0.2","28:0.1"]},{"x":"Angels are associates of evolving and ascending will creatures and co-workers with divine personalities, and all are highly individualized, unique personalities.","r":["26:1.1"]},{"x":"In this revelation the word \"angels\" refers chiefly to the seraphic offspring of the Universe Mother Spirit who are concerned with the mortal survival plan.","r":["38:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Origin and Nature of the Seraphim","items":[{"x":"Seraphim are created by the Universe Mother Spirit in projections of 41,472 at a time, and they are still being created, since Nebadon is still in the making.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"q":"Os anjos não têm corpos materiais, mas são seres definidos, contínuos e discretos; são de natureza e origem espirituais.","r":"38:2.1"},{"x":"Angels are invisible to man, yet they perceive us as we are in the flesh and understand human emotions.","r":["38:2.1"]},{"x":"Seraphim are affectionate and sympathetic but not sex-emotional creatures, and they are much like what we will be on the mansion worlds.","r":["38:2.2"]},{"x":"The Infinite Spirit seeks to create uniformly perfect seraphim, but for unknown reasons the offspring are highly diverse.","r":["39:0.1"]},{"q":"Seraphim are still being periodically created","r":"38:1.3"}]},{"h":"The Angelic Orders","items":[{"x":"Local universe seraphim are divided into seven orders: supreme, superior, supervisor, and administrator seraphim, planetary helpers, transition ministers, and seraphim of the future.","r":["39:0.2","39:0.8"]},{"x":"It is hard to say that any seraphim are inferior to other groups, and the higher orders are the more eager to be assigned to lowly service.","r":["39:0.9","39:0.11"]},{"x":"Cherubim and sanobim, of the same origin as seraphim, are the lowest angelic order; affectionate and almost human, they faithfully assist the seraphim.","r":["38:7.1","38:7.3"]},{"x":"Cherubim are positive senior personalities and sanobim negative complemental ones, and the two are functionally united as one.","r":["38:7.2"]},{"x":"Seraphim may reach Paradise by several paths, such as elevation to Evening Stars or completion of specialized service.","r":["39:8.1","39:8.3"]}]},{"h":"Angels Beside Man","items":[{"q":"The teaching about guardian angels is not a myth","r":"113:1.1"},{"x":"Since Michael's bestowal, seraphim are assigned not by race but according to human intellect, spirituality, and destiny.","r":["113:1.2"]},{"q":"Os anjos não invadem o santuário da mente humana; eles não manipulam a vontade dos mortais; nem fazem contato direto com os Ajustadores residentes.","r":"113:5.1"},{"x":"Angels are very near us and truly care for us; though they have no physical tears, they have spiritual emotions.","r":["113:5.2"]},{"x":"Seraphim work on our behalf under the orders of their superiors, regardless of our requests or whims.","r":["113:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Guides Through Death and Resurrection","items":[{"x":"Jesus said there is joy in the presence of the angels of heaven over one sinner who repents.","r":["167:7.5"]},{"q":"Os anjos são os guias seguros e celestes da alma do homem, durante o período, desconhecido e indefinido, de tempo que se interpõe entre a morte da carne e a nova vida nas moradas espirituais”.","r":"167:7.6"},{"x":"On first awakening on the mansion worlds we actually see for the first time the angelic companions who were always with us on earth.","r":["113:7.1"]},{"x":"On the morontia spheres the two attending seraphim, now open companions, aid our progress while they themselves learn and grow.","r":["113:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Seraphim in Planetary Government","items":[{"q":"OS ALTÍSSIMOS governam nos reinos dos homens por meio de forças, agentes e agências celestes, mas principalmente por meio da ministração dos serafins.","r":"114:0.1"},{"x":"At one noon roll call the planetary angels and guardians of Urantia numbered more than five hundred million pairs of seraphim.","r":["114:0.2"]},{"x":"When the Spirit of Truth was poured out, twelve corps of the master seraphim of planetary supervision came to Urantia with the first resident governor general.","r":["114:6.1","114:6.2"]},{"x":"It is through the ministry of angels that one world can keep in touch with other worlds.","r":["167:7.4"]}]}],"see":["Serafins","Guardiães seráficos","Espírito Infinito","Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Mundos das mansões","Criaturas intermediárias"]},{"n":48,"t":"Irmandade dos homens","en":"Brotherhood of Man","sum":"The brotherhood of man is the universal relationship that follows from the fact that every personality is a child of the same heavenly Father. Because God loves each individual and that love reaches all, people are bound together as brothers. Jesus taught the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man as the center of the gospel, and its realization depends not on law or force but on mutual understanding and love, and on the spiritual transformation of mankind.","sections":[{"h":"Brotherhood Flowing from Fatherhood","items":[{"x":"God loves each person as an individual child, yet because that love reaches all, a universal brotherhood arises.","r":["12:7.8","12:7.10"]},{"x":"Brotherhood is a relationship of the whole, not of the parts: the good of each helps all, and the evil of each adds to the suffering of all.","r":["12:7.11"]},{"q":"O discernimento espiritual. A irmandade dos homens é, afinal, baseada no reconhecimento da paternidade de Deus.","r":"52:6.7"},{"x":"When the belief that we are sons of God becomes effective, the feeling of brotherhood, an altruistic conviction, also becomes real.","r":["103:5.9"]}]},{"h":"The Brotherhood Jesus Taught","items":[{"x":"Jesus taught a new and greater brotherhood beyond the family of blood, the brotherhood of the sons of God.","r":["140:8.14"]},{"x":"Jesus named two laws of the heavenly family, loving the Father and loving one's brother as oneself, and said that brotherly love shows itself in unselfish service.","r":["142:7.4"]},{"q":"Amai uns aos outros como eu vos amei.","r":"180:1.1"},{"x":"Jesus also used such expressions as the family of God, the fellowship of believers, and the brotherhood of man to refer to the kingdom.","r":["170:2.24"]},{"x":"The religion Jesus founded consists in the personal experience of doing the will of God and serving the human brotherhood.","r":["196:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Spiritual Brotherhood and Social Brotherhood","items":[{"q":"O Reino do céu não é nem de ordem social nem de ordem econômica; é uma fraternidade exclusivamente espiritual, de indivíduos sabedores de Deus.","r":"99:3.2"},{"x":"Since the kingdom of heaven is a spiritual brotherhood of spirit-born sons, it can be proclaimed only by the power of the spirit, not by physical force.","r":["178:1.2"]},{"x":"Jesus showed the way to the immediate attainment of spiritual brotherhood, but social brotherhood depends on many personal and planetary changes.","r":["52:6.2"]},{"x":"Religious brotherhood cannot be realized unless all religions give up their claims of ecclesiastical authority and spiritual sovereignty.","r":["134:4.4"]},{"q":"A revelação religiosa é essencial à realização da irmandade em Urântia.","r":"52:6.2"}]},{"h":"The Way to Brotherhood","items":[{"x":"Social contact through travel, commerce, and exchange, and intellectual cross-fertilization through acquaintance with one another's thought, hasten brotherhood.","r":["52:6.3","52:6.4"]},{"x":"Ignorance breeds suspicion, and suspicion cannot coexist with sympathy and love.","r":["52:6.4"]},{"x":"Ethical awakening, political wisdom, and above all spiritual insight are needed for the realization of brotherhood.","r":["52:6.5","52:6.6","52:6.7"]},{"x":"The quickest way to brotherhood is spiritual pressure from above, enlarging the soul's capacity to understand and love one another.","r":["52:6.7"]},{"x":"On an isolated world like Urantia, religious revelation is essential for realizing brotherhood.","r":["52:6.2"]},{"q":"A ignorância gera a suspeita, e a suspeita é incompatível com a atitude essencial de compaixão e amor.","r":"52:6.4"}]},{"h":"The Contagion of Love and Future Civilization","items":[{"x":"No one can love his fellows by willpower alone; love is born of a thoroughgoing understanding of a neighbor's motives and sentiments.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"q":"Não é tão importante amar a todos os homens hoje quanto é importante que aprendais, a cada dia, a amar um ser humano a mais.","r":"100:4.6"},{"x":"If every person became a focus of love, that love would encompass all civilization, and the brotherhood of man would be realized.","r":["100:4.6"]},{"x":"The secret of a better civilization lies in Jesus' teachings about brotherhood, the good will of love and mutual trust.","r":["194:3.12"]},{"x":"The progress of civilization leads to the social achievement of the brotherhood of man and the personal status of God-consciousness.","r":["71:4.15"]},{"x":"The hope of modern Christianity lies in learning anew the living gospel of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man.","r":["195:10.21"]}]}],"see":["Filiação a Deus","Pai Universal","Reino do céu","Amor","Serviço","Civilização"]},{"n":62,"t":"Justiça","en":"Justice","sum":"Justice is the application of law; it is not the personal attitude of any one Deity but a collective function of the Paradise Trinity. The Ancients of Days and the Trinity-origin Sons render its verdicts, the personalities of the Infinite Spirit supply the evidence, and justice is always tempered by mercy. Man's idea of justice evolved from blood vengeance to the courts of the state, and Jesus taught that justice should be left to the group while the individual shows mercy.","sections":[{"h":"A Collective Function of the Trinity","items":[{"x":"Law issues from the Father, its administration belongs to the Son, its revelation and interpretation to the Spirit, and justice, the application of law, to the Trinity.","r":["10:6.1"]},{"q":"A Justiça nunca é uma atitude pessoal; é sempre uma função plural.","r":"10:6.2"},{"x":"Evidence for fairness is presented by personalities of the Infinite Spirit, and verdicts are rendered by the stationary Sons of the Trinity.","r":["10:6.3","10:6.4"]},{"x":"The Ancients of Days render the decisions of supreme equity in the seven superuniverses, but in perfect Havona this function exists only in theory.","r":["10:6.17"]},{"x":"The Supreme Trinity Personalities represent justice throughout the grand universe and function as the executive judgment of the Trinity.","r":["18:0.10"]}]},{"h":"The Justice and Fairness of God","items":[{"q":"The justice of the Universal Father cannot be influenced by the acts and performances of his creatures","r":"2:3.1"},{"x":"It is futile to plead with God to escape the just results of natural law and spiritual mandates, for one reaps what one sows.","r":["2:3.2"]},{"x":"Mercy guides God's attitude toward the individual, while fairness guides his attitude toward the whole.","r":["12:7.1"]},{"q":"A justiça é o pensamento coletivo da retidão; a misericórdia é a sua expressão pessoal.","r":"10:6.18"},{"x":"When fully understood, the righteous justice of the Trinity and the merciful love of the Father coincide as one.","r":["10:6.18","2:4.4"]}]},{"h":"The Execution of Justice and Its Delay","items":[{"x":"The final result for a being wholly identified with sin is annihilation, but its execution is delayed until the appointed processes of justice are fulfilled.","r":["2:3.2","2:3.3"]},{"x":"Between identification with sin and the execution of the sentence there must be time enough to satisfy all concerned, even the sinner himself.","r":["54:3.2","54:3.3"]},{"q":"Há uma lei básica de justiça, no universo, da qual a misericórdia é impotente para se desviar.","r":"146:2.5"},{"x":"The seraphic advocate of the courts is the mortal's defender, representing the element of mercy inherent in justice, the fairness that knows motives and tendencies.","r":["39:1.8"]},{"x":"At the adjudication of survival the Memory of Mercy is read, and justice prevails only when mercy has been exhausted.","r":["28:6.6","28:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Justice as It Evolved in Human Society","items":[{"q":"A justiça natural é uma teoria do homem; não é uma realidade.","r":"70:10.1"},{"x":"Man's idea of justice is getting his rights; though latent in the spirit-endowed mind, it grew by evolution.","r":["70:10.2"]},{"x":"Primitive society substituted trial by ordeal and blood vengeance for justice, ignoring motive and judging only by the injury inflicted.","r":["70:10.3","70:10.5","70:10.9"]},{"x":"The true administration of justice begins when vengeance is taken from the individual and the kin and given to the state.","r":["70:10.13"]},{"x":"It gradually became clear that the certainty and swiftness of punishment deter crime more than its severity.","r":["70:10.15"]}]},{"h":"Justice as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"q":"O governo civil funda-se na justiça, como a verdadeira religião funda-se na misericórdia”.","r":"132:4.8"},{"x":"A magistrate's duty is not only to punish the guilty but to acquit the innocent, so that injustice befalls not even the humblest citizen.","r":["132:4.8"]},{"x":"The individual should show mercy, but fixing punishment should be left to groups and their representatives who know all the circumstances.","r":["133:1.2","159:1.6"]},{"x":"Jesus possessed a firm sense of justice, but it was always tempered by mercy, and he recognized society's right to punish criminals.","r":["140:8.12","140:8.4"]},{"q":"Tende fé — confiança no triunfo final da justiça divina e da bondade eterna.","r":"140:8.8"}]}],"see":["Misericórdia","Trindade do Paraíso","Anciães dos Dias","Governo e sociedade","Pecado","Bondade"]},{"n":41,"t":"Livre-arbítrio","en":"Free Will","sum":"Free will is the power of choice that the Universal Father gives together with personality. God himself is the original personality with absolute free will, and man shares that will on a relative and finite level. Especially in matters of eternal survival the mortal's choice holds a sovereignty that no being can invade, so free will becomes the key by which man builds his own destiny.","sections":[{"h":"The Free Will of God","items":[{"x":"God is not an automatic force bound by law but the original personality possessed of free will.","r":["12:7.6"]},{"x":"God's free will is conditioned only by his own divine nature and perfect attributes.","r":["4:4.3"]},{"x":"He shares personality and goodness with his creatures, but infinity of will belongs to God alone.","r":["4:4.4"]},{"x":"Even though God foreknows the acts of his children, that foreknowledge does not abrogate their freedom.","r":["3:3.4","118:7.1"]}]},{"h":"The Gift of Choice Given to Personality","items":[{"x":"The two marks that distinguish creature personality are self-consciousness and the associated relative free will.","r":["16:8.5","16:8.6"]},{"x":"Man's relative free will relates to such higher functions as moral decision, spiritual choice, unselfish love, and worship.","r":["16:8.7","16:8.13","16:8.14"]},{"x":"The bestowal of personality adds to a living organism the prerogatives of self-determination and self-evolution.","r":["118:7.6"]},{"q":"O homem mortal é dotado de livre-arbítrio, de poder de escolha e, embora essa escolha não seja absoluta, contudo, ela é relativamente final, no nível finito e no que concerne ao destino da personalidade que escolhe.","r":"118:6.4"},{"q":"O homem é verdadeiramente o arquiteto do seu próprio destino eterno.","r":"103:5.10"}]},{"h":"A Will That No One Invades","items":[{"x":"God has decreed that in matters of eternal survival no being or force can interfere with the free will of a mortal.","r":["5:6.8"]},{"q":"No personal creature can be coerced into the eternal adventure;","r":"5:6.12"},{"x":"The Adjuster brings a plan for the ideal life but never arbitrarily moves man's choices; it always respects his will.","r":["110:2.1"]},{"q":"No human being will ever be spiritualized by a divine Monitor against his will;","r":"110:2.2"},{"x":"Angels, too, do not invade the sanctity of the human mind or manipulate the will, and they have no authority to curtail the prerogatives of choice.","r":["113:5.1"]},{"x":"Even a rebel like Caligastia could not force a normal person to do anything against that person's will.","r":["66:8.6"]}]},{"h":"True Liberty and False Liberty","items":[{"x":"True liberty is the reward of evolutionary progress; false liberty is a subtle deception born of the errors of time.","r":["54:1.2"]},{"q":"A verdadeira liberdade é fruto do controle de si próprio; a liberdade falsa é fruto da pretensão da afirmação do ego.","r":"54:1.6"},{"x":"Liberty without self-mastery is an illusion, and license masquerading as liberty is the forerunner of bondage.","r":["54:1.5"]},{"x":"The Lucifer rebellion paraded as liberty, but in reality it threatened to rob creatures of their freewill participation.","r":["54:2.3"]},{"x":"Sin arises from an immaturity that, dazzled by freedom of the will, fails to grasp the obligations of universe citizenship.","r":["118:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Responsibility of Choice and Destiny","items":[{"x":"Energy systems have no choice, but man, by the choices of his free will, has everything to do with determining his own destiny.","r":["112:5.3"]},{"x":"The power of choice is both the greatest opportunity and the supreme responsibility, and the Adjuster, the Father, and the Supreme Being depend on its faithfulness.","r":["112:5.5"]},{"x":"On the lower levels the range of choice is narrow, but as one ascends the universe, choice becomes ever freer.","r":["118:7.8"]},{"x":"Choosing the will of God is not the surrender of will but its consecration, enlargement, and perfection.","r":["111:5.5"]},{"q":"the portal of eternity opens only in response to the freewill choice of the freewill sons of the God of free will.","r":"5:6.12"}]}],"see":["Personalidade","Vontade de Deus","Sobrevivência","Ajustador do Pensamento","Pecado","Rebelião de Lúcifer"]},{"n":93,"t":"Luz e vida","en":"Light and Life","sum":"Light and life is the final evolutionary attainment of the worlds of time and space, the age in which a planet at last becomes settled after the successive ministries of the divine Sons. In this age the planet flourishes under one language, religion, and philosophy, war and poverty disappear, and many mortals fuse with their Adjusters without passing through death and are translated to the morontia career. This settledness begins with the planet and widens through seven stages to the system, constellation, local universe, and superuniverse.","sections":[{"h":"The Final Goal of Evolutionary Worlds","items":[{"q":"PARA um mundo do tempo e do espaço a idade de luz e vida é a realização evolucionária final.","r":"55:0.1"},{"x":"An inhabited world passes through the ages of the Planetary Prince, Adam, the Magisterial Son, and the bestowal Son, and is prepared for this age by the ministry of the Trinity Teacher Sons.","r":["55:0.1","52:7.2"]},{"x":"This age begins when the Teacher Sons complete their final mission and continues on that world without end.","r":["55:0.2","55:0.3"]},{"x":"Light and life unfolds in seven stages: planet, system, constellation, local universe, minor sector, major sector, and superuniverse.","r":["55:0.4","55:0.11"]}]},{"h":"The Morontia Temple and the New Rule","items":[{"x":"The appearance of the morontia temple at the planetary capital is the certificate that the world has entered light and life.","r":["55:1.1"]},{"x":"At the center of the temple is the shrine of the bestowal Son, flanked by the seats of the Planetary Sovereign and the chief of finaliters.","r":["55:1.2"]},{"x":"The temple is said to \"come down from heaven,\" but in fact it is built on the spot by the morontia power supervisors from designs made at the system capital.","r":["55:1.3"]},{"x":"In this age the Planetary Prince is elevated to Planetary Sovereign, and finaliters who have reached Paradise return to take part in planetary affairs.","r":["55:7.1","55:4.1"]},{"x":"The visible actual rulers are the Material Son and Daughter, and this arrangement has given renown throughout the universe to the idea of king and queen.","r":["55:7.2"]}]},{"h":"Translation Without Death","items":[{"q":"A morte natural, física, não é uma inevitabilidade para os mortais.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"Most citizens living in the final era of light and life do not die but are translated directly from the life in the flesh to the morontia existence.","r":["55:2.1","55:2.2"]},{"x":"When fusion is near, the candidate withdraws from duties and, in the morontia temple with family and friends gathered, is translated in a \"flash of life.\"","r":["55:2.3","55:2.4"]},{"x":"Those who come from such worlds are far better prepared to continue the ascent than those from disordered worlds like Urantia.","r":["55:2.10"]}]},{"h":"Life on a Settled World","items":[{"x":"The world attains one language, one religion, and normally one race, yet it is not perfect, for it still has hospitals, accidents, and senility.","r":["55:3.1"]},{"x":"One first-stage world collected a tenth of its income and spent it on truth, beauty, goodness, and disaster relief.","r":["55:3.2","55:3.6"]},{"x":"Most public offices, education, and judicial work were shared by men and women, and the highest honor was the order of \"supreme service.\"","r":["55:3.8","55:3.9"]},{"q":"A guerra transformou-se em uma questão histórica e não há mais exércitos armados nem forças policiais.","r":"55:5.4"},{"x":"As self-control replaces law, government gradually shrinks, and its extent is in inverse proportion to the morality and spirituality of the citizens.","r":["55:5.4"]},{"x":"Poverty and social inequality all but vanish, and economic life becomes ethical.","r":["55:5.2","55:5.3"]}]},{"h":"Still Mortal","items":[{"q":"Essa grande evolução não é o céu; mas é um prognóstico sublime a antever os mundos divinos, na ascensão ao Paraíso.","r":"55:6.2"},{"x":"Society grows more peaceful, and people become more altruistic and fraternal without losing independence or family love.","r":["55:6.1"]},{"x":"Even on such worlds there is still abundant potential evil to stimulate choice between truth and error, good and evil.","r":["55:3.10"]},{"x":"Communion with the Adjusters deepens from age to age, and the ministry of the Holy Spirit and the angels becomes ever more effective.","r":["55:6.4"]},{"q":"Não houvesse nenhum futuro de progresso eterno para a criatura, ainda assim as realizações evolucionárias magníficas das raças mortais, nesses mundos estabelecidos de realizações perfeccionadas, justificariam amplamente a criação do homem nos mundos do tempo e do espaço.","r":"55:6.9"}]},{"h":"Urantia and Light and Life","items":[{"x":"Urantia's greatest handicaps are disease, degeneracy, war, multicolored races, and multilingualism.","r":["55:3.21"]},{"q":"Nenhum mundo evolucionário pode esperar progredir além do primeiro estágio do estabelecimento em luz, antes de alcançar a unidade de língua, antes de ter uma única religião e uma só filosofia.","r":"55:3.22"},{"x":"When Urantia reaches that age, Machiventa Melchizedek will assume the place of Planetary Sovereign.","r":["55:7.3"]},{"x":"Even on an isolated world personal attainment is not thwarted; Jesus of Nazareth personally achieved the status of light and life on Urantia.","r":["55:11.7"]}]}],"see":["Urântia","Fusão com o Ajustador","Corpo de Finalidade","Filhos e Filhas Materiais","Evolução","Ser Supremo"]},{"n":67,"t":"Mal","en":"Evil","sum":"Evil is not created by God; it is the shadow cast when immature creatures in an imperfect finite world reject the light or choose wrongly. Evil is the unintended transgression of the Father's will and so differs from sin; when deliberately embraced, it becomes sin. Potential evil is necessary for free will and moral choice, but actual evil need not be experienced, and God brings ultimate good even out of the evil of time.","sections":[{"h":"The Nature of Evil","items":[{"x":"God is so positively good that there is no room for negative evil in him, and he does not create evil.","r":["130:1.5","54:0.2"]},{"q":"O mal é a escuridão inevitável que persegue os passos da pouca sabedoria, que rejeita a luz.","r":"130:1.5"},{"q":"“O mal é a transgressão inconsciente ou não intencional da lei divina, a vontade do Pai.","r":"148:4.3"},{"x":"Evil is a partial realization of, or maladjustment to, universe reality and indicates a deficiency of wisdom.","r":["67:1.4","67:1.5"]},{"x":"Evil is the misapplication of plans and the maladjustment of techniques, producing universe disharmony and planetary confusion.","r":["75:4.3"]}]},{"h":"A Relative Shadow","items":[{"q":"O mal é um conceito de relatividade. Surge da observação das imperfeições que sobressaem, na sombra projetada por um universo finito de coisas e seres, à medida que tal cosmo obscurece a luz viva da expressão universal das realidades eternas do Único Infinito.","r":"130:4.13"},{"x":"Evil arises from observing the imperfections in the shadow cast when a finite universe obscures the living light of the Infinite.","r":["130:4.13"]},{"x":"Error is the inevitable shadow of incompleteness cast upon the ascending path toward Paradise perfection, not an actual universe quality.","r":["130:4.11"]},{"x":"For relative good to appear, contrast with comparative evil, an imperfection that is not sin, is always necessary.","r":["4:3.6"]},{"x":"Ascending the universe scale, goodness increases and evil decreases, but the possibility of experiencing evil remains until final spirit levels are attained.","r":["132:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Free Will and Potential Evil","items":[{"x":"For evolving man to be free he must be able to err; the only world without the possibility of error is one without free intelligence.","r":["3:5.15"]},{"x":"By giving the power to choose between truth and error, the Father created potential negation, but evil actually exists only when creatures choose it.","r":["130:1.6"]},{"q":"Para que possa haver a escolha moral, a possibilidade do mal é necessária, mas não a realidade do mal.","r":"132:2.10"},{"x":"The finite mind's imperfect comprehension of the infinite is itself potential evil; when it is not corrected and error grows, it becomes actual evil.","r":["130:4.14"]},{"x":"Evil deliberately chosen becomes sin, and the persistent pursuit of sin and error becomes iniquity.","r":["54:0.2","130:1.6"]}]},{"h":"How Evil Appears","items":[{"q":"evil always results when purely personal evaluations are elevated to the levels of absolutes.","r":"100:1.1"},{"q":"O mal é uma parcialidade da criatividade, que tende para a desintegração e a destruição final.","r":"111:4.11"},{"x":"All inner conflict is evil because it inhibits the creative function; it is a kind of civil war within the personality.","r":["111:4.11"]},{"x":"Suffering is latent in evil, but much suffering has come from sin and iniquity, and the Father does not send suffering as punishment.","r":["148:5.3"]},{"x":"Man should not blame God for the results of his own choices but should overcome earthly suffering through intelligent effort.","r":["148:5.3"]}]},{"h":"The Wisdom That Permits Evil","items":[{"x":"For creatures to be truly free, the possibility of evil and sin is unavoidable, and the rulers do not deprive any being of freedom.","r":["54:3.1"]},{"x":"The Father allows good and evil to grow together, like wheat and tares, until the end of life.","r":["130:1.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks teach that the good resulting from the Satania rebellion is more than a thousandfold the sum of all the evil.","r":["54:6.6"]},{"x":"As wisdom grows through ascension, one better understands how ultimate good arises out of time-limited evil.","r":["54:6.10"]},{"x":"Even man's experience of evil is part of God's unending self-realization in the children of time.","r":["2:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Pecado","Livre-arbítrio","Bondade","Rebelião de Lúcifer","Adversidade e provações","Sabedoria"]},{"n":79,"t":"Maquiventa Melquisedeque","en":"Machiventa Melchizedek","sum":"Machiventa Melchizedek was a Melchizedek who incarnated as an emergency Son at Salem in Palestine 1,973 years before the birth of Jesus, at a time when the truth of the one God was dying out after Adam's failure. For ninety-four years he taught the covenant that God's favor is received by faith alone in El Elyon, the Most High, and through Abraham he ensured that this truth would be carried on. He prepared the way for Michael's bestowal and is now called the vicegerent Planetary Prince of Urantia.","sections":[{"h":"Incarnation of an Emergency Son","items":[{"x":"For thousands of years after the failure of Adam's mission, revealed truth was in danger of extinction, and by about 3000 B.C. the concept of God had grown very dim.","r":["93:1.1"]},{"x":"Machiventa volunteered from among the twelve planetary receivers and made an emergency Son incarnation, one of only six in the history of Nebadon.","r":["93:1.3"]},{"q":"Maquiventa outorgou-se às raças humanas de Urântia 1 973 anos antes do nascimento de Jesus.","r":"93:2.1"},{"x":"He appeared in the tent of the herder Amdon, ate material food for the first time, and that night began to reveal the truth of God's reality.","r":["93:2.1","93:2.2","93:2.3"]},{"x":"He received a Thought Adjuster but never married and could leave no offspring; his body was of the type of the one hundred staff members.","r":["93:2.6","93:2.7"]}]},{"h":"The Salem Teachings","items":[{"x":"He founded a school at Salem modeled on the training system of the Sethite priests and was known as \"priest of El Elyon\" and \"the sage of Salem.\"","r":["93:2.4","93:3.1"]},{"q":"Acredito em El Elyon, o Deus Altíssimo, o único Pai Universal e Criador de todas as coisas.","r":"93:4.2"},{"x":"The Salem creed was to believe in the Most High, accept the covenant that he grants favor for faith rather than sacrifice, and keep the seven commandments.","r":["93:4.3","93:4.4","93:4.5"]},{"q":"Não duvidarás de que a fé é a única condição necessária para a salvação eterna.","r":"93:4.8"},{"x":"He permitted no sacrifices at Salem and offered the sacrament of bread and wine in place of blood offerings.","r":["93:4.14"]},{"x":"The three concentric circles symbolized the Paradise Trinity, but most understood them as the three kingdoms of men, angels, and God.","r":["93:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Covenant with Abraham","items":[{"x":"The Melchizedek receivers had long observed Abraham's ancestors, and the family of Terah met their expectations.","r":["93:5.3","93:5.4"]},{"x":"Abraham, who harbored ambitions to become king, won the battle of Siddim despite Melchizedek's dissuasion and then paid him tithes.","r":["93:5.9","93:5.13"]},{"q":"God agrees to do everything; man only agrees to believe God's promises and follow his instructions.","r":"93:6.4"},{"x":"Melchizedek again brought the news that salvation comes by faith, but the Semitic tribes went back to the system of blood sacrifice.","r":["93:6.4"]},{"x":"The covenant was completed after Abraham publicly renounced his personal ambitions, and more than one hundred thousand people were enrolled in the Salem brotherhood.","r":["93:6.7","93:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Purpose and Spread of the Mission","items":[{"q":"Ele veio para realizar duas missões: manter viva, na Terra, a verdade de um único Deus e preparar o caminho para a outorga mortal subseqüente de um Filho do Paraíso deste Pai Universal.","r":"93:4.15"},{"x":"He taught that another Son of God would come, born of a woman.","r":["93:3.7"]},{"x":"Salem missionaries went beyond Egypt, Mesopotamia, and Asia Minor, reaching Europe and the British Isles.","r":["93:7.1","93:7.2"]},{"x":"Michael appeared on earth and confirmed everything that Melchizedek had taught about the Paradise Father.","r":["93:3.8"]},{"x":"Because Melchizedek's teachings had been lost, few recognized Michael when he came in the flesh.","r":["93:9.10"]}]},{"h":"Departure and Later Career","items":[{"x":"When people began to regard him superstitiously as a demigod, he left suddenly, soon after the destruction of Sodom and Gomorrah.","r":["93:8.1"]},{"x":"His disappearance left Abraham with a grief he never overcame for the rest of his life.","r":["93:9.1","93:9.2"]},{"x":"What the Old Testament describes as conversations between Abraham and God were actually conferences between Abraham and Melchizedek.","r":["93:9.7"]},{"x":"For nineteen centuries he worked with the prophets to preserve the truth of Salem, and he is now called the vicegerent Planetary Prince of Urantia.","r":["93:10.4","93:10.7"]},{"q":"This is the story of Machiventa Melchizedek, one of the most unique of all characters ever to become connected with the history of Urantia","r":"93:10.11"}]}],"see":["Melquisedeques","Revelação","Fé","Urântia","Auto-outorga de Jesus","Adão e Eva"]},{"n":69,"t":"Medo e preocupação","en":"Fear and Worry","sum":"Fear was a powerful emotion that bound primitive man into society and prepared the first soil of religion, but unreasoned fear and worry now become poisons that hinder the progress of the soul. Revealed religion and the Thought Adjuster seek to change the fear of God into love and trust, and Jesus taught that foresight and prudence are permitted but that worry and anxiety should be abandoned for trust in the Father. His peace is a peace that keeps the heart from being troubled or afraid.","sections":[{"h":"Fear in Evolution","items":[{"x":"Early man lived in constant fear of bad luck, and that fear had a paralyzing power.","r":["86:1.3","86:1.4"]},{"x":"If hunger and love drew men together, vanity and ghost fear held primitive society together.","r":["68:3.4","68:3.1"]},{"x":"It was not the sanctity of life but the fear aroused by the shock of death that fostered primitive religion.","r":["86:3.1","87:1.1"]},{"x":"The false fears of primitive religion prepared the soil of the mind, and the Adjusters have ever since been transforming fear into the love of God.","r":["86:7.6"]},{"x":"Evolutionary religion drives men by fear, but revealed religion leads them to seek a God of love through the longing to be like him.","r":["5:4.1","101:0.1"]}]},{"h":"A Poison to the Soul","items":[{"q":"O medo irracional é uma fraude intelectual madrasta, praticada contra a alma mortal em evolução.","r":"48:7.4"},{"x":"Mental poisons such as fear, anger, envy, and suspicion, like physical poisons, greatly hinder the spiritual progress of the soul.","r":["110:1.5"]},{"x":"The emotion in man that angels find hardest to understand is the inheritance of animal fear that throws even faith into panic.","r":["113:2.5"]},{"q":"Fear is man's chief enslaver and pride his great weakness","r":"142:0.2"},{"q":"“O ódio é a sombra do medo; a vingança é a máscara da covardia”.","r":"145:3.4"},{"q":"O desencorajamento, a preocupação e a indolência são evidências claras de imaturidade moral.","r":"160:1.6"}]},{"h":"The Worry-Free Life Jesus Taught","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not forbid prudent foresight for the future, but he opposed worry and anxiety.","r":["140:8.3"]},{"x":"Anxiety cannot add a cubit to one's stature or a day to one's life, so trust the Father who feeds even the ravens.","r":["165:5.2"]},{"x":"He counseled not to be overanxious about needs but to spread them before the Father with prayer and thanksgiving.","r":["146:2.16"]},{"x":"To Martha, troubled about many things, he said that the small things of life must give way to the greater things of the kingdom.","r":["162:8.3"]},{"x":"People spend much time crying in fear like lost children, though in fact they are not far from safety.","r":["132:6.1"]},{"x":"Returning from rest in the hills, the apostles realized that many pressing problems were the products of exaggerated fear and anxiety.","r":["143:3.6"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Overcome Fear","items":[{"x":"Jesus told a fear-ridden young man to make his mind not a slave of fear but a courageous ally in solving problems.","r":["130:6.3"]},{"x":"When the indwelling spirit is freed from the fetters of fear, the consciousness of being a child of God overcomes the fear of men.","r":["130:6.3","130:6.4"]},{"q":"Os Ajustadores do Pensamento gostariam de transformar os vossos sentimentos de medo em convicções de amor e de confiança; mas eles não podem, mecânica e arbitrariamente, fazer tais coisas; isso é tarefa vossa.","r":"108:5.8"},{"x":"The anxiety arising from the fear of being alone in the universe should be dissolved by the contemplation of faith in the Father and the rest of worship.","r":["143:7.3"]},{"x":"Happy and effective people are motivated not by fear of wrongdoing but by love of right doing.","r":["140:4.6","140:5.6"]},{"x":"Mere belief may not overcome doubt and fear, but living faith always triumphs over doubting.","r":["102:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Peace Without Fear","items":[{"x":"Jesus knew no fear; he faced the realities of life without fear and was always cheerful and glad.","r":["100:7.4","100:7.12"]},{"x":"The peace of Jesus is not passive calm but a peace that keeps the heart from being troubled or afraid amid trials and persecutions.","r":["140:5.18"]},{"q":"Que os vossos corações não se perturbem, nem fiquem temerosos. Eu venci o mundo, e em mim todos vós ireis triunfar pela fé.","r":"181:1.5"},{"x":"On the morontia worlds ascenders learn to accept challenges without complaint and to face difficulties and uncertainties without fear.","r":["48:6.35"]},{"x":"Teachers are exhorted to proclaim the love of God that casts out all fear.","r":["48:6.8"]}]}],"see":["Fé","Alegria e felicidade","Adversidade e provações","Ajustador do Pensamento","Amor","Religião institucional"]},{"n":24,"t":"Melquisedeques","en":"Melchizedeks","sum":"The Melchizedek Sons are the first-born order of the local universe, brought forth by the Creator Son, the Mother Spirit, and the Father Melchizedek together. Standing midway between the highest Divinity and the lowest creature life, they can serve the evolutionary races without incarnation, working as universe teachers, as the pattern of self-government, and as emergency Sons who are first to act in any crisis. Ascending mortals are taught by them all the way from the mansion worlds to the Melchizedek University on Salvington.","sections":[{"h":"The First-Born Sons of the Local Universe","items":[{"x":"From a new creative union of the Creator Son and the Creative Spirit the Father Melchizedek came first, and in co-operation with the two creators he brought this entire order into being.","r":["35:1.1","20:1.10"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks of Nebadon were all created within one thousand years of standard time; theirs is a nonreproducing order numbering more than ten million.","r":["35:1.3","35:2.9"]},{"q":"These Sons are naturally at the mid-point of the great personality descent","r":"35:2.1"},{"x":"So they become the natural intermediaries between higher divine existence and material life, the friends, teachers, and counselors of all intelligent beings.","r":["35:2.1"]},{"x":"The Father Melchizedek, Gabriel's first executive associate, presides over the emergency commissions and functions as chief executive of Nebadon in Gabriel's absence.","r":["35:1.2"]}]},{"h":"An Order of Self-Government and Trust","items":[{"x":"The Melchizedeks are a self-governing order that elects its own administrative heads, the first attempt at self-determination on the part of local universe beings.","r":["35:1.3","35:2.2"]},{"q":"not once throughout all the superuniverse of Orvonton have these Melchizedek Sons ever betrayed their trust.","r":"35:2.2"},{"x":"They patrol the universe on their own, reporting to the Creator Son independently of the regular agencies, and they also function as advisory review courts that travel among the worlds.","r":["35:2.3","35:2.4"]},{"q":"Os Melquisedeques são quase perfeitos em sabedoria, mas eles não são infalíveis no julgamento.","r":"35:2.8"},{"x":"In the Lucifer rebellion all the Melchizedeks remained loyal to Michael, and on Panoptia the entire population, under their leadership, stood with Michael.","r":["53:7.4","53:7.1"]}]},{"h":"Teachers of the Universe","items":[{"x":"The sphere Melchizedek, the pilot world of the Salvington circuit, and its associated worlds are called the Melchizedek University, and every ascending mortal passes through its training.","r":["35:3.1"]},{"q":"Para um ascendente, este é, provavelmente, o mundo mais interessante de todo o Nébadon.","r":"35:3.11"},{"x":"The progressive education of ascending mortals in the morontia career is conducted under the general supervision of the Melchizedeks, in association with the Trinity Teacher Sons.","r":["35:4.1"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks lead the great teaching corps of the mansion worlds, helping souls continue there the attainments they failed to achieve in the life in the flesh.","r":["45:7.1"]},{"x":"On Jerusem they conduct more than thirty educational centers, training ascending mortals in schools of administration to take up representative government.","r":["45:7.3","45:7.4"]},{"q":"O governo representativo é o ideal divino do autogoverno entre os seres que não são perfeitos.","r":"45:7.3"}]},{"h":"Emergency Sons","items":[{"q":"Sempre, e em quaisquer circunstâncias em que uma ajuda especial se fizer necessária, encontrareis ali um ou mais Filhos Melquisedeques.","r":"35:4.2"},{"x":"They are the first to act in any emergency, sometimes serving as temporary custodians of wayward planets or as receivers for planetary governments that have defaulted.","r":["35:4.4"]},{"x":"Seven times in Nebadon a Melchizedek has served an evolutionary world in the likeness of mortal flesh, Melchizedek of Salem in the days of Abraham being one of them.","r":["35:4.4","35:4.5"]},{"x":"When an Avonal Son goes on a bestowal, twelve Melchizedeks accompany him as sponsors, and they also assist the Avonals on magisterial missions.","r":["35:2.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedeks co-operate with the Life Carriers in reviewing the life plans of new worlds, and the chief of Melchizedeks often represents the Creator Son.","r":["36:2.12"]}]},{"h":"Urantia and the Melchizedeks","items":[{"x":"After the rebellion of the Planetary Prince, Urantia was administered for a long time by a council of twelve Melchizedek receivers.","r":["67:6.5","67:6.6"]},{"x":"The Melchizedek receivers warned Adam and Eve of the dangers of the rebel prince, and about seven years after Adam's arrival they turned over the world administration to him.","r":["51:3.4","74:5.1"]},{"x":"In his first bestowal Michael appeared as a stranger Melchizedek Son and shared in the emergency service of this order.","r":["119:1.3","119:1.6"]},{"q":"By universal consent he has become chief of Melchizedeks","r":"119:1.5"},{"x":"It is believed that the Melchizedeks are destined to remain in their universe of origin and to take an increasingly important part in local universe government and administration.","r":["55:10.11"]}]}],"see":["Maquiventa Melquisedeque","Filho Criador Michael","Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Filhos Avonais","Mundos das mansões","Universo local de Nébadon"]},{"n":37,"t":"Mente","en":"Mind","sum":"Mind is the gift of intelligence that originates in the Third Source and Center, the Infinite Spirit, and is bestowed upon creatures through the Seven Master Spirits and the local universe Mother Spirit. Mind deals with meanings between energy and spirit; it dominates matter while responding to the leading of spirit. In man, mind is the arena in which he makes his own decisions and chooses God or forsakes him, so the way the mind is used determines eternal survival.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Mind: The Third Source and Center","items":[{"x":"Creature mind has its origin only in the Third Source and Center, who is the bestower of mind.","r":["9:5.2"]},{"x":"The Conjoint Actor exerts a gravity pull upon all mind, and every true intellectual value and divine thought is drawn into the absolute mind circuit.","r":["9:6.1","9:6.2"]},{"x":"The mind of man is an individualized circuit, an impersonal part, of the cosmic mind bestowed on the local universe by the Creative Daughter of the Infinite Spirit.","r":["9:5.4"]},{"q":"O Criador Conjunto é a fonte da mente, mas a mente não é o Criador Conjunto.","r":"9:5.5"},{"x":"Mind is absolute on Paradise, subabsolute in Havona, and finite in Orvonton, yet all levels are overspread by the mind-gravity of the Conjoint Actor.","r":["42:10.7"]}]},{"h":"Levels of Mind and the Cosmic Mind","items":[{"x":"Preadjutant-spirit mind is mechanical, nonexperiencing mind, ministered by the Master Physical Controllers.","r":["42:10.3"]},{"x":"Adjutant-spirit mind is the teachable level ministered by the Mother Spirit through the seven adjutant mind-spirits, and here mind first becomes experiencing.","r":["42:10.4"]},{"x":"Morontia mind is the expanding consciousness of personalities in the ascending career, functioning differentially according to the 570 levels of morontia life.","r":["42:10.5"]},{"x":"The Seven Master Spirits are the sevenfold source of cosmic mind, each distributing mind to one superuniverse, and Nebadon is pervaded by its Orvonton-type modification.","r":["9:4.3","16:6.1"]},{"x":"The cosmic mind responds unerringly to three levels of reality, causation (science), duty (morality), and worship (religion), and this underlies reflective thinking.","r":["16:6.6","16:6.7","16:6.8"]},{"x":"Energy is thing, mind is meaning, and spirit is value; mind establishes relationships between energy and spirit in time and space.","r":["9:4.5"]}]},{"h":"Mind at Work Between Matter and Spirit","items":[{"q":"A mente transmuta os valores do espírito em significados do intelecto; a volição tem poder para frutificar os significados da mente, tanto no domínio material quanto no espiritual.","r":"9:4.6"},{"q":"O espírito é o arquiteto, a mente é o construtor, o corpo é a edificação material.","r":"42:12.12"},{"x":"Mind is ever creative; the liaison of the cosmic mind and the adjutant mind-spirits fashions a body suited to evolving man.","r":["42:12.9","42:12.11"]},{"x":"The universe is planned, made, and managed by mind, but lower minds cannot discern the creative spirit-mind hidden within the universe mechanism.","r":["42:11.2","42:11.8"]},{"q":"A mente domina universalmente a matéria, exatamente como esta, por sua vez, é sensível e responde ao controle último do espírito.","r":"42:12.15"}]},{"h":"The Human Mind: Animal Roots and Moral Insight","items":[{"x":"Human intellect is rooted in the material origin of the animal races, so not all phenomena of mind should be regarded as divine.","r":["9:5.5"]},{"q":"A mente é verdadeiramente de origem divina e tem um destino divino, mas as vossas mentes mortais não têm ainda a dignidade divina.","r":"9:5.6"},{"x":"Man defiles his mind with insincerity and unrighteousness, animal fear and needless anxiety, and so he should be humble before his immature intellect.","r":["9:5.7"]},{"x":"Only personality knows what it is doing before it does it, and man can exercise scientific, moral, and spiritual insight in advance of experiment.","r":["16:7.2","16:7.3"]},{"x":"To sharpen this inherent cosmic insight is the purpose of education, to ennoble it is the purpose of religion, and to unify it is the purpose of personality.","r":["16:6.11"]}]},{"h":"Mind as the Arena of Choice","items":[{"q":"A mente material é a arena dentro da qual as personalidades humanas vivem, são autoconscientes, tomam decisões e escolhem a Deus ou abandonam-No, eternizam-se ou destroem a si próprias.","r":"111:1.3"},{"x":"Mind is a temporary intellectual system lent for the material lifetime, and the way it is used accepts or rejects the potential of eternal existence.","r":["111:1.5"]},{"x":"Not what the mind comprehends but what it desires to comprehend, and what it seeks to be like, brings about survival and identification with spirit.","r":["111:1.5"]},{"x":"Mind is a cosmic instrument that, according to the will, can sound the discords of destruction or the exquisite melodies of identification with God.","r":["111:1.6"]},{"q":"A mente é a vossa embarcação, o Ajustador é o vosso piloto, a vontade humana é o capitão.","r":"111:1.9"},{"x":"Even a personal mind has no survival qualities unless it is identified with spirit; when it lacks the capacity to worship and to crave survival, it is not immortal.","r":["36:5.17"]}]}],"see":["Mente cósmica","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Espírito Infinito","Personalidade","Livre-arbítrio","Alma"]},{"n":19,"t":"Mente cósmica","en":"Cosmic Mind","sum":"A mente cósmica é a mente sétupla e diversificada do tempo e do espaço, ministrada por cada um dos Sete Espíritos Mestres a um dos sete superuniversos. É a manifestação, nos níveis finitos, da mente absoluta do Espírito Infinito; chega aos mortais do universo local por meio do Espírito Materno e dos espíritos ajudantes da mente, e dota toda criatura volitiva de três respostas à realidade: a causação, o dever e a adoração. Aqui está o fundamento da ciência, da filosofia e da religião, e de um caráter forte.","sections":[{"h":"Mente sétupla e diversificada","items":[{"x":"A mente cósmica é a mente sétupla e diversificada do tempo e do espaço; cada um dos Sete Espíritos Mestres ministra uma fase dela a um superuniverso.","r":["42:10.6"]},{"x":"Os Espíritos Mestres são a fonte sétupla da mente cósmica e o potencial intelectual do grande universo, e a mente cósmica é uma manifestação subabsoluta da mente da Terceira Fonte e Centro.","r":["16:6.1"]},{"x":"A outorga de mente aos sete superuniversos procede dos Sete Espíritos Mestres, e Nébadon é permeado pela modificação nebadônica do tipo orvontoniano de mente cósmica.","r":["9:4.3"]},{"q":"A mente que é infinita ignora o tempo, a mente última transcende ao tempo, a mente cósmica é condicionada pelo tempo.","r":"9:4.4"},{"x":"A mente cósmica funciona de modo diferente em cada um dos sete superuniversos, mas é coordenada no Ser Supremo por uma técnica de associação desconhecida.","r":["116:1.4"]},{"x":"No Paraíso a mente é absoluta, em Havona, absonita, e em Orvônton, finita.","r":["42:10.7"]}]},{"h":"Por meio do Espírito Infinito e do universo local","items":[{"x":"É no funcionamento universal da mente cósmica dos Espíritos Mestres do Paraíso que melhor se discerne, na criação finita, a presença da mente de Deus.","r":["3:1.8"]},{"x":"No entanto, a mente da ordem humana é uma outorga das filhas do Agente Conjunto, as Ministras Divinas dos universos locais.","r":["3:1.8"]},{"x":"Os urantianos vivem sob a influência do Espírito Criativo de Nébadon, e não sob a influência direta de um Espírito Mestre, mas os Espíritos Mestres dominam as reações básicas de toda mente de criatura.","r":["16:6.2","16:5.3"]},{"x":"A mente humana é um circuito individualizado e uma parte impessoal da mente cósmica outorgada ao universo local pela Filha Criadora.","r":["9:5.4"]},{"x":"A mente cósmica estende-se desde a ministração primitiva dos espíritos ajudantes até a mente dos mais altos executivos do universo, unificada sob a supervisão dos Sete Espíritos Mestres.","r":["56:2.3"]}]},{"h":"Três respostas à realidade","items":[{"x":"Em toda associação da mente cósmica com a personalidade há uma “resposta à realidade” que impede as criaturas volitivas de se tornarem vítimas indefesas dos pressupostos a priori da ciência, da filosofia e da religião.","r":["16:6.4"]},{"x":"A mente cósmica responde infalivelmente em três níveis da realidade: a causação (discriminação matemática), o dever (discriminação judicial) e a adoração (discriminação espiritual).","r":["16:6.5","16:6.6","16:6.7"]},{"q":"Este é o discernimento interior mais elevado da mente cósmica, a forma de reverência e adoração da discriminação cósmica.","r":"16:6.8"},{"x":"Quando essas três intuições se unificam na personalidade, produzem um caráter forte, que une a ciência factual, a filosofia moral e a experiência religiosa genuína.","r":["16:6.10"]},{"q":"O propósito da educação é desenvolver e tornar mais aguçados esses dons inatos da mente humana; o da civilização é expressá-los; o da experiência da vida é compreendê-los; o da religião é enobrecê-los; e o da personalidade é unificá-los.","r":"16:6.11"},{"x":"Contudo, são muito poucos em Urântia os que se comprazem em cultivar esse pensamento cósmico corajoso e independente.","r":["16:6.9"]}]},{"h":"Mentes afins e personalidade moral","items":[{"q":"Não apenas os espíritos afins atraem-se entre si, mas as mentes semelhantes também são muito fraternais, e inclinadas à cooperação umas com as outras.","r":"16:6.3"},{"x":"Assim como as nebulosas se originam nas energias cósmicas do espaço, os eus intelectuais originam-se na mente cósmica.","r":["111:1.2"]},{"x":"Somente uma personalidade sabe o que está fazendo antes de fazê-lo, pois possui discernimento anterior à experiência.","r":["16:7.3"]},{"x":"A virtude é a retidão em conformidade com o cosmo, e a virtude não é conhecida por ser nomeada, mas por ser vivida.","r":["16:7.6"]},{"x":"A moralidade não pode ser promovida pela lei nem pela força; deve espalhar-se pelo contágio do contato com os que exalam fragrância moral.","r":["16:7.9"]},{"q":"A suprema virtude, então, será escolher, de todo o coração, cumprir a vontade do Pai nos céus.","r":"16:7.10"}]},{"h":"A mente cósmica na ascensão","items":[{"x":"A conquista do primeiro círculo cósmico põe fim à influência exclusiva dos espíritos ajudantes da mente, e a mente aproxima-se cada vez mais da mente cósmica e dos dons supra-ajudantes do Espírito Criativo.","r":["110:6.21"]},{"x":"No estágio moroncial, o mortal ascendente recebe a modificação nebadônica da mente cósmica outorgada pelo Espírito Mestre de Orvônton.","r":["112:6.4"]},{"x":"Ao deixar o universo local e alcançar os níveis espirituais, o ascendente fica sintonizado com a ministração direta da mente cósmica de Orvônton.","r":["112:6.10"]},{"x":"Cada vez que uma mente em evolução se sintoniza com os circuitos da mente cósmica, a factualidade do Supremo torna-se um passo mais real no universo.","r":["117:0.3"]},{"q":"Como poderia ser estranho, então, que a mente cósmica fosse autoconscientemente sabedora da sua própria fonte, a mente infinita do Espírito Infinito, e, ao mesmo tempo consciente da realidade física dos múltiplos universos, da realidade espiritual do Filho Eterno, e da realidade da personalidade do Pai Universal?","r":"16:9.15"}]}],"see":["Sete Espíritos Mestres","Espírito Infinito","Mente","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Ser Supremo"]},{"n":88,"t":"Milagres","en":"Miracles","sum":"In the wilderness Jesus decided not to win people's attention and allegiance by miracles and wonders, and he kept that decision to the end. Yet because one with unlimited creator prerogatives was on earth, filled with divine mercy and human sympathy, extraordinary events such as healings sometimes followed apart from his will. The Urantia Book shows that many events that seemed miraculous were in fact natural occurrences, and it explains that even genuine miracles did not break natural law but involved the elimination of the time factor.","sections":[{"h":"The Decision Not to Work Miracles","items":[{"x":"During the forty days in the wilderness Jesus resolved not to use universe power to satisfy the Jewish craving for signs.","r":["136:8.1"]},{"q":"He refused to become a mere wonder-worker.","r":"136:8.2"},{"x":"Wonder-working only stirs the material mind to outward allegiance; it neither reveals God nor saves men.","r":["136:8.2"]},{"q":"Jesus chose to establish the kingdom of heaven in the hearts of mankind by natural, ordinary, difficult, and trying methods","r":"136:8.6"},{"x":"He did not break this decision even when the Pharisees demanded proof or when he was taunted at Calvary to come down from the cross.","r":["136:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Wine at Cana","items":[{"x":"At the wedding feast at Cana others expected a miracle, but the most surprised of all was Jesus himself, who had resolved not to work one.","r":["137:4.12"]},{"q":"Mas isso, em nenhum sentido, era um milagre. Nenhuma lei da natureza foi modificada, ab-rogada ou mesmo transcendida.","r":"137:4.13"},{"x":"The agents of the Creator made wine by the ordinary natural processes, only independently of time.","r":["137:4.13"]},{"x":"It would not have happened had it been contrary to the Father's will, since Jesus had already committed all things to the Father's will.","r":["137:4.14"]}]},{"h":"Events That Were Not Miracles","items":[{"x":"The great catch of fish was no miracle; Jesus, a skilled fisherman who knew the habits of fish, simply told them where the school was.","r":["145:1.3"]},{"x":"The healing of Peter's mother-in-law's fever was not a miracle either, but a miracle-seeking generation counted all such coincidences as miracles.","r":["145:2.16","145:2.17"]},{"x":"Jesus encouraged the apostles not to attribute ordinary physical events to spiritual causes but to seek the true causes of all phenomena.","r":["164:3.6"]},{"x":"The rabbis regarded blindness from birth as the result of sin, but Jesus rejected such superstitious explanations.","r":["164:3.2","164:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Sundown Healing and Genuine Miracles","items":[{"x":"At Capernaum, when Jesus said he wished his children to be made whole if it was not contrary to the Father's will, 683 persons were healed in a moment.","r":["145:3.9","145:3.10"]},{"x":"Jesus himself was the most surprised by this healing, having momentarily forgotten the warning that he could not limit the time element of creator prerogatives.","r":["145:3.11"]},{"q":"As curas miraculosas que, de quando em quando, acompanhavam a missão de Jesus na Terra, não eram parte do seu plano de proclamação do Reino.","r":"145:3.15"},{"x":"The cleansing of the leper was the first so-called miracle Jesus performed intentionally.","r":["146:4.5"]},{"q":"E esse foi o primeiro e o único milagre, com a natureza, que Jesus fez depois de um planejamento prévio consciente.","r":"152:2.10"},{"x":"When Jesus thanked the Father at the raising of Lazarus, the celestial hosts acted, and Lazarus came to life in twelve seconds of earth time.","r":["168:2.2","168:2.3"]}]},{"h":"What the Miracles Left Behind","items":[{"x":"Of the five thousand fed by the miracle, only about five hundred continued to follow Jesus.","r":["152:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus said he would not turn from his mission of revealing the Father to satisfy the curiosity of wonder-seekers.","r":["145:5.6"]},{"x":"The fame of his healings brought prejudice-raising publicity and unsought notoriety, causing Jesus much trouble.","r":["145:3.12","145:3.15"]},{"x":"The resurrection of Lazarus strengthened the faith of believers, but the religious leaders hastened their decision to destroy Jesus.","r":["168:3.1","168:3.4"]}]},{"h":"The Greatest Miracle","items":[{"x":"To local universe citizens there are few miracles, and the most intriguing of them are the incarnational bestowals of the Paradise Sons.","r":["120:4.5"]},{"q":"Jesus de Nazaré foi uma pessoa miraculosa.","r":"120:4.5"},{"x":"Even in all these extraordinary experiences the Father chose to reveal himself in normal, natural, and dependable ways.","r":["120:4.6"]}]}],"see":["Auto-outorga de Jesus","Caráter de Jesus","Fé","Misericórdia","Ensinamentos de Jesus","Ajustador do Pensamento"]},{"n":61,"t":"Misericórdia","en":"Mercy","sum":"Mercy is justice tempered by wisdom that fully knows the weaknesses and handicaps of creatures. God is merciful by nature and needs no one to persuade him; the Eternal Son is mercy itself, and the Infinite Spirit ministers that mercy throughout the universe. Mercy does not violate justice but applies it with understanding, and man learns true mercy by passing through justice, fairness, patience, and kindness.","sections":[{"h":"Justice Tempered by Wisdom","items":[{"q":"A misericórdia é simplesmente a justiça temperada por aquela sabedoria que surge da perfeição do conhecimento e que advém do reconhecimento pleno da fraqueza natural e das limitações ambientais, das criaturas finitas.","r":"2:4.1"},{"x":"Even divine justice, which lets wrongdoing reap its results, is always tempered by mercy, in proportions determined by infinite wisdom.","r":["2:3.2"]},{"x":"Mercy is not a contravention of justice but an understanding interpretation of supreme justice as fittingly applied to evolving finite creatures.","r":["2:4.5"]},{"x":"When eternal justice and divine mercy work together, what man calls fairness emerges in human experience.","r":["2:4.4","10:6.3"]},{"x":"God is not torn between justice and mercy; in his omniscience he fully satisfies both demands at once.","r":["2:4.3","2:6.6"]}]},{"h":"Mercy Flowing from the Father's Nature","items":[{"q":"A necessidade da criatura é totalmente suficiente para assegurar a fluência total da misericórdia terna do Pai e Sua graça salvadora.","r":"2:4.2"},{"x":"Mercy is the natural offspring of goodness and love; a loving father cannot withhold mercy from his children.","r":["2:4.4"]},{"x":"It is an error to think that the Eternal Son pleads with the Father for mercy; all the Son's mercy is a direct revelation of the Father's love.","r":["6:3.4"]},{"x":"God harbors no feelings of wrath or vengeance; such attitudes are inconsistent with the Father's merciful character.","r":["4:3.2","2:6.7"]},{"x":"Even a rebel who turns to righteousness is received in mercy, and God remembers his transgressions no more.","r":["2:5.4"]}]},{"h":"The Son Is Mercy, the Spirit Ministers","items":[{"q":"Deus é amor, o Filho é misericórdia. A misericórdia é o amor aplicado, é o amor do Pai em ação, na pessoa do Seu Filho Eterno.","r":"6:3.5"},{"x":"The Infinite Spirit inclines toward the Son's attribute of mercy and becomes the mercy minister of the Paradise Deities throughout the grand universe.","r":["8:2.6","8:4.7"]},{"q":"O universo da vossa origem foi forjado entre a bigorna da justiça e o martelo do sofrimento; e aqueles que brandem o martelo são filhos da misericórdia: a progênie espiritual do Espírito Infinito.","r":"9:1.8"},{"x":"Justice is the collective attitude of the Trinity, and mercy is the personal expression of that righteousness.","r":["10:6.2","10:6.18"]},{"x":"Creator Sons are inherently merciful, yet through their bestowal experiences they acquire understanding mercy in a new way.","r":["119:0.4"]},{"x":"Our superuniverse of Orvonton is a demonstration of love and mercy, noted for justice tempered by mercy and power conditioned by patience.","r":["15:14.2"]}]},{"h":"The Record and Limits of Mercy","items":[{"x":"The Memory of Mercy is a living record of the mercy ministry extended to an individual, read as testimony at the adjudication of survival.","r":["28:6.5","28:6.6"]},{"q":"Pois a misericórdia não é para ser impingida àqueles que a desprezam; a misericórdia não é um dom a ser pisoteado pelos rebeldes persistentes no tempo.","r":"28:6.7"},{"x":"Yet for one sincere of purpose and honest of heart, the credit of mercy is always far greater than he could ever exhaust.","r":["28:6.7"]},{"x":"When endless mercy and patience are exhausted, justice prevails, and what mercy cannot rehabilitate justice will eventually annihilate.","r":["21:5.7","2:3.5"]}]},{"h":"Mercy as Man Learns It","items":[{"x":"Mercy is a quality of growth: one can be truly merciful only after first becoming just, fair, patient, and kind.","r":["28:6.8"]},{"q":"Pode haver paternalização, condescendência ou caridade — a piedade, até mesmo — , mas não a misericórdia.","r":"28:6.8"},{"q":"A ministração da misericórdia é sempre trabalho do indivíduo, mas a justiça da punição é função do social, do governo ou dos grupos que administram o universo.","r":"133:1.2"},{"x":"The mercy Jesus spoke of is not passive pity but active and dynamic, the supreme fatherly loving-kindness.","r":["140:5.17"]},{"x":"Disciples are saviors, not judges of men, so they must first show their brothers the mercy they themselves would desire.","r":["140:3.17","140:3.16"]},{"x":"The rule of the kingdom is that mercy determines judgment and love determines conduct, not the reckoning of giving and receiving.","r":["140:6.9"]}]}],"see":["Justiça","Amor","Perdão","Filho Eterno","Espírito Infinito","Bondade"]},{"n":65,"t":"Moralidade","en":"Morality","sum":"Morality is the capacity unique to human personality to discern right from wrong and to judge the worth not only of means but of ends, and it distinguishes man from the animal. It evolved from self-conscious reason and grows not by law or force but by personal choice and influence. Morality is a prerequisite of religion but not the whole of religious experience, and the highest moral choice is the choice to do the will of God.","sections":[{"h":"The Moral Nature of Personality","items":[{"q":"A inteligência, por si só, não pode explicar a natureza moral. A moralidade, ou virtude, é inerente à personalidade humana.","r":"16:7.1"},{"x":"Man can exercise moral insight before exploration or experiment, and only personality knows what it is doing before it does it.","r":["16:7.2","16:7.3"]},{"x":"Intellect only selects means, but a moral being discerns the value of the ends themselves.","r":["16:7.4"]},{"x":"One who cannot discern the goal of his strivings lives on the animal level and has failed to use the advantages of personality.","r":["16:7.5"]},{"x":"A child's first moral choice appears with the seventh adjutant mind-spirit, and only after it is registered is an Adjuster assigned.","r":["108:2.1"]}]},{"h":"Virtue and Moral Choice","items":[{"q":"A virtude é retidão — conformidade com o cosmo. Dar nomes às virtudes não é defini-las; vivê-las, no entanto, é conhecê-las.","r":"16:7.6"},{"x":"Choosing between good and evil is influenced not only by moral keenness but also by ignorance, immaturity, and delusion, so a sense of proportion and the art of measurement are needed.","r":["16:7.7","16:7.8"]},{"x":"Moral conduct is the highest performance of intellect: choosing higher ends and choosing moral means suited to those ends.","r":["16:7.10"]},{"q":"A escolha moral mais elevada é a escolha do valor mais elevado possível e — em toda e qualquer esfera — , isso sempre significa escolher fazer a vontade de Deus.","r":"39:4.14"}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Morality","items":[{"x":"Morality arose from self-conscious reason; it transcends the animal but is wholly evolutionary.","r":["5:5.1"]},{"x":"Through the long and wasteful struggle to placate ghosts, man became conscious of relative right and wrong, and thus ethics was born.","r":["86:6.7","68:4.3"]},{"x":"Early feelings of duty grew out of emotional fear, but the urge to unselfish service comes from the indwelling divine spirit.","r":["103:5.1"]},{"q":"A consciência não é uma voz divina, falando à alma humana.","r":"92:2.6"},{"x":"Static ethics and traditional morality are only slightly above the animal level; ethics becomes truly human when it is dynamic and progressive.","r":["12:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Morality and Religion","items":[{"q":"A conduta moral é sempre um antecedente da religião evoluída e uma parte da própria religião revelada, mas nunca é a totalidade da experiência religiosa.","r":"5:5.4"},{"x":"The morality of evolutionary religion drives men by fear, but revealed religion draws them by a loving desire to be like God.","r":["5:4.1"]},{"x":"As religion evolves, ethics becomes the philosophy of morals, and morality becomes the discipline of self by the standards of supreme spiritual ideals.","r":["92:7.5"]},{"x":"A religion that stresses an isolated morality apart from truth and beauty fails to win the loyalty of modern people.","r":["2:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus did not put ethics in the place of religion; he taught religion as the cause and ethics as the result.","r":["170:3.8"]}]},{"h":"How Morality Grows and Spreads","items":[{"q":"A moralidade nunca pode ser promovida pela lei nem pela força.","r":"16:7.9"},{"x":"Morality is a matter of the personality's free will and must spread by the contagion of contact with morally fragrant persons.","r":["16:7.9"]},{"x":"Jesus interpreted the golden rule on the levels of the flesh, feelings, mind, brotherly love, morality, and spirit, teaching at the highest to treat people as God would treat them.","r":["147:4.3","147:4.8","147:4.9"]},{"x":"Primitive man's neighbor was only those near him, but Jesus extended the neighbor to all mankind and even to enemies, and the human heart knows this is right.","r":["103:5.2"]},{"x":"In the ages of philosophy and brotherhood people become truly moral beings and learn to live by the golden rule.","r":["50:5.8"]}]}],"see":["Bondade","Livre-arbítrio","Vontade de Deus","Experiência religiosa","Sabedoria","Pecado"]},{"n":45,"t":"Morôncia","en":"Morontia","sum":"Morontia is the vast intermediate level lying between the material and the spiritual. Since God does not change a mortal of animal origin into a perfect spirit in a single step, the surviving human passes through the many morontia worlds of the local universe and, by hundreds of gradual transformations, reaches the threshold of spirit. The morontia life actually begins on earth when the soul is conceived, and its philosophic insight is called mota.","sections":[{"h":"A Level Between Matter and Spirit","items":[{"q":"Os elos do tecido moroncial são espirituais, a sua trama é física.","r":"0:5.12"},{"x":"Morontia is a broad level of reality that may be personal or impersonal, and may consist of living or nonliving energies.","r":["0:5.12"]},{"x":"The morontia worlds are architectural spheres furnished with one hundred physical elements plus one hundred organizations of energy known as morontia materials.","r":["48:1.3"]},{"x":"Like the \"better and more enduring substance\" of which Paul spoke, morontia material is real and literal.","r":["48:1.7"]},{"x":"Morontia mind is a dual mind in which material and spiritual minds co-operate, governed by a single will.","r":["110:2.6"]}]},{"h":"Why a Morontia Stage Is Needed","items":[{"x":"The Gods do not transform creatures of animal origin into perfect spirits at once by some mysterious magic.","r":["48:0.1"]},{"x":"The belief that the single step of death instantly transforms the mortal mind into a perfected spirit is ignorant superstition.","r":["48:0.2"]},{"x":"A morontia transition always intervenes between mortal state and spirit status, and its purpose is similar in all local creations.","r":["48:0.3"]},{"x":"The morontia career is the transition life between evolutionary material existence and the higher spirit attainment.","r":["47:10.7"]},{"q":"A crença disso não é senão uma superstição ignorante envolta por uma fábula agradável.","r":"48:0.2"}]},{"h":"Morontia Bodies and Gradual Transformation","items":[{"x":"The morontia power supervisors provide 570 successive morontia bodies during the morontia career in Nebadon.","r":["48:1.5"]},{"x":"In mortal life the spirit indwells almost as something separate, but in the morontia life the spirit becomes an actual part of the personality.","r":["48:1.6"]},{"x":"Early morontia life resembles the material worlds, but on the constellation and Salvington it reaches increasingly spiritual levels.","r":["48:1.4"]},{"x":"The body that the risen Jesus bore was also a morontia body: no blood circulated in it and it did not take material food, yet it was real.","r":["190:0.3"]}]},{"h":"Those Who Help the Morontia Life","items":[{"x":"Morontia companions are offspring of the local universe Mother Spirit, friendly associates, guides, and interpreters for the ascenders.","r":["48:3.1","48:3.5","48:3.12"]},{"x":"The mansion world teachers are cherubim and sanobim left behind by their seraphim, and they conduct the schools of thinking, feeling, and doing.","r":["48:5.1","48:5.6"]},{"q":"Não existem caminhos mais nobres, nem atalhos especiais, ou sendeiros fáceis para o Paraíso.","r":"48:5.7"},{"x":"The morontia career seeks to eradicate forever such animal vestiges as procrastination, insincerity, and the avoidance of problems.","r":["48:5.8"]},{"x":"Transition seraphim help with the choice of a course, yet they respect the ascender's freewill choices as long as no harm results.","r":["48:6.5","48:6.6"]},{"q":"No act of good is ever wholly lost","r":"48:6.7"}]},{"h":"Mota and the Morontia Progressors","items":[{"x":"Mota is an insight superior to philosophy; as two eyes are to one, it gives stereoscopic depth to meanings and values.","r":["48:6.28"]},{"x":"On the first mansion world mota concepts are taught side by side with the corresponding statements of human philosophy.","r":["48:7.1"]},{"q":"A alma em evolução não se torna divina pelo que faz, mas por aquilo que se esforça por fazer.","r":"48:7.24"},{"x":"The morontia life actually begins on earth at the moment the Adjuster comes to indwell and the soul is conceived.","r":["48:6.2"]},{"x":"After graduating from the mansion worlds and until attaining spirit status, the ascender is called a morontia progressor.","r":["48:8.1"]},{"x":"The purpose of this long training is not merely eternal ease but preparation for the transcendent service of future ages.","r":["48:8.3"]},{"q":"Mota is more than a superior philosophy","r":"48:6.28"}]}],"see":["Mundos das mansões","Alma","Ascensão mortal","Morte","Ressurreição de Jesus","Filosofia"]},{"n":43,"t":"Morte","en":"Death","sum":"In The Urantia Book death is not an end but a doorway from the material life to the morontia life. For primitive man death was the supreme shock and the greatest fear, and it gave rise to the development of religion; revelation, however, shows that there are three kinds of death, spiritual, intellectual, and physical, and that the surviving soul sleeps and then awakens again on the mansion worlds. On advanced worlds even natural death becomes increasingly rare.","sections":[{"h":"Primitive Man and the Fear of Death","items":[{"q":"A morte foi o choque supremo para o homem em evolução, a combinação mais desconcertante de acaso e mistério.","r":"86:3.1"},{"x":"Not the sanctity of life but the fear inspired by the shock of death fostered early religion.","r":["86:3.1"]},{"x":"Fearing the ghosts released by death, primitive peoples destroyed the dead person's house and took a different road home from the funeral.","r":["87:1.1","87:1.3","87:1.5"]},{"x":"The concept of a future life, derived from dreams, began to soften the fear of death bound up with the instinct of self-preservation.","r":["86:4.2"]},{"x":"The basic belief of primitive religion was survival after death.","r":["92:6.1"]}]},{"h":"The Three Kinds of Death","items":[{"x":"In relation to personality survival there are three kinds of death: spiritual (soul) death, intellectual (mind) death, and physical (body and mind) death.","r":["112:3.1"]},{"x":"One who has finally rejected survival is, from the universe point of view, already dead, even while the body lives.","r":["112:3.2"]},{"x":"When the mind circuits that make volitional action possible are irretrievably destroyed, the Adjuster departs, and this too is death.","r":["112:3.3"]},{"x":"In physical death the Adjuster remains until the mind ceases to function, then departs for Divinington when the life pulsations of the brain stop.","r":["112:3.4"]}]},{"h":"What Happens After Death","items":[{"x":"The body returns to the elements, but two nonmaterial factors continue: the Adjuster and the morontia soul.","r":["112:3.5"]},{"q":"Upon death the Thought Adjuster temporarily loses personality, but not identity; the human subject temporarily loses identity, but not personality;","r":"112:3.7"},{"x":"From death until repersonalization the surviving soul is wholly unconscious, in the keeping of the guardian of destiny.","r":["112:5.13"]},{"x":"Those who go to the mansion worlds cannot send messages back to their loved ones on earth; such communication is forbidden.","r":["112:3.7"]},{"x":"In the resurrection halls the morontia form, the returning Adjuster, and the conserved soul are united, and identity is reassembled.","r":["112:5.16","112:5.18","112:5.19"]},{"q":"on the mansion worlds both reunite in eternal manifestation.","r":"112:3.7"}]},{"h":"The Eye of Faith on Death","items":[{"x":"The spirit of adventure and the dread of monotony were placed in man to suggest that death is only the beginning of an endless career of adventure.","r":["14:5.10"]},{"x":"Life after death is not essentially different from mortal existence, and every good thing done now enhances the future life.","r":["103:5.7"]},{"x":"True religion does not foster spiritual sloth through the vain hope of gaining noble virtues merely by passing through the portals of death.","r":["103:5.7"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that believers should live as if pursuing their careers with natural death always in prospect.","r":["176:3.3"]},{"q":"and which even now makes certain their resurrection from the bonds of natural death.","r":"190:0.2"},{"q":"A morte nada acrescenta à posse intelectual nem à dotação espiritual, mas ao cabedal experiencial acrescenta a consciência da sobrevivência.","r":"48:7.25"}]},{"h":"Worlds Where Death Fades Away","items":[{"q":"A morte natural, física, não é uma inevitabilidade para os mortais.","r":"55:2.1"},{"x":"On worlds settled in light and life, many fuse with their Adjusters and are translated alive into the morontia state.","r":["55:2.1","55:2.2"]},{"x":"On such worlds a \"funeral\" becomes an occasion not of weeping but of joy, deep satisfaction, and inexpressible hope.","r":["55:2.5"]},{"x":"Less advanced mortals would be helped if they too learned to view natural death with such cheerfulness and lightness of heart.","r":["55:2.6"]},{"x":"Yet even on long-settled worlds there is no system in which natural death as a way of leaving the flesh has wholly disappeared.","r":["55:2.8"]}]}],"see":["Sobrevivência","Mundos das mansões","Morôncia","Alma","Medo e preocupação","Luz e vida"]},{"n":90,"t":"Morte na cruz","en":"Death on the Cross","sum":"Jesus died on the cross at Golgotha on a Friday in A.D. 30. The Urantia Book makes clear that this death was not an atoning sacrifice to appease the wrath of God or pay mankind's debt; it was not required by the Father but planned and carried out by man. The true meaning of the cross lies not in the fact of his death but in the manner and spirit in which he met it, the supreme expression of a love that forgave even enemies, and so the cross became the eternal symbol of unselfish service.","sections":[{"h":"From the Arrest to Golgotha","items":[{"x":"When he was arrested, Jesus knew his work in the flesh was finished and took little interest in the details of the so-called trials.","r":["186:2.1"]},{"x":"He did not answer false testimony, but he always answered the question whether he was the Son of God.","r":["186:2.2"]},{"x":"Convinced that it was the Father's will for him to follow the natural course of events like an ordinary man, he did not try to change the outcome by his eloquence.","r":["186:2.3"]},{"x":"He was crucified at about half past nine on Friday morning, and the unseen hosts of the universe watched in silence as the Creator underwent a creature's death.","r":["187:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Hours on the Cross","items":[{"q":"As únicas palavras de Jesus, quando o pregavam na viga da cruz, foram: “Pai, perdoa-lhes, pois não sabem o que fazem”.","r":"187:2.4"},{"x":"Though thirsty, Jesus refused the drugged wine offered to deaden his suffering.","r":["187:2.3"]},{"x":"Unlike the brigand who mocked him, the other brigand turned wholeheartedly in his last hours and found salvation.","r":["187:4.1","187:4.2"]},{"x":"As a sandstorm darkened the sky, Jesus cried, \"It is finished,\" commended his spirit to the Father, and breathed his last.","r":["187:5.1","187:5.5"]},{"x":"A Roman centurion who saw him die confessed that he truly was a Son of God.","r":["187:5.5"]},{"q":"Jesus morreu com nobreza — como tinha vivido.","r":"187:5.6"}]},{"h":"Not an Atoning Sacrifice","items":[{"x":"Jesus did not die to atone for the racial guilt of mankind or to provide a way of approach to an offended God.","r":["188:4.1"]},{"x":"His death was neither a ransom to buy man back from fallen rulers nor a sacrifice to pay mankind's debt to God.","r":["188:4.3"]},{"x":"The whole idea of ransom and atonement is incompatible with the concept of God as a loving Father, which Jesus taught and showed.","r":["188:4.8"]},{"x":"Sin is not passed from parents to children; it is conscious rebellion committed by individual will creatures.","r":["188:4.5"]},{"x":"Even a sovereign of justice would not be satisfied with the childish scheme of substituting an innocent person for the guilty.","r":["188:4.11"]}]},{"h":"Who Killed Him","items":[{"q":"Foi o homem, e não Deus, que planejou e executou a morte de Jesus na cruz.","r":"186:5.2"},{"x":"There is no direct connection between his death and the Jewish Passover sacrificial system.","r":["186:5.1"]},{"x":"The experience required by the bestowal was already complete at his baptism; the manner of his later life and death was his personal ministry for his creatures.","r":["186:5.3"]},{"x":"The gospel of realizing sonship with God by faith does not depend on his death and was illuminated even more by his life than by his death.","r":["186:5.4"]},{"x":"The Father loved mankind just as much before Jesus lived and died as after.","r":["186:5.6"]}]},{"h":"The True Meaning of the Cross","items":[{"q":"A grande coisa sobre a morte de Jesus, no que se relaciona ao enriquecimento da experiência humana e à ampliação do caminho da salvação, não é o fato da sua morte, mas antes a maneira magnífica e o espírito sem par com o qual ele enfrentou a morte.","r":"188:4.12"},{"q":"Ela coloca, para sempre, todas as relações entre Deus e o homem na base da família.","r":"188:5.1"},{"x":"Divine love does not merely forgive wrongs; it absorbs and actually destroys them, so the forgiveness of love transcends the forgiveness of mercy.","r":["188:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus bore the cross of mortal existence for more than twenty-five years, and Golgotha was the final expression of that love.","r":["188:5.4"]},{"q":"Embora muito dificilmente seja adequado falar de Jesus como alguém que se tenha sacrificado, como o resgatador ou redentor, é totalmente correto referir-se a ele como um salvador.","r":"188:4.7"},{"x":"He lived and died not for this world alone but for the whole universe, and his death illuminated the certainty of survival after the death of the flesh.","r":["188:4.6"]}]},{"h":"The Symbol of Service","items":[{"x":"His love that laid down his life for his enemies was greater than any love then known on earth.","r":["188:5.7"]},{"x":"The cross is not a symbol of substitution appeasing wrath but of unselfish service, in which the good bestow themselves on the evil to save them by love.","r":["188:5.9"]},{"x":"Creatures on many worlds, looking upon Jesus on the cross, have not given up the struggle of faith but have pressed on once more.","r":["188:5.5"]},{"x":"On the cross there was nothing the Father required, only what Jesus willingly gave and refused to avoid.","r":["188:5.11"]},{"x":"His death was not meant to reconcile man to God but to awaken man to the Father's eternal love and the Son's mercy.","r":["188:5.13"]}]}],"see":["Auto-outorga de Jesus","Ressurreição de Jesus","Amor","Perdão","Morte","Serviço"]},{"n":44,"t":"Mundos das mansões","en":"Mansion Worlds","sum":"The mansion worlds are the seven transition worlds surrounding Jerusem, the capital of the local system, and they correspond to the \"many mansions in my Father's house\" of which Jesus spoke. After death the surviving mortal awakens in the resurrection halls of the first mansion world, makes up the deficiencies left unfinished on earth, and, passing through the seven worlds in turn, becomes less and less mortal and more and more morontial. This is the first school of the ascension, linking the material life with the spirit life.","sections":[{"h":"What the Seven Mansion Worlds Are","items":[{"x":"The \"many mansions\" of which Jesus spoke refer especially to the seven satellites of the first transition world surrounding Jerusem.","r":["47:0.1"]},{"x":"The mansion worlds are in the charge of the morontia supervisors and the Melchizedeks, and each world has an acting governor and headquarters for many groups of ministers.","r":["47:0.4"]},{"x":"When a system is settled in light and life, the mansion worlds one by one cease to serve as training spheres and are taken over by the finaliters.","r":["47:0.3"]},{"x":"The seven worlds are in fact demortalizing spheres: on the first one is still largely human, but by graduation one has become nearly morontial.","r":["47:9.5"]}]},{"h":"Awakening on the First Mansion World","items":[{"x":"At the center of the first mansion world stand the resurrection halls, the temple of personality assembly, where guardian seraphim, Adjusters, and archangels work together.","r":["47:3.2"]},{"x":"The sleeping survivor is resurrected when the morontia soul kept by the seraphim and the spirit-mind held by the Adjuster are reunited.","r":["47:3.3"]},{"q":"You begin over there right where you leave off down here.","r":"47:3.7"},{"x":"The resurrected one is granted ten days of liberty to explore the new home and look up loved ones who have gone before.","r":["47:3.6"]},{"x":"Morontia companions are assigned to the ascenders as their friendly associates and guides.","r":["47:3.11","47:3.12"]},{"q":"Nos mundos das mansões, os mortais sobreviventes ressuscitados reassumem as suas vidas exatamente no ponto em que as deixaram quando colhidos pela morte.","r":"47:3.1"}]},{"h":"Worlds That Correct Deficiencies","items":[{"x":"The experience of the first mansion world is almost wholly devoted to correcting the defects of character and deficiencies of experience left from the life in the flesh.","r":["47:3.8"]},{"x":"No ascender can escape the experience of rearing children, and fathers must pass through it as surely as mothers.","r":["47:1.6"]},{"q":"As crianças necessitam do pai tanto quanto da mãe, e os pais necessitam dessa experiência de progenitor, tanto quanto as mães.","r":"47:1.6"},{"x":"The second mansion world is devoted to removing intellectual conflicts and healing every kind of mental disharmony.","r":["47:4.8"]},{"x":"Whereas the first two worlds give negative training to make up deficiencies, truly progressive morontia culture begins on the third world.","r":["47:5.3"]}]},{"h":"From World to World","items":[{"x":"With each move to a new world one goes to sleep and awakens in a new morontia body, but at these times the Adjuster does not leave.","r":["47:4.4"]},{"x":"Memories of survival value are kept throughout the ascending career because the Adjuster has made counterparts of them.","r":["47:4.5"]},{"x":"In the morontia body one still eats, drinks, and rests, but the food is completely utilized and leaves no residue.","r":["47:4.6"]},{"x":"On the fourth world ascenders first learn true social life, based not on selfish conquest but on mutual appreciation and unselfish service.","r":["47:6.3"]},{"q":"Um nascimento real, de conscientização cósmica, acontece na mansônia de número cinco.","r":"47:7.5"},{"x":"Fusion with the Adjuster is often actually effected on the fifth or sixth world, followed by the declaration, \"This is a beloved son in whom I am well pleased.\"","r":["47:8.3","47:8.4"]},{"q":"Ganhareis um novo corpo moroncial, recém-desenvolvido e adequadamente ajustado, no momento de cada avanço de um mundo das mansões para o seguinte.","r":"47:4.4"}]},{"h":"Citizens of Jerusem","items":[{"x":"On the seventh mansion world the remnants of unfortunate heredity and unwholesome environment are cleansed away, and differences of world origin disappear.","r":["47:9.1"]},{"x":"On the seventh world ascenders visit the Father's world and begin a more spiritual worship of the invisible Father.","r":["47:9.2"]},{"x":"The graduates are sent off in classes from the sea of glass and welcomed as citizens of Jerusem.","r":["47:9.4","47:10.1"]},{"x":"Those who pass through all the mansion worlds experience the adjustment sleep and the resurrection awakening seven times, after which consciousness is never again broken.","r":["47:10.5"]},{"q":"Mortal death is a technique of escape from the material life in the flesh","r":"47:10.7"}]}],"see":["Morôncia","Morte","Sobrevivência","Ascensão mortal","Fusão com o Ajustador","Constelações e sistemas locais"]},{"n":52,"t":"Oração","en":"Prayer","sum":"Prayer is a personal and spontaneous expression of the attitude of the soul toward the spirit, the breath of the soul in the communion of sonship with God. Beginning as primitive petitions for material things, prayer gradually evolved into ethical and spiritual communion. Prayer does not change God but changes the one who prays, and it is truest when it seeks values, not things, and growth, not gratification. Jesus lived a life dedicated in prayer to the Father's will.","sections":[{"h":"What Prayer Is","items":[{"q":"Prayer is entirely a personal and spontaneous expression of the attitude of the soul toward the spirit","r":"144:2.2"},{"x":"Prayer is the communion of sonship and the expression of fellowship; the ideal prayer is spiritual communion leading to intelligent worship.","r":["144:2.2"]},{"x":"Prayer is the breath of the soul, leading one to strive persistently to ascertain the Father's will.","r":["144:2.3"]},{"x":"Prayer is the process of exchanging the human will for the divine will, part of the divine plan for making over what is into what ought to be.","r":["144:4.9"]},{"x":"True prayer is the sincere and trusting communication of the creature's spiritual nature with the omnipresent spirit of the Creator.","r":["91:8.4"]},{"q":"“A prece é o respirar da alma e deveria levar-vos à persistência na tentativa de melhor conhecerdes sobre a vontade do Pai.","r":"144:2.3"}]},{"h":"The Evolution of Prayer","items":[{"x":"Primitive man prayed for material blessings such as food and rain; this was a perversion of prayer, yet it also stimulated social and ethical effort.","r":["91:1.3"]},{"x":"Prayer is a monologue only in the most primitive minds; it soon becomes a dialogue and broadens into group worship.","r":["91:1.4"]},{"x":"Magic was an attempt to adjust Deity to conditions; prayer is an effort to adjust the personality to the will of Deity.","r":["91:8.2"]},{"x":"The idea of sacrifice, offering material things in place of the will, diminishes the efficacy of true prayer.","r":["91:2.4"]}]},{"h":"Principles of True Prayer","items":[{"x":"Selfish and materialistic prayer is incompatible with ethical religion founded on unselfish love.","r":["91:4.1"]},{"q":"A prece nunca deve ser prostituída a ponto de tornar-se uma substituta para a ação.","r":"91:4.2"},{"x":"Do not be so lazy as to ask God to solve problems for you; ask for wisdom and strength while you face them.","r":["91:6.5"]},{"q":"Orai apenas pelos valores, não pelas coisas; pelo crescimento, não pela gratificação.","r":"91:8.13"},{"x":"God answers the attitude of the soul, not words, and he answers prayer with an enlarged revelation of truth, beauty, and goodness.","r":["91:8.11","91:8.12"]},{"x":"Effective prayer requires courageously facing reality, sincere effort, choosing and carrying out the divine will, and living faith.","r":["91:9.2","91:9.5","91:9.8"]}]},{"h":"What Prayer Changes","items":[{"x":"Prayer does not change God, but great and lasting changes take place in the one who prays in faith.","r":["91:4.5"]},{"q":"A prece não muda a atitude divina para com o homem, mas muda a atitude do homem para com o imutável Pai.","r":"146:2.8"},{"x":"As a bird must spread its wings to ride rising air currents, prayer lifts one up on the spiritual currents of the universe.","r":["91:8.9"]},{"x":"The quickest way to overcome the habit of criticizing a friend is to pray for him every day.","r":["91:5.3"]},{"x":"Prayer offered sincerely in faith, even a foolish petition, never fails to enlarge the soul's capacity for spiritual receptivity.","r":["144:4.2"]},{"q":"Lembrai-vos, pois, ainda que a prece não mude Deus, muito freqüentemente ela efetua grandes e perduráveis mudanças naquele que a realiza com fé e expectativa confiantes.","r":"91:4.5"}]},{"h":"Prayer as Jesus Taught It","items":[{"x":"When one is wholly dedicated to doing the Father's will, every petition is answered, because the prayer is in accord with that will.","r":["146:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus prayed more for the spiritual progress of his brothers than for himself, and he urged prayer especially for enemies and persecutors.","r":["146:2.10","146:2.11"]},{"x":"One should be able to talk with the Father as a son not only in times of distress but also when the soul is at peace.","r":["146:2.12"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that after praying one should wait in silence for a time, giving the indwelling spirit opportunity to speak to the soul.","r":["146:2.17"]},{"x":"Jesus usually prayed in the plural rather than the singular, and he prayed for himself only in the great crises of his earth life.","r":["144:4.6"]},{"x":"For Jesus prayer was not a religious duty but a sincere expression of spiritual attitude and constant communion with God.","r":["196:0.10"]}]}],"see":["Adoração","Vontade de Deus","Fé","Filiação a Deus","Experiência religiosa","Religião pessoal"]},{"n":1,"t":"Pai Universal","en":"Universal Father","sum":"O Pai Universal é Deus, a Primeira Fonte e Centro de todas as coisas e de todos os seres. Ele é o Criador, o Controlador e o Mantenedor infinito; embora seja um espírito invisível, Ele é uma verdadeira personalidade que ama todas as Suas criaturas como um pai. Porque o Seu fragmento, o Ajustador do Pensamento, reside no homem, qualquer pessoa pode lançar-se à aventura eterna de encontrar o Pai e de tornar-se semelhante a Ele.","sections":[{"h":"Primeira Fonte e Centro","items":[{"x":"O Pai é o Deus de toda a criação, a Primeira Fonte e Centro de todas as coisas e de todos os seres, que deve ser concebido primeiro como Criador, depois como Controlador e, por último, como Mantenedor infinito.","r":["1:0.1"]},{"x":"O Pai criou pessoalmente o Paraíso e o universo central, enquanto os universos do tempo e do espaço são feitos pelos Filhos Criadores; Nébadon é a criação do Seu Filho Michael.","r":["1:2.9"]},{"x":"O Pai atua fisicamente por meio da gravidade da Ilha do Paraíso, mentalmente no Espírito Infinito e espiritualmente no Filho Eterno, e, no entanto, mantém contato direto com as Suas criaturas.","r":["1:2.10"]},{"q":"Deus não se assemelha ao homem, nem à máquina.","r":"1:2.1"},{"x":"Para Deus não há passado, presente e futuro separados; todo o tempo é presente, e nenhum acontecimento do universo jamais O surpreende.","r":["2:1.5"]}]},{"h":"Nome e realidade","items":[{"x":"A Primeira Fonte e Centro nunca revelou um nome para Si; o nome “Pai” nasceu da relação pessoal que as Suas criaturas têm com Ele.","r":["1:1.1"]},{"x":"O nome pelo qual Ele é chamado pouco importa; o que importa é o desejo de conhecê-Lo e de ser como Ele.","r":["1:1.6"]},{"x":"Deus é uma realidade transcendente, infinitamente maior do que qualquer realidade idealizada, do que qualquer lei da natureza personificada ou do que o “produto mais elevado do homem”.","r":["1:2.2"]},{"x":"A existência de Deus não pode ser provada por experimentos científicos nem pela lógica pura; ela só se realiza no âmbito da experiência humana.","r":["1:2.7"]},{"q":"Those who know God have experienced the fact of his presence","r":"1:2.8"}]},{"h":"Espírito invisível, verdadeira personalidade","items":[{"q":"“Deus é espírito”. Ele é uma presença espiritual universal.","r":"1:3.1"},{"x":"O Pai é invisível não porque Se esconda, mas porque os seres materiais não poderiam preservar a sua existência diante do Seu brilho espiritual; mas Ele pode ser discernido com o olho da fé.","r":["1:3.3"]},{"x":"A Sua infinitude não deve obscurecer a Sua personalidade; o Pai é o ápice da personalidade divina, a origem e o destino de toda personalidade.","r":["1:5.1"]},{"x":"No universo local, o Pai Se revela nas personalidades dos Filhos Criadores, de modo que quem viu o Filho viu o Pai.","r":["1:5.5","3:0.2"]}]},{"h":"O Pai amoroso","items":[{"q":"Deus ama, não à maneira de um pai, mas como Pai.","r":"2:6.4"},{"x":"O amor do Pai não foi conquistado pelo sacrifício nem pela intercessão dos Seus Filhos; Ele ama pessoalmente os Seus filhos desde o princípio.","r":["2:5.2"]},{"x":"Os profetas hebreus proclamaram Deus como o Pai de Israel, mas Jesus O revelou como o Pai de cada ser humano.","r":["2:6.4"]},{"x":"O Pai participa pessoalmente da luta de toda alma que se esforça pela perfeição: Ele sofre nas nossas aflições e triunfa nas nossas vitórias.","r":["1:5.15","1:5.16"]},{"x":"Deus, o Pai, ama a humanidade; Deus, o Filho, ministra à humanidade; e Deus, o Espírito, inspira os Seus filhos a ascender em busca do Pai.","r":["3:6.8"]}]},{"h":"O caminho para o Pai","items":[{"x":"O Pai não requer culto formal nem serviço servil; a dedicação de todo o coração a fazer a vontade do Pai é o único dom verdadeiramente pessoal que o homem pode oferecer.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"q":"\"Be you perfect, even as I am perfect.\"","r":"1:0.3"},{"x":"O homem não pode aproximar-se diretamente do Pai, não porque Ele esteja longe, mas por causa da finitude da criatura; e o caminho está aberto a todos.","r":["5:1.1","5:1.8"]},{"q":"Que erro é sonhar com Deus, distante nos céus, quando o espírito do Pai Universal vive dentro da vossa própria mente!","r":"5:2.3"},{"x":"Por mais diferente que seja a sua condição intelectual e social, todos os homens receberam a mesma presença divina, de modo que a possibilidade de progresso espiritual é igual para todos.","r":["5:1.4","5:1.5"]},{"x":"Por mais tempo que leve, o ascendente fusionado com o Ajustador estará um dia diante do centro divino e verá o Pai face a face.","r":["5:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Atributos de Deus","Personalidade de Deus","Trindade do Paraíso","Ajustador do Pensamento","Filiação a Deus","Adoração"]},{"n":87,"t":"Parábolas","en":"Parables","sum":"The parable is the storytelling method of teaching that Jesus first used with the multitude by the Sea of Galilee and that thereafter became almost his only method of public instruction. He taught that parables should not be interpreted as allegories with a hidden meaning in every detail but received as true-to-life stories that reveal one central truth. A parable appeals at once to minds of different levels, plants new truth while avoiding prejudice and controversy, and leaves each person to find its meaning in his own soul.","sections":[{"h":"The Beginning of Teaching by Parables","items":[{"x":"Jesus first used this method when, from a boat by the sea, he told the parable of the sower to a crowd of nearly a thousand.","r":["151:1.1","151:1.2"]},{"x":"It was intended that those sincerely wishing to enter the kingdom would grasp the meaning, while those seeking to entrap him would see and not understand.","r":["151:1.4"]},{"x":"From then on Jesus taught the public almost entirely in parables and explained their meaning more fully to the apostles in the evening.","r":["151:4.7"]},{"x":"Parables appealing to nature were the best reply to the charge that his work was done by the power of the devil, and they gave his enemies less to seize upon.","r":["151:3.14"]}]},{"h":"Parables, Not Allegories","items":[{"x":"Peter and Nathaniel disagreed while interpreting the parable of the sower as an allegory with a hidden meaning in every detail.","r":["151:2.1","151:2.4"]},{"x":"Thomas recalled the Master's teaching that illustrations should use true-to-life stories that reveal one central truth.","r":["151:2.5"]},{"q":"Well done, Thomas; you have discerned the true meaning of parables","r":"151:2.7"},{"x":"Jesus said that private flights of imagination may be profitable, but offering them as public teaching is a mistake.","r":["151:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus advised avoiding fables and allegories and using parables freely, especially those drawn from nature.","r":["151:3.3"]}]},{"h":"The Value of Parables","items":[{"q":"A parábola tem apelo para vários níveis diferentes, simultaneamente, da mente e do espírito.","r":"151:3.6"},{"q":"A parábola parte das coisas conhecidas e chega ao discernimento do desconhecido.","r":"151:3.7"},{"x":"The parable plants new truth in the mind while bypassing prejudice and arousing a minimum of antagonism.","r":["151:3.8"]},{"x":"Parables avoid direct conflict with tradition and authority and recall the teaching whenever the familiar scene is seen again.","r":["151:3.10","151:3.11"]},{"x":"Hearing the same story, each person can interpret a parable according to his own intellectual and spiritual level.","r":["151:3.1"]}]},{"h":"Parables of the Growing Seed","items":[{"x":"The parable of the sower reviewed the ministry up to then and foreshadowed the varied success later messengers would meet.","r":["151:3.13"]},{"x":"Appealing only to emotion or intellect bears no fruit; true change of character comes from appealing to the spirit that lives within man.","r":["152:6.3"]},{"x":"The parable of the seed that grows by itself into the full ear shows that the kingdom grows quietly beyond human understanding.","r":["151:3.15"]},{"x":"The parables of the mustard seed and the leaven tell how the kingdom, small in its beginnings, grows great and spreads like leaven through the whole lump.","r":["151:4.2","151:4.3"]}]},{"h":"Parables Portraying the Father's Love","items":[{"q":"Mas eu vim mostrar-vos que, ao mesmo tempo que estais tentando encontrar Deus, do mesmo modo Deus está buscando encontrar-vos.","r":"169:1.2"},{"q":"the Father accepts you even before you have repented","r":"169:1.3"},{"x":"The father of the prodigal saw his son returning afar off, ran to meet him, and ordered a feast before the son had finished his confession.","r":["169:1.9","169:1.10"]},{"x":"The three stories of the lost sheep, the lost coin, and the lost son show respectively the Father seeking the lost, the thoroughness of the search, and complete restoration.","r":["169:1.15"]},{"x":"The parable of the prodigal son and the story of the good Samaritan were Jesus' favorite ways of teaching the Father's love and human neighborliness.","r":["169:1.16"]}]},{"h":"Neighborliness, Humility, and Faithfulness","items":[{"x":"To the trick question \"Who is my neighbor?\" Jesus answered with the story of the good Samaritan, letting the lawyer answer for himself.","r":["164:1.2","164:1.3","164:1.4"]},{"x":"The parable of the Pharisee and the publican teaches that salvation cannot be bought by works but is a free gift to all who have faith.","r":["167:5.1"]},{"x":"The parables of the talents and the pounds show that ability is the measure of opportunity and that equal faithfulness receives equal reward.","r":["171:8.10","171:8.13"]},{"q":"Let every man find out the meaning for himself and in his own soul.","r":"167:2.4"}]}],"see":["Ensinamentos de Jesus","Reino do céu","Amor","Perdão","Misericórdia","Os doze apóstolos"]},{"n":11,"t":"Paraíso","en":"Paradise","sum":"O Paraíso é o centro eterno do universo dos universos e a Ilha eterna onde residem o Pai, o Filho e o Espírito. Ao mesmo tempo morada espiritual e esfera material composta de absolutum, é a fonte de toda energia física e de toda gravidade, e o absoluto de todos os modelos. Existe sem tempo e não tem localização no espaço, e é o destino que todo mortal que conhece Deus está destinado a alcançar ao final da longa ascensão.","sections":[{"h":"A morada da Deidade","items":[{"x":"O Paraíso é o centro eterno do universo dos universos, onde residem o Pai, o Filho e o Espírito com os Seus coordenados, e é o corpo organizado mais gigantesco do universo-mestre.","r":["11:0.1"]},{"x":"O Paraíso é, ao mesmo tempo, uma morada espiritual e uma esfera material; existe desde a eternidade, e não há registros nem tradições sobre a sua origem.","r":["11:0.1","11:0.2"]},{"x":"A presença pessoal do Pai está no centro do Paraíso superior, cercada pela presença do Filho Eterno e envolta na glória do Espírito Infinito.","r":["11:1.1"]},{"x":"Quer se sigam as linhas da gravidade, as linhas da gravidade espiritual, os circuitos da mente ou o circuito da personalidade, chega-se finalmente à residência central do Pai.","r":["11:1.4"]},{"q":"Pois, se poucas são as criaturas do universo que se hajam encontrado com Deus no Paraíso, de nenhum modo isso invalida, seja a realidade da existência Dele, seja a factualidade da Sua pessoa espiritual no centro de todas as coisas.","r":"11:1.3"}]},{"h":"A natureza da Ilha eterna","items":[{"x":"O Paraíso não é esférico, mas um elipsoide achatado, cujo diâmetro norte-sul é um sexto mais longo que o diâmetro leste-oeste, e fornece o padrão de direção absoluta no universo-mestre.","r":["11:2.2","11:2.3"]},{"x":"A Ilha divide-se em Paraíso superior, periférico e inferior; a Trindade parece presidir o plano superior, pessoal, e o Absoluto Inqualificável, o plano inferior, impessoal.","r":["11:2.4","11:2.8"]},{"x":"O Paraíso é composto de uma organização homogênea de potência do espaço que não se encontra em nenhuma outra parte do universo, e que os Melquisedeques chamam de absolutum.","r":["11:2.9"]},{"q":"O Paraíso existe fora do tempo e não tem localização no espaço.","r":"11:2.10"},{"x":"Grosso modo, o espaço parece originar-se logo abaixo do Paraíso inferior, e o tempo, logo acima do Paraíso superior.","r":["11:2.11"]}]},{"h":"O Paraíso superior e o periférico","items":[{"x":"O Paraíso superior contém a área da presença da Deidade, a Esfera Santíssima, destinada à adoração e à trinitarização, e a Área Santa, destinada à residência.","r":["11:3.1"]},{"x":"As sete zonas concêntricas da Área Santa são chamadas de “as mansões do Pai no Paraíso”, e a segunda zona está reservada aos ascendentes dos sete superuniversos.","r":["11:3.3"]},{"x":"A área residencial destinada aos ascendentes ocupa menos de um por cento da terra santa designada, deixando amplo espaço para os seres que ainda virão.","r":["11:3.4"]},{"x":"O Paraíso periférico é o local de aterrissagem dos que atravessam o espaço e abriga vastas áreas de exposição histórica e profética dos universos locais.","r":["11:4.1","11:4.3"]},{"q":"You must wait, and ascend while you wait","r":"11:4.5"}]},{"h":"O Paraíso inferior e o espaço","items":[{"x":"Toda energia física e todos os circuitos de força cósmica originam-se no Paraíso inferior, onde não reside nenhuma personalidade.","r":["11:5.1"]},{"x":"A zona interior do centro de força do Paraíso inferior pulsa como um coração gigantesco, enviando correntes até os limites mais exteriores do espaço físico.","r":["11:5.5"]},{"x":"Acredita-se que a zona exterior seja o foco central da presença espacial do Absoluto Inqualificável, cujas emanações saem e entram alternadamente em ciclos de pouco mais de um bilhão de anos.","r":["11:5.7","11:5.8"]},{"x":"Todo o espaço expande-se e contrai-se alternadamente, e um ciclo de expansão e contração dura pouco mais de dois bilhões de anos do tempo de Urântia.","r":["11:6.1","11:6.5"]},{"x":"O espaço não toca o Paraíso; o Paraíso é o núcleo imóvel das zonas de quiescência situadas entre o espaço permeado e o não permeado.","r":["11:7.1","11:7.2"]}]},{"h":"O absoluto da gravidade e dos modelos","items":[{"q":"A gravidade é a garra da atração todo-poderosa da presença física do Paraíso.","r":"11:8.1"},{"x":"A gravidade absoluta é a gravidade do Paraíso, ao passo que a gravidade local ou linear pertence ao estágio elétrico da energia materializada.","r":["11:8.3"]},{"x":"O Paraíso é a fonte absoluta e o ponto focal eterno de toda energia-matéria do universo dos universos.","r":["11:8.9"]},{"x":"O sistema Paraíso-Havona é o núcleo eterno do universo-mestre, em torno do qual os sete superuniversos e o espaço exterior giram em órbitas estabelecidas.","r":["12:1.11"]},{"x":"O Paraíso não é criador nem Deidade; é o absoluto dos modelos, e Havona é o desdobramento factual dos seus potenciais.","r":["11:9.4","11:9.5","0:4.13"]},{"x":"Quando o Pai expressou o Seu eu espiritual no Filho Eterno, revelou simultaneamente o potencial infinito do Seu eu não pessoal como Paraíso.","r":["11:9.3"]}]},{"h":"O destino final","items":[{"x":"Para todas as personalidades espirituais, o Paraíso é o reino da origem primeira e a meta do destino final.","r":["11:9.1"]},{"x":"O Paraíso é o centro geográfico da infinitude, mas não faz parte de nenhuma criação universal, nem mesmo de Havona; é uma existência eterna e exclusiva.","r":["11:9.2"]},{"q":"O Paraíso é o centro de toda a criação, a fonte de todas as energias e o local da origem primeira de todas as personalidades.","r":"11:9.7"},{"x":"O peregrino que cai no último sono do tempo no primeiro circuito de Havona desperta no Paraíso, e somente então se torna um verdadeiro filho do Paraíso.","r":["26:11.6"]},{"x":"No Paraíso prevalecem uma ordem e uma harmonia perceptíveis, e os diretores de conduta instruem os recém-chegados para que possam viver ali sem confusão.","r":["27:4.2","27:4.3"]},{"x":"A morada de Deus é o modelo de todos os mundos-sede do universo, e o universo central da Sua morada é o modelo dos ideais e do destino de todos os universos.","r":["11:9.6"]},{"q":"Cada mortal sabedor de Deus, que abraçou a carreira de cumprir a vontade do Pai, já embarcou na trilha longa que vai até o Paraíso, da busca da divindade e do alcançar da perfeição.","r":"11:9.8"}]}],"see":["Havona","Gravidade","Os três Absolutos","Pai Universal","Grande universo e universo-mestre","Ascensão mortal"]},{"n":66,"t":"Pecado","en":"Sin","sum":"Sin is not mere imperfection or mistake but the attitude of a personality that knowingly and deliberately resists the Father's will and divine reality: deliberate disloyalty to God. The moral responsibility for sin is wholly personal and is not inherited, and no one loses survival because of another's sin. All sin can be forgiven, but a personality that has become wholly identified with sin becomes unreal and eventually reaches extinction.","sections":[{"h":"What Sin Is","items":[{"q":"“O pecado é a transgressão consciente, consabida e deliberada da lei divina, a vontade do Pai.","r":"148:4.4"},{"x":"Error is the misunderstanding of reality, evil a partial maladjustment to reality, and sin a purposeful resistance to divine reality.","r":["67:1.4"]},{"x":"Error reveals a lack of intellectual keenness, evil a deficiency of wisdom, sin spiritual poverty, and iniquity failing personality control.","r":["67:1.5"]},{"x":"Good is the carrying out of the divine plan; sin is a deliberate rebellion against the divine will.","r":["75:4.3"]},{"q":"Sin must be redefined as deliberate disloyalty to Deity.","r":"89:10.2"}]},{"h":"Imperfection Is Not Sin","items":[{"x":"The natural evil tendencies and imperfections of a person before rebirth are neither sin nor iniquity but only the starting point of the ascending journey.","r":["148:4.6"]},{"x":"Finiteness in itself is neither evil nor sinful; evil and sin arise when the finite is misused and distorted.","r":["111:6.3"]},{"x":"A sense of guilt is only the awareness of having violated a moral code and does not necessarily mean sin; there is true sin only in conscious disloyalty to God.","r":["89:10.3"]},{"x":"The capacity to feel guilt is not a badge of human degradation but a mark of a being with potential greatness.","r":["89:10.4"]},{"x":"Sin reveals the immaturity of one dazzled by the liberty of the will who fails to realize the obligations of universe citizenship.","r":["118:7.4"]}]},{"h":"Consequences of and Responsibility for Sin","items":[{"x":"The effects of sin are never local, but sin is fatal to survival only when it becomes the whole attitude of mind and soul.","r":["67:7.4"]},{"q":"Sin is wholly personal as to moral guilt or spiritual consequences","r":"67:7.7"},{"x":"No being's sin can prevent another's survival; eternal survival is jeopardized only by one's own choosing.","r":["67:7.5"]},{"q":"A natureza animal — a tendência para as más ações —pode ser hereditária, mas o pecado não é transmitido de pai para filho.","r":"188:4.5"},{"x":"Repeated sin becomes habit, and the habitual sinner can easily slip into iniquity and become a wholehearted rebel against the universe.","r":["67:1.6"]}]},{"h":"God and Sin","items":[{"x":"God loves the sinner as an eternal personality reality, but sin is neither a person nor a spiritual reality, so only justice takes cognizance of it.","r":["2:6.8"]},{"q":"O amor de Deus salva o pecador; a lei de Deus destrói o pecado.","r":"2:6.8"},{"x":"A being wholly identified with sin becomes unreal and self-destroying, and once the sentence of extinction is executed, it becomes as if it had never been.","r":["2:3.2","2:3.4"]},{"q":"O pecado é uma experiência da consciência da criatura, não é parte da consciência de Deus.","r":"174:1.4"}]},{"h":"The Evolution and Correction of the Idea of Sin","items":[{"x":"For primitive man sin was the violation of a ghost-sanctioned taboo, and death was regarded as its penalty.","r":["89:2.2","70:11.4"]},{"x":"Primitive sin was an act, not a thought, and ceremonial; it gave rise to the belief in a fall from a perfect beginning.","r":["89:2.3"]},{"x":"Sacrifice for personal sin gradually developed into the doctrine of atoning sacrifice for the sins of the race.","r":["89:4.5"]},{"x":"Jesus did not die to atone for the racial guilt of mankind or to appease the wrath of God.","r":["188:4.1"]},{"x":"Confession of sin does not remove its temporal consequences, but it is essential to religious growth and spiritual progress.","r":["89:10.5","156:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Mal","Perdão","Livre-arbítrio","Justiça","Rebelião de Lúcifer","Moralidade"]},{"n":92,"t":"Pentecostes","en":"Pentecost","sum":"Pentecost is the day, after Jesus' departure, when the Spirit of Truth was poured out upon the one hundred and twenty believers in the upper chamber in Jerusalem and upon all the sincere throughout the world. The apostles, who had been hiding in fear, came out endowed with new power and boldly preached the gospel, and that day more than two thousand were baptized. The Urantia Book explains that Pentecost was not an outburst of emotion but a spiritual event that freed the religion of Jesus from the fetters of nation, race, and sex, and from dependence on physical force.","sections":[{"h":"What Happened That Day","items":[{"x":"The one hundred and twenty believers at prayer sensed a strange presence in the room and became conscious of a new and profound feeling of spiritual joy, security, and confidence.","r":["194:0.1"]},{"x":"Peter declared this to be the coming of the Spirit of Truth the Master had promised and proposed that they go to the temple to proclaim the good news.","r":["194:0.2"]},{"x":"The apostles, who had hidden for forty days, appeared boldly in the temple crowded for the feast of Pentecost.","r":["194:1.1"]},{"x":"Peter's fervent appeal, made where the Master had last taught, won more than two thousand souls.","r":["194:1.2"]},{"x":"That evening the new believers were baptized in the Master's name at the pool of Siloam, and for a time the believers remained a sect within Judaism.","r":["194:1.4","194:1.5"]}]},{"h":"The Spirit Poured Out on All","items":[{"q":"Do not overlook the fact that the Spirit of Truth was bestowed upon all sincere believers","r":"194:3.6"},{"x":"The gift of the spirit came not only to the apostles but to all the men and women in the upper chamber and to the honest of heart throughout the world.","r":["194:3.6"]},{"x":"At the same hour the spirit came wherever there were true believers, in Philadelphia, Alexandria, and elsewhere.","r":["194:3.17"]},{"x":"Jesus' mother and brother were present but received no greater gift than the others; Pentecost ended belief in holy families and special priesthoods.","r":["194:3.15"]},{"x":"The spirit came upon those quietly sitting in prayer, apart from any form, ceremony, or sacred place.","r":["194:3.10"]}]},{"h":"A Spiritual Event, Not an Emotional One","items":[{"x":"Later Pentecost was confused with uncontrolled emotionalism, but the chief mission of the outpoured spirit was to teach the truths of the Father's love and the Son's mercy.","r":["194:3.1"]},{"q":"Prayer did not bring the spirit on the day of Pentecost","r":"194:3.20"},{"x":"Prayer does not move God to give more liberally, but it had much to do with determining each believer's capacity of receptivity.","r":["194:3.20"]},{"x":"\"Baptism of the spirit\" meant only the conscious reception of the gift of the Spirit of Truth and the acknowledgment of its new power.","r":["194:2.10"]},{"x":"The apostles lost themselves and found the spirit; it was not an emotional experience but a response to their dedication of themselves to God.","r":["194:3.16"]}]},{"h":"Religion Freed from Fetters","items":[{"q":"No Dia de Pentecostes, a religião de Jesus quebrou todas as restrições das nações e das prisões raciais.","r":"194:3.5"},{"x":"That many peoples received the apostles' preaching showed that the gospel must not be identified with any race, culture, or language.","r":["194:3.9"]},{"x":"After Pentecost, in the brotherhood of the kingdom, woman stood before God equal with man.","r":["194:3.14"]},{"x":"Pentecost freed the Master's religion from all dependence on physical force, equipping it with the spiritual weapons of forgiveness, good will, and love.","r":["194:3.11"]},{"q":"A humanidade pode ser unificada apenas pelo enfoque espiritual; e o Espírito da Verdade é, neste mundo, uma influência universal.","r":"194:3.18"}]},{"h":"God Seeking Man","items":[{"q":"Up to Pentecost, religion had revealed only man seeking for God","r":"194:3.13"},{"x":"Since Pentecost there shines out the spectacle of God also seeking man and, when he has found him, sending his spirit to dwell within him.","r":["194:3.13"]},{"x":"The bestowal of the Spirit of Truth prepared the minds of all normal people for the subsequent universal bestowal of the Adjusters.","r":["194:2.3"]},{"x":"Thereafter man has threefold guidance: the Adjuster, spirit of the Father; the Spirit of Truth, spirit of the Son; and the Holy Spirit, spirit of the Spirit.","r":["194:2.11"]},{"x":"Within less than a month after the spirit came, the apostles made more spiritual progress than in their four years with Jesus.","r":["194:2.9"]}]},{"h":"The New Message and the Beginning of the Church","items":[{"x":"Their message shifted from the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man to the proclamation of the risen Christ.","r":["194:0.3","194:4.4"]},{"q":"O evangelho do Reino, a mensagem de Jesus, havia, subitamente, sido transformado no evangelho do Senhor Jesus Cristo.","r":"194:4.5"},{"x":"Calling one another brothers and sisters, the believers formed a fellowship of worship and life, breaking bread, praying, and caring for the poor.","r":["194:4.3","194:4.7"]},{"x":"Stephen's martyrdom led to the formal organization of the early church, and the persecution that followed scattered teachers to the ends of the empire.","r":["194:4.12","194:4.13"]},{"x":"Jesus' earth life becomes the anchor of time, and the Spirit of Truth the source that makes the religion he lived grow forever.","r":["194:3.8"]}]}],"see":["Espírito da Verdade","Ressurreição de Jesus","Os doze apóstolos","Religião institucional","Ajustador do Pensamento","Espírito Santo"]},{"n":68,"t":"Perdão","en":"Forgiveness","sum":"God's forgiveness flows naturally from his infinite understanding; it is given before man asks and requires no intermediary or sacrifice. Yet this forgiveness becomes real in personal religious experience only when one forgives one's fellows. Jesus taught to forgive even seventy times seven, and he said that inability to forgive others is a mark of immaturity that has not attained understanding and love.","sections":[{"h":"Forgiveness in the Father's Nature","items":[{"q":"E porque Deus sabe de tudo sobre os Seus filhos, torna-se fácil para Ele perdoar.","r":"2:4.2"},{"x":"At the bottom of God's goodness lies the universal tendency to love, show mercy, manifest patience, and minister forgiveness.","r":["2:6.9"]},{"x":"The Father is not a personality divided between justice and mercy, and he requires no mediator in order to forgive.","r":["2:6.6"]},{"x":"Divine forgiveness is an inevitable consequence inherent in God's infinite understanding, his full knowledge of his children's errors and choices.","r":["174:1.3"]},{"x":"The understanding love of wise parents usually prevents the very estrangement that would call for repentance and forgiveness.","r":["174:1.2"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Receive Forgiveness","items":[{"x":"Divine forgiveness is the renewal of severed relations of loyalty; it need not be sought, only recognized and accepted.","r":["89:10.6"]},{"q":"The Father in heaven has forgiven you even before you have thought to ask him","r":"146:2.4"},{"x":"God's forgiveness is in fact unconditioned, but in experience it becomes real only when one forgives one's fellows.","r":["146:2.4","170:3.4"]},{"x":"In forgiving his brother, a person creates in his soul the capacity to receive God's forgiveness of his own misdeeds.","r":["170:2.23"]},{"x":"Faith is the price of entrance into God's family, and forgiveness is the act of God in accepting that faith.","r":["170:3.3"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that forgiveness of sin is received by faith in God, without penance or sacrifice.","r":["138:8.2","150:5.2"]}]},{"h":"Forgive One Another","items":[{"q":"the Father in heaven forgives you your sins; therefore should you learn to forgive one another.","r":"159:1.3"},{"x":"When Peter asked whether seven times was enough, Jesus answered to forgive even seventy times seven.","r":["159:1.4"]},{"x":"With the parable of the steward forgiven a great debt by the king who would not forgive his fellow's small debt, he taught the duty of the forgiven.","r":["159:1.4","159:1.5"]},{"x":"The better one understands a neighbor, the easier it is to forgive; when one loves a brother, one has already forgiven him.","r":["2:4.2","174:1.4"]},{"q":"O homem não perdoará verdadeiramente os seus semelhantes a menos que os ame como a si próprio.","r":"170:3.5"}]},{"h":"The Immaturity That Cannot Forgive","items":[{"q":"“A vossa incapacidade ou falta de disposição de perdoar os vossos semelhantes é a medida da vossa imaturidade, do vosso insucesso em alcançar a compaixão amadurecida, a compreensão e o amor.","r":"174:1.5"},{"x":"People hold grudges and nurse vengefulness in proportion to their ignorance of others' inner nature and longings.","r":["174:1.5"]},{"x":"All sin can be forgiven, but it is doubtful that a confirmed iniquitous person would ever truly sorrow or accept forgiveness.","r":["67:1.6"]},{"x":"Those who knowingly and maliciously attribute the works of God to the forces of evil can hardly obtain forgiveness.","r":["153:4.3","165:3.6"]},{"x":"The Father is not an indulgent parent who overlooks everything; he does not condone his children's self-destructive conduct.","r":["147:5.9"]}]},{"h":"Forgiveness in History and the Example of Jesus","items":[{"x":"In primitive religion confession and forgiveness were a meaningless ritual that forgave in advance even the sins of the following week.","r":["89:2.5"]},{"x":"Hosea preached forgiveness through repentance, not sacrifice, and revived the gospel of love and divine mercy.","r":["97:4.5"]},{"x":"Before Jesus, a God who forgives repentant sinners was known, but a God who goes out first to seek the lost sheep was new.","r":["159:5.16"]},{"q":"As únicas palavras de Jesus, quando o pregavam na viga da cruz, foram: “Pai, perdoa-lhes, pois não sabem o que fazem”.","r":"187:2.4"},{"x":"Peter, who had denied the Master, fully believed he was forgiven only after the risen Jesus received him again.","r":["184:2.13","139:2.10"]}]}],"see":["Misericórdia","Pecado","Amor","Irmandade dos homens","Ensinamentos de Jesus","Filiação a Deus"]},{"n":36,"t":"Personalidade","en":"Personality","sum":"Personality is the unique gift that the Universal Father exclusively bestows upon living energy systems of matter, mind, and spirit. It is neither body, mind, spirit, nor soul; it is the one changeless reality amid ever-changing experience, and it unifies all other factors. Personality shows itself in self-consciousness and relative free will; every personality is linked to the Father by his personality circuit and survives death with the survival of the soul.","sections":[{"h":"The Father's Gift","items":[{"x":"God the Father is the bestower and conservator of every personality, and the destiny of all finite personalities who choose the divine will.","r":["5:6.1"]},{"q":"Não há personalidade fora de Deus, o Pai, e nenhuma personalidade existe senão para Deus, o Pai.","r":"5:6.4"},{"x":"Personality does not arise of itself; the impersonal never becomes personal without a direct act of the Father.","r":["0:5.4","5:6.3"]},{"x":"Personality is not attained by degrees; it is either present or absent.","r":["5:6.3"]},{"x":"Personality is bestowed directly by the Universal Father, or by the Conjoint Actor acting for him, and may be given to living energy systems endowed with mind or spirit.","r":["112:0.3","112:0.4"]}]},{"h":"What Personality Is","items":[{"q":"Personality is the one changeless reality in an otherwise ever-changing creature experience;","r":"0:5.11"},{"x":"Human personality is neither body, mind, spirit, nor soul, and it unifies all the other factors of individuality.","r":["0:5.11"]},{"x":"Personality is one of the unsolved mysteries of the universe; its components are known, but its real nature is not fully understood.","r":["5:6.2"]},{"x":"Personality has no identity of its own, yet it can unify the identity of a living energy system.","r":["112:0.7"]},{"x":"In the human system personality unifies all activities and imparts the qualities of identity and creativity.","r":["112:1.19"]}]},{"h":"Unique and Changeless","items":[{"x":"Personalities may be similar but never the same; even those of the same series and type are not identical.","r":["16:8.4"]},{"x":"Because of personality we can recognize a being as the very one we knew before, however much its form or spiritual status has changed.","r":["16:8.4"]},{"q":"they are associable but nontotalable.","r":"112:0.12"},{"x":"Adjusters are alike in nature when they come from the Father, but personality is diverse, original, and exclusive.","r":["16:8.3"]},{"x":"Through all the stages of evolution there is in each person a changeless part, the personality that endures amid change.","r":["112:0.1"]}]},{"h":"Self-Consciousness and Free Will","items":[{"x":"Creature personality is distinguished by two phenomena: self-consciousness and the associated relative free will.","r":["16:8.5"]},{"x":"Self-consciousness is awareness of one's own personality reality, and it includes the ability to recognize the reality of other personalities.","r":["16:8.6"]},{"x":"Human free will relates to seven domains, among them moral decisions, spiritual choices, unselfish love, and worship.","r":["16:8.7","16:8.8","16:8.14"]},{"q":"Ela pode proporcionar uma dádiva a Deus — a dedicação, por livre escolha, de fazer a vontade de Deus.","r":"112:0.10"},{"x":"Having provided for the growth of the soul, the Father steps aside; in the matter of eternal survival he has decreed the absolute sovereignty of the mortal will.","r":["5:6.8"]}]},{"h":"The Personality Circuit and Relationships","items":[{"x":"All personalities are circuited in the personal presence of the Universal Father, and the Father is personally conscious of every personality.","r":["5:6.10","5:6.11"]},{"x":"This personality circuit exists apart from the mission of the Thought Adjusters, and personalities not indwelt by Adjusters are also embraced in it.","r":["5:6.10","5:6.12"]},{"x":"Personality responds directly to the presence of other personality and is characterized by a morality that recognizes the relativity of its relations with others.","r":["112:0.11","112:0.13"]},{"q":"A personalidade não pode atuar bem em isolamento.","r":"112:1.16"},{"x":"Because we are conscious of God as Creator Father, we become conscious of men as creature brothers.","r":["16:9.14"]}]},{"h":"Survival and Destiny of Personality","items":[{"x":"The material self has a temporal identity and the Adjuster an eternal identity, and together they produce the surviving identity of the immortal soul.","r":["5:6.7"]},{"q":"A identidade da personalidade sobrevive por meio da sobrevivência da alma e na própria alma.","r":"16:9.3"},{"x":"Human personality is eternal yet conditional as to identity; it must choose for itself whether to stand where destiny is fulfilled.","r":["112:5.2"]},{"x":"Relationships between personalities are not scaffolding; mortal memories of personal relations have cosmic value and persist on the mansion worlds.","r":["112:5.22"]},{"x":"The fact that God became man has forever changed all the meanings and values of human personality.","r":["112:2.7"]}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Alma","Mente","Livre-arbítrio","Sobrevivência","Personalidade de Deus"]},{"n":3,"t":"Personalidade de Deus","en":"Personality of God","sum":"O Pai Universal é infinito e, no entanto, uma verdadeira personalidade. A personalidade não é um atributo entre muitos, mas o modo pelo qual se revela a totalidade da Sua natureza infinita e da Sua vontade unificada. A personalidade de toda criatura é outorgada pelo Pai e mantida no Seu circuito da personalidade, e, porque Deus é pessoal, o homem pode comungar com Ele, amá-Lo e tornar-se Seu amigo.","sections":[{"h":"Deus infinito e pessoal","items":[{"q":"Deus é tanto infinito, quanto pessoal; Ele é uma personalidade infinita.","r":"1:5.1"},{"x":"Deus transcende em muito qualquer conceito de personalidade que o homem possa apreender, mas Ele não pode ser nada menos do que uma personalidade eterna, verdadeira, boa e bela.","r":["1:5.2"]},{"x":"Sem Deus e a Sua personalidade central, não haveria personalidade em parte alguma do vasto universo.","r":["1:5.7"]},{"x":"A personalidade não é um atributo de Deus, mas a totalidade da Sua natureza infinita coordenada e da Sua vontade divina unificada: a revelação de Deus ao universo dos universos.","r":["1:5.13"]},{"x":"Deus é mais do que poder, energia, modelo ou presença; Ele é uma personalidade que exerce uma vontade soberana, experimenta a autoconsciência da divindade e revela aos Seus filhos o amor de um pai.","r":["3:6.7"]}]},{"h":"Concepções errôneas sobre a personalidade","items":[{"q":"A personalidade humana é uma imagem, uma sombra tempo-espacial projetada pela personalidade Criadora divina.","r":"1:6.1"},{"x":"A personalidade não requer um corpo material; por causa desse erro, o materialismo nega a personalidade dos mortos, e o panteísmo, a personalidade de um Deus sem corpo.","r":["1:5.12"]},{"x":"Negar a personalidade da Primeira Fonte e Centro deixa apenas os dois dilemas filosóficos do materialismo e do panteísmo.","r":["1:5.11"]},{"x":"A razão, a sabedoria e a experiência religiosa implicam a personalidade de Deus, mas não a provam; esse conceito chegou à humanidade principalmente por meio da revelação.","r":["1:5.10"]},{"q":"Deus é uma causa para a ciência; uma idéia para a filosofia; e para a religião é uma pessoa ou mesmo o Pai celeste, cheio de amor.","r":"1:6.2"},{"x":"O homem contempla o infinito a partir do finito, e Deus contempla o finito a partir do infinito; assim, o conceito da personalidade divina melhora à medida que melhora a compreensão humana da personalidade humana.","r":["1:6.3"]}]},{"h":"O outorgador da personalidade","items":[{"x":"O Pai é o outorgador e o conservador de toda personalidade, desde o mortal mais humilde até o criador mais elevado, e o destino de toda personalidade finita que escolhe a Sua vontade.","r":["5:6.1"]},{"x":"A mente, o espírito ou a energia física, por si sós, não são personalidade; a personalidade é o dom que o Pai outorga exclusivamente aos sistemas vivos de matéria, mente e espírito.","r":["5:6.3","5:6.4"]},{"q":"E a personalidade não é, também, uma conquista progressiva.","r":"5:6.3"},{"x":"Assim como toda gravidade está ligada à Ilha do Paraíso, toda mente ao Agente Conjunto e todo espírito ao Filho Eterno, toda personalidade está ligada ao circuito da personalidade do Pai.","r":["5:6.11"]},{"x":"À parte da missão dos Ajustadores, o Pai tem consciência pessoal das personalidades de todos os níveis de existência autoconsciente e está em contato com elas.","r":["5:6.10"]}]},{"h":"Respeito pelo livre-arbítrio","items":[{"x":"Ao outorgar personalidade a uma criatura, o Pai outorga-lhe também uma liberdade relativa em face da resposta servil à causação antecedente.","r":["5:6.9"]},{"x":"Tendo provido o crescimento da alma, o Pai Se retira, e decretou como lei absoluta a soberania da vontade mortal no que se refere à sobrevivência eterna.","r":["5:6.8"]},{"q":"No personal creature can be coerced into the eternal adventure","r":"5:6.12"}]},{"h":"Comunhão com um Deus pessoal","items":[{"x":"Entre coisas impessoais há apenas interação; uma comunhão como a de pai e filho só pode ser desfrutada quando ambos são personalidades.","r":["1:7.1"]},{"q":"O homem consegue a união com Deus, mas não como uma gota de água poderia encontrar a unidade com o oceano.","r":"1:7.2"},{"x":"A verdade e a beleza podem ser concebidas à parte da personalidade, mas a bondade divina só é compreendida em relação à personalidade, e somente uma personalidade pode amar e ser amada.","r":["1:7.3"]},{"x":"Porque Deus pode conhecer e ser conhecido, amar e ser amado, também o homem pode ser conhecido como amigo de Deus.","r":["1:5.8"]},{"x":"Jesus realizou plenamente o potencial da personalidade espiritual na experiência humana; por isso a Sua vida é a revelação mais prática da personalidade de Deus.","r":["1:6.8"]},{"x":"Se o homem deixar de ver o amor de um Deus pessoal, o Reino de Deus torna-se meramente o reino do bem.","r":["2:5.12"]}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Personalidade","Livre-arbítrio","Atributos de Deus","Amor","Auto-outorga de Jesus"]},{"n":30,"t":"Portadores da Vida","en":"Life Carriers","sum":"The Life Carriers are local universe Sons created jointly by the Creator Son, the Universe Mother Spirit, and one of the Ancients of Days; they design creature life, plant it on the planets, and foster its evolution. The spark of life is given through them, but its essential factor comes from the Universe Mother Spirit, and their manipulations end once beings with will appear. Urantia is a life-modification world, and its life was newly formulated right here on the planet.","sections":[{"h":"Origin and Organization","items":[{"x":"The Life Carriers are the offspring of the Creator Son, the Universe Mother Spirit, and one designated Ancient of Days; they are the only group of intelligent life in the local universe in whose creation the superuniverse rulers take part.","r":["36:1.1"]},{"q":"Estão encarregados de elaborar a vida para as criaturas e levá-la às esferas planetárias.","r":"36:0.1"},{"x":"After creating three orders of sons, including the Melchizedeks, the Son and Spirit of the local universe co-operate with the next level of God the Sevenfold to produce the Life Carriers.","r":["35:0.7"]},{"x":"One hundred million have been created in Nebadon, directed by the life-determining trio of Gabriel, the Father Melchizedek, and Nambia, the first-born Life Carrier.","r":["36:1.2"]},{"x":"They are divided into three groups: senior Life Carriers, assistants, and custodians; a corps sent to a planet usually consists of one hundred seniors, one hundred assistants, and one thousand custodians.","r":["36:1.3","36:3.2"]},{"x":"They can function on three levels: the physical level of electrochemistry, the intermediate level of quasi-morontia existence, and the semispiritual level.","r":["65:1.2","65:1.3","65:1.5"]}]},{"h":"Designing and Planting Life","items":[{"q":"A vida não aparece espontaneamente nos universos; os Portadores da Vida devem iniciá-la nos planetas até então estéreis.","r":"36:3.1"},{"x":"On the seven Life Carrier worlds of the Salvington circuit they study life planning, conservation, evolution, life associated with mind, and more; the original life designs are provided by the Creator Son.","r":["36:2.1","36:2.12"]},{"q":"A centelha vital — o mistério da vida — é conferida por intermédio dos Portadores da Vida, não por eles.","r":"36:3.4"},{"x":"They formulate the life plasm, but the energy spark that enlivens the body and presages the mind comes from the Universe Mother Spirit.","r":["36:3.4"]},{"x":"In imparting life they transmit nothing of their personal natures; as living catalytic presences they merely initiate the essential revolutions of matter.","r":["36:3.5"]},{"q":"Os Filhos de Deus podem construir as formas da vida, mas é o Espírito de Deus que realmente contribui com a centelha vital.","r":"36:6.4"}]},{"h":"Fostering Evolution and Its Limits","items":[{"x":"About half a million years of planetary time are allowed for establishing life on a new world; when that period ends, nothing new may be added.","r":["36:3.6"]},{"x":"Until moral beings appear they may manipulate the environment to favor evolution, but they are not permitted to interfere mechanically or arbitrarily with the evolutionary process.","r":["36:3.7","65:3.2"]},{"q":"E é por isso que a evolução — em Urântia, ou em outro lugar — tem sempre um propósito, nunca sendo acidental.","r":"65:0.7"},{"x":"When beings of will appear, their work is ended, and they must either leave the planet or take renunciation oaths to influence evolution no further.","r":["36:3.8","65:1.8"]},{"x":"Two senior Life Carriers and twelve custodians remain on Urantia even now as advisers, under renunciation oaths.","r":["36:3.9"]},{"x":"Since life cannot be made to unfold faster than the physical development of the planet, the Life Carriers must wait upon geologic evolution.","r":["58:1.2","65:8.2"]}]},{"h":"The Life Experiment on Urantia","items":[{"x":"Urantia is a decimal planet, a life-modification world, where the Life Carriers attempted to modify and improve the standard life designs.","r":["58:0.1","65:4.1"]},{"q":"A vida de Urântia é única, e original com o planeta.","r":"58:4.1"},{"x":"Because Urantia protoplasm was planned to function only in a salt solution, implantation waited until the sea waters had become sufficiently salty.","r":["58:1.3"]},{"x":"Five hundred and fifty million years ago the corps of Life Carriers returned and made three marine-life implantations in the sheltered tropical inlets of the central sea between the separating continents.","r":["58:4.2","58:4.4"]},{"x":"The chemical formula for wound healing was chosen after more than half a million experiments, showing that human life was intelligently planned.","r":["65:4.3","65:4.4"]},{"x":"Urantia is the only planet in Satania where human-type will appeared in a race earlier than the colored races.","r":["65:4.11"]}]},{"h":"Life, Mind, and Spirit","items":[{"x":"The seven adjutant mind-spirits always accompany the Life Carriers to a new planet, and their central focus is located on the headquarters world of the Life Carriers.","r":["36:5.4","36:2.10"]},{"q":"life springs only from life.","r":"36:6.2"},{"x":"The experimental forms of life they organize on the Salvington worlds are always without reproductive ability.","r":["36:6.3"]},{"x":"They know that life flows from the Father, through the Son, and by the Spirit, yet even they do not fully understand the nature and source of the life-activating spark.","r":["36:6.7"]},{"x":"When the universe is settled in light and life, they expect to attain a fourth, wholly spiritual, stage of existence.","r":["65:1.9"]}]}],"see":["Evolução","Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Urântia","Melquisedeques","Filho Criador Michael"]},{"n":80,"t":"Raças","en":"Races","sum":"Mankind on Urantia began nearly a million years ago with Andon and Fonta, and about five hundred thousand years ago the six colored races, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and indigo, appeared all at once in one Sangik family. The violet race of Adam and Eve was later added, forming the Andites, and no pure races remain today. The races differ in mental outlook and capacity, yet all races have the same standing before heaven and are indwelt by the same spirit.","sections":[{"h":"Andon and Fonta","items":[{"x":"Urantia was registered as an inhabited world when the twins, the first two human beings, were eleven years old.","r":["63:0.1"]},{"q":"“A mente humana apareceu no 606 de Satânia, e esses pais da nova raça serão chamados de Andon e Fonta. E todos os arcanjos oram para que essas criaturas possam rapidamente ser dotadas com a dádiva do espírito do Pai Universal, residindo nas suas pessoas”.","r":"63:0.2"},{"x":"Mankind has a history of nearly a million years; the Andonites avoided the forests and made progress in open lands and higher latitudes.","r":["64:0.2","64:1.3"]},{"x":"Again and again in Urantia's history superior stocks have mixed with inferior stocks and deteriorated.","r":["64:1.7","64:1.8"]}]},{"h":"The Emergence of the Six Sangik Races","items":[{"x":"About five hundred thousand years ago, in the highlands of northwestern India, a Sangik family produced unusually intelligent children.","r":["64:5.1","64:5.2"]},{"q":"Dessas dezenove crianças, cinco eram vermelhas, duas alaranjadas, quatro amarelas, duas verdes, quatro azuis e duas índigo-negras.","r":"64:5.3"},{"x":"On an average planet the races appear one after another beginning with the red, but on Urantia the six races came from one family at the same time.","r":["64:6.1"]},{"x":"The red, yellow, and blue are primary races and the orange, green, and indigo secondary, and their intellectual and spiritual gifts overlap.","r":["51:4.3","82:6.2"]},{"x":"Differentiation into the various colored races gives mankind desirable variation that could not be obtained otherwise.","r":["51:4.4"]}]},{"h":"Histories of the Races","items":[{"x":"Driven out of Asia by the yellow man, the red man crossed to North America about eighty-five thousand years ago, where Onamonalonton for a time restored peace.","r":["64:6.4","64:6.5","64:6.7"]},{"x":"The yellow race first achieved settled agriculture and social cooperation and, under Singlangton's leadership, worshiped \"One Truth.\"","r":["64:6.14","64:6.15"]},{"x":"The orange and green races, after endless strife, were absorbed into other races and disappeared.","r":["64:6.13","64:6.20"]},{"x":"The blue man invented the spear and laid the foundations of the modern arts; the so-called white race is mainly descended from him.","r":["64:6.21","64:6.24"]},{"x":"The violet race of Adam and Eve spread out from the second garden and blended with the Nodites and Sangik races to become the Andites.","r":["78:0.1","78:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Racial Diversity and Blending","items":[{"x":"Diversity stimulates natural selection and healthy competition, and differences among races foster tolerance and altruism.","r":["64:6.31","64:6.33","64:6.34"]},{"q":"A homogeneidade da raça humana não é desejável, antes que os povos de um mundo em evolução atinjam níveis relativamente altos de desenvolvimento espiritual.","r":"64:6.35"},{"q":"Hoje não há raças puras no mundo.","r":"82:6.1"},{"x":"The blending of superior and dissimilar stocks produces new and vigorous strains, and the dangers of race mixture have been much exaggerated.","r":["82:6.5","82:6.8"]},{"x":"Most objection to race mixture rests on social and cultural prejudice rather than on biology.","r":["82:6.7","82:6.8"]}]},{"h":"Equal Standing Before Heaven","items":[{"q":"Não obstante o seu atraso, esses povos índigos têm o mesmo status, perante os poderes celestes, de qualquer das outras raças terrenas.","r":"64:6.27"},{"q":"As mentes podem diferir racialmente, mas toda a humanidade é residida pelo mesmo espírito divino e eterno.","r":"155:6.8"},{"x":"Human unity and brotherhood can be achieved only through the religion of the spirit, which is personal experience, not through religions of authority.","r":["155:6.8"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus commanded that the gospel of the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man be wisely carried to all nations and races.","r":["191:4.4"]},{"x":"Pentecost wiped out all religious discrimination based on race, culture, caste, or sex.","r":["194:3.14"]}]}],"see":["Evolução","Adão e Eva","Urântia","Civilização","Irmandade dos homens","Caligástia"]},{"n":98,"t":"Realidade","en":"Reality","sum":"In The Urantia Book reality is the totality of all existence, originating in the infinite volition of the Universal Father and differentiated and actualized on various universe levels. Reality is divided into actual and potential, absolute and subabsolute, existential and experiential, personal and impersonal, and its totality is infinity, which no finite mind can fully grasp. Man recognizes fact, meaning, and value through science, philosophy, and religion, and spirit is the basic reality of all personality experience.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Reality","items":[{"x":"Reality originates in and by the infinite volition of the Universal Father and is differentiated and actualized on various universe levels.","r":["0:4.1"]},{"x":"Universe philosophers attribute absolute primal causation in infinity to the Universal Father functioning as the I AM.","r":["105:1.1"]},{"q":"O EU SOU é o Infinito; o EU SOU é também a infinitude.","r":"105:1.3"},{"x":"All absolute reality, the three Deities, the Isle of Paradise, and the three Absolutes, is from eternity and without beginning.","r":["105:2.1"]},{"x":"The primal differentiation of reality is into the deified and the undeified, the Deity Absolute and the Unqualified Absolute, whose tension is resolved by the Universal Absolute.","r":["0:4.5"]}]},{"h":"The Differentiation of Reality","items":[{"x":"Reality appears as undeified reality, deified reality, and the interassociated reality between the two.","r":["0:4.2","0:4.3","0:4.4"]},{"x":"From the viewpoint of time and space, reality is divided into actual and potential, absolute and subabsolute, existential and experiential, personal and impersonal.","r":["0:4.7","0:4.8","0:4.10"]},{"x":"Paradise Deity is existential, but the emerging Supreme and Ultimate are experiential.","r":["0:4.9"]},{"x":"The grand universe and the emerging master universe consist of many levels of reality beginning with the incomplete finite, and Urantia mortals are on its first level.","r":["106:0.2","106:0.3"]},{"x":"On absolute and eternal levels potential reality is as meaningful as actual reality; only to time-bound creatures do the two seem so different.","r":["118:1.10"]}]},{"h":"The Limits of the Finite Mind","items":[{"x":"Even to high intelligences infinity is only partially comprehensible, and the finality of reality only relatively so.","r":["105:0.1"]},{"q":"reality totality is infinity and therefore can never be fully comprehended by any mind that is subinfinite in concept capacity.","r":"105:0.2"},{"x":"Concepts of reality inevitably suffer serious distortion when translated to the level of mortal comprehension.","r":["105:0.3"]},{"x":"The mortal mind can hardly comprehend seven levels of relative cosmic reality, but it can grasp much of the three functioning levels of finite reality.","r":["12:8.9"]}]},{"h":"Fact, Meaning, and Value","items":[{"q":"Há apenas três elementos na realidade universal: o fato, a idéia e a relação.","r":"196:3.2"},{"x":"We call these three realities thing, meaning, and value, and science, philosophy, and religion respectively recognize them.","r":["196:3.2"]},{"x":"The three insights inherent in cosmic mind, causation, duty, and worship, make possible the recognition of scientific, moral, and spiritual reality.","r":["16:6.6","16:6.7","16:6.8"]},{"x":"Physical certainty lies in the logic of science, moral certainty in the wisdom of philosophy, and spiritual certainty in the truth of genuine religious experience.","r":["196:3.5"]},{"x":"In the final analysis matter vanishes from the senses and mind too disappears, but spirit insight still recognizes spiritual reality and supreme value.","r":["112:2.11"]}]},{"h":"Spirit, the Basic Reality","items":[{"q":"O espírito é a realidade pessoal básica nos universos; e a personalidade é básica para toda a experiência de progresso com a realidade espiritual.","r":"12:9.1"},{"x":"Because God is spirit, changeless spirit is the basic reality of all personality experience, beyond the experiential variables of mind and matter.","r":["12:8.14"]},{"x":"It is an error to regard matter as basic reality and mind and spirit as rooted in matter.","r":["8:2.3"]},{"q":"The spirit is the creative reality","r":"42:12.14"},{"x":"The physical is the time-space reflection of spirit reality; matter is the skeleton of morontia, and both are shadows of spirit reality.","r":["42:12.14","189:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Reality and God","items":[{"x":"The soul is a new morontia reality born in experience, with the indwelling spirit as father and the material mind as mother.","r":["0:5.10"]},{"q":"A compreensão progressiva da realidade é equivalente a uma aproximação de Deus.","r":"196:3.3"},{"x":"To experience total reality is the full realization of God, the finality of the God-knowing experience.","r":["196:3.3"]},{"x":"Ascending man advances at once inward toward the experience of God and outward toward the understanding of energy.","r":["103:7.3"]}]}],"see":["Os três Absolutos","Pai Universal","Ser Supremo","Experiência","Ciência e religião","Filosofia"]},{"n":76,"t":"Rebelião de Lúcifer","en":"Lucifer Rebellion","sum":"The Lucifer rebellion was the revolt launched some two hundred thousand years ago by Lucifer, sovereign of the system of Satania, together with his first assistant, Satan. It began with a \"Declaration of Liberty\" that denied the reality of the Father, the sovereignty of Michael, and the ascension plan. Thirty-seven Planetary Princes joined it, and Urantia was among their worlds. The rebellion sprang from self-contemplation and pride; the universe rulers waited long so that every being could make a full choice, and Michael's bestowal virtually ended the rebellion.","sections":[{"h":"Lucifer and the Origin of the Rebellion","items":[{"x":"Lucifer was not an ascendant being but a brilliant Son created in the local universe, and he ruled Satania with its 607 inhabited worlds.","r":["53:1.1","53:1.2"]},{"q":"A auto-admiração é sumamente desastrosa, até mesmo para as elevadas personalidades do mundo celeste.","r":"53:1.3"},{"x":"No special conditions in Satania favored rebellion; the idea of revolt originated in Lucifer's own mind.","r":["53:2.2","53:2.3"]},{"x":"In a pride that led to self-deception, he at some point became disloyal, and evil turned into deliberate sin.","r":["53:2.5"]},{"x":"On Urantia Lucifer entrusted his cause to his first assistant, Satan, and Caligastia took his side here.","r":["53:1.4","53:7.2"]}]},{"h":"The Lucifer Manifesto","items":[{"x":"Lucifer claimed that the Universal Father did not really exist and was a myth invented by the Sons to maintain their rule.","r":["53:3.2"]},{"x":"He demanded self-government for the local systems and attacked the sovereignty of Michael and the interference of the Ancients of Days as tyranny.","r":["53:3.3","53:3.4"]},{"x":"He denounced the plan of long training for ascending mortals as a waste of time and energy.","r":["53:3.6"]},{"q":"A auto-afirmação foi o grito de batalha da rebelião de Lúcifer.","r":"53:4.2"},{"x":"Lucifer pointed to the merciful delays of justice as proof that the government of the Sons was incompetent.","r":["53:4.5"]}]},{"h":"War in Heaven and Its Losses","items":[{"x":"Michael, not yet having completed his bestowals, chose noninterference, and Gabriel led the loyal hosts.","r":["53:5.1","53:5.4"]},{"x":"The war in heaven was not a physical conflict, but it was far more deadly because eternal life was at stake.","r":["53:5.6","53:5.7"]},{"x":"Thirty-seven Planetary Princes joined the rebellion; only on Panoptia did the people refuse to follow their prince and stand with Michael.","r":["53:7.1"]},{"x":"The angelic orders suffered the greatest losses, yet no being of Paradise origin and none of the Trinitized Sons went astray.","r":["53:7.5","53:7.6","53:7.8"]},{"q":"it is recorded to the glory of the wisdom of the ascension scheme that not a single member of the Satania ascendant citizenship resident on Jerusem participated in the Lucifer rebellion.","r":"53:7.10"}]},{"h":"True and False Liberty","items":[{"x":"The greatest confusion left by the Lucifer rebellion came from the failure to distinguish true liberty from false liberty.","r":["54:1.1"]},{"q":"A verdadeira liberdade é fruto do controle de si próprio; a liberdade falsa é fruto da pretensão da afirmação do ego.","r":"54:1.6"},{"x":"Liberty becomes self-destroying when it is divorced from justice, fairness, forbearance, moral obligation, and spiritual values.","r":["54:1.3","54:1.4"]},{"x":"Lucifer's folly lay in attempting to short-circuit time in an experiential universe.","r":["54:2.3"]}]},{"h":"The Wisdom of Delay and the End of the Rebellion","items":[{"q":"A justiça suprema é dominada pelo amor do Pai; portanto a justiça jamais destruirá aquilo que a misericórdia pode salvar.","r":"54:5.3"},{"x":"It was advised that an arbitrary suppression would have led at least three times as many beings astray.","r":["54:5.12"]},{"x":"Michael offered the rebels forgiveness and restoration to service if they repented, but none of the leaders accepted.","r":["53:9.1"]},{"x":"Michael's bestowal ended the rebellion throughout Satania, and Lucifer was afterward detained by the Ancients of Days.","r":["53:8.3","53:9.2"]},{"q":"faith is an effective armor against sin and iniquity.","r":"53:8.8"},{"x":"The Melchizedeks teach that the good resulting from the Satania rebellion is more than a thousand times the sum of all the evil.","r":["54:6.6"]}]}],"see":["Caligástia","Livre-arbítrio","Pecado","Mal","Filho Criador Michael","Constelações e sistemas locais"]},{"n":49,"t":"Reino do céu","en":"Kingdom of Heaven","sum":"The kingdom of God, or kingdom of heaven, is the central concept of the gospel Jesus proclaimed; above all it is the personal spiritual experience of the heavenly Father's will ruling in the believer's heart. It is founded on the fatherhood of God and the brotherhood of man, is entered now by faith, and bears fruit in loving service. In later times the kingdom concept was replaced by the institutional church, but the spiritual kingdom Jesus taught will yet be proclaimed again.","sections":[{"h":"\"The Kingdom Is Within You\"","items":[{"x":"Jesus used the kingdom of heaven and the kingdom of God with the same meaning, and made it the name for his bestowal mission.","r":["170:0.1"]},{"x":"To his apostles Jesus taught the kingdom as a personal experience lived in relation to one's fellows and to the heavenly Father.","r":["170:1.13"]},{"q":"A respeito do Reino, a sua última palavra foi: “o Reino está dentro de vós”.","r":"170:1.13"},{"x":"Jesus tried to persuade his followers to use \"the will of God\" in place of \"the kingdom,\" and to replace the idea of king and subjects with that of a heavenly family and liberated sons.","r":["170:2.11","170:2.12"]}]},{"h":"Foundations and Gifts of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"The kingdom of heaven begins with and is centered in the truth of the fatherhood of God and the fact of the brotherhood of man.","r":["170:2.1"]},{"x":"This teaching frees man from age-old animal fears and gives him new courage and spiritual power.","r":["170:2.1","170:2.2"]},{"x":"The gospel of the kingdom gives assurance and comfort even to the poor, and teaches the superiority of the spiritual over the material.","r":["170:2.3","170:2.5"]},{"x":"When the Father's will is your law, you are barely in the kingdom; when the Father's will becomes your will, you are truly in the kingdom.","r":["141:2.2"]}]},{"h":"How One Enters","items":[{"q":"Jesus ensinou que aquele que acredita pela fé entra imediatamente no Reino.","r":"170:2.20"},{"x":"The two conditions for entering the kingdom are childlike faith and sincerity, and a hunger for righteousness.","r":["170:2.21","170:2.22"]},{"x":"Simple, childlike belief is the key that opens the door, but once inside there are steps of righteousness to climb.","r":["170:3.2"]},{"q":"Faith is the price you pay for entrance into the family of God","r":"170:3.3"},{"x":"God's forgiveness is actually experienced in so far as one forgives one's fellows, and love of neighbor is the highest ethic.","r":["170:3.4","170:3.6"]},{"q":"O perdão de Deus fica de fato ao alcance do homem, que o experimenta pessoalmente tão logo ele perdoe os seus semelhantes.","r":"170:3.4"}]},{"h":"Fruits and Stages of the Kingdom","items":[{"x":"The inner religion of the kingdom increasingly shows itself in practical social service; Jesus taught religion as the cause and ethics as the result.","r":["170:3.8"]},{"q":"A religião do Reino é pessoal, individual; os frutos, os resultados, são da família, são sociais.","r":"170:3.10"},{"x":"Jesus taught two phases of the kingdom: the kingdom in this world and the kingdom in heaven.","r":["170:2.18","170:2.19"]},{"x":"The kingdom has five phases: the inner experience of the individual, the brotherhood of believers, the superhuman brotherhood, a new social order, and the age of light and life.","r":["170:4.2","170:4.4","170:4.6"]},{"x":"The kingdom is not a social or economic order but a spiritual brotherhood of God-knowing individuals.","r":["99:3.2"]}]},{"h":"The Kingdom and the Church","items":[{"x":"For Jesus the kingdom was the sum of individuals who had confessed faith in the fatherhood of God and dedicated themselves to doing his will.","r":["170:5.11"]},{"x":"The rise of the church was itself natural, but the tragedy was that it almost wholly displaced Jesus' concept of the kingdom.","r":["170:5.7","170:5.10"]},{"x":"Church membership does not mean fellowship in the kingdom; the one is spiritual, the other chiefly social.","r":["170:5.18"]},{"x":"Some day a greater John the Baptist will appear, proclaiming a return to Jesus' concept of the kingdom as the Father's will ruling in the believer's heart.","r":["170:5.19"]},{"x":"The outward church is only the larval stage of the thwarted spiritual kingdom, and the teachings of Jesus will never remain fruitless.","r":["170:5.21"]},{"q":"Não duvideis, contudo: esse mesmo Reino do céu que o Mestre ensinou, como existindo dentro do coração do crente, ainda será proclamado a esta igreja cristã, e a todas as outras religiões, raças e nações na Terra — bem como a todos os indivíduos.","r":"170:5.8"}]}],"see":["Vontade de Deus","Filiação a Deus","Irmandade dos homens","Fé","Ensinamentos de Jesus","Religião institucional"]},{"n":56,"t":"Religião institucional","en":"Institutional Religion","sum":"Institutional religion is the church and religious organization formed as individual religious experiences gather socially. It is natural for religious groups to arise when people share their faith, and such groups have practical value in fostering worship, education, and fellowship. But the more religion is institutionalized, the weaker its power for good and the greater the dangers of dogmatism, sectarianism, and alliance with secular power. The Urantia Book regards the church's displacement of Jesus' spiritual kingdom as a tragedy.","sections":[{"h":"Why Religion Becomes Social","items":[{"x":"Religion is the personal experience of knowing God as Father, but it leads to recognizing men as brothers, and so it has a social side.","r":["99:5.1"]},{"x":"When people share their religious beliefs, some form of religious group with common goals inevitably arises.","r":["99:5.7"]},{"x":"The purpose of the religious group is to dramatize loyalty, enlarge the attractions of truth, beauty, and goodness, and foster fellowship, the home, religious education, and group worship.","r":["99:6.2"]},{"x":"Prayer sooner or later becomes a technique for institutionalizing every religion, giving rise to secondary agencies such as priests, scriptures, and rituals.","r":["91:5.6"]},{"q":"As metas, mais do que as crenças, é que devem unificar os religiosos.","r":"99:5.7"}]},{"h":"Dangers of Institutionalization","items":[{"q":"O sectarismo é uma doença da religião institucionalizada, enquanto o dogmatismo é uma escravização da natureza espiritual.","r":"99:6.1"},{"q":"De longe, é melhor ter uma religião sem uma igreja, do que uma igreja sem religião.","r":"99:6.1"},{"q":"No entanto, quando a religião torna-se institucionalizada, porém, o seu poder para o bem fica reduzido, ao passo que as possibilidades para o mal se tornam grandemente multiplicadas.","r":"99:6.3"},{"x":"The dangers of formalized religion include fixation of beliefs, fossilization of truth, diversion from the service of God to the service of the church, and oppressive authority.","r":["99:6.3"]},{"q":"A religião formal restringe os homens nas suas atividades espirituais pessoais, em vez de liberá-los para o serviço mais elevado de edificadores do Reino.","r":"99:6.4"}]},{"h":"Institutional Religion and Society","items":[{"x":"Institutionalized religion has become part of the social order that must be reconstructed, and so it cannot lead the coming social reconstruction.","r":["99:2.1","99:2.2"]},{"x":"Religionists should take part in social and political life as individuals, not as groups; a religious group acting politically becomes a party or an economic organization.","r":["99:2.3","99:3.15"]},{"x":"Early Christianity was free from all civil and economic entanglements, but later institutional Christianity became part of the structure of Western civilization.","r":["99:3.1"]},{"x":"To be free from secular alliances, religion needs a critical philosophy, political and economic independence, loving fellowship, and a scientific attitude.","r":["99:3.9","99:3.10","99:3.11","99:3.14"]},{"x":"Religious peace will not come until all religions renounce ecclesiastical authority and claims of spiritual sovereignty; God alone is spiritual sovereign.","r":["134:4.4"]},{"q":"Religionists, as a group, must never concern themselves with anything but religion","r":"99:3.15"}]},{"h":"The Religion of Authority","items":[{"x":"The religion of traditional authority offers an easy refuge to fearful souls, but at the price of spiritual and religious liberty.","r":["155:5.9","155:6.5"]},{"x":"The religions of authority divide people by demanding uniformity of belief, while the religion of the spirit requires only unity of experience.","r":["155:6.9"]},{"x":"True religion is not slavish belief in threats of punishment or in promises of mystical rewards.","r":["99:5.2"]},{"x":"Jesus did not ask people to recite formulated creeds; he asked them to gather and share a supper in remembrance of his life.","r":["99:5.10"]}]},{"h":"The Church and the Kingdom of Heaven","items":[{"x":"The rise of the church was itself natural and desirable; the trouble was that it almost wholly displaced Jesus' concept of the kingdom.","r":["170:5.7"]},{"x":"A formal, institutionalized church came to take the place of the kingdom brotherhood of spirit-led individuals.","r":["170:5.9"]},{"x":"Church membership does not mean kingdom fellowship; the one is spiritual, the other mainly social.","r":["170:5.18"]},{"x":"The present church is the larval stage of the thwarted spiritual kingdom, a cocoon carrying the kingdom through the material age.","r":["170:5.21"]},{"x":"A church that worships the living God, affirms the brotherhood of man, and removes the pressure of creeds holds great hope.","r":["103:5.12"]}]}],"see":["Religião pessoal","Reino do céu","Experiência religiosa","Irmandade dos homens","Governo e sociedade","Ensinamentos de Jesus"]},{"n":55,"t":"Religião pessoal","en":"Personal Religion","sum":"Personal religion is the \"religion of the spirit,\" in which each person discovers and experiences God within his own soul, unlike the \"religion of the mind,\" which leans on tradition and ecclesiastical authority. It cannot be received, borrowed, or learned from others; it grows with loyalty to supreme values. Jesus proclaimed this religion of living personal experience beyond the religion of authority, and its fruits appear in love and service.","sections":[{"h":"Religion of the Mind and Religion of the Spirit","items":[{"x":"There is the primitive religion of fear, the religion of civilization based on traditional authority, and the religion of revelation validated in human experience.","r":["155:5.3","155:5.4","155:5.5"]},{"q":"Jesus deixou claro que a grande diferença entre a religião da mente e a religião do espírito é que, enquanto a primeira é sustentada pela autoridade eclesiástica, a última é totalmente baseada na experiência humana.","r":"155:5.6"},{"x":"The religion of authority offers an easy refuge to fearful and uncertain souls, but it demands only passive, intellectual assent.","r":["155:5.9"]},{"q":"A religião do espírito significa esforço, luta, conflito, fé, determinação, amor, lealdade e progresso.","r":"155:5.11"},{"x":"The religion of the mind ties one to the past, but the religion of the spirit, through progressive revelation, ever beckons to higher attainment.","r":["155:6.4"]}]},{"h":"Discovering God for Oneself","items":[{"x":"The greatest discovery a human soul can make is to find God for itself within itself and to live that as personal experience.","r":["155:6.3"]},{"x":"It is good to revere the God-knowing leaders of the past, but not at the cost of sacrificing one's own experience of knowing God.","r":["155:6.7"]},{"x":"Do not seek the word of God only in ancient records; the one born of the spirit discerns the word of God wherever it comes from.","r":["155:6.12"]},{"x":"Once one begins to find God in one's soul, one soon finds him in the souls of others and in all creation.","r":["155:6.13"]},{"x":"The religion of the apostles was to be not a theological refuge from fear but a real experience testifying that God had found and exalted them.","r":["155:6.18"]}]},{"h":"A Religion That Cannot Be Given","items":[{"q":"A religião não pode ser outorgada, recebida, emprestada, aprendida, nem perdida.","r":"100:1.7"},{"x":"Every child should be given the opportunity to grow his own religious experience; an adult's finished experience should not be forced upon him.","r":["100:1.3"]},{"x":"Children are permanently impressed only by the loyalties of the adults with whom they live.","r":["100:1.4"]},{"q":"A maneira mais rápida de um girino tornar-se uma rã é vivendo lealmente cada momento como um girino.","r":"100:1.4"},{"x":"Some people are too busy to grow; the chief obstacles to growth are prejudice and ignorance.","r":["100:1.2"]}]},{"h":"Growth of Personal Religion","items":[{"x":"Spiritual development depends on maintaining a living connection with true spiritual forces and bearing fruit by passing on to fellows what has been received.","r":["100:2.1"]},{"x":"Spirituality measures both nearness to God and usefulness to fellows, and it grows as the selfish qualities of love are eliminated.","r":["100:2.4"]},{"x":"Habits such as sensitivity to divine values, reflective meditation, and worshipful problem solving favor religious growth.","r":["100:1.8"]},{"x":"Even when floods of adversity and hatred sweep over, the God-knowing person has a citadel of the spirit that is never assailed.","r":["100:2.7"]},{"q":"E imediatamente a espiritualidade passa a ser indicadora da vossa proximidade de Deus e uma medida da vossa capacidade de servir aos vossos semelhantes.","r":"100:2.4"}]},{"h":"Social Fruits of Personal Religion","items":[{"x":"The religions of authority divide people, but the religion of the spirit binds them together in unity of experience and destiny while allowing diversity of belief.","r":["155:6.9"]},{"x":"The unity and brotherhood of mankind can be achieved only through the religion of personal spiritual experience.","r":["155:6.8"]},{"x":"The evidence of knowing God is the fruit of the spirit borne in daily life and a life plan that stakes everything on the adventure of survival.","r":["155:6.14","155:6.15","155:6.16"]},{"x":"The religion of the kingdom is personal, but its fruits are familial and social; no one can keep it within himself alone.","r":["170:3.9","170:3.10"]},{"x":"The Father responds to the faintest flicker of faith, but those who are called must believe with body, mind, and spirit.","r":["155:6.17"]},{"q":"The religions of authority can only divide men and set them in conscientious array against each other","r":"155:6.9"}]}],"see":["Experiência religiosa","Religião institucional","Fé","Reino do céu","Ajustador do Pensamento","Crescimento"]},{"n":91,"t":"Ressurreição de Jesus","en":"Resurrection of Jesus","sum":"Before dawn on Sunday, April 9, A.D. 30, Jesus came forth from the tomb, not in the flesh but as a morontia personality, just as ascenders awaken in the resurrection halls of the mansion worlds. His physical body remained in the tomb and was later dissolved at the request of the archangels. During forty days the risen Jesus appeared nineteen times to believers while experiencing the morontia career of ascending mortals, and his resurrection revealed the gift of life that assures every believer of rising after death.","sections":[{"h":"The Resurrection Morning","items":[{"q":"at two minutes past three o’clock, this Sunday morning, April 9, A.D. 30, the resurrected morontia form and personality of Jesus of Nazareth came forth from the tomb.","r":"189:1.1"},{"x":"Even after he came forth, his body of flesh lay wrapped in linen, and the stones of the tomb and Pilate's seals remained undisturbed.","r":["189:1.2"]},{"x":"Seven Paradise personalities surrounded the tomb, but no creature of this local universe took part in his awakening.","r":["189:1.4","189:1.5"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus told the morontia groups that he would tarry for a time to know more fully the career of ascending creatures and to further reveal the Father's will.","r":["189:1.10"]},{"x":"That same morning the morontia Michael directed Gabriel to begin the planetary roll call of the resurrection.","r":["189:3.1"]},{"x":"The sleeping survivors of Urantia since the days of Adam awoke in the resurrection halls of Mansonia; this was the third dispensational resurrection.","r":["189:3.2","189:3.3"]}]},{"h":"In What Body He Arose","items":[{"q":"O seu corpo material ou físico não é uma parte da personalidade ressuscitada.","r":"189:1.7"},{"x":"He came forth from the tomb neither as a spirit nor in the form of Michael the Creator as he was before incarnation.","r":["189:1.8"]},{"x":"He came forth as a morontia personality, like the ascenders who awaken in the resurrection halls of the first mansion world.","r":["189:1.9"]},{"x":"So that the human form of the Creator would not be seen slowly decaying, the archangels took charge of his body and dissolved it by a process of accelerated time.","r":["189:2.1","189:2.3"]},{"x":"Secondary midwayers rolled away the stones of the tomb, and the guards who saw it fled in terror.","r":["189:2.4"]}]},{"h":"The Morontia Appearances","items":[{"x":"Jesus appeared to believers nineteen times before his ascension.","r":["190:2.1"]},{"q":"Ele não apareceu para os seus inimigos, nem para aqueles que não poderiam fazer um uso espiritual da sua manifestação na forma visível.","r":"190:2.1"},{"x":"At the empty tomb Mary Magdalene took Jesus for the gardener and asked where he had taken the Master.","r":["189:4.10"]},{"q":"“Não me toques, Maria, pois eu não sou mais como tu me conheceste na carne.","r":"189:4.12"},{"x":"Human eyes could see his morontia form because of the special ministry of the transformers and the midwayers.","r":["189:4.11"]},{"x":"Jesus appeared alone to Peter, who was weighed down by the guilt of denying the Master, and enabled his faith to overcome his doubts.","r":["191:1.1","191:1.2"]},{"q":"Abençoados sejam aqueles, nas idades que virão, que acreditarão mesmo não havendo visto com os olhos da carne e escutado com os ouvidos mortais”.","r":"191:5.5"}]},{"h":"Apostles Slow to Believe","items":[{"x":"The apostles had taken lightly Jesus' words about his death and resurrection and believed only when faced with undeniable experience.","r":["190:1.1"]},{"x":"When the women reported, only John among the apostles was inclined vaguely to believe in the resurrection; the others thought the Jews had moved the body.","r":["190:1.2","190:1.3"]},{"x":"Jesus told the apostles that as the Father had sent him so he sent them, to reveal divine love in their daily lives.","r":["191:5.3"]}]},{"h":"The Meaning of the Resurrection","items":[{"q":"All this power which is inherent in Jesus—the endowment of life—and which enabled him to rise from the dead, is the very gift of eternal life which he bestows upon kingdom believers","r":"190:0.2"},{"x":"Mortals too will rise on the resurrection morning in morontia bodies like the one Jesus wore, bodies without circulating blood yet real.","r":["190:0.3"]},{"x":"Man is slow to realize that matter is the skeleton of morontia and that both are the reflected shadow of enduring spirit reality.","r":["189:1.3"]},{"x":"The greatest news the disciples proclaimed at Pentecost was the risen Lord, and this led Christianity to grow up around fellowship with the risen Christ.","r":["194:0.3","194:0.4"]}]},{"h":"The Ascension","items":[{"x":"The so-called ascension, when Jesus vanished on Olivet, was no different from his other disappearances from view during the forty days.","r":["193:5.3"]},{"x":"Passing through Jerusem and Edentia, he was released from the morontia state and returned to Paradise sonship and supreme sovereignty on Salvington.","r":["193:5.4"]},{"x":"It was about a quarter to eight that morning when Jesus vanished from the sight of the eleven and began his ascent to the Father to receive confirmation of his completed sovereignty over Nebadon.","r":["193:5.5"]}]}],"see":["Morte na cruz","Morôncia","Pentecostes","Sobrevivência","Mundos das mansões","Os doze apóstolos"]},{"n":75,"t":"Revelação","en":"Revelation","sum":"Revelation is the direct presentation by the real spiritual world of the truth that evolutionary religion seeks by circuitous ways, and it sorts and elevates evolutionary religion. Truth is autorevelation when it comes through the Adjuster and epochal revelation when it comes through celestial beings. Urantia has had five epochal revelations; revelation keeps in touch with evolution so as not to be too far removed from the thought of its age, and it coordinates science, religion, and philosophy as one truth.","sections":[{"h":"Evolutionary and Revealed Religion","items":[{"q":"A revelação é evolucionária, mas é sempre progressiva.","r":"92:4.1"},{"q":"A religião evolucionária é o retrato do caminhar em círculos viciosos que a humanidade faz para a busca da verdade; a religião reveladora é essa verdade em si mesma.","r":"92:4.3"},{"x":"Revealed religion is always characterized by belief in a Deity of final values and a concept of the survival of personality after death.","r":["92:4.2"]},{"x":"To elevate evolutionary religion, revelation must present teachings not too far removed from the thought of its age.","r":["92:4.1"]},{"x":"The morality of evolutionary religion drives by fear, but revealed religion leads people to seek a God of love through the longing to be like him.","r":["5:4.1"]}]},{"h":"The Five Epochal Revelations","items":[{"x":"There have been only five revelations of epochal significance; the first was the Dalamatia teachings of the one hundred of Caligastia's staff.","r":["92:4.4","92:4.5"]},{"x":"The second was the Edenic teachings of Adam and Eve; though interrupted by the default of the Garden, the Sethite priests carried on part of them.","r":["92:4.6"]},{"x":"The third was the revelation of Machiventa Melchizedek of Salem, who taught trust and faith.","r":["92:4.7"]},{"x":"The fourth was Jesus of Nazareth, who revealed God as the Universal Father and taught love and service.","r":["92:4.8"]},{"x":"The fifth is the Urantia Papers, presented jointly by many beings.","r":["92:4.9"]},{"q":"Nenhuma revelação, todavia, pode jamais ser completa, antes de se alcançar o Pai Universal.","r":"92:4.9"}]},{"h":"Truth Is Always a Revelation","items":[{"q":"A verdade é sempre uma revelação: é uma auto-revelação, quando surge como resultado do trabalho do Ajustador residente; é uma revelação para uma época, ou epocal, quando apresentada pelo trabalho de alguma outra agência celeste: um grupo ou personalidade.","r":"101:4.3"},{"q":"A investigação do conhecimento constitui a ciência; a busca da sabedoria é filosofia; o amor por Deus é religião; a sede da verdade é uma revelação.","r":"102:3.12"},{"x":"That the First Cause of science is a Father full of mercy can be known only through revelation.","r":["4:4.7","101:2.3"]},{"x":"Revelation does not originate science or religion; its function is to coordinate both with the truth of reality.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"x":"Revelation is validated only by human experience, and it confirms the harmony of the approaches of science, religion, and philosophy.","r":["101:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Methods and Limits of Revelation","items":[{"x":"The revelators give preference to the highest existing human concepts and resort to pure revelation only when there is no adequate expression.","r":["0:12.11"]},{"x":"These papers are based on more than a thousand human concepts gathered from God-knowing mortals.","r":["0:12.12"]},{"x":"The laws of revelation forbid imparting unearned or premature knowledge, so the cosmology contained in revelation soon becomes outdated.","r":["101:4.1","101:4.2"]},{"x":"Revelation is a spiritual phenomenon, but its statements on cosmology are not inspired; their value lies in reducing error and restoring lost knowledge.","r":["101:4.5","101:4.6","101:4.8"]},{"x":"Because of the isolation of rebellion, the revelation of truth was mixed with transient cosmologies, but eternal truth should not be slighted for that reason.","r":["102:1.3"]}]},{"h":"What Revelation Does","items":[{"x":"Revelation compensates for the absence of the morontia viewpoint, providing a technique of unity for understanding the relationships of matter and spirit.","r":["101:2.2"]},{"q":"E a verdadeira revelação jamais afasta a ciência da natureza, nem a religião da razão ou a filosofia da lógica.","r":"101:2.2"},{"x":"Revelation compensates for the weaknesses of evolving philosophy and accomplishes what metaphysics could not.","r":["103:8.6","101:2.7"]},{"x":"Revelation liberates man for the eternal adventure and gives assurance of the survival of personality.","r":["102:3.6","102:3.9"]},{"x":"Revelation glorifies man and discloses his capacity to be a partner with God.","r":["102:3.7"]}]}],"see":["Verdade","Ciência e religião","Filosofia","Maquiventa Melquisedeque","Adão e Eva","Auto-outorga de Jesus"]},{"n":64,"t":"Sabedoria","en":"Wisdom","sum":"Wisdom goes beyond knowledge to embrace facts and ideals, the relationships and meanings of things. God's wisdom exists perfectly in his infinite insight, but human wisdom evolves through experience, through trial and error, and especially through adjustment to failure. The adjutant spirit of wisdom lays its foundation, the Adjuster and the Spirit of Truth lead it toward truth, and in time thinking leads to wisdom and wisdom to worship.","sections":[{"h":"Divine Wisdom and Experiential Wisdom","items":[{"q":"Man's wisdom grows out of the trials and errors of human experience; God's wisdom consists in the unqualified perfection of his infinite universe insight","r":"4:3.4"},{"x":"Because of the discrimination of infinite wisdom, God can be both just and merciful at the same time in any situation.","r":["2:4.3","2:3.2"]},{"x":"Wisdom has a dual origin: the divine insight of perfect beings and the personal experience of evolutionary creatures.","r":["19:2.4"]},{"x":"Superuniverse administration always associates the Perfectors of Wisdom, with their divine insight, and ascendant personalities seasoned by experience.","r":["19:2.4"]},{"x":"Infinite wisdom ordains that anything be done in the best way, the right way, in the circumstances.","r":["12:7.2"]}]},{"h":"The Foundation of Wisdom in Mind","items":[{"x":"The spirit of wisdom is the highest of the adjutant mind-spirits, coordinating the work of all the others.","r":["36:5.12"]},{"q":"A sabedoria é o apogeu da atuação intelectual. A sabedoria é a meta de uma existência puramente mental e moral.","r":"36:5.12"},{"x":"Animals may possess knowledge, but only man has the potential of wisdom that weaves ideas from memory.","r":["101:6.4"]},{"x":"Wisdom is consciousness in which knowledge is elevated to new levels of meaning and activated by the adjutant of wisdom.","r":["180:5.3"]},{"q":"Conquanto o discernimento divino ou espiritual seja uma dádiva, a sabedoria humana deve evoluir.","r":"101:4.2"}]},{"h":"Wisdom Distinct from Knowledge and Truth","items":[{"q":"O conhecimento lida com os fatos; a sabedoria, com as relações; a verdade, com os valores da realidade.","r":"132:3.2"},{"x":"Science leads to fact-consciousness, religion to value-consciousness, and philosophy, or wisdom, to the co-ordinating consciousness that embraces both.","r":["102:3.5"]},{"x":"Science classifies men and religion loves men, but wisdom does justice to differing men.","r":["102:3.7"]},{"x":"When the viewpoints of material fact and spiritual value are harmonized, wisdom interprets universe phenomena through progressive personality experience.","r":["130:4.10"]},{"x":"Knowledge is gained by education, but the wisdom true culture requires comes only through experience; intelligence controls civilization, and wisdom directs it.","r":["81:6.13","81:6.27"]}]},{"h":"The Way to Wisdom","items":[{"q":"O êxito pode gerar coragem e proporcionar autoconfiança, mas a sabedoria advém somente das experiências de ajustamento aos resultados dos fracassos.","r":"160:4.14"},{"x":"Neither the idealist who ignores facts nor the materialist without spiritual outlook is wise, but only the one who adjusts facts to ideals.","r":["160:4.14"]},{"x":"Knowledge, culture, and wisdom are different, and wisdom always dominates knowledge and glorifies culture.","r":["160:4.16"]},{"x":"Wisdom is superknowledge; when people pool their minds, they can share each other's insight and avoid prejudice and narrowness.","r":["160:2.7"]},{"x":"Jesus told James that true wisdom embraces discretion as well as courage.","r":["181:2.15"]}]},{"h":"From Wisdom to Faith and Worship","items":[{"x":"Reason, wisdom, and faith are man's three highest attainments, and in the higher philosophy wisdom becomes allied to faith.","r":["103:9.6","103:9.10"]},{"x":"True wisdom counsels allowing faith to accomplish what knowledge and reason cannot.","r":["102:1.2"]},{"x":"The superphilosophic wisdom of the enlightened recognizes that to doubt God is to be untrue to the indwelling Adjuster.","r":["101:1.7"]},{"q":"No tempo, o pensar conduz à sabedoria, e a sabedoria leva à adoração; na eternidade, a adoração conduz à sabedoria, e a sabedoria manifesta-se gerando a finalidade de pensamento.","r":"112:2.13"}]}],"see":["Filosofia","Verdade","Espíritos ajudantes da mente","Mente","Ciência e religião","Experiência"]},{"n":8,"t":"Ser Supremo","en":"Supreme Being","sum":"O Ser Supremo é a Deidade experiencial que evolui no tempo e no espaço. Ele deriva a Sua personalidade espiritual da Trindade do Paraíso e o Seu poder todo-poderoso dos três primeiros níveis de Deus, o Sétuplo, e esses dois aspectos estão sendo unificados na Mente Suprema. Como supra-alma do grande universo e soma da realidade finita, Ele registra a experiência de toda criatura e de todo criador, e torna-Se um passo mais factual sempre que o homem faz a vontade de Deus.","sections":[{"h":"Deidade experiencial em evolução","items":[{"x":"O Pai, o Filho e o Espírito são Deidades existenciais, ao passo que Deus, o Supremo, Deus, o Último, e Deus, o Absoluto, são Deidades experienciais que se factualizam na evolução pós-Havona dos universos.","r":["0:7.1","0:7.5"]},{"q":"WITH God the Father, sonship is the great relationship. With God the Supreme, achievement is the prerequisite to status","r":"115:0.1"},{"x":"Havona não cresce, simplesmente é, ao passo que o crescimento é a marca do grande universo e o sinal da Deidade experiencial.","r":["116:0.3"]},{"x":"O Ser Supremo atua como uma personalidade espiritual no universo central e como Deus, o Todo-Poderoso, uma personalidade de poder, no grande universo.","r":["116:0.5"]},{"x":"O destino do Supremo é a perfeição, mas a Sua experiência atual contém elementos de crescimento e de incompletude.","r":["116:0.4"]}]},{"h":"Origens: a Trindade e Deus, o Sétuplo","items":[{"x":"A personalidade espiritual do Supremo provém da Trindade do Paraíso, e o Seu crescimento deriva das duas triunidades da factualidade e da potencialidade.","r":["115:4.2","115:4.7"]},{"x":"O poder do Todo-Poderoso assenta nos êxitos de divindade de Deus, o Sétuplo, e o Agente Conjunto outorga a mente da Supremacia, que une o poder e a personalidade espiritual.","r":["115:4.7"]},{"x":"O Ser Supremo depende absolutamente da Trindade do Paraíso para a realidade da Sua natureza pessoal e espiritual.","r":["115:5.1"]},{"x":"Deus, o Supremo, não é apenas evoluído pelos criadores e derivado da Trindade; Ele é também um ser volitivo que participa Ele próprio da Sua própria factualização.","r":["117:3.7"]},{"q":"O que a Trindade é para Deus, o Supremo, o Ajustador é para o homem em evolução.","r":"117:3.10"}]},{"h":"Supra-alma do grande universo","items":[{"q":"O Supremo é a beleza da harmonia física, a verdade do significado intelectual e a bondade do valor espiritual.","r":"117:1.1"},{"x":"No Ser Supremo, o Criador e a criatura estão unificados em uma só Deidade, cuja vontade é algo maior do que a vontade do criador ou a da criatura.","r":["117:1.5"]},{"x":"Ele é a síntese finita da experiência dos criadores que descem para revelar Deus e das criaturas que ascendem em busca de Deus.","r":["117:1.2"]},{"x":"A personalidade de quem não sobrevive é absorvida na supra-alma da criação e retorna ao Supremo como uma gota de água retorna ao mar.","r":["117:4.2","117:4.4"]},{"x":"O homem não perde a sua identidade pessoal na unificação com o Supremo, e os ecos de todas as suas experiências tornam-se parte da experiência do Supremo.","r":["117:5.5"]},{"x":"O grande universo é um organismo vivo magnificamente sensível, permeado por circuitos de inteligência e canais de energia.","r":["116:7.1"]}]},{"h":"A interdependência entre o homem e o Supremo","items":[{"x":"Na medida em que fazemos a vontade de Deus em qualquer lugar, o potencial todo-poderoso do Supremo torna-se um passo mais factual.","r":["117:0.1"]},{"x":"A criatura não pode evoluir sem o Supremo, nem a evolução do Supremo pode completar-se sem a plena evolução de todas as criaturas.","r":["117:4.9"]},{"x":"Essa relação entre o homem e o Supremo é o fundamento da moralidade cósmica, que reconhece a obrigação experiencial para com a Deidade experiencial.","r":["117:4.8"]},{"q":"De tão confiante e tão cheio de amor, Deus coloca uma parte da Sua natureza divina nas próprias mãos dos seres humanos, para a salvaguarda e para a auto-realização dos mesmos.","r":"117:4.3"},{"x":"Enquanto buscamos o Pai, o Supremo também busca, em nós e conosco, o Criador do Paraíso de todas as coisas.","r":["117:4.6"]}]},{"h":"O caminho para encontrar o Supremo","items":[{"x":"Assim como Deus é o Pai divino, o Supremo é a Mãe divina, em quem somos nutridos ao longo das nossas carreiras no universo.","r":["117:6.2"]},{"q":"Man can discover the Father in his heart, but he will have to search for the Supreme in the hearts of all other men","r":"117:6.23"},{"x":"O Pai pode ser encontrado por cada indivíduo, mas o Supremo não será encontrado individualmente senão em um futuro distante, quando todas as criaturas juntas alcançarem a maturidade cósmica e O encontrarem.","r":["117:6.16","117:6.21"]},{"x":"O amor do Pai só se torna real quando é outorgado aos semelhantes, e a afeição fraterna que flui dessa maneira é a essência do amor do Supremo.","r":["117:6.10"]},{"x":"O homem não descobre o Supremo de repente, como um terremoto que atinge, mas lenta e pacientemente, como um rio que desgasta o solo.","r":["117:6.25"]},{"q":"Compreender além do Supremo é ser mais do que finito!","r":"117:6.19"},{"x":"O mortal que conhece Deus nunca está só; o Pai o acompanha durante todo o caminho, e o próprio caminho que ele percorre é a presença do Supremo.","r":["117:6.27"]}]},{"h":"O futuro do Supremo","items":[{"x":"Quando o grande universo estiver estabelecido em luz e vida, a personalidade espiritual e o poder todo-poderoso serão unificados na Mente Suprema, e o Ser Supremo será factualizado como uma factualidade completa.","r":["117:0.2","117:7.14"]},{"x":"Acredita-se que o Supremo se tornará então o soberano factual do grande universo e que as distinções entre os sete superuniversos desaparecerão gradualmente.","r":["117:7.15"]},{"x":"Os cidadãos do universo aperfeiçoado enfrentarão então um novo desafio: a busca de Deus, o Último.","r":["117:7.17"]}]}],"see":["Deus, o Sétuplo","Trindade do Paraíso","Deus, o Último","Vontade de Deus","Luz e vida","Evolução"]},{"n":27,"t":"Serafins","en":"Seraphim","sum":"The seraphim are angels created by the local universe Mother Spirit, and with the cherubim and sanobim they form the corps of ministering spirits of the local universe. Though without material bodies, they are spirit beings with individual personalities who understand and love human beings. Divided into seven orders, from supreme seraphim to future seraphim, they assist in almost every task of the local universe: administration, education, transport, records, and planetary supervision. They themselves are ascending beings, destined to reach Paradise by way of Seraphington.","sections":[{"h":"Origin and Nature","items":[{"x":"Seraphim are created by projection of the Universe Mother Spirit, 41,472 at a time, and since Nebadon is still in the making, they continue to be created periodically.","r":["38:1.1","38:1.3"]},{"x":"As the supernaphim serve the central universe and the seconaphim the superuniverses, so in the local universe the seraphim, together with the cherubim and sanobim, make up the angelic hosts.","r":["38:0.2"]},{"q":"Os anjos não têm corpos materiais, mas são seres definidos, contínuos e discretos; são de natureza e origem espirituais.","r":"38:2.1"},{"x":"They are fully aware of human moral struggles and spiritual difficulties, enjoy music, art, and real humor, and love human beings.","r":["38:2.1"]},{"x":"Though not sex creatures, they are deeply affectionate; they live in pairs of negative and positive beings and carry out most of their assignments two by two.","r":["38:2.2","38:4.3"]},{"q":"Os anjos não fazem o julgamento da humanidade, assim como os indivíduos mortais não deveriam prejulgar os seus semelhantes.","r":"38:2.4"},{"x":"It is well to love the angels, but they are not to be worshiped; they are fellow servants with man in the worship of God.","r":["38:2.5"]}]},{"h":"Training and Organization","items":[{"x":"They spend their first millennium as observers in the schools of Salvington and the second on the seraphic worlds, then pass through the constellation and system before being commissioned as ministering spirits of time.","r":["38:5.1","38:5.3"]},{"q":"Their work in the universe is without bounds and limitations","r":"38:5.4"},{"x":"From groups of twelve pairs they are organized into companies, battalions, units, legions, hosts, and angelic armies, each twelve times larger, and the armies are commanded by Brilliant Evening Stars and others.","r":["38:6.1","38:6.2"]},{"x":"The \"more than twelve legions of angels\" that Jesus spoke of in Gethsemane refers to these very legion units of seraphim.","r":["38:6.1"]},{"x":"Since Michael's bestowal on Urantia, the seraphim and all local universe orders have come under the sovereignty of the Master Son.","r":["38:6.3"]},{"x":"The cherubim and sanobim, of the same origin as the seraphim, are the lowest order of angels; working in pairs, they are the faithful aids of the seraphim.","r":["38:7.1","38:7.3"]}]},{"h":"The Seven Orders and Their Work","items":[{"x":"The revealed seraphim are divided into seven orders: supreme, superior, supervisor, administrator, planetary helpers, transition ministers, and seraphim of the future.","r":["39:0.1","39:0.2","39:0.8"]},{"q":"A misericórdia é a tônica do serviço seráfico e da ministração angélica.","r":"39:2.5"},{"x":"Transport seraphim enseraphim ascenders and carry them from world to world; the one so enfolded sleeps for a set time and awakens at the destination.","r":["39:2.10","39:2.12"]},{"x":"The social architects among the supervisor seraphim foster genuine social contacts and help bring about efficient and harmonious working groups.","r":["39:3.4","39:3.5"]},{"x":"The moral advisers among the administrator seraphim teach the interplay of liberty and loyalty and portray mortal life as the first link in a long and unbroken chain.","r":["39:4.10","39:4.13"]},{"q":"The keys of the kingdom of heaven are: sincerity, more sincerity, and more sincerity.","r":"39:4.14"},{"x":"The transition ministers foster the morontia progress of survivors on the mansion worlds and are among the seraphim who come closest to human beings.","r":["48:6.1","48:6.34"]}]},{"h":"Angelic Ministry on the Planet","items":[{"x":"Even after the failure of the Adamic regime, the spirits of brotherhood, the souls of peace, and the spirits of trust among the planetary helpers continue their work on Urantia.","r":["39:5.4","39:5.5","39:5.8"]},{"x":"The idea that angels have wings derives largely from traditions of ancient observations of seraphim preparing for transport.","r":["39:5.12"]},{"x":"With the outpouring of the Spirit of Truth came the twelve legions of master seraphim of planetary supervision, caring for epochs, progress, religion, nations, races, education, health, the home, industry, diversion, and more.","r":["114:6.1","114:6.4"]},{"x":"While the angels of progress promote new advances, the religious guardians carry the immortal values within older forms to the next generation, and so the two balance each other.","r":["114:6.6","114:6.7"]},{"q":"Nenhum desses grupos angélicos exerce o controle direto ou arbitrário sobre o domínio dos seus compromissos.","r":"114:6.18"}]},{"h":"The Destiny of the Seraphim","items":[{"x":"Seraphim may reach Paradise by several paths, among them the perfect attainment of specialized service, summons to Seraphington, and the guardianship of evolutionary mortals.","r":["39:8.2","39:8.3","39:8.4"]},{"x":"Angels are not certain of their eternal future until they reach Seraphington, and no angel who has attained Seraphington is known ever to have gone astray.","r":["39:8.9"]},{"x":"Cherubim and sanobim, too, may be reborn as full seraphim after long service and repeated embraces of the Universe Mother Spirit.","r":["38:8.6"]},{"x":"Many paths open to completion seraphim, but they most desire to serve as bestowal attendants of incarnated Paradise Sons.","r":["39:9.3"]},{"q":"Em toda a ascensão moroncial, e na subseqüente ascensão espiritual, a vossa fraternidade com os serafins será ideal; o vosso companheirismo será esplêndido.","r":"38:2.6"}]}],"see":["Hostes angélicas","Guardiães seráficos","Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Criaturas intermediárias","Mundos das mansões","Morôncia"]},{"n":63,"t":"Serviço","en":"Service","sum":"Service is one way in which divinity is revealed on the personal level: the Son serves mankind, and the Infinite Spirit and his children possess by nature the urge to minister. For man, service is the social fruit of true religion, the inner experience of loving God flowing out as loving service to one's fellows. Jesus showed by washing feet that the one who serves is great, and the path of ascension leads on into endless universe service.","sections":[{"h":"The Source of Divine Service","items":[{"x":"On personality levels creatures can comprehend divinity as love, mercy, and ministry.","r":["0:1.17"]},{"q":"Deus, o Pai, ama os homens; Deus, o Filho, serve aos homens;","r":"3:6.8"},{"x":"Ministry to mind is the essence of the Infinite Spirit, and all his spirit offspring share the divine urge to serve.","r":["8:4.1","8:4.2"]},{"x":"The family of the Infinite Spirit is forever devoted to ministering the love of God and the mercy of the Son, becoming a living ladder by which mortals ascend.","r":["9:8.25"]},{"x":"The attributes of mercy and service displayed by the descending Sons derive from the Eternal Son.","r":["7:6.2"]}]},{"h":"The Fruit of True Religion","items":[{"q":"A religião não é a técnica para alcançar uma paz mental estática e abençoada; é um impulso para organizar a alma para o serviço dinâmico.","r":"100:3.1"},{"x":"One who has found God seeks out and serves less enlightened fellows, not to boast but out of overflowing goodness.","r":["102:3.4"]},{"q":"O sinal intelectual de identificação da religiosidade é a certeza; a característica filosófica é a coerência; os frutos sociais são o amor e o serviço.","r":"102:7.5"},{"x":"Jesus taught religion as the cause and ethics and service as the effect; inner religion shows itself in practical social service.","r":["170:3.8","170:3.9"]},{"x":"Religion becoming a personal experience is not dangerous so long as it does not lose the motive of unselfish social service.","r":["99:4.7"]},{"x":"Contact with the Adjuster is fostered by meditation, but it occurs more often in loving service to one's fellows.","r":["91:7.1"]}]},{"h":"The Way of Service Jesus Showed","items":[{"x":"At the Last Supper, before apostles quarreling over places, Jesus knelt like a servant and washed the feet of all twelve, even Judas.","r":["179:3.1","179:3.7"]},{"q":"He who would be great among you, let him become as the younger; while he who would be chief, let him become as one who serves.","r":"179:3.9"},{"x":"The lesson of the foot washing was that the secret of greatness in the spiritual kingdom differs from the methods of power in the material world.","r":["179:3.8"]},{"q":"O meu Reino funda-se no amor, é proclamado na misericórdia e é estabelecido por meio do serviço não-egoísta.","r":"155:1.2"},{"x":"Jesus asked not for sacrifice but for loyalty; service rendered by a friend for a friend cannot be called sacrifice.","r":["180:1.6"]},{"x":"Even a small loving service, like a cup of cold water given to a thirsty soul, is always recorded by the Father's messengers.","r":["159:2.1"]}]},{"h":"Service in Society and Civilization","items":[{"q":"Na economia, a motivação do lucro está para a motivação do serviço, como o medo está para o amor, na religião.","r":"71:6.2"},{"x":"The profit motive should not be abolished suddenly but gradually transformed into unselfish motives.","r":["71:6.2"]},{"x":"Apart from parental instinct, altruism does not arise spontaneously, so an unselfish social order requires the impulses of reason, morality, and religion.","r":["16:9.7"]},{"x":"True parents engage in continuous service-ministry that their children, as they grow, will come to recognize and appreciate.","r":["84:7.26"]},{"x":"The social service and intellectual fellowship of believers are precious, but as by-products of inner transformation they cannot replace the proclamation of the gospel.","r":["178:1.11"]}]},{"h":"Service That Continues into Eternity","items":[{"x":"On the fourth mansion world ascenders first experience a social order based on the love of mutual service rather than selfish conquest.","r":["47:6.3"]},{"x":"What the Father and the Sons bestow on us we bestow in turn on our fellows and the Supreme; the experience of love, joy, and service is mutual.","r":["56:8.3"]},{"x":"Entry into the Mortal Corps of the Finality is the beginning of eternal service to the Paradise Trinity.","r":["27:7.8","27:7.10"]},{"x":"In the present universe age the finaliters return to the universes of time and serve in one superuniverse after another.","r":["31:0.10"]}]}],"see":["Amor","Irmandade dos homens","Experiência religiosa","Corpo de Finalidade","Ensinamentos de Jesus","Espírito Infinito"]},{"n":20,"t":"Sete Espíritos Mestres","en":"Seven Master Spirits","sum":"Os Sete Espíritos Mestres são as personalidades primárias do Espírito Infinito, e cada um expressa uma das sete associações possíveis das três Deidades: o Pai, o Filho e o Espírito. A partir da periferia do Paraíso, cada um supervisiona um dos sete superuniversos, e eles são a fonte sétupla da mente cósmica e os ancestrais dos diretores de potência. As criaturas de cada superuniverso trazem para sempre o caráter distintivo do seu Espírito Mestre, e o Espírito Mestre Número Sete, que supervisiona Orvônton, representa o Ser Supremo.","sections":[{"h":"Sete associações possíveis","items":[{"x":"Os Sete Espíritos Mestres são as personalidades primárias do Espírito Infinito, e, como há apenas sete associações possíveis inerentes às três Deidades, o universo é administrado em sete grandes divisões.","r":["16:0.1"]},{"x":"Cada um deriva o seu caráter de uma de sete semelhanças: o Pai, o Filho, o Espírito, o Pai e o Filho, o Pai e o Espírito, o Filho e o Espírito, e o Pai, o Filho e o Espírito.","r":["16:0.2","16:0.9"]},{"q":"Já chegamos a referir-nos à personalização tríplice da Deidade como sendo a inevitabilidade absoluta e, ao mesmo tempo, encaramos o surgimento dos Sete Espíritos Mestres como sendo a inevitabilidade subabsoluta.","r":"16:1.1"},{"x":"Personalizados pelo primeiro ato criador de Deidade do Espírito Infinito, eles são os distribuidores do Espírito Infinito aos universos.","r":["9:8.2"]},{"x":"Em caráter e natureza espirituais, os Sete Espíritos são como um só, mas em todos os outros aspectos da identidade são claramente diferentes.","r":["16:0.11"]},{"q":"Os Espíritos Mestres têm muitas funções; no momento presente, contudo, o seu âmbito específico é a supervisão central dos sete superuniversos.","r":"16:0.12"}]},{"h":"A voz do Espírito Infinito","items":[{"q":"Fora do Paraíso e de Havona, o Espírito Infinito fala apenas pelas vozes dos Sete Espíritos Mestres.","r":"16:2.2"},{"x":"A presença do Espírito Infinito no superuniverso, em qualquer mundo, é condicionada pela natureza distintiva do Espírito Mestre que supervisiona aquele segmento.","r":["16:2.3"]},{"x":"Os atributos de onipotência, onisciência e onipresença só aparecem quando eles atuam juntos; individualmente, cada um está limitado ao superuniverso sob a sua supervisão.","r":["16:2.4"]},{"x":"Quando os Sete Espíritos Mestres se reúnem em torno do Agente Conjunto, representam coletivamente o poder, a sabedoria e a autoridade funcionais da Trindade nos universos evolucionários.","r":["16:1.3"]},{"x":"Eles são o terceiro nível de Deus, o Sétuplo; os ascendentes, passando pelos Anciães dos Dias, descobrem a personalidade de um Espírito Mestre antes de prosseguir até o Pai.","r":["0:8.4","0:8.9"]}]},{"h":"O caráter distintivo dos Sete","items":[{"x":"O Espírito Mestre Número Um expressa diretamente o Pai, está estreitamente associado ao chefe dos Ajustadores e, no conselho, fala sempre pelo Pai.","r":["16:3.2"]},{"x":"O Número Dois retrata o Filho Eterno, o Número Três o Espírito Infinito e o Número Quatro a natureza combinada do Pai e do Filho.","r":["16:3.4","16:3.6","16:3.8"]},{"x":"O Número Cinco retrata o Pai e o Espírito e é o conselheiro dos diretores de potência e dos controladores físicos, ao passo que o Número Seis retrata o Filho e o Espírito.","r":["16:3.10","16:3.12"]},{"x":"O Espírito Mestre Número Sete, que preside Orvônton, retrata igualmente o Pai, o Filho e o Espírito e tem uma relação pessoal e orgânica com a pessoa espiritual do Ser Supremo.","r":["16:3.14","16:3.15"]},{"q":"Durante a presente idade do universo, de não-contatabilidade da pessoa do Supremo, o Espírito Mestre Número Sete funciona no lugar do Deus das criaturas ascendentes, para as questões de relacionamentos pessoais.","r":"16:3.19"}]},{"h":"A supervisão do superuniverso e a mente cósmica","items":[{"x":"Cada Espírito Mestre tem a sua sede na periferia do Paraíso, defronte ao superuniverso que supervisiona, e ali convergem as linhas radiais das fronteiras desse superuniverso.","r":["16:0.12"]},{"x":"Os Espíritos Mestres entram em contato com os governos dos superuniversos por meio dos Sete Executivos Supremos e mantêm comunicação constante com os Espíritos Refletivos de cada capital de superuniverso.","r":["17:1.2","16:3.20"]},{"q":"É literalmente verdade que esses Sete Espíritos sejam o poder físico personalizado, a mente cósmica e a presença espiritual da Deidade trina, “os Sete Espíritos de Deus enviados a todo o universo”.","r":"16:4.1"},{"x":"Eles são a fonte sétupla da mente cósmica e os ancestrais dos diretores de potência do universo, e também ajudam materialmente os Filhos Criadores que organizam os universos locais.","r":["16:4.2","16:4.3","16:6.1"]},{"x":"A substância moroncial e a mente moroncial, que combinam matéria e espírito, parecem estar relacionadas a atividades não reveladas dos Espíritos Mestres.","r":["16:4.5"]},{"x":"No entanto, eles nada têm a ver com a outorga e a ministração dos Ajustadores nem com a função do Absoluto Inqualificável.","r":["16:4.16"]},{"x":"Na presente idade, o potencial da mente do Supremo está confiado aos Sete Espíritos Mestres, e o Sétimo Espírito Mestre, em particular, conhece o Supremo e está em contato pessoal com Ele.","r":["116:1.3","116:4.2"]}]},{"h":"Um caráter impresso nas criaturas","items":[{"x":"Cada mundo desfruta da sabedoria combinada de todos os sete Espíritos Mestres, mas recebe o seu toque e o seu colorido pessoais de apenas um.","r":["16:5.1"]},{"x":"Um Espírito Mestre não entra diretamente na mente material dos mortais; a sua influência chega por meio da ministração do Espírito Criativo do universo local, que se assemelha muito a ele.","r":["16:5.3"]},{"q":"Por toda a eternidade, um mortal ascendente trará as características indicativas do Espírito que preside ao seu superuniverso de nascimento.","r":"16:5.5"},{"x":"Por isso, mesmo o Corpo de Finalidade, quando retrata uma relação completa com a criação evolucionária, reúne um grupo de sete finalitores, um de cada superuniverso.","r":["16:5.5"]},{"x":"No sétimo circuito de Havona, o ascendente deve apreender a identidade do Espírito Mestre do seu superuniverso antes de avançar para o sexto circuito.","r":["14:5.4"]},{"x":"Há sete grandes avenidas que levam ao Pai Universal, e cada ascensão se realiza por meio da divindade de um dos Sete Espíritos Mestres.","r":["117:6.15"]}]}],"see":["Espírito Infinito","Mente cósmica","Os sete superuniversos","Deus, o Sétuplo","Ser Supremo","Anciães dos Dias"]},{"n":14,"t":"Os sete superuniversos","en":"The Seven Superuniverses","sum":"Os sete superuniversos são as criações que evoluem no tempo e no espaço, formadas pela divisão em sete segmentos do primeiro nível espacial além de Havona. Cada superuniverso contém cerca de um trilhão de mundos habitáveis, é governado por três Anciães dos Dias a partir de um mundo-sede arquitetônico e é supervisionado do Paraíso por um dos Sete Espíritos Mestres. Orvônton, o sétimo superuniverso, ao qual pertence Urântia, é conhecido como uma demonstração universal de amor e misericórdia.","sections":[{"h":"A roda gigantesca","items":[{"x":"No que diz respeito à Trindade do Paraíso, há apenas sete universos habitados fora de Havona, e eles têm jurisdição sobre o primeiro nível espacial além de Havona.","r":["15:0.1"]},{"q":"the hub being the eternal Isle of Paradise, the seven spokes the radiations of the Seven Master Spirits, the rim the outer regions of the grand universe.","r":"15:0.1"},{"x":"O plano sétuplo de organização dos superuniversos foi estabelecido no início da materialização da criação universal, e o sistema administrativo atual existe quase desde a eternidade.","r":["15:0.2"]},{"x":"Os sete superuniversos giram em sentido anti-horário em torno do Paraíso e de Havona, ao longo de uma enorme trajetória elíptica.","r":["15:1.2","15:3.14"]},{"x":"Urântia não está mergulhando às cegas em um espaço desconhecido, mas segue a trajetória ordenada e predeterminada do nível espacial dos superuniversos.","r":["15:1.3"]}]},{"h":"Unidades de organização","items":[{"q":"Only the Universal Father knows the location and actual number of inhabited worlds in space","r":"15:2.1"},{"x":"Cerca de mil mundos habitáveis formam um sistema, cem sistemas uma constelação e cem constelações um universo local.","r":["15:2.3","15:2.4","15:2.5"]},{"x":"Cem universos locais formam um setor menor, cem setores menores um setor maior e dez setores maiores um superuniverso, que contém cerca de um trilhão de planetas habitáveis.","r":["15:2.6","15:2.7","15:2.8"]},{"x":"Para todo o grande universo estão previstos cerca de sete trilhões de mundos habitáveis, mas esses números são apenas aproximações.","r":["15:2.9","15:2.25"]},{"x":"Os setores menores são governados por três Recentes dos Dias, os setores maiores por três Perfeições dos Dias e os superuniversos por três Anciães dos Dias.","r":["15:2.6","15:2.7","15:2.8"]}]},{"h":"Orvônton e o nosso lugar","items":[{"x":"Quase todas as estrelas visíveis a olho nu de Urântia pertencem a Orvônton, o sétimo superuniverso, e a Via Láctea é o núcleo central de Orvônton.","r":["15:3.1"]},{"x":"O centro de rotação do nosso setor menor situa-se na nuvem estelar de Sagitário, e todos os setores de Orvônton giram em torno de Uversa, a sua sede.","r":["15:3.5","15:3.7"]},{"x":"Urântia é o 606º mundo do sistema de Satânia e pertence a Orvônton por meio de Satânia, Norlatiadeque, Nébadon, Ensa e Esplândon.","r":["15:14.5","15:14.6","15:14.7"]},{"q":"O vosso planeta é membro de um enorme cosmo; vós pertenceis a uma família quase infinita de mundos, mas a vossa esfera é tão precisamente administrada e fomentada, com tanto e tal amor, que é como se ela fosse o único mundo habitado em toda a existência.","r":"15:14.9"}]},{"h":"Formação física e controle da energia","items":[{"x":"Os organizadores da força do Paraíso são iniciadores de nebulosas: mobilizam as forças do espaço para pôr em movimento as vastas rodas matrizes que dão origem aos sóis e aos sistemas.","r":["15:4.4"]},{"x":"A energia é distribuída universalmente, e não por nebulosas, de modo que cada universo local detém exatamente um centésimo de milésimo da energia total do seu superuniverso.","r":["15:4.6"]},{"x":"Todos os corpos espaciais, exceto as esferas arquitetônicas, são de origem evolucionária, e o nosso sistema solar consiste em planetas nascidos de um processo de explosão gravitacional.","r":["15:5.5","15:6.7"]},{"x":"A luz é matéria real, que tem peso, como mostram as caudas dos cometas, que apontam na direção oposta ao sol.","r":["15:6.13"]},{"q":"As nebulosas podem dispersar-se, os sóis, consumir-se, os sistemas, desaparecer e os planetas, perecer, mas os universos não se esvaem.","r":"15:8.10"}]},{"h":"O governo do superuniverso","items":[{"x":"As sedes dos superuniversos são mundos arquitetônicos especialmente construídos, que dão luz sem calor e situam-se perto do centro astronômico de cada superuniverso.","r":["15:7.1"]},{"q":"Na realidade, todos os mundos-sede são paradisíacos.","r":"15:7.3"},{"x":"O executivo do governo do superuniverso é formado pelos Anciães dos Dias, pelos Perfeccionadores da Sabedoria, pelos Conselheiros Divinos e pelos Censores Universais, juntamente com os mortais ascendentes glorificados: os Mensageiros Poderosos, Aqueles Elevados em Autoridade e Aqueles Sem Nome Nem Número.","r":["15:10.3","15:10.12"]},{"x":"Cada superuniverso é supervisionado por um dos Espíritos Mestres do Paraíso por meio dos Espíritos Refletivos estacionados na sua capital.","r":["9:8.3","116:4.4"]},{"x":"Os Filhos do universo local podem decretar a sobrevivência dos mortais, mas os veredictos executivos sobre a vida e a morte eternas são proferidos somente pelos Anciães dos Dias.","r":["15:12.2"]},{"x":"A assembleia deliberativa de Uversa é composta de representantes eleitos entre os graduados ascendentes qualificados para Havona, e nunca discordou do executivo.","r":["15:11.2","15:11.3"]}]},{"h":"Admissão na confederação e propósito","items":[{"x":"Um universo local só pode entrar na confederação do superuniverso depois de alcançar a estabilidade física e a lealdade espiritual ao seu Filho Soberano.","r":["15:9.16","15:9.17"]},{"x":"Nébadon ainda nem pertence à ordem física estabelecida do superuniverso, mas o governo do superuniverso anseia pela sua plena admissão e está ajudando-o.","r":["15:9.18"]},{"x":"Os superuniversos estão isolados uns dos outros e só sabem dos assuntos uns dos outros por meio da agência de distribuição do Paraíso, isolamento que continuará até que a soberania do Ser Supremo seja factualizada.","r":["15:10.23"]},{"x":"Cada um dos sete propósitos principais da evolução dos superuniversos é expresso mais plenamente em um superuniverso.","r":["15:14.1"]},{"q":"Orvônton é um universo que é uma demonstração de amor e de misericórdia.","r":"15:14.2"},{"x":"Em Orvônton, os propósitos dos outros seis superuniversos estão sendo interligados, e conjectura-se que Deus, o Supremo, poderá um dia governar, a partir de Uversa, os sete superuniversos aperfeiçoados.","r":["15:14.3","117:7.16"]}]}],"see":["Anciães dos Dias","Sete Espíritos Mestres","Universo local de Nébadon","Grande universo e universo-mestre","Havona","Ser Supremo"]},{"n":42,"t":"Sobrevivência","en":"Survival","sum":"Survival means that the mortal personality, beyond the death of the flesh, awakens again in the morontia worlds and continues the eternal ascent. The Urantia Book teaches that survival is a gift of God, but a gift that man must desire and choose for himself. What survives is the soul built together with the Adjuster, and the key to it is not knowledge or doctrine but the sincere determination to find God and be like him, and a living faith.","sections":[{"h":"Survival Is a Chosen Gift","items":[{"q":"survival is a gift of the Gods which must be desired by the creatures of time.","r":"110:2.2"},{"x":"Human identity is real only in so far as the personality chooses to become a continuing universe phenomenon, and that path must be pursued by free will.","r":["112:5.3"]},{"x":"Personality is destined for a divine goal, but man must choose for himself whether he will be present where that goal is attained.","r":["112:5.2"]},{"x":"The capacity to reject survival did not arise with the Lucifer rebellion; it is an endowment of choice that mortals have always possessed.","r":["54:6.9"]},{"q":"The energy system must continue, it has no choice; but man has everything to do with determining his own destiny.","r":"112:5.3"}]},{"h":"What Survives","items":[{"x":"The reality that survives the death of the material body and mind is the soul, the morontia self born of man and the Adjuster together.","r":["112:5.12"]},{"x":"After death the Adjuster goes to Divinington bearing the memory transcript of the life, and the soul is held by the guardian of destiny.","r":["112:3.5"]},{"x":"The surviving self evolves only by transferring the seat of identity from the material body to the immortal morontia soul.","r":["112:2.20"]},{"x":"Memories without spiritual meaning perish with the brain, but memories of relationships between personalities have cosmic value and remain.","r":["112:5.22"]},{"x":"Man survives mortal death by the identification of his identity with the indwelling spark of divinity.","r":["132:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Conditions of Survival","items":[{"q":"O segredo da sobrevivência está envolto no desejo humano supremo de ser semelhante a Deus e na conseqüente vontade empenhada no ato de fazer, e de ser, todas e quaisquer das coisas essenciais à maestria da realização final desse desejo.","r":"110:3.2"},{"x":"Success or failure in survival depends less on theories of belief than on decisions, determinations, and steadfast faith.","r":["110:3.2"]},{"q":"Apenas a resistência consciente ao guiamento do Ajustador pode impedir a sobrevivência da alma imortal em evolução.","r":"110:3.5"},{"x":"Ignorance, confusion, or fearful doubt alone cannot prevent the survival of the God-knowing soul.","r":["110:3.5"]},{"x":"Doing the will of God is the secret of survival and of perfection in survival.","r":["111:5.2"]}]},{"h":"Faith and the Assurance of Survival","items":[{"x":"Religious experience leads at last to a sure consciousness of God and an undoubted assurance of the survival of the believing personality.","r":["101:1.6"]},{"x":"Jesus taught that once one has established himself by faith as a son of God, there is nothing more to worry about regarding the certainty of survival.","r":["176:3.3"]},{"x":"The risen Jesus said that survival depends first on being born of the spirit that seeks truth and God.","r":["193:2.2"]},{"q":"Faith in the survival of supreme values is the core of religion;","r":"111:3.5"},{"x":"The faith-activated soul cannot stop, because it has the task of finding God, and once it reaches the goal it can never end.","r":["132:3.7"]}]},{"h":"Merciful Adjudication and the Orders of Survival","items":[{"x":"Every will creature is sure to experience one genuine opportunity to make an unquestioned final choice.","r":["112:5.9"]},{"x":"Those who, through no fault of their own, have not mastered the circles on earth are given extended probation if they have the will to survive.","r":["112:5.6"]},{"x":"When a verdict is in doubt, the universe government always decides in favor of the individual.","r":["112:5.7"]},{"x":"Survivors reach the mansion worlds in several orders, among them dispensational group roll calls, individual ascensions, and probationary dependents.","r":["49:6.4","49:6.8","49:6.11"]},{"x":"Those who attained the third circle or higher and received personal guardians may be repersonalized on the mansion worlds on the third day after death.","r":["49:6.9","112:4.12"]},{"q":"Seria preferível assumir o risco de uma rebelião sistêmica a arcar com o perigo de privar um mortal esforçado, vindo de qualquer mundo evolucionário, de continuar a sua luta até o eterno regozijo de perseguir a carreira ascensional.","r":"112:5.8"}]}],"see":["Morte","Alma","Ajustador do Pensamento","Mundos das mansões","Livre-arbítrio","Fé"]},{"n":97,"t":"Tempo e espaço","en":"Time and Space","sum":"In The Urantia Book time and space are the conjoined mechanism of the master universe, provided so that finite creatures can coexist with the Infinite. Space is a bestowal of Paradise that alternately expands and contracts as if breathing, and time arises from motion and from mind's awareness of sequence. Paradise has neither time nor space, and the maturing personality, by unifying past and future in the present, gradually transcends the limitations of time and participates in eternal purposes.","sections":[{"h":"A Device for Finite Creatures","items":[{"q":"O tempo e o espaço são um mecanismo conjunto do universo-mestre.","r":"118:9.1"},{"x":"Time and space insulate finite creatures from the absolute levels, and without them no mortal could exist.","r":["118:9.1"]},{"x":"Time and space are inseparably bound together only within the time-space creations of the seven superuniverses.","r":["12:5.3","65:8.1"]},{"q":"The grand universe is mechanism as well as organism, mechanical and living","r":"118:9.4"}]},{"h":"Space","items":[{"x":"Space is a bestowal of Paradise, yet it is neither infinite nor absolute, and we do not know its absolute limits.","r":["12:5.2","11:7.4"]},{"q":"O espaço não existe, em nenhuma das superfícies do Paraíso.","r":"11:7.1"},{"x":"Between pervaded and unpervaded space lie the relatively quiet midspace zones that separate them.","r":["11:7.2","11:7.3"]},{"x":"All space alternately contracts and expands as if breathing; when universe space expands, reservoir space contracts.","r":["11:6.1","11:6.2"]},{"x":"Space is not empty; it is the nonabsolute reality nearest to the absolute that man knows.","r":["130:7.6","118:3.5"]},{"x":"Space may be thought of as a property of bodies, so that when a body moves it carries its space with it.","r":["118:3.6"]}]},{"h":"Time","items":[{"x":"Time too is an indirect bestowal of Paradise, arising from motion and from mind's awareness of sequence.","r":["12:5.1"]},{"q":"O tempo é a corrente, que flui, dos eventos temporais percebidos pela consciência da criatura.","r":"130:7.4"},{"x":"Time is perceived on three levels: duration perceived by mind, motion toward God perceived by spirit, and the unique awareness of presence held by personality.","r":["12:5.6","12:5.9"]},{"x":"As man progresses inwardly, the sequence of events is increasingly seen as one related whole.","r":["130:7.5"]},{"x":"For an individual creature the standard of time is the length of its own life, and to those not bound by time evolution is not so long a process.","r":["65:8.3"]}]},{"h":"Time and Maturity","items":[{"x":"In any intelligence there is a direct relation between the degree of maturity and the unit of time consciousness.","r":["118:1.3"]},{"q":"Patience is exercised by those mortals whose time units are short","r":"118:1.6"},{"x":"True maturity transcends patience by a forbearance born of real understanding.","r":["118:1.6"]},{"x":"To mature is to live more intensely in the present while transcending its limits by embracing past experience and future values.","r":["118:1.5","118:1.7"]},{"x":"A spirit-indwelt person has forward-looking insight, and only a progressive, forward-looking attitude is personally real.","r":["12:5.10"]}]},{"h":"Truth and Eternity","items":[{"q":"As coisas são condicionadas pelo tempo, mas a verdade está fora do tempo.","r":"118:3.2"},{"x":"The more truth we know, the better we can understand the past and comprehend the future.","r":["118:3.2"]},{"x":"In the evolving universes eternity is temporal everlastingness, the everlasting now.","r":["118:1.1"]},{"x":"On infinite and absolute levels the present moment contains all of the past and all of the future.","r":["118:1.9"]},{"x":"Eternity cannot be comprehended by the finite minds of time, but it is better thought of as an endless circle than as a straight line.","r":["32:5.4","32:5.6"]}]},{"h":"Personality Transcending Time","items":[{"x":"Mortal personality can become eternal by choosing to do the Father's will and becoming one with the indwelling spirit.","r":["118:1.2"]},{"x":"To God as an absolute, an ascending mortal who has made the eternal decision is already a Paradise finaliter.","r":["118:1.10"]},{"x":"Paradise pilgrims become unconscious as they pass through the midspace zones in crossing from time to eternity.","r":["12:5.4"]},{"x":"As spiritual values are recognized, personality is gradually freed from the limitations of time and transcends the bounds of space.","r":["65:8.6"]}]}],"see":["Paraíso","Grande universo e universo-mestre","Realidade","Ser Supremo","Experiência","Busca da perfeição"]},{"n":10,"t":"Os três Absolutos","en":"The Three Absolutes","sum":"Os três Absolutos são os Absolutos da potencialidade: o Absoluto da Deidade, o Absoluto Inqualificável e o Absoluto Universal. O Absoluto da Deidade é a totalidade de todo potencial de Deidade; o Absoluto Inqualificável é a finalidade da realidade não deificada e de todo potencial impessoal; e o Absoluto Universal unifica e coordena os dois. Eles existem eternamente juntamente com a diferenciação da realidade feita pelo livre-arbítrio do Pai, e são o fundamento cósmico que torna possível a coexistência dos universos e das personalidades finitas com o Infinito.","sections":[{"h":"A diferenciação da realidade e os três Absolutos","items":[{"x":"A realidade infinita total existe em sete Absolutos coordenados, três dos quais são o Absoluto da Deidade, o Absoluto Universal e o Absoluto Inqualificável.","r":["0:3.1","104:3.5"]},{"x":"O Absoluto Universal resolve a tensão primordial que surgiu quando o Pai, por Seu livre-arbítrio, dividiu a realidade em deificada e não deificada.","r":["0:3.21","0:4.5"]},{"x":"Quando Havona foi criado, o Pai separou a sua presença do potencial infinito, e esse potencial está oculto no Absoluto Inqualificável e abrangido pelo Absoluto da Deidade.","r":["0:11.1"]},{"q":"Em última análise, e em uma compreensão final, todos os três são apenas um Absoluto.","r":"0:11.15"},{"x":"Nos níveis subinfinitos, os três Absolutos existem separadamente, mas na infinitude parecem ser um só.","r":["56:9.1"]}]},{"h":"O Absoluto da Deidade","items":[{"x":"O Absoluto da Deidade são as possibilidades causativas e potencialmente pessoais da realidade universal, a totalidade de todo potencial de Deidade.","r":["105:3.6"]},{"q":"O Absoluto de Deidade é qualificador do absoluto e absolutizador do qualificado — o iniciador do destino.","r":"105:3.6"},{"x":"O Absoluto da Deidade nunca parece reagir de modo subabsoluto a nenhuma situação, mas parece sempre reagir em função do bem-estar de toda a criação e de toda a eternidade futura.","r":["0:11.5"]},{"x":"Os valores espirituais existenciais encontram a sua origem e o seu destino na triunidade do Pai Universal, do Filho-Espírito e do Absoluto da Deidade.","r":["104:4.20","104:4.21"]},{"x":"O Filho Eterno domina os valores espirituais factuais, ao passo que o Absoluto da Deidade parece permear o vasto domínio dos valores espirituais que ainda são potenciais.","r":["7:1.10"]},{"x":"Deus, o Absoluto, existe agora como o Absoluto da Deidade, e postula-se que Ele possa tornar-Se experiencialmente personalizado por meio da função da Trindade Absoluta.","r":["0:2.18","106:6.6"]},{"q":"Eu amo e adoro a Deus, o Pai; mas respeito e honro o Absoluto da Deidade.","r":"10:8.5"}]},{"h":"O Absoluto Inqualificável","items":[{"x":"O Absoluto Inqualificável é não pessoal e não divino, e nem os fatos, nem a verdade, nem a experiência, nem a revelação podem penetrar a sua natureza.","r":["0:11.7"]},{"q":"The Unqualified Absolute is a positive universe overcontrol in infinity","r":"0:11.8"},{"x":"Não é uma influência vaga, como um conceito panteísta ou a hipótese do éter da ciência antiga, mas uma presença factual que permeia o grande universo e o espaço além dele.","r":["0:11.8","0:11.9"]},{"x":"O Absoluto Inqualificável é coordenado com o Paraíso, e em todo o espaço somente a sua presença está em quiescência.","r":["105:3.4","105:3.7"]},{"x":"A potência do espaço, a energia que ainda não responde à gravidade do Paraíso, deriva do Absoluto Inqualificável.","r":["0:6.5"]}]},{"h":"O Absoluto Universal","items":[{"x":"O Absoluto Universal unifica o deificado e o não deificado e correlaciona o absoluto e o relativo.","r":["105:3.8"]},{"q":"The finite can coexist in the cosmos along with the Infinite","r":"0:11.13"},{"x":"Isso é possível porque o Absoluto Universal equaliza as tensões entre o tempo e a eternidade, o finito e o infinito, o homem e Deus.","r":["0:11.13"]},{"x":"A diferença de potencial infinito entre o Absoluto Inqualificável e o Absoluto da Deidade torna possível a existência dos universos materiais e das personalidades finitas no tempo.","r":["0:11.12"]},{"x":"Acredita-se que a presença imprevisível que atua ao lado dos circuitos da mente derive em parte da função do Absoluto Universal.","r":["9:6.8"]}]},{"h":"A triunidade da potencialidade e o destino","items":[{"x":"A associação dos três Absolutos não é uma trindade, mas a triunidade da potencialidade, já que nem todos os três são Deidade.","r":["104:5.7","106:5.4"]},{"x":"A triunidade da potencialidade correlaciona todas as realidades latentes de energia, espirituais, mentais e cósmicas, e é infinita em potencialidade.","r":["104:5.11"]},{"x":"Os potenciais podem em parte deixar de se realizar no tempo, mas não falham na sua totalidade, e a vontade de Deus acaba por prevalecer.","r":["115:3.13"]},{"x":"Dentro dos três Absolutos sempre permanecem possibilidades desconhecidas que nenhum desenvolvimento experiencial poderá jamais esgotar.","r":["106:7.1"]},{"q":"A busca de Deus é infindável!","r":"106:7.5"},{"x":"Os Absolutos não são uma deidade impessoal panteísta; em tudo o que diz respeito à personalidade do universo, eles estão estritamente limitados pela Trindade e dominados pela Deidade.","r":["0:11.16"]}]}],"see":["Trindade do Paraíso","Pai Universal","Paraíso","Deus, o Último","Realidade","Energia e matéria"]},{"n":6,"t":"Trindade do Paraíso","en":"Paradise Trinity","sum":"A Trindade do Paraíso é a união indivisível de Deidade de três pessoas coordenadas: o Pai, o Filho e o Espírito. A Trindade não é ela própria uma personalidade, mas é uma realidade verdadeira e absoluta cujas funções são mais do que a soma dos atributos das três pessoas. Ela administra a justiça e exerce o supracontrole da totalidade nos universos, e é o único fato inevitável do universo, aquele que liberta o Pai do absolutismo da personalidade, de modo que Ele possa outorgar-Se sem reservas.","sections":[{"h":"A única união inevitável","items":[{"x":"A Trindade une a expressão da vontade pessoal infinita de Deus ao caráter absoluto da Deidade, libertando o Pai das limitações do absolutismo da personalidade.","r":["10:0.1"]},{"q":"we can discover only one inescapable inevitability in universe affairs, and that is the Paradise Trinity.","r":"10:0.3"},{"x":"O Pai transmitiu aos Seus Filhos todo o poder e toda a autoridade que podem ser delegados; a personalidade divina não é egocêntrica e compraz-se em compartilhar.","r":["10:1.2","10:1.3"]},{"x":"Ao outorgar personalidade absoluta ao Filho, o Pai tornou-Se o Pai do Filho, e o Pai e o Filho, juntos, outorgaram personalidade conjunta ao Espírito Infinito.","r":["10:1.4","10:2.2"]}]},{"h":"Três pessoas, uma Deidade","items":[{"q":"Não obstante exista apenas uma Deidade, há três personalizações positivas e divinas da Deidade.","r":"10:3.1"},{"x":"Cada um dos três é original, nenhum é duplicata do outro e, no entanto, todos estão unidos.","r":["10:2.6"]},{"x":"Somente o Filho Eterno experimenta ao mesmo tempo a filiação em relação ao Pai e a paternidade em relação ao Espírito, e assim conhece a plenitude da relação de personalidade divina.","r":["10:2.7"]},{"q":"God speaks through the Son and, with the Son, acts through the Infinite Spirit","r":"10:3.3"},{"x":"A paternidade não é real sem a filiação, e o Pai nunca existiu sozinho, sem o Filho e o Espírito.","r":["10:3.5"]},{"x":"Fora de Havona, o Pai atua por meio dos Filhos Criadores, da gravidade, do Filho, do Criador Conjunto, do circuito da personalidade e dos Ajustadores, e, como Deidade total, Ele atua somente na Trindade.","r":["10:3.9","10:3.16"]}]},{"h":"Uma realidade verdadeira, não uma personalidade","items":[{"x":"A Trindade é uma associação de pessoas infinitas que atuam em uma capacidade impessoal, mas não contrária à personalidade, comparável a uma corporação que age segundo a vontade pessoal dos seus membros.","r":["10:4.3"]},{"q":"A Trindade é uma realidade de Deidade que é uma supersomatória e factualiza-se na conjunção das três Deidades do Paraíso.","r":"104:2.4"},{"x":"As três Deidades, como indivíduos, podem cooperar como quiserem, mas tal cooperação não é a Trindade.","r":["10:4.4"]},{"x":"Assim como o potencial de um grupo excede a soma dos atributos dos seus membros, as funções da Trindade são mais do que a simples soma dos atributos das três Deidades.","r":["10:5.2"]},{"x":"Há muitas triunidades existenciais, mas uma só Trindade existencial; a Trindade não é uma associação funcional, mas Deidade indivisa.","r":["104:3.15","104:3.16"]}]},{"h":"A justiça e o supracontrole cósmico","items":[{"x":"A lei procede do Pai, a administração da lei espiritual cabe ao Filho, a revelação da lei ao Espírito, e a justiça, que é a aplicação da lei, pertence à Trindade.","r":["10:6.1"]},{"q":"A Justiça nunca é uma atitude pessoal; é sempre uma função plural.","r":"10:6.2"},{"x":"Os Filhos estacionários da Trindade, como os Anciães dos Dias, administram os julgamentos dos superuniversos com base nas provas apresentadas pelas personalidades do Espírito Infinito.","r":["10:6.4","10:6.17"]},{"x":"A justiça é o pensamento coletivo da retidão, e a misericórdia é a sua expressão pessoal; quando plenamente compreendidos, a justiça da Trindade e o amor do Pai coincidem.","r":["10:6.18"]},{"x":"Em relação ao finito, a Trindade atua como a Trindade da Supremacia e, em relação ao absonito, como a Trindade da Ultimidade.","r":["10:5.4","10:5.5"]},{"x":"Mesmo as catástrofes e as mudanças inexplicáveis da vida podem ser entretecidas em um desenho significativo por meio das funções do Supremo e do supracontrole da Trindade.","r":["10:7.5"]}]},{"h":"A compreensão humana da Trindade","items":[{"x":"Os conceitos de deidade trina da religião evolucionária surgiram de associações naturais, como as falanges de um dedo ou um banquinho de três pernas, e devem ser distinguidos do conceito revelado da Trindade.","r":["104:0.1","104:0.3"]},{"q":"Uma verdadeira concepção trinitária não é apenas um agrupamento de três deuses separados.","r":"104:1.7"},{"x":"Em Urântia, a Trindade foi apresentada sucessivamente pelo corpo de assessores de Caligástia, por Adão e Eva e por Maquiventa Melquisedeque.","r":["104:1.1","104:1.2","104:1.3"]},{"x":"O conceito cristão da Trindade, embora errôneo quanto aos fatos, era praticamente verdadeiro no que diz respeito às relações espirituais.","r":["104:1.13"]},{"x":"Uma Deidade pessoal requer relação com outras personalidades iguais; um conceito de Deidade sem tal relação facilmente se reduz a um absoluto panteísta.","r":["104:2.2"]},{"x":"O reconhecimento do conceito da Trindade torna possível certa compreensão da inter-relação entre o amor e a lei nas criações do tempo e do espaço.","r":["104:2.3"]}]}],"see":["Pai Universal","Filho Eterno","Espírito Infinito","Os três Absolutos","Ser Supremo","Justiça"]},{"n":15,"t":"Universo local de Nébadon","en":"Local Universe of Nebadon","sum":"Nébadon é o universo local, organizado e governado pelo Filho Criador Michael e pelo Espírito Materno do Universo, ao qual pertence Urântia. Destinado a ser composto de cem constelações e dez mil sistemas, é uma criação relativamente jovem de Orvônton; a partir da sua capital, Sálvington, Michael governa como representante do Pai e do Filho, enquanto Gabriel serve como executivo-chefe. O universo local é evolucionário, e as criaturas alcançam a perfeição ascendendo passo a passo a partir de baixo.","sections":[{"h":"Um universo local em evolução","items":[{"x":"Um universo local é obra de um Filho Criador da ordem de Michael; é composto de cem constelações, cada uma das quais contém cem sistemas.","r":["32:0.1"]},{"x":"Todos os universos do tempo e do espaço são evolucionários, e os planos dos Filhos Criadores seguem sempre o caminho do desenvolvimento progressivo das criaturas.","r":["32:0.2"]},{"x":"Um universo local é concebido pelos Arquitetos do Universo-Mestre no Paraíso, e o Filho Criador só começa a organizá-lo depois que os diretores de potência mobilizaram as energias do espaço.","r":["32:0.4","32:1.2"]},{"x":"Nébadon estende-se até onde chega a presença espacial do Espírito Materno de Sálvington; o que está além encontra-se fora de Nébadon.","r":["41:0.1"]},{"q":"Exceto no universo central, a perfeição é alcançada progressivamente.","r":"32:3.3"}]},{"h":"Organização e o nosso lugar","items":[{"x":"A primeira criação física concluída em Nébadon foi o mundo-sede, Sálvington, seguido de cem sedes de constelação e de dez mil sedes de sistema.","r":["32:2.3"]},{"x":"Sálvington está situado no centro exato de energia-massa do universo local.","r":["32:2.4"]},{"x":"No último registro, Nébadon tinha 3.840.101 planetas habitados, e a organização de moradas planetárias ainda está em andamento.","r":["32:2.9"]},{"x":"Nébadon situa-se perto da borda de Orvônton, e Satânia, por sua vez, na periferia de Nébadon.","r":["32:2.11"]},{"x":"Nébadon é o octogésimo quarto universo do setor menor de Ensa, e Sálvington é a sua capital.","r":["15:14.6"]}]},{"h":"Michael, o Filho Soberano","items":[{"x":"Michael de Nébadon é a 611.121ª personalização de um conceito original procedente do Pai e do Filho Eterno; ele não é o próprio Filho Eterno do Paraíso.","r":["33:1.1","33:1.2"]},{"q":"To our universe and all its inhabited worlds the Sovereign Son is, to all practical intents and purposes, God.","r":"33:1.4"},{"x":"Tendo completado as suas sete auto-outorgas como criatura, Michael governa Nébadon como um soberano de misericórdia compreensiva.","r":["119:0.4","119:0.7"]},{"x":"O seu poder só é limitado pelos circuitos da gravidade do Paraíso e pelos Anciães dos Dias, que se reservam o veredicto final sobre a extinção da personalidade.","r":["33:2.2"]},{"x":"Na administração do universo local, o Pai atua somente por meio do Filho Criador, mas Ele está intimamente presente nos mortais como o Ajustador residente.","r":["33:0.1","32:3.4"]}]},{"h":"O governo conjunto do Filho e do Espírito","items":[{"x":"O Espírito Materno do Universo cria e governa o universo juntamente com Michael, e o Filho concede ao Espírito uma posição coordenada e autoridade igual em todos os assuntos.","r":["33:3.2","33:3.3"]},{"x":"Quando Michael voltou da sua auto-outorga em Urântia, o Espírito do Universo reconheceu publicamente, pela primeira vez, a sua subordinação ao Filho.","r":["33:3.5"]},{"x":"O Filho proclamou então, na “Proclamação da Igualdade”, que o Espírito é igual a ele em todos os atributos de personalidade, um ideal elevado para a família e o casamento.","r":["33:3.6"]},{"q":"O Filho e o Espírito-Mãe agora presidem ao universo de uma forma muito semelhante àquela pela qual um pai e uma mãe velam pela sua família de filhos e filhas, e suprem-na.","r":"33:3.7"},{"x":"Diante da rebelião, somente o Filho atua como salvador, mas nenhum Filho poderia ter êxito sem a cooperação incessante da Ministra Divina.","r":["33:3.4"]}]},{"h":"Administração e tribunais","items":[{"x":"Gabriel, o Brilhante Estrela Matutino, nascido da primeira criação conjunta do Filho e do Espírito, é o executivo-chefe de Nébadon.","r":["32:2.6","33:4.5"]},{"x":"Emanuel de Sálvington, o embaixador da Trindade, é a única personalidade de Nébadon que não reconhece subordinação a Michael, e só aconselha quando solicitado.","r":["33:5.1","33:5.2"]},{"x":"Os sistemas ocupam-se principalmente dos problemas biológicos, as constelações da unidade e da estabilidade sociais, e os governantes do universo do estado espiritual dos reinos.","r":["33:6.3"]},{"x":"Michael ocupa-se somente da criação, da sustentação e da ministração; os criadores nunca se sentam para julgar as suas próprias criaturas.","r":["33:7.1"]},{"q":"Vós estais vivendo em um universo bem ordenado e, mais cedo ou mais tarde, podeis confiar que sereis tratados com a justiça devida e até mesmo com misericórdia.","r":"33:7.8"}]},{"h":"A ascensão e o propósito das criaturas","items":[{"q":"É um fato: aquele que houver visto um Filho Criador terá visto o Pai.","r":"32:3.6"},{"x":"Quanto mais baixo uma criatura está na escala da vida, mais difícil lhe é reconhecer o Pai no Filho Criador, mas apegar-se à verdade da presença do Pai nos Seus Filhos é a salvaguarda mais segura.","r":["32:3.6"]},{"x":"A origem evolucionária animal não é um estigma; os que sobem a escada da vida a partir de baixo obtêm maior honra e uma experiência mais plena.","r":["32:3.10"]},{"x":"O universo local é o ponto de partida da verdadeira evolução, onde personalidades imperfeitas cocriam o seu próprio futuro e no qual até os criadores evoluem.","r":["116:4.8"]},{"x":"Na mente de Deus há um plano eterno de oportunidade infinita e de vida sem fim que abrange toda criatura.","r":["32:5.7"]},{"q":"A meta da eternidade está adiante!","r":"32:5.8"}]}],"see":["Filho Criador Michael","Espírito Materno do Universo Local","Constelações e sistemas locais","Os sete superuniversos","Auto-outorga de Jesus","Urântia"]},{"n":95,"t":"Urântia","en":"Urantia","sum":"Urantia is the universe name of the earth on which we live, the 606th inhabited world of the system of Satania, in the constellation of Norlatiadek, in the local universe of Nebadon. Urantia is a life-modification world where the Life Carriers formulated an original life, and an isolated world spiritually quarantined through Caligastia's betrayal and Adam's default. Yet it is also known throughout the universe as the \"World of the Cross,\" where Michael, the Creator Son, made his final bestowal.","sections":[{"h":"Its Place in the Universe","items":[{"q":"O vosso mundo é chamado de Urântia, e o seu número é 606, no grupo planetário, ou sistema, que é o de Satânia.","r":"15:14.5"},{"x":"Urantia belongs to Norlatiadek, one of the one hundred constellations of the local universe of Nebadon, which is part of the superuniverse of Orvonton.","r":["43:0.1","0:0.5"]},{"x":"Satania is an unfinished system with only 619 inhabited worlds, and the number 606 means that this was the 606th world in it on which human beings appeared.","r":["49:0.3"]},{"x":"Urantia reached its present size about a billion years ago and was entered under this name in the physical registry of Nebadon.","r":["57:8.1"]}]},{"h":"A Life-Modification World","items":[{"x":"Urantia originated from your sun, which is one of the many offspring of the Andronover nebula.","r":["57:1.1"]},{"x":"There are only sixty-one life-modification planets like Urantia in all Satania, and Urantia was a decimal planet on which the life designs could be modified.","r":["58:0.1","58:1.1"]},{"q":"A vida de Urântia é única, e original com o planeta.","r":"58:4.1"},{"x":"The ancient inland seas were the cradle of evolution, recording the history of life on pages of stone.","r":["57:8.26"]},{"x":"Man can live in comfort thanks to more than forty seemingly accidental protective factors, such as the ozone layer.","r":["58:2.4"]},{"x":"Urantia was officially recognized as a planet of human habitation 993,408 years ago, and its first parents were Andon and Fonta.","r":["62:7.7","63:0.2"]}]},{"h":"An Isolated World","items":[{"q":"Uma parte muito grande da dificuldade que os mortais de Urântia têm de compreender Deus deve-se às conseqüências, de longo alcance, da rebelião de Lúcifer e da traição de Caligástia.","r":"4:3.3"},{"x":"Since Caligastia's betrayal, Urantia has been one of the isolated worlds of Norlatiadek, with a Most High observer stationed on it.","r":["43:5.17"]},{"x":"The Life Carriers regret that Caligastia's betrayal and Adam's default greatly hindered their efforts to improve intelligent life.","r":["65:5.1"]},{"x":"The planet's spiritual isolation had no effect on the presence and function of the spirit-gravity circuit of the Eternal Son.","r":["7:1.7"]},{"x":"Urantia is still under partial spiritual quarantine, so the reflective seraphim cannot function freely.","r":["28:7.4"]}]},{"h":"The Opportunity of Isolation","items":[{"q":"Entretanto, o isolamento dessas esferas proporciona às suas raças uma oportunidade única para o exercício da fé e o desenvolvimento de uma qualidade especial de confiabilidade cósmica: uma convicção que não depende da vista nem de qualquer outro aspecto material.","r":"50:7.1"},{"x":"Mortals from worlds quarantined because of rebellion may turn out in the end to be extremely fortunate.","r":["50:7.1"]},{"x":"Though Urantia mortals differ in opportunity and endowment, their spiritual endowment is equal, since all enjoy the same indwelling divine spirit.","r":["5:1.5"]}]},{"h":"The World of the Bestowal","items":[{"x":"Your little world has become known throughout Nebadon as the place where Michael completed the experience required for sovereignty.","r":["119:8.2"]},{"q":"É um fato que Urântia tornou-se conhecida, em outros planetas habitados vizinhos, como o “Mundo da Cruz”.","r":"188:4.1"},{"x":"On completing his Urantia bestowal Michael received the title Planetary Prince of Urantia and sought to set right the confusion left by Caligastia's betrayal.","r":["120:2.3"]},{"x":"The life lived on Urantia was intended as an inspiration not only to this planet but to beings on all the worlds of Nebadon.","r":["120:2.7"]}]},{"h":"The Future of Urantia","items":[{"x":"Urantia's greatest handicaps on the way to light and life are disease, degeneracy, war, multicolored races, and multilingualism.","r":["55:3.21"]},{"x":"When that time comes, Machiventa Melchizedek, the vicegerent Planetary Prince, will take the place of Planetary Sovereign.","r":["55:7.3"]},{"x":"Even if Urantia is restored to the system circuits, difficulties will remain for a time because all of Satania is isolated.","r":["46:8.2"]},{"q":"Jesus de Nazaré, como homem entre os homens, pessoalmente alcançou o status de luz e vida há mais de dezenove séculos, no passado, em Urântia.","r":"55:11.7"}]}],"see":["Universo local de Nébadon","Constelações e sistemas locais","Evolução","Rebelião de Lúcifer","Caligástia","Auto-outorga de Jesus"]},{"n":57,"t":"Verdade","en":"Truth","sum":"Truth is a spirit-discerned living reality that goes beyond knowledge, which deals with facts, and wisdom, which deals with relationships, to deal with reality values. God is the first truth, and all truth issues from him. Truth cannot be confined in words or creeds but is defined only by living, and static truth is dead truth. The Spirit of Truth enables people to realize this living, growing truth, and truth is unified with beauty and goodness in God.","sections":[{"h":"What Truth Is","items":[{"q":"A verdade não pode ser definida por palavras, apenas vivendo-a.","r":"132:3.2"},{"x":"Knowledge originates in science, wisdom in philosophy, and truth in the religious experience of spiritual living; truth deals with reality values.","r":["132:3.2"]},{"x":"Knowledge is demonstrable, but truth is experienced; knowledge is a possession of the mind, truth an experience of the soul.","r":["130:4.10"]},{"x":"God is the first truth and the last fact, so all truth takes origin in him.","r":["102:6.6"]},{"x":"Truth is always a revelation: autorevelation when it comes through the work of the Adjuster, epochal revelation when presented by celestial agencies.","r":["101:4.3"]}]},{"h":"Living Truth","items":[{"x":"Physical facts are uniform, but truth is a living and flexible factor in the philosophy of the universe.","r":["2:7.2"]},{"x":"Truth cannot be imprisoned in formulas, codes, or creeds; when one attempts to formulate it, it speedily dies.","r":["180:5.2"]},{"q":"Verdade estática é verdade morta, e apenas a verdade morta pode ser mantida como uma teoria.","r":"180:5.2"},{"x":"Truth is unshaken by shocks and free from all temporal fluctuations, yet it is never formalized and is always vital.","r":["118:3.3"]},{"x":"It is folly to regard the past as the only source of truth, for truth lives always in the present and finds new expression in each generation.","r":["79:8.8"]},{"q":"A verdade é relativa e está em expansão; ela vive sempre no presente, alcançando uma nova expressão em cada geração de homens — e mesmo em cada vida humana.","r":"79:8.8"}]},{"h":"The Way to Know Truth","items":[{"x":"Truth cannot become man's possession without faith, for a person's thoughts and ideals can never rise higher than his faith.","r":["132:3.5"]},{"q":"Revealed truth, personally discovered truth, is the supreme delight of the human soul","r":"132:3.4"},{"x":"Fearing the unknown, man tends to fixate science, formalize philosophy, and dogmatize truth.","r":["132:3.3"]},{"x":"There is never conflict between true knowledge and truth; conflict arises between knowledge and human beliefs colored by prejudice and fear.","r":["132:3.4"]},{"x":"The more one knows truth and the more one becomes truth, the more one can understand the past and grasp the future.","r":["118:3.2"]}]},{"h":"The Spirit of Truth","items":[{"x":"The Spirit of Truth is not the letter or law of truth but the conviction of true meanings on real spirit levels, a living and growing teacher.","r":["180:5.1"]},{"x":"The God-knowing person lifts wisdom to the level of living truth, but the spiritually unprogressive soul drags living truth down to dead wisdom.","r":["180:5.4"]},{"x":"Even the golden rule remains a mere ethical rule without the insight of the Spirit of Truth; its meaning is realized only by living it.","r":["180:5.5","180:5.11"]},{"x":"Truth, the understanding of cosmic relationships and spiritual values, is best attained through the ministry of the Spirit of Truth.","r":["103:7.8"]},{"q":"A verdade divina é uma realidade viva discernida pelo espírito.","r":"180:5.2"}]},{"h":"Truth, Beauty, and Goodness","items":[{"q":"A verdade é bela, porque é tanto completa quanto simétrica.","r":"2:7.4"},{"x":"Because truth can be acted upon and lived, happiness follows the recognition of truth, while disappointment and sorrow follow error.","r":["2:7.6"]},{"x":"All truth, whether material, philosophic, or spiritual, is both beautiful and good.","r":["2:7.11"]},{"x":"Truth is coherent, beauty attractive, and goodness stabilizing; when these are harmonized, they become a high love.","r":["2:7.12"]},{"x":"Truth is the basis of science and philosophy and the intellectual foundation of religion.","r":["56:10.10"]}]}],"see":["Beleza","Bondade","Espírito da Verdade","Sabedoria","Fé","Revelação"]},{"n":50,"t":"Vontade de Deus","en":"Will of God","sum":"The will of God is the eternal purpose of the First Source and Center, and in the life of the individual it is partnership with the way and choice of God. The Urantia Book regards doing the will of God as the secret of survival and of perfection, and says that it is not a surrender of will but its consecration and expansion. Throughout his life Jesus lived \"not my will but yours\" and became the example of that way.","sections":[{"h":"What the Will of God Is","items":[{"x":"The will of God is the purpose of the First Source and Center, personalized in the Eternal Son and shown in universe action in the Infinite Spirit.","r":["117:0.1"]},{"q":"“A vontade de Deus é o caminho de Deus, é compartilhar da escolha de Deus em face de qualquer alternativa potencial.","r":"130:2.7"},{"x":"Doing the will of God is therefore the experience of becoming more and more like God, the source of all that is good, beautiful, and true.","r":["130:2.7"]},{"x":"Doing the will of God reveals a willingness to share one's inner life with God, and sharing is a divine thing.","r":["111:5.1"]},{"x":"In his mind Jesus unified all the attributes of God in \"the will of the Father in heaven.\"","r":["196:0.2"]}]},{"h":"The Gift of a Dedicated Will","items":[{"x":"The loving dedication of the human will to doing the Father's will is the highest and the only truly valuable gift man can offer God.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"x":"God requires no coerced worship or slavish service; man must of himself love and worship God.","r":["1:1.2"]},{"q":"Such a creature choice is not a surrender of will. It is a consecration of will, an expansion of will, a glorification of will, a perfecting of will","r":"111:5.5"},{"x":"This choice lies less in the negation \"not my will but yours\" than in the positive affirmation \"it is my will that your will be done.\"","r":["111:5.6"]},{"x":"God too first consented to entrust a fragment of himself to the human will and to dwell within it.","r":["111:5.3","111:5.4"]},{"q":"The affectionate dedication of the human will to the doing of the Father's will is man's choicest gift to God","r":"1:1.2"}]},{"h":"The Fruits of a Life That Does His Will","items":[{"x":"The imitation of God is the key to perfection, and doing his will is the secret of survival and perfection.","r":["111:5.2"]},{"x":"Peace in this life, survival after death, perfection in the next life, and service in eternity are already achieved in spirit when one chooses to submit the will to the Father's will.","r":["111:5.4"]},{"x":"By choosing to do the Father's will, the mortal personality may become one with the indwelling spirit and so become eternal.","r":["118:1.2"]},{"x":"A life that lives the Father's will is founded on truth, sensitive to beauty, governed by goodness, and shown outwardly in loving service.","r":["106:9.12"]},{"x":"In many cases the Thought Adjuster is dispatched at the very moment a person quietly resolves to do the Father's will.","r":["108:2.10"]},{"q":"A imitação de Deus é a chave da perfeição; fazer a Sua vontade é o segredo da sobrevivência e da perfeição na sobrevivência.","r":"111:5.2"}]},{"h":"The Adventure of Finding and Doing His Will","items":[{"q":"Jamais esqueçais de que só há uma aventura que pode ser mais satisfatória e emocionante do que tentar descobrir a vontade do Deus vivo, e essa é a experiência suprema de tentar honestamente fazer a vontade divina.","r":"155:6.11"},{"x":"The will of God can be done in any occupation, and for those who are spirit led there is no division between holy and secular callings.","r":["155:6.11"]},{"x":"When one is wholly dedicated to the Father's will, prayer comes into harmony with that will, and every petition is answered.","r":["146:2.7"]},{"x":"The idea of sacrifice impairs the efficacy of true prayer by offering material things instead of one's own will.","r":["91:2.4"]},{"x":"The will of God does not prevail from moment to moment, but viewed over a whole lifetime it becomes ever clearer in the fruits of those who are led by the spirit.","r":["12:7.7"]}]},{"h":"Jesus, the Example of a Life Lived in the Father's Will","items":[{"q":"“A despeito de quem eu seja e do poder que possa ou não exercer, eu tenho sempre sido, e sempre serei, submisso à vontade do meu Pai do Paraíso”.","r":"128:7.2"},{"x":"In every situation of life the mind of Jesus held to \"not my will but yours,\" and this consecration is the true passport to divine attainment.","r":["109:6.5"]},{"x":"The great task of Michael's bestowal was to reveal God to the creatures of flesh by living a life that did the Father's will.","r":["120:2.8"]},{"x":"By dedicating his will to doing the divine will, Jesus made the greatest offering man can make to God.","r":["196:0.10"]},{"x":"Jesus tried to persuade his disciples to use \"the will of God\" in place of the word \"kingdom.\"","r":["170:2.11"]}]}],"see":["Livre-arbítrio","Reino do céu","Oração","Adoração","Caráter de Jesus","Ser Supremo"]}];
